[{"sha":"3bb7b1c8903e90b77630324222956eb9d83fc4b9","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDNiYjdiMWM4OTAzZTkwYjc3NjMwMzI0MjIyOTU2ZWI5ZDgzZmM0Yjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-14T06:42:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T06:42:31Z"},"message":"docs: comparison table — \"PII detection & flagging\", not \"quarantine\" (#345)\n\n## Summary\n\nFollow-up to #344. That PR fixed the Governance bullet (PII\n*\"auto-detected and flagged\"*) but missed the **capability comparison\ntable**, which still advertised **`PII detection & quarantine ✅`** for\nMemClaw.\n\nThe OSS engine only **detects and flags** PII —\n`merge_enrichment_fields.py` sets `metadata.contains_pii` / `pii_types`\nand nothing else (no status change, no visibility downgrade, no\nredaction, no blocking). Quarantine / boundary enforcement is an\nenterprise-gateway capability, not OSS.\n\nRelabel the row to `PII detection & flagging` so the table matches both\nthe OSS behavior and the corrected bullet.\n\nDocs-only.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d07c8dd5284bc361bf986ab3f2b8edf52f77f64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0d07c8dd5284bc361bf986ab3f2b8edf52f77f64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/3bb7b1c8903e90b77630324222956eb9d83fc4b9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLk1XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiekQAA1gqR8W1usQ5yuDd0nys5OO\nDsnftK0V2VDgZb9lEUi9uWqjHBqKkiLEv/fyS8ZE3O6CMsQuXE+vc4/2UCd/7wSY\nBHPHCi2ugLQa6sEmdwxwm1CQRR4X1oXZyPSh0I+rOw9QPVi8OrJIfbu11DId13tn\nZZ2LFEqBPL7LJ4MBdfiOtrHhLqS5RNHOXUbjTNryVDNYV/mvFfb0RDw1mv0y4Qsj\nV2QvZWjk0KEYMj958ojIXPRsGr5Xki69qd/4sp4tH7Vwldj8CmbxaVcV86gyQwph\n2S0iFBdk+MXnNkdzNVdqEfZJwtPIMtjBNl3j2JwlEujR8spH2mdF7S7OF7dO0TBN\nMBcArcCeULLYUkKru8VKZPMh7xVFZgp8slEa+sOBE4xTEO7W11fl74wI+RS3x9ul\nNkRdIMAkBA+UHt0LgjMPZWfTGBDTqGMQ399qfZAM36gtJHVBeV6IIlAzO6zJ8iSR\nEgIHt3JxyDJm51Af57g+X5OM9UH+nJrkao7sr6AzZ76szF5JiEvKh00EHtgHxdpH\nsf9C8E5qrsB5yM1twp4BtlzLEqHs/VyOJ2ruhI1WfJETfXucITOuU095fblUxiwL\nV5LRilPzotTodBHuEsoy9RKGL95AQ4cJ+j/QhPw0TpD5N9zk4WgdFgJ5x3Mxyu2t\nzwrCSqBlfzankcJ4Q6Qx\n=poT7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0d07c8dd5284bc361bf986ab3f2b8edf52f77f64\nparent 94dcbcd6f0bd69b0b93e94bf57ce9cb9719559ab\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781419351 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781419351 +0300\n\ndocs: comparison table — \"PII detection & flagging\", not \"quarantine\" (#345)\n\n## Summary\n\nFollow-up to #344. That PR fixed the Governance bullet (PII\n*\"auto-detected and flagged\"*) but missed the **capability comparison\ntable**, which still advertised **`PII detection & quarantine ✅`** for\nMemClaw.\n\nThe OSS engine only **detects and flags** PII —\n`merge_enrichment_fields.py` sets `metadata.contains_pii` / `pii_types`\nand nothing else (no status change, no visibility downgrade, no\nredaction, no blocking). Quarantine / boundary enforcement is an\nenterprise-gateway capability, not OSS.\n\nRelabel the row to `PII detection & flagging` so the table matches both\nthe OSS behavior and the corrected bullet.\n\nDocs-only.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T06:42:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3bb7b1c8903e90b77630324222956eb9d83fc4b9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3bb7b1c8903e90b77630324222956eb9d83fc4b9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3bb7b1c8903e90b77630324222956eb9d83fc4b9/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254