n* cross-tenant search widening, non-default LLM structured-output\nkwargs, event deploy safety\n([#322](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/322))\n([f161607](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/f1616070b72efbfba712de4095f6f556669368cc))\n* **embedding:** fall back to default model when OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL\nis empty ([#336](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/336))\n([d1f1f5a](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/d1f1f5a6f8ac4a631b4bb8dfa89801384e4aea44))\n* **entities:** scope-filter relations in get_entity and drop the\nper-memory agent lookup\n([#321](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/321))\n([e355f87](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/e355f87fba54ca45b634bf2affd4b9893a0e3528))\n* **entity-linking:** bind reinforce weight directly — LEAST over\nuntyped params coerced to text\n([#341](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/341))\n([b4a5712](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/b4a57120107c2319013e8ac64aa6aaecc87d0751))\n* **entity-linking:** synchronize_session=False on the entity-embedding\nbackfill bulk update\n([#342](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/342))\n([c310ecf](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/c310ecfd61ee14b0545234b7bb4773fbc0e1685e))\n* **events:** publisher candidate cleanups also called the nonexistent\nclose() ([#331](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/331))\n([610fe8e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/610fe8e385c38237cf22276a02ef35e9345772d2))\n* **events:** pubsub shutdown never flushed the publisher — final\nbatches silently lost\n([#330](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/330))\n([1c2aba5](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1c2aba577a1a7cd4347faff3118d7179c39a7368))\n* **llm:** explicit httpx per-phase timeouts — 5s connect too tight\nbehind VPC connector\n([#332](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/332))\n([ea89a61](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ea89a61cb3b6b4331b92183dfe09f3bbfc24e879))\n* **logging:** reroute idempotency guard mis-keys on captured handlers\n([#328](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/328))\n([352689d](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/352689d3f18c2d00b4444cca62d80d1b4b340109))\n* **mcp:** enforce gateway perimeter on the /mcp header-trust path\n([#319](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/319))\n([109d837](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/109d837950550a577f4fcb8e585e76105b961d9b))\n* **mcp:** memclaw_tune crashed with 'dict' object has no attribute 'id'\n([#338](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/338))\n([30e3cff](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/30e3cff097c73d0af6faec739f638c5fecf46aef))\n* **plugin:** point agents at the memclaw skill by name, not by\nfilesystem path (CAURA-000)\n([#323](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/323))\n([ec3fcaf](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ec3fcaf45a7545568e9f713a6f1db631dfa1c2f3))\n* **release:** keep plugin/src/version.ts in sync on release-please PRs\n([#335](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/335))\n([e26a3c5](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/e26a3c561b542fbf58b4fd556ec2919e87286dfd))\n* **search:** consume the inflight embedding future's exception when no\njoiner awaits it\n([#340](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/340))\n([a06ec53](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/a06ec539449d89fc3d3f58e45c645ed3ca456ae1))\n* **search:** skip entity hop-boost when classifier declined the entity\nmatch as over-broad\n([#327](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/327))\n([4744732](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/4744732196c05fb1fd207f53f5bd03a849472f7d))\n* **storage-client:** retry POSTs on connection-phase failures —\nnever-sent requests cannot double-insert\n([#333](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/333))\n([2d91e33](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/2d91e33baa968459443005fd5a86d127c6c0c4d1))\n\n\n### Documentation\n\n* add eToro proof, comparison table, FAQ, and star ask to README\n([#326](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/326))\n([e6395b5](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/e6395b535f58fd92906138c83b45a5c40a67be89))\n* bump eToro memory count 21,500 → 26,500 + social card\n([#329](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/329))\n([ea0e52b](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ea0e52b3fe43e72a279f365f38cd81301f1a6fce))\n* correct Claude Code MCP setup — claude mcp add -s user, not\nsettings.json\n([#343](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/343))\n([fc6324b](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/fc6324b6c60206efe814c3e9cdfc42d0f85266f4))\n* fix README/AGENT-INSTALL inaccuracies (PII, health shape, write\nresponse) ([#344](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/344))\n([2dea567](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/2dea567b802e9effaad3455284a7aab8e1cf124d))\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>plugin: 2.10.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.10.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/plugin-v2.9.0...plugin-v2.10.0)\n(2026-06-13)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **skills:** gate the OpenClaw install path to active-only skills\n([#317](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/317))\n([50488fc](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/50488fc6eb07d244297ad1d3e065887c8cb3e47e))\n* **skills:** per-node skill-reconcile observability on the heartbeat\n([#325](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/325))\n([d806114](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/d806114bc943a1d97480584192091e0583d41545))\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **plugin:** point agents at the memclaw skill by name, not by\nfilesystem path (CAURA-000)\n([#323](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/323))\n([ec3fcaf](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ec3fcaf45a7545568e9f713a6f1db631dfa1c2f3))\n* **release:** keep plugin/src/version.ts in sync on release-please PRs\n([#335](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/335))\n([e26a3c5](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/e26a3c561b542fbf58b4fd556ec2919e87286dfd))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-13T19:22:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/94dcbcd6f0bd69b0b93e94bf57ce9cb9719559ab","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/94dcbcd6f0bd69b0b93e94bf57ce9cb9719559ab","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/94dcbcd6f0bd69b0b93e94bf57ce9cb9719559ab/comments","author":{"login":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","id":265395343,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9Gcjw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229147182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/caura-deploy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2dea567b802e9effaad3455284a7aab8e1cf124d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2dea567b802e9effaad3455284a7aab8e1cf124d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2dea567b802e9effaad3455284a7aab8e1cf124d"}]},{"sha":"2dea567b802e9effaad3455284a7aab8e1cf124d","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDJkZWE1NjdiODAyZTllZmZhYWQzNDU1Mjg0YTdhYWI4ZTFjZjEyNGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-13T18:21:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-13T18:21:15Z"},"message":"docs: fix README/AGENT-INSTALL inaccuracies (PII, health shape, write response) (#344)\n\n## Summary\n\nThree doc claims that don't match the running OSS stack. All verified\nagainst a live instance.\n\n### 1. PII is detected & tagged, not \"quarantined\"\n\n`README.md` (Governance) claimed:\n> PII auto-detected **and quarantined before it can cross fleet\nboundaries**\n\nThe code only sets `metadata.contains_pii` / `pii_types` on write (see\n`merge_enrichment_fields.py`). Nothing changes a memory's `status`,\n`visibility`, or content, and it stays `scope_team` and fully\nrecallable. Reworded to \"flagged on every write (surfaced in memory\nmetadata as `contains_pii`/`pii_types`)\".\n\n### 2. `/api/v1/health` key is `storage`, not `database`\n\nDocs showed `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"database\":\"connected\",...}`. Actual\nresponse:\n```json\n{\"status\":\"ok\",\"storage\":\"connected\",\"redis\":\"connected\",\"event_bus\":\"ok\"}\n```\nFixed in `README.md` and both `AGENT-INSTALL.md` verify steps (3 spots).\n\n### 3. Write response: `weight`, and async on fast-write\n\n`README.md` said the write response includes `importance_score`. The\nfield is **`weight`** (the importance score); there is no\n`importance_score`. Also, on the **default fast-write path** the\nimmediate response is `enrichment_pending` and the inferred\n`title`/`summary`/`tags` populate asynchronously — the previous wording\nimplied a synchronous, fully-enriched response.\n\n## Scope\n\nDocs-only; no code changes. Kept separate from the MCP-setup docs PR\n(#343) since these are unrelated accuracy fixes.\n\n(Three further tutorial-only items — the `memclaw_evolve`\n`scope=\"fleet\"` nuance for cross-agent reinforcement, the \"9 tools\"\nundercount vs the actual 12, and the simplified architecture diagram —\nlive only in the external tutorial draft and aren't repo-doc bugs.)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5c4d0d5dd9de5dbdebc5e3ddf6ae29bff1ecebd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a5c4d0d5dd9de5dbdebc5e3ddf6ae29bff1ecebd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/2dea567b802e9effaad3455284a7aab8e1cf124d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLZ+bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArvoQACS5OGxixutJ+u21rxd/bagC\n4MCSLld0ln28hgC6kmRzWUcVBlYiWmOcbK/a95dNyR/02SdiHjwfdfReVvAEKZmN\nktmxnD0FIvIzpyxt6g6B8vx7wxR2ZjVpvc64SDgXQrQFaIX2nymtNIR2CQMCMcxB\n4TYcvj3V/d8WELkinYj6Z/l4/JjeRn63GjmtWC0MXwyqBBGjNhkYlxN7YmW4u6ow\nvEUUJliaJF4AT1CVhIozoJ88dNC2pwAp9dePpPV155hKZW5zpMabD1qfNovcLVIO\ntOK9ZHKipvqaRdasimcXYRwFbw1AyC+Kjei8yEtxox+MyUN83Z9UiQDVHl1RA4vm\njx7XKngdQxEfYu8S0eshQgEA+o7FL9SWLZJA3nOR9B1II0IbhP/xsRrjE+QIJl2e\nmkbD5xg6s5gAgHpNflqFKftp4qNYhxv9E5r9bawa+Yp1xnYumLzmvx+DGsKhAHIE\n00J19lYGw2hp9qVrxubBDwQgjtTeW9AztQ9WcRuZdZLHf2JOx7AyU1nGWDDq/Non\n8hb6Lwbp7NXUpvZLAuX/Ci2PKHFdp+GI4djKX68EMqlCsT9dYBOHIQVTvl7XCUNf\nCIvOLi4rXFibiFosKWwXG1IcP43991MXy8lB4fLnSIcbBkN4aioVmwe4KBWDVz87\nD9UpwnrIl1RMlcJUyRcp\n=vTRE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a5c4d0d5dd9de5dbdebc5e3ddf6ae29bff1ecebd\nparent fc6324b6c60206efe814c3e9cdfc42d0f85266f4\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781374875 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781374875 +0300\n\ndocs: fix README/AGENT-INSTALL inaccuracies (PII, health shape, write response) (#344)\n\n## Summary\n\nThree doc claims that don't match the running OSS stack. All verified\nagainst a live instance.\n\n### 1. PII is detected & tagged, not \"quarantined\"\n\n`README.md` (Governance) claimed:\n> PII auto-detected **and quarantined before it can cross fleet\nboundaries**\n\nThe code only sets `metadata.contains_pii` / `pii_types` on write (see\n`merge_enrichment_fields.py`). Nothing changes a memory's `status`,\n`visibility`, or content, and it stays `scope_team` and fully\nrecallable. Reworded to \"flagged on every write (surfaced in memory\nmetadata as `contains_pii`/`pii_types`)\".\n\n### 2. `/api/v1/health` key is `storage`, not `database`\n\nDocs showed `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"database\":\"connected\",...}`. Actual\nresponse:\n```json\n{\"status\":\"ok\",\"storage\":\"connected\",\"redis\":\"connected\",\"event_bus\":\"ok\"}\n```\nFixed in `README.md` and both `AGENT-INSTALL.md` verify steps (3 spots).\n\n### 3. Write response: `weight`, and async on fast-write\n\n`README.md` said the write response includes `importance_score`. The\nfield is **`weight`** (the importance score); there is no\n`importance_score`. Also, on the **default fast-write path** the\nimmediate response is `enrichment_pending` and the inferred\n`title`/`summary`/`tags` populate asynchronously — the previous wording\nimplied a synchronous, fully-enriched response.\n\n## Scope\n\nDocs-only; no code changes. Kept separate from the MCP-setup docs PR\n(#343) since these are unrelated accuracy fixes.\n\n(Three further tutorial-only items — the `memclaw_evolve`\n`scope=\"fleet\"` nuance for cross-agent reinforcement, the \"9 tools\"\nundercount vs the actual 12, and the simplified architecture diagram —\nlive only in the external tutorial draft and aren't repo-doc bugs.)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-13T18:21:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2dea567b802e9effaad3455284a7aab8e1cf124d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2dea567b802e9effaad3455284a7aab8e1cf124d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2dea567b802e9effaad3455284a7aab8e1cf124d/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fc6324b6c60206efe814c3e9cdfc42d0f85266f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fc6324b6c60206efe814c3e9cdfc42d0f85266f4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fc6324b6c60206efe814c3e9cdfc42d0f85266f4"}]},{"sha":"fc6324b6c60206efe814c3e9cdfc42d0f85266f4","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGZjNjMyNGI2YzYwMjA2ZWZlODE0YzNlOWNkZmM0MmQwZjg1MjY2ZjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-13T16:58:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-13T16:58:44Z"},"message":"docs: correct Claude Code MCP setup — claude mcp add -s user, not settings.json (#343)\n\n## Summary\n\nTwo MCP-setup errors in the install docs prevent Claude Code from ever\nconnecting to MemClaw, even when the user follows them exactly.\n\n### 1. `settings.json` block is silently ignored (#4)\n\n`README.md` and `AGENT-INSTALL.md` told Claude Code users to add an\n`mcpServers` block to `~/.claude/settings.json`:\n\n```\n- **Claude Code** — `~/.claude/settings.json` under `\"mcpServers\"`\n```\n\nClaude Code does **not** read MCP servers from `settings.json`. MCP\nconfig lives in `~/.claude.json` (written by `claude mcp add`) or a\nproject `.mcp.json`. The block is accepted into the file but never\nloaded — `claude mcp list` shows nothing, with no error. (Verified\nempirically: the block yields \"No MCP servers configured.\")\n\n### 2. Default `claude mcp add` scope is `local` (#3)\n\nThe prerequisite note pointed at a bare `claude mcp add` with no scope.\nThat defaults to **`local`** scope — the server is registered only for\nthe directory it was run in. Anyone running agents from multiple working\ndirectories (e.g. a fleet of per-agent dirs) finds the server present in\nthe first folder and missing everywhere else.\n\n## Fix\n\n- **Claude Code** bullet now points at `claude mcp add -s user`\n(available in every directory) as the primary path, explains why `local`\nbites, and notes `.mcp.json` for project scope.\n- Prerequisite note's command made explicit (`-s user`).\n- Claude Desktop / Cursor guidance — which genuinely use a config-file\nblock — left unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy\n\nVerified against **Claude Code 2.1.154**:\n```\n-s, --scope <scope>   Configuration scope (local, user, or project) (default: \"local\")\n```\n`.mcp.json` (project scope) and `~/.claude.json` (local/user, via\n`claude mcp add`) are the real config locations; `settings.json` is not\none of them.\n\nDocs-only; no code changes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2e2ea186360f5c24a32bd62d1f7901c8c97389cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/2e2ea186360f5c24a32bd62d1f7901c8c97389cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/fc6324b6c60206efe814c3e9cdfc42d0f85266f4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLYxECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqIIQAApYDO8dh+FIwTiumdGua4iu\nOZtkQ2hZM7AmXjowj1rWA1XMAF2VAiyHLgLJUhmDSDNA4QIKwyThkkR7sBq2CJRu\nrJi1Dm64k/XC5XrlYh8mHKjoNONnJLI32yTkSGkENKPxFqAVnSRuSouAFaBaoPPz\nEQT1MV8n+1uze+O1ECyzLBCnmExB/w4OwJxQmCuwC2XC5QtvRpLmjW7UFrMdyI5i\npQ9WX25z/kBr7x14zSChfQltdHGJrO7F2heNP16GjS17TnyvI1XB1C8eczqho4LT\nhH1CtLxL5ciu0LKcTs76oS89S8qr5IXQyFySUdqoNoNj9fCv7Y59/FKvZWN4H65A\nNvADDq0eAloPugWE+IXJrc2Gyga86W3HHeSAJtzgzOxOjHybALzcLrinYMCcwmuk\nnZ2rb2tMRAjDDRAsrW3Yo96SNTb7/mWCk5CdnZzlQKlzCMEPoJJ+IiM7ogw7C9RZ\nqL2QrlU0dLbFeQwtVPu/yLKM368emrUh4o7a8FkoECi4ydDjSwUfuZfuzrwfiYy6\nzc7W5wSCmrXCXbc8G3wmDCvQ8to/yN9UcJPBXjbcd4/xjYkN4zTQimwmJukv/7vq\nO7wTVR/lWFB5np1BEx2bv44dAO7DQaTjU5qpy0i1ZrTPBeDo0KaSGZfsioiw9+Jj\nq9I8iB9Wn6qDTmVCG4He\n=IcwZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2e2ea186360f5c24a32bd62d1f7901c8c97389cc\nparent 4d2d6ef008de5c743b848f566b51f461d117e06a\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781369924 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781369924 +0300\n\ndocs: correct Claude Code MCP setup — claude mcp add -s user, not settings.json (#343)\n\n## Summary\n\nTwo MCP-setup errors in the install docs prevent Claude Code from ever\nconnecting to MemClaw, even when the user follows them exactly.\n\n### 1. `settings.json` block is silently ignored (#4)\n\n`README.md` and `AGENT-INSTALL.md` told Claude Code users to add an\n`mcpServers` block to `~/.claude/settings.json`:\n\n```\n- **Claude Code** — `~/.claude/settings.json` under `\"mcpServers\"`\n```\n\nClaude Code does **not** read MCP servers from `settings.json`. MCP\nconfig lives in `~/.claude.json` (written by `claude mcp add`) or a\nproject `.mcp.json`. The block is accepted into the file but never\nloaded — `claude mcp list` shows nothing, with no error. (Verified\nempirically: the block yields \"No MCP servers configured.\")\n\n### 2. Default `claude mcp add` scope is `local` (#3)\n\nThe prerequisite note pointed at a bare `claude mcp add` with no scope.\nThat defaults to **`local`** scope — the server is registered only for\nthe directory it was run in. Anyone running agents from multiple working\ndirectories (e.g. a fleet of per-agent dirs) finds the server present in\nthe first folder and missing everywhere else.\n\n## Fix\n\n- **Claude Code** bullet now points at `claude mcp add -s user`\n(available in every directory) as the primary path, explains why `local`\nbites, and notes `.mcp.json` for project scope.\n- Prerequisite note's command made explicit (`-s user`).\n- Claude Desktop / Cursor guidance — which genuinely use a config-file\nblock — left unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy\n\nVerified against **Claude Code 2.1.154**:\n```\n-s, --scope <scope>   Configuration scope (local, user, or project) (default: \"local\")\n```\n`.mcp.json` (project scope) and `~/.claude.json` (local/user, via\n`claude mcp add`) are the real config locations; `settings.json` is not\none of them.\n\nDocs-only; no code changes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-13T16:58:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fc6324b6c60206efe814c3e9cdfc42d0f85266f4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fc6324b6c60206efe814c3e9cdfc42d0f85266f4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fc6324b6c60206efe814c3e9cdfc42d0f85266f4/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4d2d6ef008de5c743b848f566b51f461d117e06a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4d2d6ef008de5c743b848f566b51f461d117e06a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4d2d6ef008de5c743b848f566b51f461d117e06a"}]},{"sha":"4d2d6ef008de5c743b848f566b51f461d117e06a","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDRkMmQ2ZWYwMDhkZTVjNzQzYjg0OGY1NjZiNTFmNDYxZDExN2UwNmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-13T15:02:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-13T15:02:40Z"},"message":"fix(api): default agent_id to \"mcp-agent\" on standalone POST /memories (#339)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe documented quickstart — `POST /api/v1/memories` with `{tenant_id,\ncontent}` — returns `422 {\"loc\":[\"body\",\"agent_id\"],\"msg\":\"Field\nrequired\"}`. It's the reader's first hands-on API call **and** the\nStep-1 pipeline smoke test (\"send one raw sentence, watch it get\nenriched\"), so the failure cascades: nothing is written, and the\nfollow-up search demo returns empty.\n\nRoot cause: `MemoryCreate.agent_id` was required with no default, while\nthe curl (and `README.md:175`) omits it. The MCP `memclaw_write` tool\ndoesn't hit this because its tool param defaults `agent_id=\"mcp-agent\"`.\n\n## Change\n\nMake `agent_id` optional (`str | None = None`, matching the existing\n`BulkMemoryCreate.agent_id`) and resolve a missing value in\n`write_memory`:\n\n- **Standalone** (`settings.is_standalone`) → default to the reserved\n`\"mcp-agent\"` identity. Mirrors `mcp_server._DEFAULT_AGENT_ID` and the\n`evolve`/`insights` REST routes. This is what makes the quickstart work.\n- **Tenant-scoped key / enterprise gateway** → still require an explicit\n`agent_id` (now a clearer 422 instead of the raw Pydantic one).\n\n## Why gate on `is_standalone` (the safety-critical part)\n\nA naive \"just default the schema to `mcp-agent`\" would regress a\ndeliberate protection. The MCP layer **refuses** `\"mcp-agent\"` when a\ntenant-scoped key comes through the gateway\n(`_refuse_default_agent_on_gateway`), because otherwise every anonymous\nwrite collapses onto one shared identity (a documented friction-report\nfootgun: \"agent row missing from list_agents\"). The REST write route has\n**no** such guard, and its only backstop — `trust_level == 0 → 403` —\ndoesn't fire by default (`require_agent_approval` defaults to `False`,\n`DEFAULT_TRUST_LEVEL = 1`), so a defaulted `mcp-agent` would\nauto-register and write successfully.\n\nGating the default on `is_standalone` keeps the gateway/managed path\nrequiring a real agent_id, preserving that boundary.\n\n## Impact analysis (checked, no regressions)\n\n- **Internal `MemoryCreate(...)` constructors** — crystallizer\n(`\"crystallizer\"`), evolve (`agent_id=`), stm (`agent_id=`) all pass it\nexplicitly. Default never applies.\n- **OpenClaw plugin** — its REST `POST /memories`\n(`plugin/src/context-engine.ts:518`) passes `agent_id:\n\"__health_check__\"`. Unaffected.\n- **Tenant-scoped / gateway REST callers** — behavior unchanged: still\nrejected when omitting agent_id (clearer message).\n- **Tests** — no existing test asserts a 422 specifically on missing\n`agent_id`; no contract broken.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `py_compile` clean on both files.\n- Pydantic check: missing `agent_id` → `None` (route then resolves);\nexplicit `agent_id` → preserved.\n- `HTTPException` and `app_settings` already imported in the route.\n\n## Scope\n\nSingle-write path only. `BulkMemoryCreate` already allowed\n`agent_id=None` (and passes it straight through without this standalone\ngate); left as-is to keep the change focused — worth a follow-up to give\nbulk the same guard.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"efa318a1591ab14b193c498adcb2b5e5b3e15171","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/efa318a1591ab14b193c498adcb2b5e5b3e15171"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/4d2d6ef008de5c743b848f566b51f461d117e06a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLXEQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaikQAE17AzbjY7v+oXfq2rgLZcwo\noX9rLK2Aljc/n3BD0wFyGm9hRszQ4f4gZVk3ZNs9Lj2i41b8fHBabGj3Lri2fsz7\ncUVneCDdCfT0I+SuTIPgLAjL+INYOslZA5M9kKSshgjQQrkEfq6gEQeN8X9prGb+\nUqQVXVMGGN1FVTszTkzHCwHcs81Ksoj9+ihYbnqDLdgoIRRA/HRvx4pkieG0f+Am\newAgQDJVnCisA0E0Tylc9UHC3/vCVL9r+Ib5u/jBsaL+YY+GYU4brdaVqowaK2xZ\nNTXhsxBSLOydBB6JA9YIdf8OWVj8nclinfe0M5+LTMBMQVLIoTJNr0VEvUSenxQM\ndMhIpixG8tUtInggfpwMQs2rq/auv42s7VULxXbkbCRBqnuMOK24ngECQ+omBBL2\narqUPPuQt4t+6MA7MYHO6dns4UJEsL7LljV90mhDebo1lW5uA/e0u+PcnKVbpZ/1\nWtqB6KO0xj2cU/o8IFQncTi/iJpeYHwmVV6DnHDfzfEYTfB3U5vFCeGRRwS8xjtl\n+kYkB7QxsNnn0nWuigIj9dMc+R0fgxr7GtWcM93cjINoBJ9UwFWpOQIDlUpMn43o\nwDhomNeTQkiP7FjsvnBj4BPqJaF4096/+lvvJd2xDO/FC2hahBzwahObD9IVnb5p\nKqN7f81Q+tslOd8PrzJV\n=zAiN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree efa318a1591ab14b193c498adcb2b5e5b3e15171\nparent c310ecfd61ee14b0545234b7bb4773fbc0e1685e\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781362960 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781362960 +0300\n\nfix(api): default agent_id to \"mcp-agent\" on standalone POST /memories (#339)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe documented quickstart — `POST /api/v1/memories` with `{tenant_id,\ncontent}` — returns `422 {\"loc\":[\"body\",\"agent_id\"],\"msg\":\"Field\nrequired\"}`. It's the reader's first hands-on API call **and** the\nStep-1 pipeline smoke test (\"send one raw sentence, watch it get\nenriched\"), so the failure cascades: nothing is written, and the\nfollow-up search demo returns empty.\n\nRoot cause: `MemoryCreate.agent_id` was required with no default, while\nthe curl (and `README.md:175`) omits it. The MCP `memclaw_write` tool\ndoesn't hit this because its tool param defaults `agent_id=\"mcp-agent\"`.\n\n## Change\n\nMake `agent_id` optional (`str | None = None`, matching the existing\n`BulkMemoryCreate.agent_id`) and resolve a missing value in\n`write_memory`:\n\n- **Standalone** (`settings.is_standalone`) → default to the reserved\n`\"mcp-agent\"` identity. Mirrors `mcp_server._DEFAULT_AGENT_ID` and the\n`evolve`/`insights` REST routes. This is what makes the quickstart work.\n- **Tenant-scoped key / enterprise gateway** → still require an explicit\n`agent_id` (now a clearer 422 instead of the raw Pydantic one).\n\n## Why gate on `is_standalone` (the safety-critical part)\n\nA naive \"just default the schema to `mcp-agent`\" would regress a\ndeliberate protection. The MCP layer **refuses** `\"mcp-agent\"` when a\ntenant-scoped key comes through the gateway\n(`_refuse_default_agent_on_gateway`), because otherwise every anonymous\nwrite collapses onto one shared identity (a documented friction-report\nfootgun: \"agent row missing from list_agents\"). The REST write route has\n**no** such guard, and its only backstop — `trust_level == 0 → 403` —\ndoesn't fire by default (`require_agent_approval` defaults to `False`,\n`DEFAULT_TRUST_LEVEL = 1`), so a defaulted `mcp-agent` would\nauto-register and write successfully.\n\nGating the default on `is_standalone` keeps the gateway/managed path\nrequiring a real agent_id, preserving that boundary.\n\n## Impact analysis (checked, no regressions)\n\n- **Internal `MemoryCreate(...)` constructors** — crystallizer\n(`\"crystallizer\"`), evolve (`agent_id=`), stm (`agent_id=`) all pass it\nexplicitly. Default never applies.\n- **OpenClaw plugin** — its REST `POST /memories`\n(`plugin/src/context-engine.ts:518`) passes `agent_id:\n\"__health_check__\"`. Unaffected.\n- **Tenant-scoped / gateway REST callers** — behavior unchanged: still\nrejected when omitting agent_id (clearer message).\n- **Tests** — no existing test asserts a 422 specifically on missing\n`agent_id`; no contract broken.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `py_compile` clean on both files.\n- Pydantic check: missing `agent_id` → `None` (route then resolves);\nexplicit `agent_id` → preserved.\n- `HTTPException` and `app_settings` already imported in the route.\n\n## Scope\n\nSingle-write path only. `BulkMemoryCreate` already allowed\n`agent_id=None` (and passes it straight through without this standalone\ngate); left as-is to keep the change focused — worth a follow-up to give\nbulk the same guard.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-13T15:02:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4d2d6ef008de5c743b848f566b51f461d117e06a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4d2d6ef008de5c743b848f566b51f461d117e06a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4d2d6ef008de5c743b848f566b51f461d117e06a/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c310ecfd61ee14b0545234b7bb4773fbc0e1685e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c310ecfd61ee14b0545234b7bb4773fbc0e1685e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c310ecfd61ee14b0545234b7bb4773fbc0e1685e"}]},{"sha":"c310ecfd61ee14b0545234b7bb4773fbc0e1685e","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGMzMTBlY2ZkNjFlZTE0YjA1NDUyMzRiN2JiNDc3M2ZiYzBlMTY4NWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-13T10:12:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-13T10:12:46Z"},"message":"fix(entity-linking): synchronize_session=False on the entity-embedding backfill bulk update (#342)\n\n## Why\n\nProd 2026-06-13: **every** `backfill_entity_embeddings` batch fails with\n\n```\nsqlalchemy.exc.InvalidRequestError: bulk synchronize of persistent objects not supported\nwhen using bulk update with additional WHERE criteria right now.\nadd synchronize_session=None execution option to bypass synchronize of persistent objects.\n  at core-api/.../entity_linking/backfill_entity_embeddings.py:68\n```\n\n6 occurrences in ~10h. The step runs an ORM\n`update(Entity).where(id==:eid,\ntenant_id==…).values(name_embedding=:emb)` over an **executemany param\nlist**; SQLAlchemy refuses to session-synchronize that shape. Result:\nentities with a NULL `name_embedding` are **silently never backfilled**,\ndegrading entity-name vector matching. (Surfaced from the same full\nprod-error sweep that found infer_relations / #341.)\n\n## What\n\nAdd `.execution_options(synchronize_session=False)` — there's no live\nORM session state to keep in sync (the backfill writes the embedding and\nmoves on), so skipping synchronization is correct, exactly as the error\nmessage instructs.\n\n**Third `entity_linking_full` sibling to surface post-Phase-J** (the\nre-embed created the entities/links that make these steps fire):\n`discover_cross_links` (#337, executemany+RETURNING), `infer_relations`\n(#341, LEAST over untyped binds), and now this. A repo-wide sweep found\n**no other** `update().where().values()` over a param list with this\nlatent bug.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New `tests/pipeline/test_backfill_entity_embeddings.py`: asserts the\nUPDATE statement carries `synchronize_session=False` (mock-based shape\npin, **verified red** against the unfixed step) + the empty-rows skip\npath.\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` clean; `mypy` clean. DCO signed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5fbcf995ee0c5b7f4175f6c469cf835a88d30e69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/5fbcf995ee0c5b7f4175f6c469cf835a88d30e69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/c310ecfd61ee14b0545234b7bb4773fbc0e1685e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLS0eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaY0QAH3aibxdADbqNcoZLqg32jTR\nJbsDBbwDcDzpcVeaRcujoiJRM2MFk5FqnI9D1XfE59LqQ4vwO4PkYyQYIQE9NQ7T\nZrcpXqeJeOLH2YTldSImLE/CzXkmBca4qV/C95pX3M/fWa/g/Fdmp1Y3gUkR54GO\n/DhEP3BlXp8uwez+KAJ5eCqi35KAvSQjAKstAvSOo9wvLx6vgEsejteSJFYfYREZ\nmRtY1jKWxgEBIpxtJDJ34xp54anAXV9dUf/6LbB1Q5wbD/5jG9DRtQpnvDfxtYEV\nD8ttLcl1dlx1BLLFTlKehc5ZbwJ45kuLUqk0f1shsyC/sNelqLzMocrJBvjlFUVt\ncBhnM0NEgWIzHykMAF27wj2gJiRKd1EVcCfrxqm5q4hZu1Yi4NWShc9VXYLqzEyZ\n4mb1mqBzDGWvo3gBZN/br2dYqsOxRbLbmr1i+LppTuvGYbcSakEXi7ctk9oJYuWg\nq5XxSuAsqPTTi29kwbwUjFuPAM8R4NlvPwkeK8zFdRfqzq8ctThYpwYkM6AXdcSr\nZB9QOs2go9oqzuATkXngQk9vvRuCN+OLXhunv4y2JhykdRXOIqUxi/rlJbktN/tF\nV615Cqx8jFatnWxBi4BSdJdM0Fw9XswRq1Nz1uHCWYKN7i5tf/nZdPPrSOxWlgWs\n9BOmcz9F7X6CwAf5TVH2\n=nOk1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5fbcf995ee0c5b7f4175f6c469cf835a88d30e69\nparent b4a57120107c2319013e8ac64aa6aaecc87d0751\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781345566 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781345566 +0300\n\nfix(entity-linking): synchronize_session=False on the entity-embedding backfill bulk update (#342)\n\n## Why\n\nProd 2026-06-13: **every** `backfill_entity_embeddings` batch fails with\n\n```\nsqlalchemy.exc.InvalidRequestError: bulk synchronize of persistent objects not supported\nwhen using bulk update with additional WHERE criteria right now.\nadd synchronize_session=None execution option to bypass synchronize of persistent objects.\n  at core-api/.../entity_linking/backfill_entity_embeddings.py:68\n```\n\n6 occurrences in ~10h. The step runs an ORM\n`update(Entity).where(id==:eid,\ntenant_id==…).values(name_embedding=:emb)` over an **executemany param\nlist**; SQLAlchemy refuses to session-synchronize that shape. Result:\nentities with a NULL `name_embedding` are **silently never backfilled**,\ndegrading entity-name vector matching. (Surfaced from the same full\nprod-error sweep that found infer_relations / #341.)\n\n## What\n\nAdd `.execution_options(synchronize_session=False)` — there's no live\nORM session state to keep in sync (the backfill writes the embedding and\nmoves on), so skipping synchronization is correct, exactly as the error\nmessage instructs.\n\n**Third `entity_linking_full` sibling to surface post-Phase-J** (the\nre-embed created the entities/links that make these steps fire):\n`discover_cross_links` (#337, executemany+RETURNING), `infer_relations`\n(#341, LEAST over untyped binds), and now this. A repo-wide sweep found\n**no other** `update().where().values()` over a param list with this\nlatent bug.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New `tests/pipeline/test_backfill_entity_embeddings.py`: asserts the\nUPDATE statement carries `synchronize_session=False` (mock-based shape\npin, **verified red** against the unfixed step) + the empty-rows skip\npath.\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` clean; `mypy` clean. DCO signed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-13T10:12:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c310ecfd61ee14b0545234b7bb4773fbc0e1685e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c310ecfd61ee14b0545234b7bb4773fbc0e1685e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c310ecfd61ee14b0545234b7bb4773fbc0e1685e/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b4a57120107c2319013e8ac64aa6aaecc87d0751","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b4a57120107c2319013e8ac64aa6aaecc87d0751","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b4a57120107c2319013e8ac64aa6aaecc87d0751"}]},{"sha":"b4a57120107c2319013e8ac64aa6aaecc87d0751","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGI0YTU3MTIwMTA3YzIzMTkwMTNlOGFjNjRhYTZhYWVjYzg3ZDA3NTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-13T09:58:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-13T09:58:01Z"},"message":"fix(entity-linking): bind reinforce weight directly — LEAST over untyped params coerced to text (#341)\n\n## Why\n\nProd 2026-06-13: **every** relation-reinforce batch in `infer_relations`\nfails with\n\n```\nasyncpg.exceptions.DatatypeMismatchError: column \"weight\" is of type double precision but expression is of type text\n  at core-api/.../entity_linking/infer_relations.py:137\n```\n\n**45 occurrences in ~9h across prod (26) + staging (19)**, multiple\ntenants. Postgres resolves `LEAST(:new_weight, :max_weight)` over two\n**untyped** bind params as `text`, then rejects assigning that to the\n`double precision` `weight` column. The step returns FAILED, so\nco-occurrence relations are **silently never reinforced**. (Surfaced\nfrom my staging cutover-soak scan; it's the same class in the prod alert\nlist — distinct from the connect-timeout residual.)\n\n## What\n\n`new_weight` is **already** clamped to `MAX_RELATION_WEIGHT` in Python\n(`min(current_weight + cooccur*DELTA, MAX_RELATION_WEIGHT)`), so the\nSQL-side `LEAST` was redundant double-clamping — and the source of the\ntype ambiguity. Bind `:new_weight` directly (`SET weight =\n:new_weight`), exactly like the sibling INSERT path binds `:weight`\n(which is why INSERT was unaffected — column context infers the type).\nDrop the now-unused `max_weight` key.\n\nLikely surfaced post-Phase-J: the re-embed created many more entity\nlinks/relations, so the reinforce path (UPDATE existing) started firing\nwhere before it rarely did.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New `tests/pipeline/test_infer_relations.py` (mock-based → asserts\nstatement SHAPE + the Python clamp the fix relies on): reinforce UPDATE\nbinds `:new_weight` with **no `LEAST`**; weight stays clamped to MAX in\nPython; INSERT path unchanged; empty co-occurrence skips. **Verified red\nagainst the unfixed SQL.**\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` clean; `mypy` clean. DCO signed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ca3d67c20ae6901240788b43d5fa812dc8194d8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ca3d67c20ae6901240788b43d5fa812dc8194d8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b4a57120107c2319013e8ac64aa6aaecc87d0751","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLSmpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6eAQAFxA0qVCA8GKz+UawYn3237T\niOIW11jhhLwFK1zP71TyNBX/BHHX3++8qlR4KteNKDCxV/kmQRHV+G28TosRjUGL\nIEMVLGMK9TdHRvn5QIDEC6gWDX6IMoE8IjMVC+Uz/n7Zc2GUj/CX0hqV5wS80lbz\nzZrV/GTKzgmQzoNQlWpOC6pp2rixxQ+KzXklOG58BCtwwkVrpXbJojREAE1eSjW+\nRhkhMF7XO8I3IAdmLpsKLoDWX4zCoPdUHMIehBPjV662KSHSYNSHh8/ntzzHXDAq\nVZBWBlGQ1CTdiWDl6kgrlG6/ooS4yfMv2GG71YuSpv+x7xTL1uJ1W55t7L/zJv+2\n8RTT3e5Pg5wG7sYV6L/PPwKqjP4BAgTZv6kuBO7mbcCS+uQw+ueYbnm2iQ1MG3PS\np0jfXNq+gIaaOVW6/T5nekeQ+89LJsuv4K1noLkFMxMBYJ93MegSkEX7jMlXjtNM\nmLRIGgv45yquWEx48xP7KUQwleB1PW0aWA3agTLezywBue6b0aAS9xxqofdpBl39\nsG+zRwHRFzSXwAH/NhBFq4UALeNSsIpfCycKrYlKdg1CwSjMg2Ho3q6v+nqbqwIV\nqzsVA9lmgFTqvsRJ0cly4pMuNLTMXQ1c2q+srH8w5MIcVge9fiyBViE8TrziSnjj\nS8a0QiRuJuuUAR4W/jPv\n=xbBB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ca3d67c20ae6901240788b43d5fa812dc8194d8e\nparent a06ec539449d89fc3d3f58e45c645ed3ca456ae1\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781344681 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781344681 +0300\n\nfix(entity-linking): bind reinforce weight directly — LEAST over untyped params coerced to text (#341)\n\n## Why\n\nProd 2026-06-13: **every** relation-reinforce batch in `infer_relations`\nfails with\n\n```\nasyncpg.exceptions.DatatypeMismatchError: column \"weight\" is of type double precision but expression is of type text\n  at core-api/.../entity_linking/infer_relations.py:137\n```\n\n**45 occurrences in ~9h across prod (26) + staging (19)**, multiple\ntenants. Postgres resolves `LEAST(:new_weight, :max_weight)` over two\n**untyped** bind params as `text`, then rejects assigning that to the\n`double precision` `weight` column. The step returns FAILED, so\nco-occurrence relations are **silently never reinforced**. (Surfaced\nfrom my staging cutover-soak scan; it's the same class in the prod alert\nlist — distinct from the connect-timeout residual.)\n\n## What\n\n`new_weight` is **already** clamped to `MAX_RELATION_WEIGHT` in Python\n(`min(current_weight + cooccur*DELTA, MAX_RELATION_WEIGHT)`), so the\nSQL-side `LEAST` was redundant double-clamping — and the source of the\ntype ambiguity. Bind `:new_weight` directly (`SET weight =\n:new_weight`), exactly like the sibling INSERT path binds `:weight`\n(which is why INSERT was unaffected — column context infers the type).\nDrop the now-unused `max_weight` key.\n\nLikely surfaced post-Phase-J: the re-embed created many more entity\nlinks/relations, so the reinforce path (UPDATE existing) started firing\nwhere before it rarely did.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New `tests/pipeline/test_infer_relations.py` (mock-based → asserts\nstatement SHAPE + the Python clamp the fix relies on): reinforce UPDATE\nbinds `:new_weight` with **no `LEAST`**; weight stays clamped to MAX in\nPython; INSERT path unchanged; empty co-occurrence skips. **Verified red\nagainst the unfixed SQL.**\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` clean; `mypy` clean. DCO signed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-13T09:58:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b4a57120107c2319013e8ac64aa6aaecc87d0751","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b4a57120107c2319013e8ac64aa6aaecc87d0751","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b4a57120107c2319013e8ac64aa6aaecc87d0751/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"http