643f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0a47c24195ff703f47e3b85d2dfc9b2dcdb5643f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/a06ec539449d89fc3d3f58e45c645ed3ca456ae1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLB5XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfI8QAEJmqdJUnMfwrdcY1viV0owu\nwdFHfKVq2GwgiUkip9E7vEsqj9j8nuNzvMh+C5Vw39k9S3I6AUmTKsyeL/Yckl6a\njuCiwIKDyA8dV046TrvAoH06lvIwbFWH8Z02a06FYJHuShSxkD95+tHZWsqJ45E7\nQ/EgdM/siX1SoL9WyNKvLIoVOz7QY4yeEc1Pmt7oNrdaJNy8HT0cT3EwJoo+U0IK\nZz+FLs63MR7hZDVIHE7XZgltkS/PPqXLYjjHHsP3/78/uKDxh25jfS5fDjdqqT56\nfqzhjMrS1lHkDupxM6nnPL1PiGwg8pFLsjUUhQhAAsfzbGcX4SzKTX+QsD9Mo0Hk\nslkFQAX5BhiSuxEmchCBERWdOIl0yA6HvAV017cxR5ucWUM6RQmprqxl3334Wbcq\nSeFzt5xn9hrj7BB0E9ckRHekM/6N+L+J8VK5Hf26fZw2nF9g/ZoPPICtk2IzDstg\nyqNI/zTHFVDXzoJAUzQSDRmlj8kr49SS+sfSUFGLjK7uvqlJIC5CNpbjGaHAcQe7\nQC+lL740am6W4KtfFHRSvaGXyHtV//vPdSh3hZS0bjmqhSsEzYpVyfCfFnASyywM\nrSjF+TRWPgS4zrFWGBKZ1+RUw0HngKMRn7TkrjvhnvySaxccjhfDL+FA4QEbbToT\nU8rpFzSYiHDYapjEiyoC\n=kJFQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0a47c24195ff703f47e3b85d2dfc9b2dcdb5643f\nparent 8bbdeedb84c5a85655a88485583dcabd7b21d9a6\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781276247 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781276247 +0300\n\nfix(search): consume the inflight embedding future's exception when no joiner awaits it (#340)","verified_at":"2026-06-12T14:57:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a06ec539449d89fc3d3f58e45c645ed3ca456ae1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a06ec539449d89fc3d3f58e45c645ed3ca456ae1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a06ec539449d89fc3d3f58e45c645ed3ca456ae1/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8bbdeedb84c5a85655a88485583dcabd7b21d9a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8bbdeedb84c5a85655a88485583dcabd7b21d9a6","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8bbdeedb84c5a85655a88485583dcabd7b21d9a6"}]},{"sha":"8bbdeedb84c5a85655a88485583dcabd7b21d9a6","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDhiYmRlZWRiODRjNWE4NTY1NWE4ODQ4NTU4M2RjYWJkN2IyMWQ5YTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-12T09:19:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T09:19:35Z"},"message":"fix(cross-links): single multi-VALUES insert — executemany cannot RETURN rows (#337)\n\n## Why\n\nProd 2026-06-12 06:31Z + 06:46Z (`prod-memclaw-core-api`, tenant\n`ct-a-synthetic-prod-77abc3`):\n\n```\nError bulk-inserting 3 cross-links for tenant ct-a-synthetic-prod-77abc3\nsqlalchemy.exc.ResourceClosedError: This result object does not return rows. It has been closed automatically.\n```\n\n#298 fixed the `RETURNING id` → real-columns issue but kept\n`execute(text_stmt, to_insert)` — passing a **params list** flips\nSQLAlchemy into the executemany path, where RETURNING rows are\nunavailable and `result.all()` raises. Every **multi-row** batch fails\n(step → FAILED, links lost); the 1-row batches seen before now happened\nto be the only shape exercised, which is why this stayed latent since\n06-08.\n\n## What\n\nOne `pg_insert(MemoryEntityLink).values(rows)` multi-VALUES statement\n(the CAURA-686 pattern from core-storage's memories router) +\n`.on_conflict_do_nothing(index_elements=[\"memory_id\",\"entity_id\"]).returning(memory_id,\nentity_id)` — RETURNING works for any row count, conflicts still\nexcluded from the count. Bounds: worst case\n`CROSS_LINK_MEMORY_BATCH_SIZE (200) × LIMIT 10 = 2,000` inlined rows —\nroutine for Postgres. A repo sweep found no other executemany+RETURNING\nsites.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tests/pipeline/test_entity_linking.py` — the shape-pinning test now\nalso asserts the executemany trigger is absent (exactly one positional\n`execute` arg) and that a 3-row batch compiles to a **single** statement\ncarrying all rows + `ON CONFLICT ... DO NOTHING` + real-columns\nRETURNING. 10 passed (incl. wiring tests).\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` clean; mypy clean on the touched file.\nDCO signed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"38cde2b04d9d3fdb4f001d91aacd6a0e25a385d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/38cde2b04d9d3fdb4f001d91aacd6a0e25a385d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/8bbdeedb84c5a85655a88485583dcabd7b21d9a6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK88nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu5gQAE/Mzv1eGyitGQx5NRsbZunQ\nEpIB64lXX+CR9FrVOrSjk4PMV5WtZc1vHCtPi7gMoO3a+9QWZW/E2DR8g8EC3XbL\n25UMkMsNOd7VqYy5vF4yJKvURVN/73G0u7bc1jmJm8eEcRschUtnWofvuuPU5guR\nhC7oaE/K+KHSljX2LLwbm8CqFlIwuTBVK/K/F5V2/lZ4TT298Mn3QLzT4293YvBn\ns5cqFSU2c78bjOWaEzyekIFa3OY5EzVrHyHm7xGPsaVJm+GxEu1dw7HvywF9R80C\nlqNjmJ/cNo0niwuD5MTTI1k7biOO1c0Ay80sZTXYdoXGqHLQoey4CdVZH1yI9cf9\nj1zVWfrNW1pxnQ+4FaGjuXjQhKlpYEBmesWE0HCfAObMj9C4md5kIIEKNTYaMKyC\nKF3+kLzB2PgmCaM6ferm9Z4P3+02NfWwghAj40h+LKk3PYXGIETzIgQTWZafQzIx\nePVzhKx7H8YySq2KBnMqZcqY6oo+Z527bLxbuACPEZgH7XcXFITDj9X/mlxZ/mid\nTGOwDBD7oThs+lvtseVbeE6oLeoahpHg7nCLiypIhtm55od40zFvIP8Ow8IL5oXu\nQU5AFnmz8V0boBD+uQFWC+gapz5J3LscKZdmkWlEzEjmpZ7k2yDhYvgcMOpbkxE1\nl5ScF3Lnu530FnNKYzgB\n=dmFK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 38cde2b04d9d3fdb4f001d91aacd6a0e25a385d1\nparent 30e3cff097c73d0af6faec739f638c5fecf46aef\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781255975 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781255975 +0300\n\nfix(cross-links): single multi-VALUES insert — executemany cannot RETURN rows (#337)\n\n## Why\n\nProd 2026-06-12 06:31Z + 06:46Z (`prod-memclaw-core-api`, tenant\n`ct-a-synthetic-prod-77abc3`):\n\n```\nError bulk-inserting 3 cross-links for tenant ct-a-synthetic-prod-77abc3\nsqlalchemy.exc.ResourceClosedError: This result object does not return rows. It has been closed automatically.\n```\n\n#298 fixed the `RETURNING id` → real-columns issue but kept\n`execute(text_stmt, to_insert)` — passing a **params list** flips\nSQLAlchemy into the executemany path, where RETURNING rows are\nunavailable and `result.all()` raises. Every **multi-row** batch fails\n(step → FAILED, links lost); the 1-row batches seen before now happened\nto be the only shape exercised, which is why this stayed latent since\n06-08.\n\n## What\n\nOne `pg_insert(MemoryEntityLink).values(rows)` multi-VALUES statement\n(the CAURA-686 pattern from core-storage's memories router) +\n`.on_conflict_do_nothing(index_elements=[\"memory_id\",\"entity_id\"]).returning(memory_id,\nentity_id)` — RETURNING works for any row count, conflicts still\nexcluded from the count. Bounds: worst case\n`CROSS_LINK_MEMORY_BATCH_SIZE (200) × LIMIT 10 = 2,000` inlined rows —\nroutine for Postgres. A repo sweep found no other executemany+RETURNING\nsites.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tests/pipeline/test_entity_linking.py` — the shape-pinning test now\nalso asserts the executemany trigger is absent (exactly one positional\n`execute` arg) and that a 3-row batch compiles to a **single** statement\ncarrying all rows + `ON CONFLICT ... DO NOTHING` + real-columns\nRETURNING. 10 passed (incl. wiring tests).\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` clean; mypy clean on the touched file.\nDCO signed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-12T09:19:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8bbdeedb84c5a85655a88485583dcabd7b21d9a6","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8bbdeedb84c5a85655a88485583dcabd7b21d9a6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8bbdeedb84c5a85655a88485583dcabd7b21d9a6/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"30e3cff097c73d0af6faec739f638c5fecf46aef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/30e3cff097c73d0af6faec739f638c5fecf46aef","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/30e3cff097c73d0af6faec739f638c5fecf46aef"}]},{"sha":"30e3cff097c73d0af6faec739f638c5fecf46aef","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDMwZTNjZmYwOTdjNzNkMGFmNmZhZWM3MzlmNjM4YzVmZWNmNDZhZWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-12T09:04:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T09:04:15Z"},"message":"fix(mcp): memclaw_tune crashed with 'dict' object has no attribute 'id' (#338)\n\n## Summary\n\n`memclaw_tune` raises `'dict' object has no attribute 'id'` on **any**\ncall that actually sets a tuning parameter (e.g. `top_k=5`,\n`min_similarity=0.5`). A no-argument call succeeds, which is why the\nfailure wasn't obvious.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`get_or_create_agent()` returns a **dict**. The handler reads it\ndict-safely one line before the bug, then reverts to attribute access:\n\n```python\nagent = await get_or_create_agent(db, tenant_id, agent_id)\ncurrent = (agent.get(\"search_profile\") if isinstance(agent, dict) else agent.search_profile) or {}  # dict-safe\nif updates:                                   # only true when a param was supplied\n    ...\n    await agent_repo.update_search_profile(db, agent.id, current)  # agent.id on a dict -> AttributeError\n```\n\n`agent.id` is attribute access on a dict → `AttributeError`. The crash\nlives **inside** `if updates:`, so a no-arg `memclaw_tune` skips it\nentirely and returns fine — which is also why the existing tests\n(registration, scope/auth guards) never caught it: none exercise the\n`update_search_profile` write branch.\n\n## Fix\n\nResolve the primary key dict-safely, mirroring `routes/agents.py:141`\n(which already does `agent[\"id\"]`) and the `isinstance` guard used two\nlines up:\n\n```python\nagent_pk = agent[\"id\"] if isinstance(agent, dict) else agent.id\nawait agent_repo.update_search_profile(db, agent_pk, current)\n```\n\n`update_search_profile` expects the `Agent.id` primary key;\n`agent[\"id\"]` is confirmed present on the returned dict (same field the\nREST tune route uses).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python -m py_compile` on the module passes.\n- Reproduced originally via direct MCP call on a live instance:\n`memclaw_tune {\"agent_id\":\"code-reviewer\",\"top_k\":5}` returned the\n`'dict' object has no attribute 'id'` error, while\n`{\"agent_id\":\"code-reviewer\"}` (no params) succeeded — exactly matching\nthe `if updates:` analysis above.\n\n## Scope\n\nMinimal one-line-of-logic fix. Worth a follow-up: a regression test\ncovering the `memclaw_tune` write branch (mock `get_or_create_agent` →\ndict, assert `update_search_profile` is called with the PK), since that\npath is currently untested.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"409b476ce9239f581b7c822f09af4454b79f26d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/409b476ce9239f581b7c822f09af4454b79f26d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/30e3cff097c73d0af6faec739f638c5fecf46aef","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK8uPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdZIQAFvlbSqaUcOIqPEvy8+7mFIz\njC1kAXMNFIZNfokahInqkIdqQh9y7QnH5Duf460UZXiuqo00cvaIox08knkYB+hM\nY1v3D9En7bJJPrdEIhqFMx9K6DvqQ4mKEpoyFTevzWJIKbST82SpTRzpA8al7mGi\neYrRDJRDBbLtRhXuZTH6re7YvfG0eMucLrokg2/+fphoD2geTY6qtsoDbxfwxYZQ\ntmxtdHGP80CMLPeJHxW7VTlAMUyBs6Y5OZXxATMfegwCikHLQ6lF4CnvzNblp3xQ\nOjoaCtwCZkxj4NHr1wemTSD2/YOtyO1Zl5QDX+bROxPySRB7Q3Dmw66gJtsK8OaV\ntaR8gH2580Bd8Tpk2c3WwKkHXWHXkgNVLnw7pIw4Pm309PM2IuDdACln/l9fMrCk\nhG291GjFpRwDeev+cyZv9pMdzfTpir2dibMIyXCwKEZECX5PJ0hhSjdgaeyPnev3\nUEoaT3x91wmO0G+gxss+s5pzY+Sq7oO3mMjJ1tKjZx8Ca2k5xLZdiIDjGwOZXxdD\nRVmef/6k3dsUHvVf+c2ieiXZq8cxDvjjTHfzYw86maAdeBc7ogQnlVGQO0s1aDrJ\n9CIMeiSMVL94EUqd2X63YpwXa8KH/w+pHQksJ1yk/HQXHerFOVY3jXW0zq7zuEBV\n7dwO6e2Uqw1bc8GPnNpC\n=J60b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 409b476ce9239f581b7c822f09af4454b79f26d1\nparent d1f1f5a6f8ac4a631b4bb8dfa89801384e4aea44\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781255055 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781255055 +0300\n\nfix(mcp): memclaw_tune crashed with 'dict' object has no attribute 'id' (#338)\n\n## Summary\n\n`memclaw_tune` raises `'dict' object has no attribute 'id'` on **any**\ncall that actually sets a tuning parameter (e.g. `top_k=5`,\n`min_similarity=0.5`). A no-argument call succeeds, which is why the\nfailure wasn't obvious.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`get_or_create_agent()` returns a **dict**. The handler reads it\ndict-safely one line before the bug, then reverts to attribute access:\n\n```python\nagent = await get_or_create_agent(db, tenant_id, agent_id)\ncurrent = (agent.get(\"search_profile\") if isinstance(agent, dict) else agent.search_profile) or {}  # dict-safe\nif updates:                                   # only true when a param was supplied\n    ...\n    await agent_repo.update_search_profile(db, agent.id, current)  # agent.id on a dict -> AttributeError\n```\n\n`agent.id` is attribute access on a dict → `AttributeError`. The crash\nlives **inside** `if updates:`, so a no-arg `memclaw_tune` skips it\nentirely and returns fine — which is also why the existing tests\n(registration, scope/auth guards) never caught it: none exercise the\n`update_search_profile` write branch.\n\n## Fix\n\nResolve the primary key dict-safely, mirroring `routes/agents.py:141`\n(which already does `agent[\"id\"]`) and the `isinstance` guard used two\nlines up:\n\n```python\nagent_pk = agent[\"id\"] if isinstance(agent, dict) else agent.id\nawait agent_repo.update_search_profile(db, agent_pk, current)\n```\n\n`update_search_profile` expects the `Agent.id` primary key;\n`agent[\"id\"]` is confirmed present on the returned dict (same field the\nREST tune route uses).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python -m py_compile` on the module passes.\n- Reproduced originally via direct MCP call on a live instance:\n`memclaw_tune {\"agent_id\":\"code-reviewer\",\"top_k\":5}` returned the\n`'dict' object has no attribute 'id'` error, while\n`{\"agent_id\":\"code-reviewer\"}` (no params) succeeded — exactly matching\nthe `if updates:` analysis above.\n\n## Scope\n\nMinimal one-line-of-logic fix. Worth a follow-up: a regression test\ncovering the `memclaw_tune` write branch (mock `get_or_create_agent` →\ndict, assert `update_search_profile` is called with the PK), since that\npath is currently untested.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-12T09:04:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/30e3cff097c73d0af6faec739f638c5fecf46aef","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/30e3cff097c73d0af6faec739f638c5fecf46aef","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/30e3cff097c73d0af6faec739f638c5fecf46aef/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d1f1f5a6f8ac4a631b4bb8dfa89801384e4aea44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d1f1f5a6f8ac4a631b4bb8dfa89801384e4aea44","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d1f1f5a6f8ac4a631b4bb8dfa89801384e4aea44"}]},{"sha":"d1f1f5a6f8ac4a631b4bb8dfa89801384e4aea44","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGQxZjFmNWE2ZjhhYzRhNjMxYjRiYjhkZmE4OTgwMTM4NGU0YWVhNDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-12T07:15:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T07:15:02Z"},"message":"fix(embedding): fall back to default model when OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL is empty (#336)\n\n## Summary\n\nFollowing the documented quickstart (`cp .env.example .env`, set\n`OPENAI_API_KEY`, `docker compose up -d`) leaves the stack **unable to\nembed anything**: every write logs `OpenAI 400 \"you must provide a model\nparameter\"`, `POST /api/v1/search` returns\n`{\"error\":{\"code\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"message\":\"Embedding service\nunavailable\"}}`, and any memory written in the meantime stays\npermanently unembedded (the re-embed retries exhaust against the same\nbroken config). This one-line change makes the embedding model default\nfire when the env var is **empty**, not just when it's absent.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe default lives in `common/embedding/constants.py`:\n\n```python\nOPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL: str = os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL\", \"text-embedding-3-small\")\n```\n\nBut `docker-compose.yml` maps the var as:\n\n```yaml\nOPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL: \"${OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL:-}\"\n```\n\n`.env.example` ships `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL` **commented out** (line\n137). So for a clean quickstart `.env`, Compose's `:-` interpolation\nturns \"absent from `.env`\" into **`OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=`\n(present-but-empty)** inside the container.\n\n`os.environ.get(key, default)` only substitutes the default when the key\nis **absent** — an empty string is a real value, so it returns `\"\"`. The\nprovider (`common/embedding/providers/openai.py`) then calls\n`embeddings.create(model=\"\", ...)`, which OpenAI rejects with 400. The\nPython default is effectively dead code on the Docker path.\n\n## Fix\n\n```python\nOPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL: str = (\n    os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL\") or \"text-embedding-3-small\"\n)\n```\n\n`or` falls back on any falsy value, so it covers **all** entry paths\nuniformly: Compose's empty-string injection, an empty hand-written\n`.env`, and an empty shell export. Explicit overrides\n(`text-embedding-3-large`, a local `bge-m3` via the TEI sidecar, etc.)\nare untouched. The fix is at the single point the code actually reads\nthe value, so it needs no coordinated change in `docker-compose.yml` or\n`.env.example`.\n\n## Verification\n\nLogic check across the three cases:\n\n| `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL` | resolves to |\n|---|---|\n| unset | `text-embedding-3-small` |\n| `\"\"` (the Compose case) | `text-embedding-3-small` |\n| `text-embedding-3-large` | `text-embedding-3-large` |\n\nReproduced end-to-end on a fresh Ubuntu 24.04 VM following the\nquickstart verbatim: before the change, writes 400'd and search returned\n\"Embedding service unavailable\"; setting the model (equivalent to this\nfallback) made writes enrich and hybrid search return results.\n\n## Scope\n\nDeliberately minimal — fixes the bug at its authoritative source. Two\nadjacent hardening options were considered and intentionally left out to\navoid duplicating the default string across files:\n- Compose default `${OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL:-text-embedding-3-small}`\n(cosmetic: makes `printenv` show the real value).\n- Uncommenting `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small` in\n`.env.example` (discoverability; note there's a second\n`OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=BAAI/bge-m3` line for the local-TEI sidecar that\nmust stay commented).\n\nHappy to fold either in if maintainers prefer the defense-in-depth.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9fcca8aa47f1f8d3903196b2eb72a97e05095015","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9fcca8aa47f1f8d3903196b2eb72a97e05095015"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/d1f1f5a6f8ac4a631b4bb8dfa89801384e4aea44","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK7H2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHosQADJhHph9AVwY3vrVjFMeUbId\nb5u3RpH3PjugsZ7BXAlSKIdG5EW7lfvC8PE3R40/Fw/KydqZyg02uxEGz+YPUQfS\neEOK9Ei2NFm/Ap3hGNcxHlqoqj/eBPIxrsjHc2WlqBKbSULLl+PaA6ncs1Jp/Yc5\ndpIlBHv3NWyl0a0qMXeKbERcLFyRHk4dE2Al+2udrZt3cdD1yMFDXXtwUMGd8imw\n/TxbqJ/ZANUI4bk+9PQLJa9TzD6Wto2vPsWd8k2sIHyQ8cQG3FbFF2JVs0d7rRcn\nYuiuzyayRkf3/Nwe70GIlL7kyYyD11oKH/6ovHeyB32k/0+r/lRCNHzxTp6H74+z\neUcUkvq2QuCUjsWJgK/iygI4/FPy0BbfSTQIcNZKwSr31mEqAN1AUAjLOYrvHS1l\nsazC6+N694jrGzj67FlUPtCxnXM2FWi00ixQ3GmHkmskcJqdqQmmB062/8fJPWd6\nm/tj7TyzPgWCscQ1x6RH9b/oN8Tgrp0BmZFAJalGMu8B/uLa8nrZ8bl9ujT3QE0p\n7j2Id6kns7A8b0757daapBeCesO+1uPJoVHG8vqwuesu6LpoDRPsWcwCmPaRwER3\nU3Iq3naCWlFQuxM0UqgPPqbyMucaTwtcXP9cD8tiYIVulgi1llq6gBhTwyL+Kb8L\n77PXQJZ+aMwLg8yttt/s\n=W/9n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9fcca8aa47f1f8d3903196b2eb72a97e05095015\nparent 43b3d8191b3567beba9cc6025f2df8e9aabb02de\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781248502 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781248502 +0300\n\nfix(embedding): fall back to default model when OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL is empty (#336)\n\n## Summary\n\nFollowing the documented quickstart (`cp .env.example .env`, set\n`OPENAI_API_KEY`, `docker compose up -d`) leaves the stack **unable to\nembed anything**: every write logs `OpenAI 400 \"you must provide a model\nparameter\"`, `POST /api/v1/search` returns\n`{\"error\":{\"code\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"message\":\"Embedding service\nunavailable\"}}`, and any memory written in the meantime stays\npermanently unembedded (the re-embed retries exhaust against the same\nbroken config). This one-line change makes the embedding model default\nfire when the env var is **empty**, not just when it's absent.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe default lives in `common/embedding/constants.py`:\n\n```python\nOPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL: str = os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL\", \"text-embedding-3-small\")\n```\n\nBut `docker-compose.yml` maps the var as:\n\n```yaml\nOPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL: \"${OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL:-}\"\n```\n\n`.env.example` ships `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL` **commented out** (line\n137). So for a clean quickstart `.env`, Compose's `:-` interpolation\nturns \"absent from `.env`\" into **`OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=`\n(present-but-empty)** inside the container.\n\n`os.environ.get(key, default)` only substitutes the default when the key\nis **absent** — an empty string is a real value, so it returns `\"\"`. The\nprovider (`common/embedding/providers/openai.py`) then calls\n`embeddings.create(model=\"\", ...)`, which OpenAI rejects with 400. The\nPython default is effectively dead code on the Docker path.\n\n## Fix\n\n```python\nOPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL: str = (\n    os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL\") or \"text-embedding-3-small\"\n)\n```\n\n`or` falls back on any falsy value, so it covers **all** entry paths\nuniformly: Compose's empty-string injection, an empty hand-written\n`.env`, and an empty shell export. Explicit overrides\n(`text-embedding-3-large`, a local `bge-m3` via the TEI sidecar, etc.)\nare untouched. The fix is at the single point the code actually reads\nthe value, so it needs no coordinated change in `docker-compose.yml` or\n`.env.example`.\n\n## Verification\n\nLogic check across the three cases:\n\n| `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL` | resolves to |\n|---|---|\n| unset | `text-embedding-3-small` |\n| `\"\"` (the Compose case) | `text-embedding-3-small` |\n| `text-embedding-3-large` | `text-embedding-3-large` |\n\nReproduced end-to-end on a fresh Ubuntu 24.04 VM following the\nquickstart verbatim: before the change, writes 400'd and search returned\n\"Embedding service unavailable\"; setting the model (equivalent to this\nfallback) made writes enrich and hybrid search return results.\n\n## Scope\n\nDeliberately minimal — fixes the bug at its authoritative source. Two\nadjacent hardening options were considered and intentionally left out to\navoid duplicating the default string across files:\n- Compose default `${OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL:-text-embedding-3-small}`\n(cosmetic: makes `printenv` show the real value).\n- Uncommenting `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small` in\n`.env.example` (discoverability; note there's a second\n`OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=BAAI/bge-m3` line for the local-TEI sidecar that\nmust stay commented).\n\nHappy to fold either in if maintainers prefer the defense-in-depth.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-12T07:15:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d1f1f5a6f8ac4a631b4bb8dfa89801384e4aea44","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d1f1f5a6f8ac4a631b4bb8dfa89801384e4aea44","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d1f1f5a6f8ac4a631b4bb8dfa89801384e4aea44/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"43b3d8191b3567beba9cc6025f2df8e9aabb02de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/43b3d8191b3567beba9cc6025f2df8e9aabb02de","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/43b3d8191b3567beba9cc6025f2df8e9aabb02de"}]},{"sha":"43b3d8191b3567beba9cc6025f2df8e9aabb02de","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQzYjNkODE5MWIzNTY3YmViYTljYzYwMjVmMmRmOGU5YWFiYjAyZGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T22:57:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T22:57:58Z"},"message":"fix(core-worker): retry connection-phase failures on storage calls — shared policy in common/http_retry (#334)\n\n## Why\n\nFollow-up to #333, which gave core-api's storage POSTs connection-phase\nretry after the 2026-06-11 prod incident (42× contradiction-detection\nfailures + dropped audit events — all first-attempt `ConnectTimeout`\nbehind the VPC connector). core-worker's storage client had the **same\nexposure with no retry at all** on its four POSTed SQL primitives\n(`archive_expired`, `archive_stale`, `purge_soft_deleted`,\n`upsert_tenant_suppression`) — and in the worker each connect failure is\nworse: it burns a Pub/Sub delivery attempt against the DLQ budget for a\nrequest that never reached storage.\n\n## What\n\n- **`common/http_retry.py` (new)** — the retry policy extracted from\ncore-api's client (`with_retry`, `with_connect_phase_retry`,\nexception/status constants, incident history) so the two storage clients\ncannot silently diverge. core-api behavior is unchanged — its helpers\nnow import the shared module (its retry tests pass unmodified).\n- **core-worker** — `with_connect_phase_retry` wired into\n`_signed_call`, the single choke point every storage call already goes\nthrough (same drift-proofing argument as its auth signing).\n**Connection-phase only, for all methods**: the worker's designed retry\npath for sent-but-failed requests is raise → nack → Pub/Sub redelivery;\nan in-process ReadTimeout/5xx retry would double-layer that.\nConnection-phase failures are the exception because the request provably\nnever reached storage.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `core-worker/tests/test_storage_client_retry.py` (new, mirrors the\ncore-api retry tests through the public endpoint helpers): POST\nprimitives retry ConnectTimeout/ConnectError and recover; give up after\n3 attempts; ReadTimeout and 5xx propagate un-retried for the nack path;\nGET/PATCH ride the same choke point. → 18 passed (incl. existing\n`test_storage_client_auth.py` — the 401-rotation interleaving is\nunchanged).\n- `pytest tests/test_storage_client_retry.py tests/test_audit_queue.py\ntests/test_storage_client_routing.py tests/test_embedding_backfill.py`\n(core-api side) → 53 passed.\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` clean; `mypy core-worker/src` clean;\ncore-api mypy delta vs main: none.\n(`test_consumer_enrich.py::test_enrichment_pending_cleared_even_with_heuristic_fallback`\nfails identically on clean main — pre-existing.)\n\n## Enterprise vendoring note\n\nNo manifest obligation: `scripts/check_vendored_drift.py` in the\nenterprise repo only requires classification for `common/` files present\nin **both** trees. `common/http_retry.py` is OSS-only until enterprise\nchooses to vendor it (at which point it should be added as `identical`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"142411d2bd02451c849581bb41d5030ced840a78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/142411d2bd02451c849581bb41d5030ced840a78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/43b3d8191b3567beba9cc6025f2df8e9aabb02de","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKz12CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAObIQACXRXDcfSvBJnT2ho19TSZFf\nDehwM3iiFwvZ1ElDQD6JBtEPO0S544EWhBL4l6zcvIPx+b+VYCHpM3huQB7/rD/Z\n/vX++25LhtZphktI0dtpEgLFUHrcR1fov25+Es7E1MSTRLOxgS0+Dlarq1xwzTUV\nUf94TPgWQLzd7WP4+Oq3OLJLes41TV6AzVmAQKmTmsLrmXHyQxiYmqv0IyNVIA0g\n6u5JozriOsLe9DihAmHfB1wXPnrDEwYHp1vaMuD1XGx+k38n+yf68OcH6CnCNuI/\nGpRyNX3ASobRi5fEA1vJtf+Li5vE7YMM1YMBKmAspfi5cFimOGCrfyNips+zFZpe\n1KNUJIOCaCivcrrAe5u+RJEdzSC3QGx8+8wQrHj1mxOhILyDwhsWQj9SOgRGBgMw\ndD3ILpYkRAzmeLJLAGFIsHzWX2tF78Eh/syC0b8EL4BGiRw+N4y//j52d7BveqD2\n30wMz+EsYTL6MYXnpRuUXSWOArhquNrbaYYjMpqV48aPMPKVVwkEOHi5NdbaxftZ\nHiN23bNl7EfFAVyvhBkdJ9tKXzvoQfJWaaUDdnSr7V9c6Jdk6kLGaSrxuRF8UAjN\nVe34y8iEITP/uLfuNy2EL1MmaeK5bsmS1clA+5balmeGGma5fin8zG/QW31nN81A\n1og3vylWzGpPAJRuKHOb\n=jvS1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 142411d2bd02451c849581bb41d5030ced840a78\nparent e26a3c561b542fbf58b4fd556ec2919e87286dfd\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781218678 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781218678 +0300\n\nfix(core-worker): retry connection-phase failures on storage calls — shared policy in common/http_retry (#334)\n\n## Why\n\nFollow-up to #333, which gave core-api's storage POSTs connection-phase\nretry after the 2026-06-11 prod incident (42× contradiction-detection\nfailures + dropped audit events — all first-attempt `ConnectTimeout`\nbehind the VPC connector). core-worker's storage client had the **same\nexposure with no retry at all** on its four POSTed SQL primitives\n(`archive_expired`, `archive_stale`, `purge_soft_deleted`,\n`upsert_tenant_suppression`) — and in the worker each connect failure is\nworse: it burns a Pub/Sub delivery attempt against the DLQ budget for a\nrequest that never reached storage.\n\n## What\n\n- **`common/http_retry.py` (new)** — the retry policy extracted from\ncore-api's client (`with_retry`, `with_connect_phase_retry`,\nexception/status constants, incident history) so the two storage clients\ncannot silently diverge. core-api behavior is unchanged — its helpers\nnow import the shared module (its retry tests pass unmodified).\n- **core-worker** — `with_connect_phase_retry` wired into\n`_signed_call`, the single choke point every storage call already goes\nthrough (same drift-proofing argument as its auth signing).\n**Connection-phase only, for all methods**: the worker's designed retry\npath for sent-but-failed requests is raise → nack → Pub/Sub redelivery;\nan in-process ReadTimeout/5xx retry would double-layer that.\nConnection-phase failures are the exception because the request provably\nnever reached storage.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `core-worker/tests/test_storage_client_retry.py` (new, mirrors the\ncore-api retry tests through the public endpoint helpers): POST\nprimitives retry ConnectTimeout/ConnectError and recover; give up after\n3 attempts; ReadTimeout and 5xx propagate un-retried for the nack path;\nGET/PATCH ride the same choke point. → 18 passed (incl. existing\n`test_storage_client_auth.py` — the 401-rotation interleaving is\nunchanged).\n- `pytest tests/test_storage_client_retry.py tests/test_audit_queue.py\ntests/test_storage_client_routing.py tests/test_embedding_backfill.py`\n(core-api side) → 53 passed.\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` clean; `mypy core-worker/src` clean;\ncore-api mypy delta vs main: none.\n(`test_consumer_enrich.py::test_enrichment_pending_cleared_even_with_heuristic_fallback`\nfails identically on clean main — pre-existing.)\n\n## Enterprise vendoring note\n\nNo manifest obligation: `scripts/check_vendored_drift.py` in the\nenterprise repo only requires classification for `common/` files present\nin **both** trees. `common/http_retry.py` is OSS-only until enterprise\nchooses to vendor it (at which point it should be added as `identical`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T22:57:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/43b3d8191b3567beba9cc6025f2df8e9aabb02de","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/43b3d8191b3567beba9cc6025f2df8e9aabb02de","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/43b3d8191b3567beba9cc6025f2df8e9aabb02de/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/or