PHuah75+Sk/qEL1epa7ATgwYVak6SUoPVOdMzsCZK\nSVy4D80gYBnmyD5oGzHy\n=jzd6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d3f33f4a75e3e434fed443a1996a39bb2ceb8f9c\nparent 2d91e33baa968459443005fd5a86d127c6c0c4d1\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781212877 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781212877 +0300\n\nfix(release): keep plugin/src/version.ts in sync on release-please PRs (#335)","verified_at":"2026-06-11T21:21:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e26a3c561b542fbf58b4fd556ec2919e87286dfd","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e26a3c561b542fbf58b4fd556ec2919e87286dfd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e26a3c561b542fbf58b4fd556ec2919e87286dfd/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2d91e33baa968459443005fd5a86d127c6c0c4d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2d91e33baa968459443005fd5a86d127c6c0c4d1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2d91e33baa968459443005fd5a86d127c6c0c4d1"}]},{"sha":"2d91e33baa968459443005fd5a86d127c6c0c4d1","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDJkOTFlMzNiYWE5Njg0NTk0NDMwMDVmZDVhODZkMTI3YzZjMGM0ZDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T18:26:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T18:26:36Z"},"message":"fix(storage-client): retry POSTs on connection-phase failures — never-sent requests cannot double-insert (#333)\n\n## Why\n\nProd 2026-06-11 (11:30–17:30Z): **42×** `Async contradiction detection\nfailed` (`find_similar_candidates`) and **2×** audit flush failures\n(`create_audit_logs_bulk` — events permanently lost for the affected\ntenant). Every single one was a **first-attempt `httpx.ConnectTimeout`**\nreaching core-storage-api through the VPC connector during the Phase J\nre-embed backlog drain. Idempotent siblings (GET/PATCH/DELETE) recovered\nvia the F5 retry wrapper; POST was excluded from retry because a retry\nafter partial success could double-insert.\n\nNote this is a **different leg** than #332: that fixed the\nAsyncOpenAI/LLM client's connect timeout; these failures are on the\ncore-storage-api client's unretried POSTs and would have continued even\nwith #332 deployed.\n\n## What\n\nThe blanket POST exclusion is broader than the safety argument requires.\n`ConnectTimeout` / `ConnectError` / `PoolTimeout` are all raised\n**before a single request byte is written** — retrying them cannot\nduplicate anything. `ReadTimeout` and 5xx stay non-retried for POST\n(request reached storage, may have committed; safe retry there still\nneeds storage-side idempotency keys).\n\n- `_with_retry` gains `retryable_exceptions` / `retryable_statuses`\nparams — defaults unchanged for idempotent callers.\n- `_post_with_retry` encodes the POST policy once (connection-phase\nexceptions, no status retries); wired into `_post`, `_post_optional`,\nand the bespoke `claim_idempotency` POST.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pytest tests/test_storage_client_retry.py tests/test_audit_queue.py\ntests/test_storage_client_routing.py` → 46 passed. New tests: POST\nretries ConnectTimeout/ConnectError and recovers; gives up after max\nattempts; does **not** retry ReadTimeout or 5xx; `_post_optional`\ncovered.\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` clean; mypy delta vs main: none (19\npre-existing transitive errors unchanged).\n\n## Follow-up (separate PR)\n\ncore-worker's storage client has four unretried POSTs\n(`archive_expired`, `archive_stale`, `purge_soft_deleted`,\n`upsert_tenant_suppression`) with the same exposure.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"70bcfa7f304ddff8a627e5618a113f5245a8712d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/70bcfa7f304ddff8a627e5618a113f5245a8712d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/2d91e33baa968459443005fd5a86d127c6c0c4d1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKv3cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+EwQACeeTrLPAaY4tBnpxA3++NGu\n8LnXXdHjrTcBuzDYBoReG6H/8IZ9t2au21/Zdn9fPyhmBag9/U5ofJas+fxn0v1C\nPcsLIEOlPpkD5urIanTlwBFhOhcNhtxNaV59FW6iGxzNT9vVu+SEVJcIS160D5o/\nwZYMxLBLsZJbUO4rwyor9K3mYP0YtxN0mTFKot7zLodaWGF4Kf9J1VPPmSmZyUyj\nLkxkl9x0uuJl4FZXpt5Eer1m2Qpv1VEjCK+do62tXQgPsmInxBfJ0WQtBfVGjtf+\nvr16fWqTlsKvkTe/CXSVzRrJkA8XuhuATM1yzKaxzym+cgW54lYBtWaWzzzZVIei\nZy0AiixtyZRgJE2gBLgsaWDeslsI5VC+PXu1x32uN4OvF+uNSXs3JG8eMGRlP+op\ntfYgQFJQNbzPs1DDpTo8gncN7OJ2OY77Purododq8QNXdbMEiUfouCW0FZDRjkVE\nBM67DVH1QGUEmotPPrv/DHApbtC1aVDmP0igJ67ayegb8pA1Im/jQO3Ek4fmjg7Z\n5GXiN/2PS9UelpZALz5+Sp2Z6MNdfhBgYbYm6CTGJElVNSPxqmqfj/LCgOMbCIhH\ncTwkpiiye4icfWTDzROPr6sm6gEJvdalPIOrY7K8K1QokepDB9c90wxm3jUChXvU\nGnxmS7yYMQTcwr0bTcWO\n=NKYi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 70bcfa7f304ddff8a627e5618a113f5245a8712d\nparent ea89a61cb3b6b4331b92183dfe09f3bbfc24e879\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781202396 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781202396 +0300\n\nfix(storage-client): retry POSTs on connection-phase failures — never-sent requests cannot double-insert (#333)\n\n## Why\n\nProd 2026-06-11 (11:30–17:30Z): **42×** `Async contradiction detection\nfailed` (`find_similar_candidates`) and **2×** audit flush failures\n(`create_audit_logs_bulk` — events permanently lost for the affected\ntenant). Every single one was a **first-attempt `httpx.ConnectTimeout`**\nreaching core-storage-api through the VPC connector during the Phase J\nre-embed backlog drain. Idempotent siblings (GET/PATCH/DELETE) recovered\nvia the F5 retry wrapper; POST was excluded from retry because a retry\nafter partial success could double-insert.\n\nNote this is a **different leg** than #332: that fixed the\nAsyncOpenAI/LLM client's connect timeout; these failures are on the\ncore-storage-api client's unretried POSTs and would have continued even\nwith #332 deployed.\n\n## What\n\nThe blanket POST exclusion is broader than the safety argument requires.\n`ConnectTimeout` / `ConnectError` / `PoolTimeout` are all raised\n**before a single request byte is written** — retrying them cannot\nduplicate anything. `ReadTimeout` and 5xx stay non-retried for POST\n(request reached storage, may have committed; safe retry there still\nneeds storage-side idempotency keys).\n\n- `_with_retry` gains `retryable_exceptions` / `retryable_statuses`\nparams — defaults unchanged for idempotent callers.\n- `_post_with_retry` encodes the POST policy once (connection-phase\nexceptions, no status retries); wired into `_post`, `_post_optional`,\nand the bespoke `claim_idempotency` POST.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pytest tests/test_storage_client_retry.py tests/test_audit_queue.py\ntests/test_storage_client_routing.py` → 46 passed. New tests: POST\nretries ConnectTimeout/ConnectError and recovers; gives up after max\nattempts; does **not** retry ReadTimeout or 5xx; `_post_optional`\ncovered.\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` clean; mypy delta vs main: none (19\npre-existing transitive errors unchanged).\n\n## Follow-up (separate PR)\n\ncore-worker's storage client has four unretried POSTs\n(`archive_expired`, `archive_stale`, `purge_soft_deleted`,\n`upsert_tenant_suppression`) with the same exposure.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T18:26:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2d91e33baa968459443005fd5a86d127c6c0c4d1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2d91e33baa968459443005fd5a86d127c6c0c4d1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2d91e33baa968459443005fd5a86d127c6c0c4d1/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ea89a61cb3b6b4331b92183dfe09f3bbfc24e879","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ea89a61cb3b6b4331b92183dfe09f3bbfc24e879","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ea89a61cb3b6b4331b92183dfe09f3bbfc24e879"}]},{"sha":"ea89a61cb3b6b4331b92183dfe09f3bbfc24e879","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGVhODlhNjFjYjNiNmI0MzMxYjkyMTgzZGZlMDlmM2JiZmMyNGU4Nzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T17:06:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T17:06:35Z"},"message":"fix(llm): explicit httpx per-phase timeouts — 5s connect too tight behind VPC connector (#332)\n\n## Why\n\nProd core-api shows a steady trickle of `httpcore.ConnectTimeout` from\nthe enrichment/entity-extraction handlers (a few per hour, predates\nrecent deploys). Root cause: passing a bare float to\n`AsyncOpenAI(timeout=...)` keeps httpx's **default 5s connect/pool\nphases**, and with `all-traffic` VPC egress every outbound call rides\nthe connector + Cloud NAT — cold connections intermittently exceed 5s.\nTwo effects: nack/redelivery noise (self-healing — 12h DLQ deliveries:\nzero), and **`Entity extraction failed` is caught as non-fatal, so the\nmemory is acked without entity links — a permanent silent gap**.\n\n## What\n\n- `httpx.Timeout(connect=15, read=<request budget>, write=15, pool=10)`\non the OpenAI-compatible client; connect/pool env-tunable\n(`OPENAI_HTTPX_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`,\n`OPENAI_HTTPX_POOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`).\n- The bespoke `OPENAI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` reader generalised to\n`_read_float_env` and reused.\n\nDeliberately scoped: no keepalive-pool resizing and no handler-level\nretry in this PR — the runbook'd next steps if the trickle persists\nafter this lands (expected reduction: most of it).\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest tests/test_p4_1_llm_fallback.py tests/test_events` → 118\npassed (full-suite collection errors are a pre-existing local `tiktoken`\ngap, also on main).\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` clean. DCO signed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5fe5f9ae6ccc911c1597c95cbfc8e8952fa7aa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a5fe5f9ae6ccc911c1597c95cbfc8e8952fa7aa4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ea89a61cb3b6b4331b92183dfe09f3bbfc24e879","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKusbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcxwQAA1Md7TIFvi08Krv2J3Huy6R\n0QFYcy5HEqLGUm3jfTzNYymwkmr5uP2FRYU7tZiJldUbDe7yj98E2SV0PpeJ1e6N\n5MCXDjxzzlQi7cRJ0VInBdjEMzUXbx+tRWkYld3474Av9bAIW1Q7WParo93Ec6wi\nkkk1Hcje8mQhg+WBeahsis+a9qjifYZxUqcBQGybG0lIpaYPZ6ngiuC+9m5fkazs\nMOvsKllda5gBBZdu5fFA+BIvrocmBVmbiFO/AHbeB6G8gyGknJJRnQWm9CSYPzgc\nYzdEB9T5CKcCHWB6+As3h1tSRfiBhVz5rvNv+dG47XuNDh6UqsgaIBLwr0dxNmiN\nhu+V3muVRRc0HtTfuX5ANfVo7LxTRzk/a/OClA1c9m0VUS/wSbgqT4xfYTB0iZud\nXaIexEBZ7039XeEwAQHc6e45rOt02hsMaJESCP20e7bzrozmhHODHdEatSgXgXGq\nZbEzoRYGm5mE12caCs/NHBKDTwF1RwiL8l9Phv3PDRTEylrz7c7cGicKkZOmmr6O\ncE/0U+4qAE+eTICRkK6EOfDsJlj81aY8iThZJiUMcN2zCyT+KHTfBGcQmNyYYkLq\nFO9vguxLgdQV7mQhQTiAQbTkVyV5RQu8mzwwVgnxme+11cpBOBmv9WWxa86PMnik\nA2/iufqmRvYYW6FIcCTh\n=jhxR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a5fe5f9ae6ccc911c1597c95cbfc8e8952fa7aa4\nparent 610fe8e385c38237cf22276a02ef35e9345772d2\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781197595 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781197595 +0300\n\nfix(llm): explicit httpx per-phase timeouts — 5s connect too tight behind VPC connector (#332)\n\n## Why\n\nProd core-api shows a steady trickle of `httpcore.ConnectTimeout` from\nthe enrichment/entity-extraction handlers (a few per hour, predates\nrecent deploys). Root cause: passing a bare float to\n`AsyncOpenAI(timeout=...)` keeps httpx's **default 5s connect/pool\nphases**, and with `all-traffic` VPC egress every outbound call rides\nthe connector + Cloud NAT — cold connections intermittently exceed 5s.\nTwo effects: nack/redelivery noise (self-healing — 12h DLQ deliveries:\nzero), and **`Entity extraction failed` is caught as non-fatal, so the\nmemory is acked without entity links — a permanent silent gap**.\n\n## What\n\n- `httpx.Timeout(connect=15, read=<request budget>, write=15, pool=10)`\non the OpenAI-compatible client; connect/pool env-tunable\n(`OPENAI_HTTPX_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`,\n`OPENAI_HTTPX_POOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`).\n- The bespoke `OPENAI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` reader generalised to\n`_read_float_env` and reused.\n\nDeliberately scoped: no keepalive-pool resizing and no handler-level\nretry in this PR — the runbook'd next steps if the trickle persists\nafter this lands (expected reduction: most of it).\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest tests/test_p4_1_llm_fallback.py tests/test_events` → 118\npassed (full-suite collection errors are a pre-existing local `tiktoken`\ngap, also on main).\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` clean. DCO signed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T17:06:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ea89a61cb3b6b4331b92183dfe09f3bbfc24e879","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ea89a61cb3b6b4331b92183dfe09f3bbfc24e879","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ea89a61cb3b6b4331b92183dfe09f3bbfc24e879/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"610fe8e385c38237cf22276a02ef35e9345772d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/610fe8e385c38237cf22276a02ef35e9345772d2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/610fe8e385c38237cf22276a02ef35e9345772d2"}]},{"sha":"610fe8e385c38237cf22276a02ef35e9345772d2","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDYxMGZlOGUzODVjMzgyMzdjZjIyMjc2YTAyZWYzNWU5MzQ1NzcyZDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T15:51:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T15:51:08Z"},"message":"fix(events): publisher candidate cleanups also called the nonexistent close() (#331)\n\nFollow-up to #330 (raced its merge — this was meant as an amendment).\nThe three fire-and-forget publisher-**candidate** cleanup paths\n(`_close_pending`, `_close_post_stop`, `_close_loser`) had the same\nnonexistent-`PublisherClient.close()` bug: no data loss (an uninstalled\ncandidate has no batches), but the swallowed AttributeError meant the\nSDK commit thread was never joined — a thread leak + debug-log noise on\nevery TOCTOU/cancelled construction.\n\n- All three now call `candidate.stop()`; log messages updated.\n- TOCTOU test fakes now model the real `PublisherClient` surface\n(`stop()`, no `close()`) so a regression can't pass.\n- Subscriber-side `close()` calls untouched (valid API there).\n\n80 events tests green; ruff check + format clean; DCO signed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"db56e988e6d55632f0723491043bb95f37fb3a90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/db56e988e6d55632f0723491043bb95f37fb3a90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/610fe8e385c38237cf22276a02ef35e9345772d2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKtlsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAy1wQACYIhtnwkS0S61juwfWFcgAa\nEMPGa9taTuGVSf2XN7TKvBE21/757bW+uK41c8iptRoB8v4ZGrCtt9MNCOFDsyRc\nZRekcZ19JjlJg4G5OHSiBuYR8s2zVdKUSvpzxBH8Yj6FXV/rRW7tYYFZLTD6a9ew\nZ3jS4WMKzGwTk3NaS5rvdcw7AAaKSUbpRfSHkxp5tltmr1ZQyqao0ZbKK3Fti8jd\nnSt68OxtLk+Ws+hF6yYQf2K3tQZ8Uu7h3iNEDeLowRd3bSjLUfHBp6N1CSkI/lyQ\n1U7LRwrrt6ofUNMSNQlKlO6qYVyGjCiu+4yoa+SH5Db2RMDcUOyHOuBKH6PSwK2C\nHUB8WgvDX/H+IG5UolvgiWte5/YwT+p32xdEO98I2efBAHctt3lQlyKFOa04hpiN\nlcMKBsr0T9bFVrtOySA5dzhBjrTkZJVyr+vx9kEmsmXuaBvO7nxFTDXlFqzSn0dJ\noN+Wd8xKf5wgOz2JIomBD553dJvkqFxJPBW8i1TMsKXRQ5MPd1wqTzLnLkO6HzpX\n518PFyG9/Sj7NExxqsaURmlFQA82WtgnBecp9SSMplPCOHmTKzUUxMyVixAQeJwT\nQr5rMv59E6i1kaGKy8t/scZvLD32IdWMViswpxXhzbCu3J7QK2wdKRhTxJzpE8cf\nTGVWWrG9PiW2K67/CONJ\n=3yls\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree db56e988e6d55632f0723491043bb95f37fb3a90\nparent 1c2aba577a1a7cd4347faff3118d7179c39a7368\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781193068 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781193068 +0300\n\nfix(events): publisher candidate cleanups also called the nonexistent close() (#331)\n\nFollow-up to #330 (raced its merge — this was meant as an amendment).\nThe three fire-and-forget publisher-**candidate** cleanup paths\n(`_close_pending`, `_close_post_stop`, `_close_loser`) had the same\nnonexistent-`PublisherClient.close()` bug: no data loss (an uninstalled\ncandidate has no batches), but the swallowed AttributeError meant the\nSDK commit thread was never joined — a thread leak + debug-log noise on\nevery TOCTOU/cancelled construction.\n\n- All three now call `candidate.stop()`; log messages updated.\n- TOCTOU test fakes now model the real `PublisherClient` surface\n(`stop()`, no `close()`) so a regression can't pass.\n- Subscriber-side `close()` calls untouched (valid API there).\n\n80 events tests green; ruff check + format clean; DCO signed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T15:51:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/610fe8e385c38237cf22276a02ef35e9345772d2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/610fe8e385c38237cf22276a02ef35e9345772d2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/610fe8e385c38237cf22276a02ef35e9345772d2/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1c2aba577a1a7cd4347faff3118d7179c39a7368","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1c2aba577a1a7cd4347faff3118d7179c39a7368","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1c2aba577a1a7cd4347faff3118d7179c39a7368"}]},{"sha":"1c2aba577a1a7cd4347faff3118d7179c39a7368","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDFjMmFiYTU3N2ExYTdjZDQzNDdmYWZmMzExOGQ3MTc5YzM5YTczNjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T15:45:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T15:45:09Z"},"message":"fix(events): pubsub shutdown never flushed the publisher — final batches silently lost (#330)\n\n## Why\n\n`PubSubEventBus.stop()` calls `publisher.close()` — **which doesn't\nexist on `PublisherClient`** (that's a SubscriberClient method). The\nAttributeError is swallowed by the per-step guard and logged as\n`publisher.close() failed; continuing teardown` on every service\nshutdown (visible in prod logs today). The real API is\n`PublisherClient.stop()`: commits outstanding batches + joins the commit\nthread — and it's the **only** flush in the pipeline, since `publish()`\nis fire-and-forget into the client's batch queue.\n\n**Impact**: long-running services rarely notice (the commit thread\ntransmits within ~10ms), but short-lived processes lose their entire\nfinal batch. Verified in prod 2026-06-11: a tenant re-embed backfill\n(`core_worker.cli backfill-embeddings`) reported `published=16` while\n**zero events reached the topic** — confirmed via topic\n`send_message_operation_count` and a probe job that awaited the publish\nfuture.\n\n## What\n\n- `stop()` → `publisher.stop()` (drains); log message updated.\n- `core_worker.cli` drains the bus in its `finally` (the prod incident's\ndirect trigger).\n- Corrected `publish()`'s at-least-once comment (only holds when\n`stop()` runs before exit).\n- Test publisher mocks **spec-limited** to the real client surface — a\npermissive `MagicMock` accepting `.close()` is exactly how this survived\nthe existing `stop()` tests. Assertions moved to `.stop()`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pytest tests/test_events/` → 80 passed; `tests/test_logging.py`\nunaffected (21 passed).\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean. DCO signed.\n- Operationally proven in prod: re-running the same backfill with an\nexplicit `PublisherClient.stop()` flush delivered 16/16 events (tenant\nfully re-embedded).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"981a18bc9f73c3206bb0b031cd45210d8babc965","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/981a18bc9f73c3206bb0b031cd45210d8babc965"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/1c2aba577a1a7cd4347faff3118d7179c39a7368","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKtgFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjkAQAFtToZpl92+nr19UGGMvhvFs\nuAFsx2u7yZ8AlltSpTz/goLxfY9wQmR0M5dacITd8Xsk3CZg66hgltepMcE4oiJU\nA+0iEo2xNlxI59Dn2snneUCoc0ZjXBcH5Gg+t92HLPK1Zu1V277o/zIhXO2ed/OA\nvuCUEGhhCXmF+wa7g/exuyeUtq3udeBfMDyWzGEjtQWgxjvnkl/VDQn1YVMIBZ95\nuTyH24jmEM/0fZj2R+dOHCWLbqRngDoSG7L/qichnRDZY3dwY6lvJApj0JaBxrf4\nATSXc9CwRm7gu3+wWPc+BfHNmX2BhqUVUKImmz6F0ivu/BxKqH2Xiwhtfmn8bpiH\nUKMY7OXMH/XIaF5VRdTvEFthm/R4hN9h9zLDJm3Kr37EofXOWgyRnjjOJEPTtKV7\nPx3wKmH1Mtgp8IA/JKYOBH5Sr1TsaBIKFw+DZbAlMJseOV2uosbYYMKi6YBHTu3L\nrAMj+d3c17/EnHAiyBl/kPvtNpf12Bcxr7iA2amX9N7qZDaOEF9wYov7Lq93OHG8\nFsp4R8N0gQmlxvp9ty3+zeW0TxIRfT7p7enOPtVQ7uzjSv86QqftKoZE4eOV6yKs\n5llxbrb3fHfZZG5jQwYEawi6xJdw02Ep3HNHbvlqZRDhCuPEJYykYRq7zPKTigbj\nWnCqIKjgy+Si6HadQ/7i\n=WLYK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 981a18bc9f73c3206bb0b031cd45210d8babc965\nparent d806114bc943a1d97480584192091e0583d41545\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781192709 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781192709 +0300\n\nfix(events): pubsub shutdown never flushed the publisher — final batches silently lost (#330)\n\n## Why\n\n`PubSubEventBus.stop()` calls `publisher.close()` — **which doesn't\nexist on `PublisherClient`** (that's a SubscriberClient method). The\nAttributeError is swallowed by the per-step guard and logged as\n`publisher.close() failed; continuing teardown` on every service\nshutdown (visible in prod logs today). The real API is\n`PublisherClient.stop()`: commits outstanding batches + joins the commit\nthread — and it's the **only** flush in the pipeline, since `publish()`\nis fire-and-forget into the client's batch queue.\n\n**Impact**: long-running services rarely notice (the commit thread\ntransmits within ~10ms), but short-lived processes lose their entire\nfinal batch. Verified in prod 2026-06-11: a tenant re-embed backfill\n(`core_worker.cli backfill-embeddings`) reported `published=16` while\n**zero events reached the topic** — confirmed via topic\n`send_message_operation_count` and a probe job that awaited the publish\nfuture.\n\n## What\n\n- `stop()` → `publisher.stop()` (drains); log message updated.\n- `core_worker.cli` drains the bus in its `finally` (the prod incident's\ndirect trigger).\n- Corrected `publish()`'s at-least-once comment (only holds when\n`stop()` runs before exit).\n- Test publisher mocks **spec-limited** to the real client surface — a\npermissive `MagicMock` accepting `.close()` is exactly how this survived\nthe existing `stop()` tests. Assertions moved to `.stop()`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pytest tests/test_events/` → 80 passed; `tests/test_logging.py`\nunaffected (21 passed).\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean. DCO signed.\n- Operationally proven in prod: re-running the same backfill with an\nexplicit `PublisherClient.stop()` flush delivered 16/16 events (tenant\nfully re-embedded).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T15:45:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1c2aba577a1a7cd4347faff3118d7179c39a7368","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1c2aba577a1a7cd4347faff3118d7179c39a7368","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1c2aba577a1a7cd4347faff3118d7179c39a7368/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d806114bc943a1d97480584192091e0