ls): per-node skill-reconcile observability on the heartbeat (#325)","verified_at":"2026-06-11T14:12:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d806114bc943a1d97480584192091e0583d41545","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d806114bc943a1d97480584192091e0583d41545","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d806114bc943a1d97480584192091e0583d41545/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9fdc47ee1883089b2202644d3819321cd372435e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9fdc47ee1883089b2202644d3819321cd372435e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9fdc47ee1883089b2202644d3819321cd372435e"}]},{"sha":"9fdc47ee1883089b2202644d3819321cd372435e","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDlmZGM0N2VlMTg4MzA4OWIyMjAyNjQ0ZDM4MTkzMjFjZDM3MjQzNWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T13:40:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T13:40:20Z"},"message":"CAURA-134 fix(contradiction): raise context-fetch timeout 5s → 30s + improve failure log (#324)\n\n## Summary\n\nWet test on dev v2.14.0 today (post-CAURA-133, with CAURA-131 wiring +\nCAURA-133 prompt both deployed) showed the priya silence still present:\n**0 / 5 trials surfaced a contradiction** even though every trial had\nboth sides resolved to the same canonical `priya` entity row.\n\nCAURA-132 forensic logs revealed the cause is **not** the prompt and\n**not** the wiring — it's the 5-second `asyncio.wait_for` budget on the\ncontext fetch timing out:\n\n```\nPATH_C_DETECTION entry           candidates_initial=8\nPATH_C_DETECTION after_a1_17     remaining=8\nPATH_C_DETECTION judge_selection candidates=8 entity_aware=0 base=8  ← !!\nPATH_C_DETECTION verdict         judge=base verdict=False  (× 8)\n\nWARNING: Path C entity-links context fetch failed for memory <id>: .\n         Falling through to base LLM judge.\n```\n\nThe empty bit after `failed:` is the fingerprint of\n`asyncio.TimeoutError` (whose default `str(e)` is empty). With dev's\naccumulated tenant state, the parallel `_fetch_entity_context` gather\nexceeds 5s — every candidate falls back to the base judge. **CAURA-131's\nentity-aware judge is silently bypassed; CAURA-133's prompt rewrite is\nnever exercised.**\n\n## What this PR changes\n\n| Layer | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Context-fetch timeout | hard-coded `5.0` at both call-sites | new\n`_CONTEXT_FETCH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 30.0` module constant; both call-sites\nreference it |\n| WARNING log shape | `… failed: %s. Falling through …` (empty for\n`TimeoutError`) | `… failed: %s: %s. Falling through …` with\n`type(e).__name__` always rendered |\n| Symmetric failure observability | success log only (`PATH_C_DETECTION\ncontext_fetched`) | + new `PATH_C_DETECTION context_fetch_failed\nmemory=… exc_type=… candidates=N` INFO log |\n\nBoth call-sites:\n- Retraction path (CAURA-129, ~`contradiction_detector.py:1414`) — gets\nprefix `PATH_C_RETRACTION context_fetch_failed`.\n- Detection path (CAURA-131, ~`contradiction_detector.py:1700`) — gets\nWARNING update + INFO failure log.\n\n## Why 30s is safe (not user-facing latency)\n\nPath C runs in a **fire-and-forget background task after the write has\nalready returned 201**. The timeout only bounds the background task's\nwall-clock — it never gates user-perceived write latency. The only side\neffects of raising it are:\n- **Time-to-flag on slow tenants improves** (was: never, because the 5s\ntimeout silenced them; now: ~10-30s).\n- Hung Pub/Sub leases extend from ≤5s to ≤30s on storage stalls. Worker\nconcurrency is async-bound and sized for this.\n\n## Tests\n\n| File | New / changed | Asserts |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_caura_131_entity_aware_path_c_detection.py` | extended\n`test_fallback_to_base_judge_when_context_fetch_fails` | WARNING\nincludes `RuntimeError` class name; INFO `context_fetch_failed` fires\nwith `exc_type=RuntimeError` |\n| | **NEW** `test_fallback_to_base_judge_logs_timeouterror_explicitly` |\nRaises `asyncio.TimeoutError` (dominant prod failure, empty `str(e)`);\nasserts WARNING still names the class. Locks in the diagnosability fix\nagainst the empty-str(e) trap. |\n| | **NEW** `test_context_fetch_timeout_constant_is_generous_enough` |\nGuards against anyone tightening `_CONTEXT_FETCH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` back\nbelow 15s. |\n| `test_a4_13_path_c_retraction.py` | **NEW**\n`test_retraction_context_fetch_failure_logs_exc_type` | Retraction\nWARNING has `PATH_C_RETRACTION context_fetch_failed` prefix +\n`TimeoutError` class name. |\n\nTests collected:\n- `test_caura_131_entity_aware_path_c_detection.py`: **10** (was 8 + 2\nnew)\n- `test_a4_13_path_c_retraction.py`: **12** (was 11 + 1 new)\n\nValidation: `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `pytest --collect-only`\nall clean.\n\n## Wet-test plan (post-deploy)\n\nCAURA-134 is the **unblocker for CAURA-131/133 verification**. Today we\ncannot tell if those PRs work because the judge they wire to isn't being\ninvoked.\n\n| Probe | Verifies |\n|---|---|\n| W1 | GCP query for `\"context fetch failed\"` warnings — pre vs post —\ndrops materially |\n| W2 | `repro_contradictions_collision.py` × 5 → `context_fetched` lines\nreappear → `judge_selection entity_aware>0 base=0` |\n| W3 | For W2 trials with `entity_aware>0`: pull `PATH_C_DETECTION\nverdict judge=entity_aware` → **≥4/5 verdict=True** verifies CAURA-133's\nprompt fix |\n| W4 | 10-min sweep for any new warning classes (no regressions) |\n| W5 | Retraction-path warnings also drop (same fetch, same fix) |\n\n## Rollback\n\nSingle `git revert`. Constant bump + log format + 1 new log line. No\nschema, no migration, no behavior change in success paths.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"4a67e0e8fb7515298b38ccbee9a8dc73e8a42577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4a67e0e8fb7515298b38ccbee9a8dc73e8a42577"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/9fdc47ee1883089b2202644d3819321cd372435e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKrrECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcB4QAGfxCBaAAtlxBfsamtAuWr/P\ncNN1EUpUAzURcB+DilIFRFri9h6HdCKP4LDDUeKD0vwo4PLOFWcDD2NZ2nbHZVGI\nzk+HFswC/eRu8VoMBaWfGAJS/fsVzfi6kkMYnrKT6MD8cWwBRPqcCqn9ScNsjDWP\n0z387K5Xy3c4CRKM3FD/3WRL+ne27aQXDdTnKAUoolB2UC7aX4QUyjzHhuORb2wC\n14hmI2hPS0MkgiUPwapXU7IQgoDV1kqn+nQPGQogYWWwj9VeDL2VAViNqLdEJG5T\n9AVL+gTX/onyXQpbXSmgSSTmszVGhYD0ZCO7haeeDdrwUM1NLxg1M5OrT2K/iZXC\ncYD058kf0ee5l56494uvq+OPHQWxZ+AYGkDsn1OI2KcAx2xc34He9R2tuDQHdMCb\nQzvR1DOiqpAoINZCs2c4mDslKK5q0GYRsRMIOgWOpcgWM9JIMQJqwOMB/OBLCyCK\nG2PqW6hT9lQboFpSGhdZrMLEuWLQhbKM/HP7diyVnqA5aTauxbYfwhNbfFD+GEGf\nEnXUgpQYw0bv80opiFKLdkFXhv5xX3KLaGAEYrpWGSC1ZDY+vabA/wd4vfueLaTR\nfVyECrHZtsNcnhygWrzNzv9mTUAn1kcnsFAok1X8PZ3lk3HCTEXBWON10kOKUPJ1\n+RiJCfrbN9LWUBewojG1\n=Uh6o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4a67e0e8fb7515298b38ccbee9a8dc73e8a42577\nparent ea0e52b3fe43e72a279f365f38cd81301f1a6fce\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781185220 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781185220 +0300\n\nCAURA-134 fix(contradiction): raise context-fetch timeout 5s → 30s + improve failure log (#324)\n\n## Summary\n\nWet test on dev v2.14.0 today (post-CAURA-133, with CAURA-131 wiring +\nCAURA-133 prompt both deployed) showed the priya silence still present:\n**0 / 5 trials surfaced a contradiction** even though every trial had\nboth sides resolved to the same canonical `priya` entity row.\n\nCAURA-132 forensic logs revealed the cause is **not** the prompt and\n**not** the wiring — it's the 5-second `asyncio.wait_for` budget on the\ncontext fetch timing out:\n\n```\nPATH_C_DETECTION entry           candidates_initial=8\nPATH_C_DETECTION after_a1_17     remaining=8\nPATH_C_DETECTION judge_selection candidates=8 entity_aware=0 base=8  ← !!\nPATH_C_DETECTION verdict         judge=base verdict=False  (× 8)\n\nWARNING: Path C entity-links context fetch failed for memory <id>: .\n         Falling through to base LLM judge.\n```\n\nThe empty bit after `failed:` is the fingerprint of\n`asyncio.TimeoutError` (whose default `str(e)` is empty). With dev's\naccumulated tenant state, the parallel `_fetch_entity_context` gather\nexceeds 5s — every candidate falls back to the base judge. **CAURA-131's\nentity-aware judge is silently bypassed; CAURA-133's prompt rewrite is\nnever exercised.**\n\n## What this PR changes\n\n| Layer | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Context-fetch timeout | hard-coded `5.0` at both call-sites | new\n`_CONTEXT_FETCH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 30.0` module constant; both call-sites\nreference it |\n| WARNING log shape | `… failed: %s. Falling through …` (empty for\n`TimeoutError`) | `… failed: %s: %s. Falling through …` with\n`type(e).__name__` always rendered |\n| Symmetric failure observability | success log only (`PATH_C_DETECTION\ncontext_fetched`) | + new `PATH_C_DETECTION context_fetch_failed\nmemory=… exc_type=… candidates=N` INFO log |\n\nBoth call-sites:\n- Retraction path (CAURA-129, ~`contradiction_detector.py:1414`) — gets\nprefix `PATH_C_RETRACTION context_fetch_failed`.\n- Detection path (CAURA-131, ~`contradiction_detector.py:1700`) — gets\nWARNING update + INFO failure log.\n\n## Why 30s is safe (not user-facing latency)\n\nPath C runs in a **fire-and-forget background task after the write has\nalready returned 201**. The timeout only bounds the background task's\nwall-clock — it never gates user-perceived write latency. The only side\neffects of raising it are:\n- **Time-to-flag on slow tenants improves** (was: never, because the 5s\ntimeout silenced them; now: ~10-30s).\n- Hung Pub/Sub leases extend from ≤5s to ≤30s on storage stalls. Worker\nconcurrency is async-bound and sized for this.\n\n## Tests\n\n| File | New / changed | Asserts |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_caura_131_entity_aware_path_c_detection.py` | extended\n`test_fallback_to_base_judge_when_context_fetch_fails` | WARNING\nincludes `RuntimeError` class name; INFO `context_fetch_failed` fires\nwith `exc_type=RuntimeError` |\n| | **NEW** `test_fallback_to_base_judge_logs_timeouterror_explicitly` |\nRaises `asyncio.TimeoutError` (dominant prod failure, empty `str(e)`);\nasserts WARNING still names the class. Locks in the diagnosability fix\nagainst the empty-str(e) trap. |\n| | **NEW** `test_context_fetch_timeout_constant_is_generous_enough` |\nGuards against anyone tightening `_CONTEXT_FETCH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` back\nbelow 15s. |\n| `test_a4_13_path_c_retraction.py` | **NEW**\n`test_retraction_context_fetch_failure_logs_exc_type` | Retraction\nWARNING has `PATH_C_RETRACTION context_fetch_failed` prefix +\n`TimeoutError` class name. |\n\nTests collected:\n- `test_caura_131_entity_aware_path_c_detection.py`: **10** (was 8 + 2\nnew)\n- `test_a4_13_path_c_retraction.py`: **12** (was 11 + 1 new)\n\nValidation: `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `pytest --collect-only`\nall clean.\n\n## Wet-test plan (post-deploy)\n\nCAURA-134 is the **unblocker for CAURA-131/133 verification**. Today we\ncannot tell if those PRs work because the judge they wire to isn't being\ninvoked.\n\n| Probe | Verifies |\n|---|---|\n| W1 | GCP query for `\"context fetch failed\"` warnings — pre vs post —\ndrops materially |\n| W2 | `repro_contradictions_collision.py` × 5 → `context_fetched` lines\nreappear → `judge_selection entity_aware>0 base=0` |\n| W3 | For W2 trials with `entity_aware>0`: pull `PATH_C_DETECTION\nverdict judge=entity_aware` → **≥4/5 verdict=True** verifies CAURA-133's\nprompt fix |\n| W4 | 10-min sweep for any new warning classes (no regressions) |\n| W5 | Retraction-path warnings also drop (same fetch, same fix) |\n\n## Rollback\n\nSingle `git revert`. Constant bump + log format + 1 new log line. No\nschema, no migration, no behavior change in success paths.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T13:40:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9fdc47ee1883089b2202644d3819321cd372435e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9fdc47ee1883089b2202644d3819321cd372435e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9fdc47ee1883089b2202644d3819321cd372435e/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ea0e52b3fe43e72a279f365f38cd81301f1a6fce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ea0e52b3fe43e72a279f365f38cd81301f1a6fce","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ea0e52b3fe43e72a279f365f38cd81301f1a6fce"}]},{"sha":"ea0e52b3fe43e72a279f365f38cd81301f1a6fce","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGVhMGU1MmIzZmU0M2U3MmEyNzlmMzY1ZjM4Y2Q4MTMwMWYxYTZmY2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T13:30:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T13:30:52Z"},"message":"docs: bump eToro memory count 21,500 → 26,500 + social card (#329)\n\n## What\n\nFollow-up to #326. Updates the eToro production memory count from\n`21,500+` to the current `26,500+` across all surfaces, and adds the\nmatching social-preview card.\n\n### Changes\n- **README hero proof block** — `21,500+` → `26,500+`\n- **README FAQ** (\"Who runs MemClaw in production?\") — `21,500+` →\n`26,500+`\n- **Added `static/images/memclaw-social-preview.png`** (1280×640) —\nregenerated with `26,500+` so the social card matches the README.\n\n### Note\nThis moves the public README ahead of the eToro blog post, which still\nsays `21,500+`. To keep surfaces consistent, the [blog\npost](https://memclaw.net/blog/etoro-company-brain/) should be updated\nto `26,500+` as well (separate, not in this repo).\n\nThe social-preview PNG still needs a manual upload via **Settings →\nGeneral → Social preview** (no CLI/API path for that).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"241fce47e5049486a948654122afd40a22dde5ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/241fce47e5049486a948654122afd40a22dde5ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ea0e52b3fe43e72a279f365f38cd81301f1a6fce","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKriMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVCUQAI/9++RgHU6S1BQL7o0KwktT\nWK6/8/Q7BYhrvUWEznYwMFSsz+CKmaXP1IpsJP6628ZdhXcBVBUj4e5lhc8bvcof\nK9TzdNQVSWlRQnsDiADSfWohOxRELZYu4EyrnrThuB99ODXyIZIIn6G4SZWC9NoO\n6h1snVTtaTIYKLacPJGzqXB4i/EHXHlDbm7V+qG0qpu59+dmAg+N4VwNPK9EHVlo\nrsPy8gvXuYHnUSDbUKn3FNZDxVlztQIQ1UfnzuD7RqiBqkGiOINQV+awmgR6Hbhh\nzete1xA81GdGOX6X4KsFY5WD1s6hDDQZ6gbHFsn2TpciW+eO4SSUDrSBDpGAXQq+\ntnFuV0cHlncJZDFiWdJj/cuYst7JIlcyMi38gNXh620yEWj0KFmpDqniUNKsHMvD\nGEABQfDDeG6THZ9LsEWNS+HTjY8AAOJsvQ++fa9AkdXEysFg77Tji+9BlxaAufnE\nXResZGST9OctL9esSpF+2r4+FdZVrZlFKtRmGfoMM3QnXZs34dNCxUP2g2u74tQJ\n91YarU2ur8vMjEeMs4+S/K2di+zf83Otz3dmG2GJjQHLUj6FGmWFSeJ1DS6w3y7K\nVIWuDS8ae9Cg8lGNojwiTFVwyF3M6vlBoIouBWMBKcYaYFTG4c0g8VtgOd94NvYY\nRSm/85Z6cjeUQnh99njK\n=weqT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 241fce47e5049486a948654122afd40a22dde5ec\nparent 352689d3f18c2d00b4444cca62d80d1b4b340109\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781184652 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781184652 +0300\n\ndocs: bump eToro memory count 21,500 → 26,500 + social card (#329)\n\n## What\n\nFollow-up to #326. Updates the eToro production memory count from\n`21,500+` to the current `26,500+` across all surfaces, and adds the\nmatching social-preview card.\n\n### Changes\n- **README hero proof block** — `21,500+` → `26,500+`\n- **README FAQ** (\"Who runs MemClaw in production?\") — `21,500+` →\n`26,500+`\n- **Added `static/images/memclaw-social-preview.png`** (1280×640) —\nregenerated with `26,500+` so the social card matches the README.\n\n### Note\nThis moves the public README ahead of the eToro blog post, which still\nsays `21,500+`. To keep surfaces consistent, the [blog\npost](https://memclaw.net/blog/etoro-company-brain/) should be updated\nto `26,500+` as well (separate, not in this repo).\n\nThe social-preview PNG still needs a manual upload via **Settings →\nGeneral → Social preview** (no CLI/API path for that).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T13:30:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ea0e52b3fe43e72a279f365f38cd81301f1a6fce","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ea0e52b3fe43e72a279f365f38cd81301f1a6fce","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ea0e52b3fe43e72a279f365f38cd81301f1a6fce/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"352689d3f18c2d00b4444cca62d80d1b4b340109","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/352689d3f18c2d00b4444cca62d80d1b4b340109","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/352689d3f18c2d00b4444cca62d80d1b4b340109"}]},{"sha":"352689d3f18c2d00b4444cca62d80d1b4b340109","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDM1MjY4OWQzZjE4YzJkMDBiNDQ0NGNjYTYyZDgwZDFiNGIzNDAxMDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T13:14:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T13:14:42Z"},"message":"fix(logging): reroute idempotency guard mis-keys on captured handlers (#328)\n\n## Why\n\n`_route_third_party_to_root`'s already-rerouted check required the\nsnapshot's handler list to be non-empty, so a logger rerouted from\n`propagate=False, no-handlers` (snapshot `([], False, lvl)`) was never\nconsidered done — a re-call (e.g. ASGI lifespan startup after uvicorn\ninitialised) fell through to the uninitialised early-exit branch and\nemitted a spurious **'rerouting was a no-op' WARNING** in Cloud Logging.\n\n## What\n\n- Key the idempotency guard on snapshot presence alone — the snapshot is\nonly stored when rerouting actually ran, so `name in dict` is the\ncomplete signal.\n- Fix the module comment claiming the uninitialised case 'logs a debug\nline' (it logs a WARNING).\n- Regression test for the handler-less reroute + re-call path — verified\nto fail pre-fix and pass post-fix.\n\nFound by review on caura-memclaw-enterprise#423 (the enterprise vendor\nof this file); the enterprise copy will be re-vendored from this.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest tests/test_logging.py` → 21 passed.\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean.\n- DCO signed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"82cac53271c0ca10ba8aff0368c608ce28226c6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/82cac53271c0ca10ba8aff0368c608ce28226c6e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/352689d3f18c2d00b4444cca62d80d1b4b340109","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKrTCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAosUQAHzxvVTHXsAkqsqG7u5izUl9\nqL6dAxyEI1A9+AZC2Lhh1oI4pGihfbVpa5bHY8R5jha/muUit6Z8jZRiRD/Z1Ti5\n+6bG53ETrzLYpCKF7eNjlsqzx1qvCP4ZlqMav6MDN8bO6QpwmM3HT7u4xGOBo7Rh\n5sr6bDOWf3PVWqDxtksGuNSPHvTdaOy/7aJqhL34sGFvjSWNTVa9MHfXJY48O0Ri\nMO4SDaoKDtuvGhd/l07532kHNwVAB1UUZAIg7j8EaOfaJsMxKSys+F+pZIEmrHK4\nkeVA2AqVVqqyZXKcxVUYRI1/R8XwdYTqkMUXh2tTxfNZVJFBEpROdmv9/XJ4HTAr\nfh1e49r/CBIGtJGJnJfCIZ3OXAnAb6hKyp83WS3C1AWcQsjJUzaosphAQGW539O/\nXTW8LyN1TbB/JthOIOuUYLNF4H6G7GUiidsfBEPgrH9MBlvjToi7gaKOtJ6pE0J5\ngRfGOi/ZxqhyeUV0l4ptRDHrqyuhoG3TwJXwWp6FwZSNfvqR5DHplPCAsZw3MJ8h\n+OTcXi/RvcMstpHAPWLEMcubp3Wz4VJxftmKOoZA4NrfJ4PuzAODSlciNz/AMJ8u\nDNbo/3ZYgjVYxVZD4f9JKLbTiOx21zcKq/OCpXAM3S37/fP2axwGWyWYaT698B25\nFKZt2ucJ6xzIgJFMXTok\n=JSt3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 82cac53271c0ca10ba8aff0368c608ce28226c6e\nparent 4744732196c05fb1fd207f53f5bd03a849472f7d\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781183682 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781183682 +0300\n\nfix(logging): reroute idempotency guard mis-keys on captured handlers (#328)\n\n## Why\n\n`_route_third_party_to_root`'s already-rerouted check required the\nsnapshot's handler list to be non-empty, so a logger rerouted from\n`propagate=False, no-handlers` (snapshot `([], False, lvl)`) was never\nconsidered done — a re-call (e.g. ASGI lifespan startup after uvicorn\ninitialised) fell through to the uninitialised early-exit branch and\nemitted a spurious **'rerouting was a no-op' WARNING** in Cloud Logging.\n\n## What\n\n- Key the idempotency guard on snapshot presence alone — the snapshot is\nonly stored when rerouting actually ran, so `name in dict` is the\ncomplete signal.\n- Fix the module comment claiming the uninitialised case 'logs a debug\nline' (it logs a WARNING).\n- Regression test for the handler-less reroute + re-call path — verified\nto fail pre-fix and pass post-fix.\n\nFound by review on caura-memclaw-enterprise#423 (the enterprise vendor\nof this file); the enterprise copy will be re-vendored from this.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest tests/test_logging.py` → 21 passed.\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean.\n- DCO signed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T13:14:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/352689d3f18c2d00b4444cca62d80d1b4b340109","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/352689d3f18c2d00b4444cca62d80d1b4b340109","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/352689d3f18c2d00b4444cca62d80d1b4b340109/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4744732196c05fb1fd207f53f5bd03a849472f7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4744732196c05fb1fd207f53f5bd03a849472f7d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4744732196c05fb1fd207f53f5bd03a849472f7d"}]},{"sha":"4744732196c05fb1fd207f53f5bd03a849472f7d","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQ3NDQ3MzIxOTZjMDVmYjFmZDIwN2Y1M2Y1YmQwM2E4NDk0NzJmN2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-11T13:10:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T13:10:35Z"},"message":"fix(search): skip entity hop-boost when classifier declined the entity match as over-broad (#327)\n\n## Problem\n\nS1 retrieval@10 collapses at corpus scale even after #304: **22/25 @\nK=1000 → 11/25 @ K=10000** (10,000 entity-attribute facts, 50-query\nreplay).\n\nPer-failure anatomy (`Comet #0002's launch_date`, gold present in DB\namong 272 `Comet #NNNN launch_date` siblings / 813 distinct Comet\nentities):\n\n- The CAURA-698 decline fires identically at both corpus sizes (86 and\n815 entity-FTS matches > `ENTITY_LOOKUP_MAX_MATCHES=20`; the entity FTS\nis OR-over-tokens, so `comet` alone matches every sibling). Both route\nto `semantic_search` — the decline does not explain the collapse.\n- On pure hybrid scoring the gold ranks **#1**: vec_sim 0.9084 vs 0.8651\nfor the best sibling, and it is the only row matching the FTS query (its\ntsvector contains `0002`).\n- What buries it: `ParallelEmbedAndEntityBoost` re-runs the same\ntokenizer + entity FTS **with no knowledge of the classifier's\ndecline**, re-derives the same over-broad match, and hands\n`GRAPH_HOP_BOOST[0]=1.3` to the first `GRAPH_MAX_BOOSTED_MEMORIES=50`\nmemory links it encounters. With hundreds of entities tied at hop 0,\nlink order is arbitrary — the boost is a fixed-50 lottery over the\nsibling pool. P(gold boosted) ≈ 50/N_siblings: ~57% at K=1000 (gold\nboosted → rank 1, verified live), ~6% at K=10000 (gold unboosted at\n~0.66 buried under ~50 boosted siblings at 0.78–0.85).\n\nOne step concludes the entity match is too broad to mean anything and\ndiscards it; the next step recomputes the identical match and acts on\nit.\n\n## Fix\n\nThread the verdict through the pipeline context:\n\n- `ClassifyQuery` sets `ctx.data[\"entity_match_declined\"] = True` when\nthe CAURA-698 decline fires.\n- `ParallelEmbedAndEntityBoost` skips its entity-boost leg on that flag\n(embedding — the critical path — is unaffected; without the flag,\nbehavior is unchanged).\n\n## Measurements (S1 replay, local stack, retrieval@10)\n\n| configuration | K=1000 | K=10000 |\n|---|---|---|\n| main (#304) | 22/25 | 11/25 |\n| this fix | 22/25 (no regression) | 16/25 |\n| this fix, `search.recall_boost=false` pinned (deterministic replay) |\n22/25 | **18/25** |\n\nThe recall_boost pin removes reused-tenant contamination: `TrackRecalls`\nincrements `recall_count` on returned rows, so earlier replays had fed\nrecall_boost to the wrong siblings they returned. Remaining K=10000\nmisses are pre-existing classes (person-hub expansion, true semantic\nnear-duplicate dilution) tracked as A30 — the exact-first cascade.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/test_skip_entity_boost_on_decline.py` — 4 new unit tests\npinning both halves of the flag plus the no-flag default (boost still\nruns).\n- Adjacent `tests/test_d7_parallel_embed_per_task_timeout.py` (7 tests)\nstill green — the None-task guards preserve the D7 split-budget\ncontract.\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format` / `mypy` clean on touched files.\n\nRegression bench used for the numbers:\n`caura-bench-memcomp/scripts/s1_regression_bench.py` (replay-only\nagainst seeded k1k/k10k tenants, committed baselines).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"fbabb3bfbf93b17f38f34fd8a91c0a9722890ea1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/fbabb3bfbf93b17f38f34fd8a91c0a9722890ea1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/4744732196c05fb1fd207f53f5bd03a849472f7d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKrPLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqOEQAC//dZSWBg5btZLqndSlbs2x\nmfa1Og+hoiGOiliJP0f5Z//8K+Bs65RE5xRtfVj8CHGRYu8iZLwR+q4rMOKTTJgl\nHevK8OGDsrVZHPUy7XSGY8Fh9hXxb7E9HC6vxWyJ6M7Eok8Q67GUQOcIvZgQC3ew\nOpF46nLmC+CAhhbbEOdkCozV8wA/xKZrKSZCAiHt9djSXJWIFwTT0877AYX3qA1J\nn3A+2NaKMXUtb4u9tCIJNg8tOO20ZrSkN8GsqeHz6f1jnl7kYqDun/KOSTzKXdzS\njg2NYVSRAvKoX4OhUW59S+ZCndyPA3FGFsKRa7sIHHFyuzesNs26t4KGtplTMna0\nhlmIN3bO+hqrawlSIXgAhX4g2eF9omyf3iY2JsCLws5Rivl4nMwSYKbElEuq1ckv\nkW1xk0SljPcT9TngBMjLcoNPPVhGHDlw6ikwZw3jZvnSYILCe7F4/zNGRab/PsMc\nU0eO8rUk74JaDlhmxfVAK/iIFxKjC3ZuzAzxGaVhR5mpoe4WQThJsfrZo3PdEgRy\n/2gCbsPo9pXfuT73gUeEHdCq7cG04gMQCcShkvqUxsfatSNJADFMlKOOG/wwQtYG\nV2WgRIa1R9wyhG5Tss96ZBsGrw5szEmggJNAm9Ss4JZice4ruw6jFBdXuTQ+2suy\n4FyMU0CjE94wI/QzsF+R\n=0ro2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fbabb3bfbf93b17f38f34fd8a91c0a9722890ea1\nparent f1616070b72efbfba712de4095f6f556669368cc\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1781183435 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781183435 +0300\n\nfix(search): skip entity hop-boost when classifier declined the entity match as over-broad (#327)\n\n## Problem\n\nS1 retrieval@10 collapses at corpus scale even after #304: **22/25 @\nK=1000 → 11/25 @ K=10000** (10,000 entity-attribute facts, 50-query\nreplay).\n\nPer-failure anatomy (`Comet #0002's launch_date`, gold present in DB\namong 272 `Comet #NNNN launch_date` siblings / 813 distinct Comet\nentities):\n\n- The CAURA-698 decline fires identically at both corpus sizes (86 and\n815 entity-FTS matches > `ENTITY_LOOKUP_MAX_MATCHES=20`; the entity FTS\nis OR-over-tokens, so `comet` alone matches every sibling). Both route\nto `semantic_search` — the decline does not explain the collapse.\n- On pure hybrid scoring the gold ranks **#1**: vec_sim 0.9084 vs 0.8651\nfor the best sibling, and it is the only row matching the FTS query (its\ntsvector contains `0002`).\n- What buries it: `ParallelEmbedAndEntityBoost` re-runs the same\ntokenizer + entity FTS **with no knowledge of the classifier's\ndecline**, re-derives the same over-broad match, and hands\n`GRAPH_HOP_BOOST[0]=1.3` to the first `GRAPH_MAX_BOOSTED_MEMORIES=50`\nmemory links it encounters. With hundreds of entities tied at hop 0,\nlink order is arbitrary — the boost is a fixed-50 lottery over the\nsibling pool. P(gold boosted) ≈ 50/N_siblings: ~57% at K=1000 (gold\nboosted → rank 1, verified live), ~6% at K=10000 (gold unboosted at\n~0.66 buried under ~50 boosted siblings at 0.78–0.85).\n\nOne step concludes the entity match is too broad to mean anything and\ndiscards it; the next step recomputes the identical match and acts on\nit.\n\n## Fix\n\nThread the verdict through the pipeline context:\n\n- `ClassifyQuery` sets `ctx.data[\"entity_match_declined\"] = True` when\nthe CAURA-698 decline fires.\n- `ParallelEmbedAndEntityBoost` skips its entity-boost leg on that flag\n(embedding — the critical path — is unaffected; without the flag,\nbehavior is unchanged).\n\n## Measurements (S1 replay, local stack, retrieval@10)\n\n| configuration | K=1000 | K=10000 |\n|---|---|---|\n| main (#304) | 22/25 | 11/25 |\n| this fix | 22/25 (no regression) | 16/25 |\n| this fix, `search.recall_boost=false` pinned (deterministic replay) |\n22/25 | **18/25** |\n\nThe recall_boost pin removes reused-tenant contamination: `TrackRecalls`\nincrements `recall_count` on returned rows, so earlier replays had fed\nrecall_boost to the wrong siblings they returned. Remaining K=10000\nmisses are pre-existing classes (person-hub expansion, true semantic\nnear-duplicate dilution) tracked as A30 — the exact-first cascade.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/test_skip_entity_boost_on_decline.py` — 4 new unit tests\npinning both halves of the flag plus the no-flag default (boost still\nruns).\n- Adjacent `tests/test_d7_parallel_embed_per_task_timeout.py` (7 tests)\nstill green — the None-task guards preserve the D7 split-budget\ncontract.\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format` / `mypy` clean on touched files.\n\nRegression bench used for the numbers:\n`caura-bench-memcomp/scripts/s1_regression_bench.py` (replay-only\nagainst seeded k1k/k10k tenants, committed baselines).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T13:10:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4744732196c05fb1fd207f53f5bd03a849472f7d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4744732196c05fb1fd207f53f5bd03a849472f7d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4744732196c05fb1fd207f53f5bd03a849472f7d/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f1616070b72efbfba712de4095f6f556669368cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f1616070b72efbfba712de4095f6f556669368cc","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f1616070b72efbfba712de4095f6f556669368cc"}]},{"sha":"f1616070b72efbfba712de4095f6f556669368cc","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGYxNjE2MDcwYjcyZWZiZmJhNzEyZGU0MDk1ZjZmNTU2NjY5MzY4Y2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T12:57:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T12:57:52Z"},"message":"fix: cross-tenant search widening, non-default LLM structured-output kwargs, event deploy safety (#322)\n\n## Summary\nFour findings.\n\n- **search** — `ExecuteScoredSearch` forwarded `readable_tenant_ids`\nonly when `len(readable) > 1`, while the entity-lookup short-circuit\nuses `readable != [tenant_id]`. A cross-tenant credential whose readable\nset is exactly one foreign tenant was silently narrowed to home-tenant\nreads on the scored-search path — same request, different visibility\ndepending on whether the query matched an entity token. Both paths now\nuse the explicit comparison.\n- **llm** — Gemini / Vertex / Fake `complete_json` rejected the\nstructured-output kwargs (`seed`, `response_schema`) with `TypeError`.\nThe fallback retry loop swallowed it, so entity extraction silently\ndegraded to the regex fallback for every non-OpenAI deployment. The\nkwargs are now accepted-and-ignored and the provider protocol documents\nthat contract.\n- **events** — lifecycle payloads used `extra=\"forbid\"`; an additive\npublisher field would fail validation and silently drop every\narchive/purge/forge request during a rolling deploy. Now\n`extra=\"ignore\"`, matching the other consumer schemas.\n- **events** — the lifecycle consumer built payloads via kwargs-splat; a\nmalformed (non-dict) payload raised `TypeError`, escaped `except\nValidationError`, and nacked into redeliver-forever. Now\n`model_validate`.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_audit_s6_c1_events.py` (8 cases) covering all four.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7d7882fa7d99f38217d82520415e47f6f12a9171","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/7d7882fa7d99f38217d82520415e47f6f12a9171"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/f1616070b72efbfba712de4095f6f556669368cc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKrDQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcb8QAD+g8eyu0rG+0B5X/SPptYo3\nZ+5MlZdNMd1tIcu83SRKInMPkcOGw4LH0YO31f1m8Zqg1XZP5qvgKG5vF1QN1rt0\n1aKTvTKrOAm6UITtXWqkpYg/IXo74bkaW880lkfcVUExdEv2OrtnT7Hz3vxodRZv\ney0KveIymIKmtrIRXu2v/qbus3CacwYmybB6dcPCbDZUGmdAwO5VA/otJBRWn3TG\nYJ+K6dz1KQ0qVBG0RDc1TwIurDJ+A6YJiFCwgdNlLC87laXGJewbDlw15OQUQeSs\nWif+PNWxSs1GWb7EZy00vaeN6DfpuS546CtGlAdsotbG4szLrl4Nr5DAxC1ovRz6\nWpkHV7UVWVQzWYSl8nK+i1Iu/2g0aiHK89zizskqALeszgtU3CLLLiBUnUy6CAOg\nF9eSVplMZB4tuLoUd7q2PvRBwcznLQdoAHvyABMv12VNnAwuEXOe88eznYF9IVRm\ndwkaFRztVh49x7VmclBl+DVt2By/s4nmZ9d5Grzu6o61ppEzroSEIvhr5vKDwgHi\nFsQ/jFYpoviD6JQAG1PL1OnsROWLuA6bkOajbjaeSjoIaVH38k8chISEtXaedTJO\nW6Tkpdj5XCa/VG0vY2/GWBIMrkOaqq3kntZpIGbbZa+98PjMekgT0bJATHOtzT7+\n5F5ak1LuPdZ5qipzj2ef\n=CsCU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7d7882fa7d99f38217d82520415e47f6f12a9171\nparent e355f87fba54ca45b634bf2affd4b9893a0e3528\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1781182672 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781182672 +0300\n\nfix: cross-tenant search widening, non-default LLM structured-output kwargs, event deploy safety (#322)\n\n## Summary\nFour findings.\n\n- **search** — `ExecuteScoredSearch` forwarded `readable_tenant_ids`\nonly when `len(readable) > 1`, while the entity-lookup short-circuit\nuses `readable != [tenant_id]`. A cross-tenant credential whose readable\nset is exactly one foreign tenant was silently narrowed to home-tenant\nreads on the scored-search path — same request, different visibility\ndepending on whether the query matched an entity token. Both paths now\nuse the explicit comparison.\n- **llm** — Gemini / Vertex / Fake `complete_json` rejected the\nstructured-output kwargs (`seed`, `response_schema`) with `TypeError`.\nThe fallback retry loop swallowed it, so entity extraction silently\ndegraded to the regex fallback for every non-OpenAI deployment. The\nkwargs are now accepted-and-ignored and the provider protocol documents\nthat contract.\n- **events** — lifecycle payloads used `extra=\"forbid\"`; an additive\npublisher field would fail validation and silently drop every\narchive/purge/forge request during a rolling deploy. Now\n`extra=\"ignore\"`, matching the other consumer schemas.\n- **events** — the lifecycle consumer built payloads via kwargs-splat; a\nmalformed (non-dict) payload raised `TypeError`, escaped `except\nValidationError`, and nacked into redeliver-forever. Now\n`model_validate`.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_audit_s6_c1_events.py` (8 cases) covering all four.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T12:57:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f1616070b72efbfba712de4095f6f556669368cc","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f1616070b72efbfba712de4095f6f556669368cc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f1616070b72efbfba712de4095f6f556669368cc/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e355f87fba54ca45b634bf2affd4b9893a0e3528","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e355f87fba54ca45b634bf2affd4b9893a0e3528","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e355f87fba54ca45b634bf2affd4b9893a0e3528"}]},{"sha":"e355f87fba54ca45b634bf2affd4b9893a0e3528","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGUzNTVmODdmYmE1NGNhNDViNjM0YmYyYWZmZDRiOTg5M2EwZTM1Mjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T12:54:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T12:54:10Z"},"message":"fix(entities): scope-filter relations in get_entity and drop the per-memory agent lookup (#321)\n\n## Summary\n`get_entity` filtered an entity's linked memories through the\nfleet/scope contract but emitted `relations` straight from the raw\nentity — an agent credential could enumerate relation edges and\n`evidence_memory_id`s pointing at memories it cannot read (scope\nside-door).\n\n## Changes\n- A relation is now visible iff its evidence memory is readable by the\ncaller: evidence already in the authorized linked set passes, unknown\nevidence is resolved in **one** `bulk_get_memories` round-trip, and\nmissing/cross-tenant evidence hides the edge. No-evidence relations and\ntenant/user credentials are unchanged.\n- The scope filter resolved the caller's agent row once per linked\nmemory (identical lookups, N+1). The agent row is now fetched once and\nauthorization runs through a pure predicate\n(`memory_access_allowed_for_agent`) shared with\n`authorize_memory_access`.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_entity_relations_scope.py` — relation filtering for agent vs\ntenant credentials, and a single-lookup assertion (5 memories + 5\nrelations ⇒ exactly 1 agent lookup).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5596b55f01c84e73a80b1e108801c2528ac87148","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/5596b55f01c84e73a80b1e108801c2528ac87148"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/e355f87fba54ca45b634bf2affd4b9893a0e3528","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKq/yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMw4QAKyv27FJGfq72kOzrc5z+j0C\ng9H+7b7At+0AygRgQFrysm7WWX6Pu/7Sy7lM64d/IAIQ988YbgN5jyFq9seOylr1\nSbFEHDm5dsE7lpGiAnAPnmExD8QLL79DB4SkHWVCHAIaj9rX9VEw2Nd0X7hyS+NO\nodJFhtIKe3mx5yVc6EkeqEeEXgeN9GM4cPcfQHgIcy7D94G5E8YwvzKnViD4/S4f\niXCqGBMvWOxwANL1RpW5RXDpu3OEuF5DIPWjr/MLLYN+6gRg1F4anPjGh7NSL3ep\nIxx3V4ETsfUCZVetBg0iCLOiD/fmf117PlZUXYwJZdrknLFMQhe9q1spzjnS0U0k\n3lBzzdQxSM4ZVBnrJayFKu81kKvbfCJxn8y44q8spTh1LFhvRRr22jnBBt79ZFsv\nazhKV9rdsfThFZv4KjrAF8ad1JjeOJccNAeF67WOv+HvTiGXntLALLpl50arUhuI\nhCx9HmUsmk0jmQq4ia+D27yyVI3z60w33osTIAU4OC+u5FYilXelHOfY9toDT/Io\nj7TkKX0ipDCabvBWAA++Vggk6mGEGaHNXG3WNFCgqnYGLDuOrfIrQXmyyeZSgA+K\nlU70GG25qfEQw/jeavHbM/Tr8YHIvn1GVrmgSO/WrkdJxl/H7396cKYJk7slGt82\nI9N6HY/cGBtQWKSWS8Xw\n=qz0e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5596b55f01c84e73a80b1e108801c2528ac87148\nparent fcf96c74c28022415d1f691d3507c96ba8c99b22\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1781182450 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781182450 +0300\n\nfix(entities): scope-filter relations in get_entity and drop the per-memory agent lookup (#321)\n\n## Summary\n`get_entity` filtered an entity's linked memories through the\nfleet/scope contract but emitted `relations` straight from the raw\nentity — an agent credential could enumerate relation edges and\n`evidence_memory_id`s pointing at memories it cannot read (scope\nside-door).\n\n## Changes\n- A relation is now visible iff its evidence memory is readable by the\ncaller: evidence already in the authorized linked set passes, unknown\nevidence is resolved in **one** `bulk_get_memories` round-trip, and\nmissing/cross-tenant evidence hides the edge. No-evidence relations and\ntenant/user credentials are unchanged.\n- The scope filter resolved the caller's agent row once per linked\nmemory (identical lookups, N+1). The agent row is now fetched once and\nauthorization runs through a pure predicate\n(`memory_access_allowed_for_agent`) shared with\n`authorize_memory_access`.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_entity_relations_scope.py` — relation filtering for agent vs\ntenant credentials, and a single-lookup assertion (5 memories + 5\nrelations ⇒ exactly 1 agent lookup).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T12:54:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e355f87fba54ca45b634bf2affd4b9893a0e3528","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e355f87fba54ca45b634bf2affd4b9893a0e3528","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e355f87fba54ca45b634bf2affd4b9893a0e3528/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fcf96c74c28022415d1f691d3507c96ba8c99b22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fcf96c74c28022415d1f691d3507c96ba8c99b22","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fcf96c74c28022415d1f691d3507c96ba8c99b22"}]},{"sha":"fcf96c74c28022415d1f691d3507c96ba8c99b22","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGZjZjk2Yzc0YzI4MDIyNDE1ZDFmNjkxZDM1MDdjOTZiYThjOTliMjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T12:50:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T12:50:28Z"},"message":"fix(api): close cross-tenant and caller-asserted-identity authz gaps (#320)\n\n## Summary\nFour route-level authorization gaps.\n\n- **fleet `command_result`** — the storage UPDATE keyed only on\n`command_id`, so any authenticated tenant could mark another tenant's\nfleet command `done`/`failed` (and inject a `result`) by UUID. The\nUPDATE is now tenant-scoped (admin stays unscoped) and the route 404s\nwhen no row matches. The storage route also now actually persists\n`done`/`failed` status + result + `completed_at`, which the caller has\nalways sent but the old handler silently dropped for every status except\n`acked`.\n- **memories `redistribute`** — the `trust_level >= 3` gate ran against\nthe caller-controlled `agent_id` query param instead of the\nauthenticated identity, so a trust-1 agent credential could clear it by\nnaming a trust-3 agent. The authenticated agent identity now takes\nprecedence (same pattern as `delete`/`update_memory`).\n- **STM `clear_notes` / `clear_bulletin` / `promote`** — added\n`enforce_read_only` (all three), `enforce_usage_limits` (promote), and\nagent-identity binding so an agent credential can't wipe a peer's notes\nor promote into LTM on the peer's behalf.\n- **`delete_memory` audit row** — now attributes the effective identity\ninstead of the raw query param, which logged `None` for gateway agents.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_route_authz_gaps.py` (11 cases) covering cross-tenant 404,\nsame-tenant persistence, the redistribute precedence matrix, STM\nread-only/peer-agent rejection, and delete audit attribution.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8abf87ce371c032cd3c9594748da802f595f4e34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/8abf87ce371c032cd3c9594748da802f595f4e34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/fcf96c74c28022415d1f691d3507c96ba8c99b22","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKq8UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxycQAElOn9Z3gnwFi7bhya9ryFoj\nAo/rInZ1O/DZ6O0ex7sMQf7pmFDRuwc1DJfA3YtN3usQ7CETnORVpuJmIsnpSAU1\n+b9R8H5QnvYBSMqyeceFb12gRrMbePqB2nyOp4c4YpEazCbIkQPa2My3FRJ6OsIi\njCWfAWBxKKekbM3eGoZm/y1bjrRSNdMapas1Nih3qSM7+2Z4eMhtnmHLJxHKyKe3\n/b+zfb+hFcdWmJo8QXBBl/27RcXN/zxqZ//j+QN99eGbZKnIqggvoKkKv4PPqf7K\nkyqpd3O2zywhFv/mSASlhTvm/2nk+bgx9k2rG1yP5Do1AEoT2roletPs7GZpxbLr\nEauH7z75GjZNEc3PD/4CTo+9aLtooSnZKsRZOB81jdxXXpyVAQidtsuQO7aiWF4f\nA5AfWfeez27/verj/f1Gaf0itGa95P50xQQAgwbiaVHbHGOHyobWL1xBjUMgALO9\nxInwQRBJ1MhidEu+Jh9P5EUlX0EK1wyjps3f3EBruf4VsG2LvcQjrQSw+pRQbFka\nRbxhNOc9hxWfxhdYbVk8OsTgvuOURfPQPdbcP7vSsPm7G4fOCef1+vKTnJ4zOR28\nvaebmHOBbZVUgaNBT4XPspwdhnDgPc/JGMlD9boDkbTeKYqNbbGRENYK8/IsRl56\noUNULAPm7NDlSlPj7Wan\n=lzfn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8abf87ce371c032cd3c9594748da802f595f4e34\nparent 109d837950550a577f4fcb8e585e76105b961d9b\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1781182228 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781182228 +0300\n\nfix(api): close cross-tenant and caller-asserted-identity authz gaps (#320)\n\n## Summary\nFour route-level authorization gaps.\n\n- **fleet `command_result`** — the storage UPDATE keyed only on\n`command_id`, so any authenticated tenant could mark another tenant's\nfleet command `done`/`failed` (and inject a `result`) by UUID. The\nUPDATE is now tenant-scoped (admin stays unscoped) and the route 404s\nwhen no row matches. The storage route also now actually persists\n`done`/`failed` status + result + `completed_at`, which the caller has\nalways sent but the old handler silently dropped for every status except\n`acked`.\n- **memories `redistribute`** — the `trust_level >= 3` gate ran against\nthe caller-controlled `agent_id` query param instead of the\nauthenticated identity, so a trust-1 agent credential could clear it by\nnaming a trust-3 agent. The authenticated agent identity now takes\nprecedence (same pattern as `delete`/`update_memory`).\n- **STM `clear_notes` / `clear_bulletin` / `promote`** — added\n`enforce_read_only` (all three), `enforce_usage_limits` (promote), and\nagent-identity binding so an agent credential can't wipe a peer's notes\nor promote into LTM on the peer's behalf.\n- **`delete_memory` audit row** — now attributes the effective identity\ninstead of the raw query param, which logged `None` for gateway agents.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_route_authz_gaps.py` (11 cases) covering cross-tenant 404,\nsame-tenant persistence, the redistribute precedence matrix, STM\nread-only/peer-agent rejection, and delete audit attribution.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T12:50:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fcf96c74c28022415d1f691d3507c96ba8c99b22","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fcf96c74c28022415d1f691d3507c96ba8c99b22","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fcf96c74c28022415d1f691d3507c96ba8c99b22/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"109d837950550a577f4fcb8e585e76105b961d9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/109d837950550a577f4fcb8e585e76105b961d9b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/109d837950550a577f4fcb8e585e76105b961d9b"}]},{"sha":"109d837950550a577f4fcb8e585e76105b961d9b","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDEwOWQ4Mzc5NTA1NTBhNTc3ZjRmY2I4ZTU4NWU3NjEwNWI5NjFkOWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T12:47:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T12:47:07Z"},"message":"fix(mcp): enforce gateway perimeter on the /mcp header-trust path (#319)\n\n## Summary\nThe MCP ASGI middleware trusted the gateway identity headers\n(`X-Tenant-ID`, `X-Agent-ID`, `X-Readable-Tenant-IDs`, `X-Capabilities`)\nverbatim, while the REST auth stack refuses that header-trust path\nunless a matching `X-Gateway-Secret` is presented. A caller reaching\ncore-api's `/mcp` directly could set `X-Tenant-ID` to any tenant and\nfully impersonate it.\n\n## Changes\n- Validate `X-Gateway-Secret` (`hmac.compare_digest`) before honoring\n`X-Tenant-ID`; reject with 401 on mismatch. No-op when the secret is\nunset (standalone / dev).\n- Honor the gateway identity headers only on the gateway-verified path,\nso direct callers can't self-assert an agent identity, cross-tenant read\nset, or capability set.\n- Prepend the home tenant to the readable set (parity with REST) so\nrecall/list/stats can't exclude the caller's own rows.\n- `memclaw_entity_get`: add the canonical error tail so storage errors\nsurface as `isError` envelopes instead of escaping unwrapped.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_mcp_gateway_secret.py` (7 cases) — covers\nsecret-missing/wrong/correct, secret-unset back-compat, home-tenant\nprepend, and gateway-only header trust. Verified live: spoofed tenant →\n401, correct secret → 200, REST parity intact.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a60fd802eac447675595af98b2f3ca004d5215cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a60fd802eac447675595af98b2f3ca004d5215cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/109d837950550a577f4fcb8e585e76105b961d9b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKq5LCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApakQAHbfLzs2UU6W9xpH/FfRIdU1\nm10SRkpFJc7Ijf1obvZEEEW6zOqnFI3dMIwPxXrjbFugESFeAkzsSJ7Qt/RDY+Ot\nlBHfMM+AC7oiSBrxmSxFFTqCGWEcZqW9v4d/eBsAjgaAWorA3Nw/J6Y5NfzpS+xH\ncmH56Nua9xGBIYPF796fmkM8s8coif57cMYZDkcjv+MNZhtRKAhktS8F4sCOJtjb\nRptYZsUjfA6V+AF+yydXgzr6w5aI2rMA9OY5ImoaL1P+EwKLaYQZZQ0F3QeLxBye\n9Xk3t6Yq37EErNRNjB2XOigk0vRDOupYLWzW+Onx4NICbnmYlH4GtoxwIDP9p/kR\nTss58aL3+B1GV/uV/NND5ek2cMvBvUeTFUCUu2FMB0jQbh2QdKiyYdPxihjq1cxa\njl6+sDBAA8/lOOaLBEiMYG3IXx2vj2ECprdOiI8Dl+R/js+oOr/Sf9g5yG+916H5\nQ+bOH4CyO1S7VDZWmxcVpWeCuI2XUuYZh20JUAE6Nq47fRL2sP8FsxzkNMyJkVg+\nL+Jvtglss3JcxIGSkoH8d72tHb+e6t6MWrjTIMfvCqJzrLZC2u3ENiCd5Ja1bcZ4\nU13BlUfXzJwgEKh3NPmGjXX2FShVRQNmDE+64i/vM79oyjYevtqDpAM1K+3QvwNm\nmZo6P0xy/iGyaHTxCbjG\n=FTNM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a60fd802eac447675595af98b2f3ca004d5215cd\nparent e6395b535f58fd92906138c83b45a5c40a67be89\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1781182027 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781182027 +0300\n\nfix(mcp): enforce gateway perimeter on the /mcp header-trust path (#319)\n\n## Summary\nThe MCP ASGI middleware trusted the gateway identity headers\n(`X-Tenant-ID`, `X-Agent-ID`, `X-Readable-Tenant-IDs`, `X-Capabilities`)\nverbatim, while the REST auth stack refuses that header-trust path\nunless a matching `X-Gateway-Secret` is presented. A caller reaching\ncore-api's `/mcp` directly could set `X-Tenant-ID` to any tenant and\nfully impersonate it.\n\n## Changes\n- Validate `X-Gateway-Secret` (`hmac.compare_digest`) before honoring\n`X-Tenant-ID`; reject with 401 on mismatch. No-op when the secret is\nunset (standalone / dev).\n- Honor the gateway identity headers only on the gateway-verified path,\nso direct callers can't self-assert an agent identity, cross-tenant read\nset, or capability set.\n- Prepend the home tenant to the readable set (parity with REST) so\nrecall/list/stats can't exclude the caller's own rows.\n- `memclaw_entity_get`: add the canonical error tail so storage errors\nsurface as `isError` envelopes instead of escaping unwrapped.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_mcp_gateway_secret.py` (7 cases) — covers\nsecret-missing/wrong/correct, secret-unset back-compat, home-tenant\nprepend, and gateway-only header trust. Verified live: spoofed tenant →\n401, correct secret → 200, REST parity intact.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T12:47:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/109d837950550a577f4fcb8e585e76105b961d9b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/109d837950550a577f4fcb8e585e76105b961d9b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/109d837950550a577f4fcb8e585e76105b961d9b/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e6395b535f58fd92906138c83b45a5c40a67be89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e6395b535f58fd92906138c83b45a5c40a67be89","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e6395b535f58fd92906138c83b45a5c40a67be89"}]},{"sha":"e6395b535f58fd92906138c83b45a5c40a67be89","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGU2Mzk1YjUzNWY1OGZkOTI5MDYxMzhjODNiNDVhNWM0MGE2N2JlODk","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T11:44:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T11:44:06Z"},"message":"docs: add eToro proof, comparison table, FAQ, and star ask to README (#326)\n\n## What\n\nREADME growth pass to give skeptical GitHub visitors production evidence\nand LLM-quotable comparative content. Implements the verified-gaps audit\n(GIF intentionally deferred — concept PNG retained).\n\n### Additions\n1. **eToro proof blockquote** (hero, above the concept image) — 300+\nagents, 21,500+ memories, 1,372 skills, 23 ms p50.\n2. **\"How MemClaw compares\"** capability/governance matrix vs Mem0 / Zep\n/ Letta (between Features and Performance).\n3. **FAQ** section (before License) — what is it, vs vector DB, vs\nMem0/Zep, MCP clients, cross-vendor, free?, who's in prod.\n4. **Star ask** after the Quick Start first-success step.\n\n### Verification notes (changes from the source report)\n- **Memories count corrected to `21,500+`** — the report's `26,500` did\nnot match the [eToro case\nstudy](https://memclaw.net/blog/etoro-company-brain/), which states\n21,500+. Aligned in both the hero block and FAQ.\n- **Dropped the \"Anthropic agent answered 90s after creation\" claim** —\nnot substantiated by the cited blog post. Removed from the hero block\nand softened the FAQ cross-vendor answer.\n- **Letta \"MCP-native\" set to ⚠️ (partial), not ❌** — Letta documents\nMCP support (consumes MCP tools), so absent was inaccurate.\n- Zep \"PII ✅\" left as-is (couldn't independently confirm; generous to\ncompetitor). Worth a maintainer double-check.\n\n### Deferred / not in this PR\n- Demo GIF (per request — staying with the PNG for now).\n- GitHub repo metadata (description, topics, social preview) — handled\nseparately, not via README.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e2a536cf28ccab13aa163f9442965362a507bf59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/e2a536cf28ccab13aa163f9442965362a507bf59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/e6395b535f58fd92906138c83b45a5c40a67be89","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKp+GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3FMQAEuZedRV4TmJvIqC11wBnubb\nNV6T083cbpG3UCnEo5DrjGXugQuCXmZ+If3Q287sCcC1U6zzUPr9PhHvbowfSHgP\nL9zog9gfvDebkyLXze83DnGLH39sc/Up6p3llDMqmBYh2q46qQ1HLOwmgz93cWDz\nXGXFcnTjP1GzGSLVkeeIt0ouEiwsM+f+rybZ7To5NspcZQe5y0ZyN2bxunnnSt7/\n1QKBscZgBB+iMGBNjN3G/ATdPO1Guxqzn0XK6+dm0KQmWXOF22t34i523mznxmmq\nueC0/R7h6FMKdYiosbirOuG0ZBrMq6w4HMJmdb5t4g3I2GCjf8tB+ODTzqefOFJB\nm2PiIWrkaAVOjA+OYCNXS3Sog0XQpouBHAlK4bMn5Unz9EgqUMnKUpFk0PC6jK38\nnbK2H+eBxQkMqw/KsG++G5RWJmv/h17hXhP7IjZ5GATMDdxkHlg3fcTV66PRfm9N\naIx3BH1a2h87RoFqdH88PIeYHGlxFjwNJXJt0BnQBDiDKk5dOXMzh7sgjZCdnAEW\nHvAeQPuDvAqn6J3j/TEKmuQEFHdY/NHCFS6kawtNjARlqfZ4eVxD2u36/+g+n+Lh\nHZKDzU7NxjFaBZCbisDwOJO9tiBvaEd82hCdBtCaITJ71TgZwCoXvqFo2ivgOXdy\nalOiooQ7T21/4bTuyfIb\n=ipMZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e2a536cf28ccab13aa163f9442965362a507bf59\nparent ec3fcaf45a7545568e9f713a6f1db631dfa1c2f3\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781178246 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781178246 +0300\n\ndocs: add eToro proof, comparison table, FAQ, and star ask to README (#326)\n\n## What\n\nREADME growth pass to give skeptical GitHub visitors production evidence\nand LLM-quotable comparative content. Implements the verified-gaps audit\n(GIF intentionally deferred — concept PNG retained).\n\n### Additions\n1. **eToro proof blockquote** (hero, above the concept image) — 300+\nagents, 21,500+ memories, 1,372 skills, 23 ms p50.\n2. **\"How MemClaw compares\"** capability/governance matrix vs Mem0 / Zep\n/ Letta (between Features and Performance).\n3. **FAQ** section (before License) — what is it, vs vector DB, vs\nMem0/Zep, MCP clients, cross-vendor, free?, who's in prod.\n4. **Star ask** after the Quick Start first-success step.\n\n### Verification notes (changes from the source report)\n- **Memories count corrected to `21,500+`** — the report's `26,500` did\nnot match the [eToro case\nstudy](https://memclaw.net/blog/etoro-company-brain/), which states\n21,500+. Aligned in both the hero block and FAQ.\n- **Dropped the \"Anthropic agent answered 90s after creation\" claim** —\nnot substantiated by the cited blog post. Removed from the hero block\nand softened the FAQ cross-vendor answer.\n- **Letta \"MCP-native\" set to ⚠️ (partial), not ❌** — Letta documents\nMCP support (consumes MCP tools), so absent was inaccurate.\n- Zep \"PII ✅\" left as-is (couldn't independently confirm; generous to\ncompetitor). Worth a maintainer double-check.\n\n### Deferred / not in this PR\n- Demo GIF (per request — staying with the PNG for now).\n- GitHub repo metadata (description, topics, social preview) — handled\nseparately, not via README.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T11:44:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e6395b535f58fd92906138c83b45a5c40a67be89","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e6395b535f58fd92906138c83b45a5c40a67be89","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e6395b535f58fd92906138c83b45a5c40a67be89/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ec3fcaf45a7545568e9f713a6f1db631dfa1c2f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ec3fcaf45a7545568e9f713a6f1db631dfa1c2f3","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ec3fcaf45a7545568e9f713a6f1db631dfa1c2f3"}]},{"sha":"ec3fcaf45a7545568e9f713a6f1db631dfa1c2f3","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGVjM2ZjYWY0NWE3NTQ1NTY4ZTlmNzEzYTZmMWRiNjMxZGZhMWMyZjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T11:22:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T11:22:19Z"},"message":"fix(plugin): point agents at the memclaw skill by name, not by filesystem path (CAURA-000) (#323)\n\n## Summary\n\nCron-run error on bridgeclaw (plugin 2.9.0):\n\n```\nchannel=cron sessionKey=agent:bridgeclaw:cron:... duration=171759ms outcome=error\nerror=\"search \"~/.openclaw/agents/bridgeclaw/agent/codex-home\"\n       -> search \"memclaw/SKILL.md$|memclaw\" (agent) failed\"\n```\n\n**Interpretation**: this is OpenClaw's built-in **`search` tool**\nfailing — not a memclaw tool. The agent was trying to *locate* our skill\nfile, driven by our own prompt/educate text: *\"the operating contract\nlives in `skills/memclaw/SKILL.md` — read it before your first call.\"*\n\nThat path-style pointer was correct when the plugin wrote `SKILL.md`\nper-workspace. But the skill is now shipped **once at plugin-root** and\n**manifest-discovered** via `openclaw.plugin.json:skills` — there is no\nper-workspace file. A cron agent (no human in the loop) took the path\nliterally, ran the `search` tool against its `codex-home` workspace,\nscanned for **2m51s**, found nothing, and failed the turn.\n\n## Fix\n\nThree emit sites carried the path-style pointer:\n- `prompt-section.ts` — per-turn system-prompt fragment\n- `educate.ts` `buildToolsMd()` — TOOLS.md (per-workspace bootstrap)\n- `educate.ts` `buildAgentsMd()` — AGENTS.md (per-workspace bootstrap)\n\nAll three reworded to:\n1. Reference the **memclaw** skill **by name** (not a path)\n2. State the runtime loads it automatically\n3. Explicitly instruct the agent **not to search the filesystem** for it\n\n**No runtime or behavior change — prompt wording only.**\n\nExample (AGENTS.md, after):\n> Before your first MemClaw call this session, open the **memclaw**\nskill — your runtime loads it automatically, so do NOT search the\nfilesystem for it — for signatures, cadences, quality, prohibitions,\nrecall policy, and sharing.\n\n## Tests\n\nThree existing assertions *locked in the bug* (they required the\n`skills/memclaw/SKILL.md` path string). Updated all three to instead\nrequire:\n- absence of the `skills/memclaw/SKILL.md` path string\n- the by-name `**memclaw** skill` reference\n- the `do NOT search the filesystem` guard\n\n(`educate.test.ts` ×2, `tool-definitions.test.ts` ×1. Whitespace\nnormalised before matching — the source template wraps phrases across\nlines.)\n\n- 310/310 plugin tests pass\n- manifest drift 11/11 pass\n- tsc clean\n\n## Wet test\n\nPure prompt-string change — there's no runtime code path to exercise on\nthe VM beyond what the unit tests already render (they assert the exact\nemitted strings). Skipped the VM round-trip deliberately.\n\n## Not in scope\n\n- `plugin/skills/memclaw/SKILL.md` has one internal self-reference to\n`<workspace>/skills/memclaw/SKILL.md` (line ~352). That's *inside* the\nskill — by the time it's read, the skill is already loaded, so it can't\ntrigger the search-storm. Left as-is to keep this change minimal.\n- Why OpenClaw's `search` tool *throws* (rather than returning empty) on\na no-match is OpenClaw-side behavior, not ours.\n\n## Version\n\nPlugin 2.9.0 → 2.9.1.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] 310/310 unit tests\n- [x] manifest drift 11/11\n- [x] rendered TOOLS.md / AGENTS.md / system-prompt fragment inspected —\npath string gone, by-name + no-search guard present\n- [ ] Customer: once 2.9.1 ships, cron agents stop emitting the `search\n... memclaw/SKILL.md ... failed` error\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9fc0aa74e0fa3364a215e4b87117c8afbed4b6ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9fc0aa74e0fa3364a215e4b87117c8afbed4b6ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ec3fcaf45a7545568e9f713a6f1db631dfa1c2f3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKpprCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGPgQAGLnA4rj5hL2UZ2bXsXItPld\nVcCTfHhJOKSNvvmnqitc2R6kVYOTwCT5sRSr6XcRNrkTxotzdJisnchXLPLX9l4A\nX7UHAnGt8vAHAgj6+t1zjbowTWAo1sdjxZRVTpDZGIb3CgJAG9Lm3EgSgO9dl1mA\n5H3Px4TQVUcOWh/NuZYgrIg2YDmCdnp98ojWvK7eMbWfLX9B2iEMzaOEV2nN0Vd/\nQsNS21Eqpx2NNxWbgFLm7B57dtuldIgAuL8WjxuYLoLsiMLs7DR8daShraCarQ7T\nHnliyODtsBaIiv9LC8xIeVbwZ3KsehMqZCEVZEbNOxUoVxZZ38XMkgKm4SDR7yD9\nkvP4lLCX1pWhfEYXbMY8duhUVn7/JNge49JSJ41LwRwR9MubtZSCR1ga1/enRBEZ\ngbbluc6RRLd0ec4QQjEXQPrk/8ak+iyp0zbNXoVFfvFeO+24GbsbeI4OJr+xFGrM\nAo0uISx4unqcXmRcyZMHRoJYkoV22NJy89VIqnJs3gBiq362Y70u5TE6x7LB0sbI\n7dkPm2VBKsgo/l9tD9VqfjrFqoeVH46pIHS10xb9UpvkFxcDG2dwPrZ0kCVFozaK\nB8BM3kMkiCn2sVExP/m+4f3RHyVlxybzeUM4i38gSpuvTWpUzjN/BKO7rJRd7vFm\nod/1ZySzhdFz20BtTHzd\n=cArk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9fc0aa74e0fa3364a215e4b87117c8afbed4b6ac\nparent 50488fc6eb07d244297ad1d3e065887c8cb3e47e\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781176939 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781176939 +0300\n\nfix(plugin): point agents at the memclaw skill by name, not by filesystem path (CAURA-000) (#323)\n\n## Summary\n\nCron-run error on bridgeclaw (plugin 2.9.0):\n\n```\nchannel=cron sessionKey=agent:bridgeclaw:cron:... duration=171759ms outcome=error\nerror=\"search \"~/.openclaw/agents/bridgeclaw/agent/codex-home\"\n       -> search \"memclaw/SKILL.md$|memclaw\" (agent) failed\"\n```\n\n**Interpretation**: this is OpenClaw's built-in **`search` tool**\nfailing — not a memclaw tool. The agent was trying to *locate* our skill\nfile, driven by our own prompt/educate text: *\"the operating contract\nlives in `skills/memclaw/SKILL.md` — read it before your first call.\"*\n\nThat path-style pointer was correct when the plugin wrote `SKILL.md`\nper-workspace. But the skill is now shipped **once at plugin-root** and\n**manifest-discovered** via `openclaw.plugin.json:skills` — there is no\nper-workspace file. A cron agent (no human in the loop) took the path\nliterally, ran the `search` tool against its `codex-home` workspace,\nscanned for **2m51s**, found nothing, and failed the turn.\n\n## Fix\n\nThree emit sites carried the path-style pointer:\n- `prompt-section.ts` — per-turn system-prompt fragment\n- `educate.ts` `buildToolsMd()` — TOOLS.md (per-workspace bootstrap)\n- `educate.ts` `buildAgentsMd()` — AGENTS.md (per-workspace bootstrap)\n\nAll three reworded to:\n1. Reference the **memclaw** skill **by name** (not a path)\n2. State the runtime loads it automatically\n3. Explicitly instruct the agent **not to search the filesystem** for it\n\n**No runtime or behavior change — prompt wording only.**\n\nExample (AGENTS.md, after):\n> Before your first MemClaw call this session, open the **memclaw**\nskill — your runtime loads it automatically, so do NOT search the\nfilesystem for it — for signatures, cadences, quality, prohibitions,\nrecall policy, and sharing.\n\n## Tests\n\nThree existing assertions *locked in the bug* (they required the\n`skills/memclaw/SKILL.md` path string). Updated all three to instead\nrequire:\n- absence of the `skills/memclaw/SKILL.md` path string\n- the by-name `**memclaw** skill` reference\n- the `do NOT search the filesystem` guard\n\n(`educate.test.ts` ×2, `tool-definitions.test.ts` ×1. Whitespace\nnormalised before matching — the source template wraps phrases across\nlines.)\n\n- 310/310 plugin tests pass\n- manifest drift 11/11 pass\n- tsc clean\n\n## Wet test\n\nPure prompt-string change — there's no runtime code path to exercise on\nthe VM beyond what the unit tests already render (they assert the exact\nemitted strings). Skipped the VM round-trip deliberately.\n\n## Not in scope\n\n- `plugin/skills/memclaw/SKILL.md` has one internal self-reference to\n`<workspace>/skills/memclaw/SKILL.md` (line ~352). That's *inside* the\nskill — by the time it's read, the skill is already loaded, so it can't\ntrigger the search-storm. Left as-is to keep this change minimal.\n- Why OpenClaw's `search` tool *throws* (rather than returning empty) on\na no-match is OpenClaw-side behavior, not ours.\n\n## Version\n\nPlugin 2.9.0 → 2.9.1.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] 310/310 unit tests\n- [x] manifest drift 11/11\n- [x] rendered TOOLS.md / AGENTS.md / system-prompt fragment inspected —\npath string gone, by-name + no-search guard present\n- [ ] Customer: once 2.9.1 ships, cron agents stop emitting the `search\n... memclaw/SKILL.md ... failed` error\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T11:22:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ec3fcaf45a7545568e9f713a6f1db631dfa1c2f3","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ec3fcaf45a7545568e9f713a6f1db631dfa1c2f3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ec3fcaf45a7545568e9f713a6f1db631dfa1c2f3/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"50488fc6eb07d244297ad1d3e065887c8cb3e47e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/50488fc6eb07d244297ad1d3e065887c8cb3e47e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/50488fc6eb07d244297ad1d3e065887c8cb3e47e"}]},{"sha":"50488fc6eb07d244297ad1d3e065887c8cb3e47e","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDUwNDg4ZmM2ZWIwN2QyNDQyOTdhZDFkM2UwNjU4ODdjOGNiM2U0N2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-11T07:47:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T07:47:03Z"},"message":"feat(skills): gate the OpenClaw install path to active-only skills (#317)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #315 closed the active-only leak on the MCP **pull** surface\n(`memclaw_doc`), but the **push** surface stayed open. The OpenClaw\nplugin reconciler (`plugin/src/reconcile-skills.ts`) mirrors the\n`skills` catalog to each node's disk via `POST /documents/query` with\n`where={}` — **all statuses**. For a Skill-Factory-opted-in tenant that\npushes `candidate` / `staged` / `quarantined` skills onto every node's\ndisk and into the agent's palette — exactly the leak #315 closed for\npull, still open on push.\n\nThis wires push and pull behind **one server-side gate**.\n\n## What's new\n\n**`POST /api/v1/skills/installable`**\n(`core-api/.../routes/documents.py`) — the agent-harness install\nsurface. Same active-only + opt-in gate as the MCP path, enforced\nserver-side:\n- opted-in tenant → only `status='active'` skills;\n- non-opted-in → every visible skill (`where={}`), byte-identical to the\nlegacy reconcile (a legacy skill predating Skill Factory may lack a\n`status` field; forcing `active` would wrongly drop it — so we don't\nfilter at all);\n- settings-lookup failure → **503, fail closed**, storage never queried.\n\nThe request model has **no `where`** — a caller can't widen the filter\nto pull non-active skills.\n\n**Reconciler switch-over** (`plugin/src/reconcile-skills.ts`) — pulls\nfrom `/skills/installable` instead of `/documents/query{where:{}}`. The\nclient carries zero policy: no status filter, no opt-in flag.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- **De-activation reactivity (free):** a skill flipping `active →\nrejected/quarantined` drops out of `installable`; the reconciler's\nexisting orphan-removal path deletes it from disk next tick. Push stays\nin sync with the gate.\n- **Fail-safe end-to-end:** server fails closed (503); reconciler fails\nsafe on a non-2xx (preserves on-disk skills, writes nothing) — an outage\ncan never push a non-active skill to disk.\n- **No blast radius:** `/documents/query` untouched (dashboards / inbox\nthat legitimately need non-active skills unaffected). Old plugins keep\nworking (ungated, as before — `/documents/query` still exists); new\nplugins are gated. The plugin sends no version-coupled change beyond the\nendpoint URL.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is the **first** of the OpenClaw-install PRs (the \"close the gate\ngap\" slice). Deliberately out of scope, for follow-ups:\ninstall/bootstrap hardening (`/install-plugin`, gateway restart, version\npinning) and operator-facing per-node reconcile observability.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/test_skills_installable_endpoint.py` — active-only when\nopted-in; `where={}` when not; 503 + storage-not-queried on settings\nerror; caller `where` ignored.\n- `plugin/src/reconcile-skills.test.ts` — endpoint switch-over;\nde-activation removes from disk next tick; server 503 → reconciler fails\nsafe.\n- 246 server tests across the documents/installable/mcp_doc/skill sweep;\n312 plugin tests. ruff + format clean; 0 mypy errors in the touched\nroute.\n\n## Docs\n\n`docs/mcp-skill-delivery.md` — documents the push path and the shared\ngate; OpenClaw promoted from \"future\" to the first per-harness install.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"745ad309a9e903f99c4cc9021ddfa7b40b2a8ebc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/745ad309a9e903f99c4cc9021ddfa7b40b2a8ebc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/50488fc6eb07d244297ad1d3e065887c8cb3e47e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKmf3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUAoQAIj+LXQB8fkFMXQnfa+3ooo3\ntzw88JYqWTXvdY/d2YwssnmnvNbr4d4OC/0tIujcdmvImBMqtog4T8TaZiOth67U\nZ1LOElvrprXVZ51Y8vCBsMtnetl8y1myH5DnormlWaC2YPnxIYmCN3CzpZZK3L6Q\nNMBMcGwZ+9K6PwIyqSp2e78K3Iqu3dhCe3XfLokjPho2NCQEhqa2QwwhDuIjr31O\ny6hag1WhkNx1nHL20FO+E7CA2PT52+ctSiYvWLFsyv6PzrHQHj/QFZvMa6AvEs52\nIagaCEy6/wsr0qCk4H24c7c/Eqh84MktsOuE4RgPYkx7qzrInw8VfXBK3GONo5vi\nUJHjqKywIb8uKFa76+7m22vATGi+qZYkex8lI1jLJ75lChqFExURg5Lc5ofLbufC\ndaWnvMrWypMAWmc8bgit23wusVTGF30xYPdb5BhMY5R7W637hmJ12tvnAwm0cEs9\nSFz4Ib6B4JB5OjQHfGO2173q/mEXxoGDVrvrBxRL1RloBDcxEgCtPqDzNvTo7GtI\nqVWzr5Y++9e+5vf0JmQ1Mr4CmWebIliT+zSnkoH6HHLq6ZpFaKaD2G/iGf1FkS+J\nl44jjMu/wPOZxuWZjG+VO+GqK5S5ZZmMyE7gG06P0hDrx+/cyoMX2z+OQ6fvlev8\n9ByHtUETZyNk2n8MWG/b\n=IE4t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 745ad309a9e903f99c4cc9021ddfa7b40b2a8ebc\nparent 42bd51372d6f2640d2110c6a06a464412a6c4d04\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781164023 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781164023 +0300\n\nfeat(skills): gate the OpenClaw install path to active-only skills (#317)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #315 closed the active-only leak on the MCP **pull** surface\n(`memclaw_doc`), but the **push** surface stayed open. The OpenClaw\nplugin reconciler (`plugin/src/reconcile-skills.ts`) mirrors the\n`skills` catalog to each node's disk via `POST /documents/query` with\n`where={}` — **all statuses**. For a Skill-Factory-opted-in tenant that\npushes `candidate` / `staged` / `quarantined` skills onto every node's\ndisk and into the agent's palette — exactly the leak #315 closed for\npull, still open on push.\n\nThis wires push and pull behind **one server-side gate**.\n\n## What's new\n\n**`POST /api/v1/skills/installable`**\n(`core-api/.../routes/documents.py`) — the agent-harness install\nsurface. Same active-only + opt-in gate as the MCP path, enforced\nserver-side:\n- opted-in tenant → only `status='active'` skills;\n- non-opted-in → every visible skill (`where={}`), byte-identical to the\nlegacy reconcile (a legacy skill predating Skill Factory may lack a\n`status` field; forcing `active` would wrongly drop it — so we don't\nfilter at all);\n- settings-lookup failure → **503, fail closed**, storage never queried.\n\nThe request model has **no `where`** — a caller can't widen the filter\nto pull non-active skills.\n\n**Reconciler switch-over** (`plugin/src/reconcile-skills.ts`) — pulls\nfrom `/skills/installable` instead of `/documents/query{where:{}}`. The\nclient carries zero policy: no status filter, no opt-in flag.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- **De-activation reactivity (free):** a skill flipping `active →\nrejected/quarantined` drops out of `installable`; the reconciler's\nexisting orphan-removal path deletes it from disk next tick. Push stays\nin sync with the gate.\n- **Fail-safe end-to-end:** server fails closed (503); reconciler fails\nsafe on a non-2xx (preserves on-disk skills, writes nothing) — an outage\ncan never push a non-active skill to disk.\n- **No blast radius:** `/documents/query` untouched (dashboards / inbox\nthat legitimately need non-active skills unaffected). Old plugins keep\nworking (ungated, as before — `/documents/query` still exists); new\nplugins are gated. The plugin sends no version-coupled change beyond the\nendpoint URL.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is the **first** of the OpenClaw-install PRs (the \"close the gate\ngap\" slice). Deliberately out of scope, for follow-ups:\ninstall/bootstrap hardening (`/install-plugin`, gateway restart, version\npinning) and operator-facing per-node reconcile observability.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/test_skills_installable_endpoint.py` — active-only when\nopted-in; `where={}` when not; 503 + storage-not-queried on settings\nerror; caller `where` ignored.\n- `plugin/src/reconcile-skills.test.ts` — endpoint switch-over;\nde-activation removes from disk next tick; server 503 → reconciler fails\nsafe.\n- 246 server tests across the documents/installable/mcp_doc/skill sweep;\n312 plugin tests. ruff + format clean; 0 mypy errors in the touched\nroute.\n\n## Docs\n\n`docs/mcp-skill-delivery.md` — documents the push path and the shared\ngate; OpenClaw promoted from \"future\" to the first per-harness install.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T07:47:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/50488fc6eb07d244297ad1d3e065887c8cb3e47e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/50488fc6eb07d244297ad1d3e065887c8cb3e47e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/50488fc6eb07d244297ad1d3e065887c8cb3e47e/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"42bd51372d6f2640d2110c6a06a464412a6c4d04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/42bd51372d6f2640d2110c6a06a464412a6c4d04","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/42bd51372d6f2640d2110c6a06a464412a6c4d04"}]},{"sha":"42bd51372d6f2640d2110c6a06a464412a6c4d04","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQyYmQ1MTM3MmQ2ZjI2NDBkMjExMGM2YTA2YTQ2NDQxMmE2YzRkMDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","email":"265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-10T18:35:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T18:35:08Z"},"message":"chore: release main (#312)\n\n:robot: I have created a release *beep* *boop*\n---\n\n\n<details><summary>backend: 2.14.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.14.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/backend-v2.13.0...backend-v2.14.0)\n(2026-06-10)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **skills:** auto-approve clean Forge candidates (skip HITL inbox)\n([#313](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/313))\n([6f3452d](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/6f3452d8197083a25cc34489a1c39c3adafebc81))\n* **skills:** MCP-direct delivery — agents discover only active skills\n([#315](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/315))\n([1ac4f1f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1ac4f1f14a0af7384ebed9a6df696641b8d60627))\n* **skills:** wire Forge into the lifecycle cron fanout\n([#311](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/311))\n([0523ed0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/0523ed0ab172942d7e25f9d54a29175ec2394ea1))\n\n\n### Documentation\n\n* replace concept SVG with rendered PNG diagram in README\n([#316](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/316))\n([f32ba1b](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/f32ba1bd675d1465d089fcd3b7e4862e9ae0f981))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"001abaa28e802c0cc3ed9926627489bc96f93dbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/001abaa28e802c0cc3ed9926627489bc