oped.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2bf7848dbbc4f4504fd5ba64664f346342771ff9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/2bf7848dbbc4f4504fd5ba64664f346342771ff9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/f654ddb9b2c8eb1956e8f9e73b75572ddf65f012","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJx5rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFdoQAFtlmMtHZIgZ43IP1/ZpGWEp\n9dv3itFhk8+DlRDZluJURf9E88HW5CWDx1fh/WrHM4S4980kLn6e1bHD+ljb923G\ngro76hH2vA3DXh/w3oc0R1m+zg8vzxtn1EsWaF+pTeetmc2/ooNGe6sE+zj1phDq\nGil9VMSJhwhHxmiW2duyNf0npbHcVC5ys2Nze8nBYR+9olNcPL6K1ppf9WCAZrq5\nLHvWT9hclHaW/SiiXb6lPRXlAn45pGtQ/76uKjpi/ltrxpnRW2NVPhnaqja+jMEJ\nll1ZGc2vZ74ZndbXjU7JI1+dbwnTSal7Z7yCA/GjvK0yu5k/5JVdA0baVh4gcdzG\nNJ/LGeKzzppCDgj3aVgvIFXFWD6wRZVN5NaihveUhzgZzo0Pd23bVKbLA/Yjq3Ab\n7Pp3MB/THJMlTEsJPKIM3zIpj6vUobrqFUBFcv+7/wTZwZBn1tC+kv8mrAgDYYUp\nuRw1v3an6HHJu7+wC/F8SX1pL0FfzeJAtZT12jmU1++YFMAU9jtp4u++h+WXtbVX\nQiHCArgr9V1D1pwNUuxokmqPWUiRE5nZZdwRzqTnQyImrRL9LbnT5GHYbg3xTK6P\nkl1fAyocAVvtB9DGwfge7xXtOb4VGIRyGU7z5ZRPafBqz5+xkLX43buhDB3qvLbX\n2ek0eJc2Ei7u1yiQpq3Y\n=qKhN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2bf7848dbbc4f4504fd5ba64664f346342771ff9\nparent 2aab828324ca054024ba075a2bbc682f749c6f8a\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780948587 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780948587 +0300\n\nfeat(skills): Skill Factory · Phases 0, 1, and 2 (partial — backend only) (#293)\n\n**Restores PR #284** which was accidentally closed when the source\nbranch was deleted during a Phase-2 push. The branch + commits are\nintact at `98b098b1`; the GitHub PR record could not be reopened because\nthe closed-PR head SHA (`e085bcc…`) drifted from this branch's actual\ntip.\n\n## Scope\n\nThree commits, all DCO-signed, **flag-gated** behind\n`org_settings.skills_factory.enabled` (default `False` — zero behavior\nchange for non-opted-in tenants):\n\n- `dc2f96e` **Phase 0** — schema (v1) + flag-gated validator + 5\nmigrations (020 forge_rejected_fingerprints, 021 session_traces, 022\nskills backfill) + Sentinel stub + org_settings.skills_factory.* (8\nkeys) + lifecycle publisher\n- `da7dd48` **Phase 1** — Forge dry-run pipeline: 6 outcome-inference\nsignals, session-trace builder, cluster fingerprint (P1-P6 stable),\ndistill prompt+parse, eval harness, memclawctl CLI\n- `98b098b` **docs** — Live Memory pitch deck (8 SVGs) + Skill Factory\nimplementation plan + spec\n\n## Validation\n\n- 339/339 unit tests pass\n- ruff check + format clean on `core-api/src/` + `core-storage-api/src/`\n- DCO sign-off on all 3 commits\n- Migration 022 was dry-run THREE times against eToro production\n(read-only `BEGIN…ROLLBACK`); v2 (json/jsonb cast round-trip) is the one\npersisted here\n\n## Phase 2\n\nPhase 2 backend (HITL Inbox + Sentinel real checks) lands as a separate\nPR ([#285] when opened) branched off this branch's tip — keeps reviews\nscoped.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T19:56:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f654ddb9b2c8eb1956e8f9e73b75572ddf65f012","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f654ddb9b2c8eb1956e8f9e73b75572ddf65f012","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f654ddb9b2c8eb1956e8f9e73b75572ddf65f012/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2aab828324ca054024ba075a2bbc682f749c6f8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2aab828324ca054024ba075a2bbc682f749c6f8a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2aab828324ca054024ba075a2bbc682f749c6f8a"}]},{"sha":"2aab828324ca054024ba075a2bbc682f749c6f8a","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDJhYWI4MjgzMjRjYTA1NDAyNGJhMDc1YTJiYmM2ODJmNzQ5YzZmOGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-08T15:35:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T15:35:17Z"},"message":"fix(plugin): don't create plugins.allow from nothing on autoFix (CAURA-000) (#307)\n\n## Summary\n\nCustomer-reported: installing memclaw 2.8.1 on a fresh OpenClaw gateway\ncaused the `openai/gpt-5.5` agent model to become unknown ~2 minutes\nafter install (`FailoverError: Unknown model: openai/gpt-5.5`). The\ngateway log told the story directly: `http server listening (1 plugin:\nmemclaw; 0.8s)` — OpenClaw loaded ONLY memclaw, blocking every other\nplugin including the bundled `openai` provider.\n\n**The customer's suspicion was correct: our plugin was to blame.**\n\n## Root cause\n\n`autoFixAllowlist` step 1 in `config.ts`:\n```typescript\nif (!isMemclawAllowed(config)) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(config.plugins.allow)) config.plugins.allow = [];\n  config.plugins.allow.push(\"memclaw\");\n}\n```\n\nOn a fresh `openclaw.json` with no `plugins.allow` field, this\n**created** `plugins.allow = [\"memclaw\"]`. Verified against OpenClaw\n2026.6.1's plugin gate (read from\n`/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/*.js`):\n\n```js\nentry?.enabled === true &&\n  (plugins.allow.length === 0 || plugins.allow.includes(pluginId))\n```\n\n**A non-empty `plugins.allow` is a STRICT allowlist.** Empty or missing\n= no restriction. By materialising `[\"memclaw\"]` from nothing, we\nflipped a permissive config into a restrictive one and locked out every\nother plugin.\n\nConfirmation from the OpenClaw error strings in the same dist files:\n- `\"plugins.allow does not include browser. Add \\\"browser\\\" to\nplugins.allow or remove the restrictive plugin allowlist.\"`\n- `\"Add ${formatPluginList(ownerPluginIds)} to plugins.allow or remove\nplugins.allow.\"`\n\n## Fix\n\nTwo minimal changes in `plugin/src/config.ts`:\n\n1. **`isMemclawAllowed`**: missing or empty `plugins.allow` now returns\n`true` (matches OpenClaw's runtime semantics — memclaw can load anyway).\nOnly returns `false` when allow is a non-empty array that excludes\nmemclaw.\n\n2. **`autoFixAllowlist` step 1**: only appends memclaw to an EXISTING,\nnon-empty allowlist. Never materialises one from nothing.\n\nThe post-fix invariant:\n- User had no `plugins.allow` → autoFix leaves it missing (permissive —\nmemclaw + openai + others all load)\n- User had `plugins.allow = []` → autoFix leaves it empty (permissive)\n- User had `plugins.allow = [\"browser\", \"filesystem\"]` → autoFix adds\nmemclaw → `[\"browser\", \"filesystem\", \"memclaw\"]`\n- User had `plugins.allow = [\"browser\", \"memclaw\"]` → no-op\n\n## Validation\n\n### Unit tests\n- 310/310 pass plugin-side (was 301, +9 new):\n  - 5 `isMemclawAllowed` tests pinning all 4 input shapes\n- 4 `autoFixAllowlist` tests driving the real function against temp\n`openclaw.json` files (verifies no-creation, empty-preserved,\nappended-to-restrictive, no-duplicate)\n- 1 existing `isMemclawFullyConfigured` test updated: pre-fix it used\n`plugins.allow = []` to mean \"not allowlisted\", which assumed empty =\nrestrictive; now uses an explicit non-empty allowlist that excludes\nmemclaw (the only real \"not allowed\" case under corrected semantics).\n\n### Wet test on `openclaw-test-ran` (GCE, OpenClaw 2026.6.1, plugin\n2.8.6)\n\n8/8 scenarios PASS:\n\n```\n✓ A. fresh install (no plugins.allow) — autoFix must NOT create restrictive allowlist\n     plugins.allow after autoFix = undefined\n✓ B. plugins.allow = [] (empty) — autoFix must leave it empty\n✓ C. restrictive allow (without memclaw) — autoFix adds memclaw + preserves rest\n     [\"browser\",\"filesystem\",\"memclaw\"]\n✓ D. existing allow already with memclaw — no duplicate added\n✓ E1. isMemclawAllowed: missing allow → true (permissive)\n✓ E2. isMemclawAllowed: empty allow → true (permissive)\n✓ E3. isMemclawAllowed: non-empty allow with memclaw → true\n✓ E4. isMemclawAllowed: non-empty allow without memclaw → false\n```\n\nScenario A is the **direct regression test for the customer bug**:\npre-fix the same input produced `plugins.allow = [\"memclaw\"]` (the\nrestrictive trap); post-fix it stays `undefined`.\n\n## Customer recovery\n\nOnce 2.8.6 ships, the customer should:\n1. Pull plugin 2.8.6 on the affected gateway (via the existing deploy\nmachinery — note that PR #305 and #306 in this same batch fix the\ndeploy-loop pathology, so the upgrade itself is no longer fragile)\n2. Manually clear the bad `plugins.allow` in their `openclaw.json` (or\nremove the key entirely). Future installs/upgrades won't re-introduce\nthe problem.\n\n## Version\n\nPlugin 2.8.5 → 2.8.6. No backend change.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] 310/310 unit tests pass\n- [x] Wet test on OpenClaw 2026.6.1 — 8/8 scenarios pass, including the\ndirect customer-bug regression check\n- [x] tsc clean (via `npm test` prefix)\n- [x] DCO sign-off\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3900239091268aeb11195f67dc984a706b20b342","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/3900239091268aeb11195f67dc984a706b20b342"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/2aab828324ca054024ba075a2bbc682f749c6f8a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJuE1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbBoQAAT2pl64L3EHL788ClJV/Z9A\nxbF/d2x07Z16zyV+O2SEKNSstjrEZMnFTfTCkdJQruCexNjhUgacwfrg2hgXVAfw\nrtGh4qNzOMepShrWSypvdYaAvmLUXSgbfReSlMzrIxcIi5Iygwu9RcwiO55OsEPV\nzmboe/DEia8GcVR9RyXVOyO6T57dKZWOlsd6Ibf9yzog0PdLGRDZ/u8begnKlTfF\nYqe51fMpf/4+7SxPO9A4xzTtecxBCK5bdlrPqM2XQiSsjPRzYAd8KWjkgbqI0BaT\n+ehPJz9v90YyzQOe9FUOJGFDB5Af1ixZ3TWlS6pVk0/OPis7/OhBV0IZ0I4b7UZO\nvvqAbfT6fzrdWn1S2A+djVIPiFTWd6UhPNAcbZ6aNNjuVxC+zXXf3kBhCyo6GUnP\nUlpwQxDslPYuOPJFkSQofKNkurWM4e9rWvgDwsQKgxAVSvwiVFDcFrovF3473c2s\nLMqRAKIaCBV8wacuPfQ145v8bBGhiQCAGNt7AZr34TGJ14lEr9dWNUGQjdof3ood\nZguwSjAatTGSJGMCw/yPPCpRob1TM10ar6/CXQ8iitIrdqOCTjhcyZdJm6PZbhLn\nStZOM9fq+QkyELT8r3UXH49Dn1MYjJA2C+MFjDwvcA5wIelF/fBBRestsskO+rxC\naqOiItJhjf68Kq+gavil\n=tndp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3900239091268aeb11195f67dc984a706b20b342\nparent a94d0ab0664c4a1f36c28713b929e8489a5103cc\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780932917 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780932917 +0300\n\nfix(plugin): don't create plugins.allow from nothing on autoFix (CAURA-000) (#307)\n\n## Summary\n\nCustomer-reported: installing memclaw 2.8.1 on a fresh OpenClaw gateway\ncaused the `openai/gpt-5.5` agent model to become unknown ~2 minutes\nafter install (`FailoverError: Unknown model: openai/gpt-5.5`). The\ngateway log told the story directly: `http server listening (1 plugin:\nmemclaw; 0.8s)` — OpenClaw loaded ONLY memclaw, blocking every other\nplugin including the bundled `openai` provider.\n\n**The customer's suspicion was correct: our plugin was to blame.**\n\n## Root cause\n\n`autoFixAllowlist` step 1 in `config.ts`:\n```typescript\nif (!isMemclawAllowed(config)) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(config.plugins.allow)) config.plugins.allow = [];\n  config.plugins.allow.push(\"memclaw\");\n}\n```\n\nOn a fresh `openclaw.json` with no `plugins.allow` field, this\n**created** `plugins.allow = [\"memclaw\"]`. Verified against OpenClaw\n2026.6.1's plugin gate (read from\n`/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/*.js`):\n\n```js\nentry?.enabled === true &&\n  (plugins.allow.length === 0 || plugins.allow.includes(pluginId))\n```\n\n**A non-empty `plugins.allow` is a STRICT allowlist.** Empty or missing\n= no restriction. By materialising `[\"memclaw\"]` from nothing, we\nflipped a permissive config into a restrictive one and locked out every\nother plugin.\n\nConfirmation from the OpenClaw error strings in the same dist files:\n- `\"plugins.allow does not include browser. Add \\\"browser\\\" to\nplugins.allow or remove the restrictive plugin allowlist.\"`\n- `\"Add ${formatPluginList(ownerPluginIds)} to plugins.allow or remove\nplugins.allow.\"`\n\n## Fix\n\nTwo minimal changes in `plugin/src/config.ts`:\n\n1. **`isMemclawAllowed`**: missing or empty `plugins.allow` now returns\n`true` (matches OpenClaw's runtime semantics — memclaw can load anyway).\nOnly returns `false` when allow is a non-empty array that excludes\nmemclaw.\n\n2. **`autoFixAllowlist` step 1**: only appends memclaw to an EXISTING,\nnon-empty allowlist. Never materialises one from nothing.\n\nThe post-fix invariant:\n- User had no `plugins.allow` → autoFix leaves it missing (permissive —\nmemclaw + openai + others all load)\n- User had `plugins.allow = []` → autoFix leaves it empty (permissive)\n- User had `plugins.allow = [\"browser\", \"filesystem\"]` → autoFix adds\nmemclaw → `[\"browser\", \"filesystem\", \"memclaw\"]`\n- User had `plugins.allow = [\"browser\", \"memclaw\"]` → no-op\n\n## Validation\n\n### Unit tests\n- 310/310 pass plugin-side (was 301, +9 new):\n  - 5 `isMemclawAllowed` tests pinning all 4 input shapes\n- 4 `autoFixAllowlist` tests driving the real function against temp\n`openclaw.json` files (verifies no-creation, empty-preserved,\nappended-to-restrictive, no-duplicate)\n- 1 existing `isMemclawFullyConfigured` test updated: pre-fix it used\n`plugins.allow = []` to mean \"not allowlisted\", which assumed empty =\nrestrictive; now uses an explicit non-empty allowlist that excludes\nmemclaw (the only real \"not allowed\" case under corrected semantics).\n\n### Wet test on `openclaw-test-ran` (GCE, OpenClaw 2026.6.1, plugin\n2.8.6)\n\n8/8 scenarios PASS:\n\n```\n✓ A. fresh install (no plugins.allow) — autoFix must NOT create restrictive allowlist\n     plugins.allow after autoFix = undefined\n✓ B. plugins.allow = [] (empty) — autoFix must leave it empty\n✓ C. restrictive allow (without memclaw) — autoFix adds memclaw + preserves rest\n     [\"browser\",\"filesystem\",\"memclaw\"]\n✓ D. existing allow already with memclaw — no duplicate added\n✓ E1. isMemclawAllowed: missing allow → true (permissive)\n✓ E2. isMemclawAllowed: empty allow → true (permissive)\n✓ E3. isMemclawAllowed: non-empty allow with memclaw → true\n✓ E4. isMemclawAllowed: non-empty allow without memclaw → false\n```\n\nScenario A is the **direct regression test for the customer bug**:\npre-fix the same input produced `plugins.allow = [\"memclaw\"]` (the\nrestrictive trap); post-fix it stays `undefined`.\n\n## Customer recovery\n\nOnce 2.8.6 ships, the customer should:\n1. Pull plugin 2.8.6 on the affected gateway (via the existing deploy\nmachinery — note that PR #305 and #306 in this same batch fix the\ndeploy-loop pathology, so the upgrade itself is no longer fragile)\n2. Manually clear the bad `plugins.allow` in their `openclaw.json` (or\nremove the key entirely). Future installs/upgrades won't re-introduce\nthe problem.\n\n## Version\n\nPlugin 2.8.5 → 2.8.6. No backend change.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] 310/310 unit tests pass\n- [x] Wet test on OpenClaw 2026.6.1 — 8/8 scenarios pass, including the\ndirect customer-bug regression check\n- [x] tsc clean (via `npm test` prefix)\n- [x] DCO sign-off\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T15:35:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2aab828324ca054024ba075a2bbc682f749c6f8a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2aab828324ca054024ba075a2bbc682f749c6f8a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2aab828324ca054024ba075a2bbc682f749c6f8a/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a94d0ab0664c4a1f36c28713b929e8489a5103cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a94d0ab0664c4a1f36c28713b929e8489a5103cc","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a94d0ab0664c4a1f36c28713b929e8489a5103cc"}]},{"sha":"a94d0ab0664c4a1f36c28713b929e8489a5103cc","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGE5NGQwYWIwNjY0YzRhMWYzNmMyODcxM2I5MjllODQ4OWE1MTAzY2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-08T14:20:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T14:20:27Z"},"message":"fix(fleet): bound deploy-queue runaway when a previous deploy is acked (CAURA-000) (#305)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe auto-upgrade gate in `_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade` was blind to\n`acked`-but-not-completed deploy commands. Every heartbeat queued\nanother duplicate, the plugin processed it, restarted via `systemctl`\n(sending SIGTERM to itself), and the cycle repeated every 60 seconds —\nexactly matching the customer-reported \"SIGTERM every 60 seconds\" on the\naffected gateway.\n\nThis PR adds a second gate that consults the repository for any\nin-flight deploy (`status IN (pending, acked)`, `created_at` within a\n10-minute window) and short-circuits if one is found.\n\n## Customer ground truth (read-only ssh)\n\nPostgres on `134.98.155.239`, `2026-06-08`:\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| Deploy commands stuck at `status='acked'` | **1,381** |\n| Stuck-acked on a single node (`cb457f2c-…`) | **1,223** |\n| Timestamps between consecutive stuck commands | 60s |\n| All target_version | `\"2.8.1\"` |\n\n\"Removing memclaw plugin solved it\" because the plugin's\n`setInterval(sendHeartbeat, 60_000)` is what pulled the\nperpetually-fresh deploy command and triggered the restart cycle. No\nplugin → no heartbeat → no pull → no restart.\n\n## Mechanism (full trace in commit message)\n\n1. Heartbeat handler fetches `pending` commands → empty (previous deploy\nwas `acked`)\n2. Gate `_has_recent_deploy_command_from_list` sees no deploy in pending\n→ allows queue\n3. New deploy queued (`status=pending`) → re-fetched → `ack_commands`\ntransitions to `acked` → sent to plugin\n4. Plugin's `processCommand(\"deploy\")` schedules `systemctl restart` in\n2s\n5. The plugin POSTs the result, but if the POST takes >2s the restart's\nSIGTERM kills it mid-flight\n6. Command stays at `acked` forever\n7. 60s later, repeat from step 1\n\n## Fix (smallest blast radius — backend only)\n\n| | File | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `core-api/.../repositories/fleet_repository.py` | New\n`has_recent_in_flight_deploy` method — direct SQLAlchemy query |\n| 2 | `core-api/.../routes/fleet.py` | Import `fleet_repo`, define\n`DEPLOY_IN_FLIGHT_WINDOW = 10 min`, add a second gate check inside\n`_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade` AFTER the cheaper pending-list check, falls\nopen on repo exception |\n\nThe cheaper pending-list check still fires first (no DB roundtrip on the\nhappy path with a fresh pending deploy already in the list). The new DB\ncheck only runs when the auto-upgrade is otherwise eligible. The\n10-minute window means a genuinely-abandoned deploy auto-recovers\nwithout operator intervention.\n\n## What this PR explicitly does NOT do\n\n- **No plugin change.** The plugin's `setTimeout(systemctl restart,\n2000)` race with the result POST is a real bug that should be fixed in a\nfollow-up PR. But the backend gate makes the customer's loop bounded\nregardless of plugin version.\n- **No DB cleanup.** The 1,381 existing stuck-acked rows on the\ncustomer's prod will be naturally bypassed by the new gate (they're\noutside any future 10-min window). Optional follow-up: `UPDATE\nfleet_commands SET status='failed' WHERE status='acked' AND created_at <\nnow() - interval '1 hour'` if the customer wants the queue trimmed.\n- **No constant changes.** `MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION`, retry\nsemantics, ack timing — all unchanged.\n\n## Wet test (against real customer prod data)\n\nRead-only SQL simulation on `memclaw-postgres-1` (no writes; queries\nonly):\n\n```\ntotal_queued_deploys | would_have_been_blocked_by_new_gate | pct_blocked\n---------------------+-------------------------------------+-------------\n                1223 |                                1218 |       99.6\n```\n\nThe 5 unblocked are the **first** commands in the cycle (gate has\nnothing to see yet — first attempt must pass). After that the gate would\nhave suppressed every follow-up for 10 minutes. Result: 60s → 10min cap\non the SIGTERM cadence, AND zero runaway once a deploy completes\nsuccessfully.\n\n## Tests\n\n5 new in `tests/test_fleet_heartbeat_auto_upgrade.py`:\n- `test_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade_skips_when_acked_deploy_in_flight` —\nheadline behavior\n- `test_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade_queues_when_no_in_flight` — happy path\nunchanged\n- `test_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade_fails_open_on_repo_error` — DB hiccup\nsafety\n- `test_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade_skips_pending_before_querying_repo` —\ngate ordering (cheaper check first)\n- `test_deploy_in_flight_window_is_sensible` — pins the constant value\nrange\n\n| Test scope | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `test_fleet_heartbeat_auto_upgrade.py` (full file) | **51/51 pass**\n(was 46, +5) |\n| Broader `pytest -k \"fleet or heartbeat\" -m unit` | 24/24 pass, 0\nregressions |\n| `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` | clean |\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests: 51/51 pass in the auto-upgrade file\n- [x] Broader fleet/heartbeat sweep: 24/24 pass\n- [x] Wet test against customer prod data (read-only SQL): 1,218/1,223\n(99.6%) of past stuck commands would have been blocked\n- [ ] Customer redeploy: expect `[memclaw] command deploy reported` log\nlines to drop to ≤1 per 10 min on previously-stuck nodes;\n`[fleet.heartbeat] skipping auto-upgrade for node=...` INFO lines start\nappearing\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fee71fe19c9aa4cd6922e7d51da780258255a595","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/fee71fe19c9aa4cd6922e7d51da780258255a595"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/a94d0ab0664c4a1f36c28713b929e8489a5103cc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJs+rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFtkQAB/+bnQ8bE6hyIAB8synGLZw\n9bLxDwnj22wOIDeb3U9zfxV2C232NyY+khotXbj9MYpbSJcJUuZ5sRYVOJnBuKd7\nsP0rS9sfnErWk6TmwsbdBG14KmCWQoa9Kr2RMchp/w5M9tQvIjFFLDflnlcdooBa\nZYMN7p/olUBhFAG5M5A+cZ5LN+O784z6QDcnhzmH2MI+/Gs+rbdbwpcB6zJ/f3ex\nu/kFO3lskKXoizDjSKnwpT6T/YHFEmNor8Lvld+1qMxqAM8DXDgGLHJg3kMgk+GK\nE4W6zlJKddhEYEOTF5N+R2NuHgmxsGxZIgJ5zblPI5WuJF3C31NYG7SqEkwm9hf5\n2CxmGmvopn98wswupAqFf36ZbCHT9yL6644THJG8VARQkSBtSTMtFOXvhHNbFTva\nNz5zNHSst/ZtxMf/6v/xx6YsUytRlSYoz26ZteG9+gu2MmSe2igM2aCoJ3jDbeXu\nqcLW09EQIxTyxw7rvcUsqs0Pu3AUNfb4bZTPiqsEal4bzxuwfvym+rEOmcg+4wC4\n53ojtIakOMC5SbK+Lt1i4sBcL0ogss3aOFp9HGwuFgiANRyaVDGomwKfPPqOh2Ib\n0wLMzZyU0U9xzR2IxRgG0pLu0lGM8poua+LWF1PrYd1SQzCGEHlg/X93Y5RX5Av1\nWWLZeuRYa4Y+KhPQ/G45\n=GsFm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fee71fe19c9aa4cd6922e7d51da780258255a595\nparent fe8ad26df789c60f65d38ea64b2fff5a3f82f210\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780928427 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780928427 +0300\n\nfix(fleet): bound deploy-queue runaway when a previous deploy is acked (CAURA-000) (#305)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe auto-upgrade gate in `_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade` was blind to\n`acked`-but-not-completed deploy commands. Every heartbeat queued\nanother duplicate, the plugin processed it, restarted via `systemctl`\n(sending SIGTERM to itself), and the cycle repeated every 60 seconds —\nexactly matching the customer-reported \"SIGTERM every 60 seconds\" on the\naffected gateway.\n\nThis PR adds a second gate that consults the repository for any\nin-flight deploy (`status IN (pending, acked)`, `created_at` within a\n10-minute window) and short-circuits if one is found.\n\n## Customer ground truth (read-only ssh)\n\nPostgres on `134.98.155.239`, `2026-06-08`:\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| Deploy commands stuck at `status='acked'` | **1,381** |\n| Stuck-acked on a single node (`cb457f2c-…`) | **1,223** |\n| Timestamps between consecutive stuck commands | 60s |\n| All target_version | `\"2.8.1\"` |\n\n\"Removing memclaw plugin solved it\" because the plugin's\n`setInterval(sendHeartbeat, 60_000)` is what pulled the\nperpetually-fresh deploy command and triggered the restart cycle. No\nplugin → no heartbeat → no pull → no restart.\n\n## Mechanism (full trace in commit message)\n\n1. Heartbeat handler fetches `pending` commands → empty (previous deploy\nwas `acked`)\n2. Gate `_has_recent_deploy_command_from_list` sees no deploy in pending\n→ allows queue\n3. New deploy queued (`status=pending`) → re-fetched → `ack_commands`\ntransitions to `acked` → sent to plugin\n4. Plugin's `processCommand(\"deploy\")` schedules `systemctl restart` in\n2s\n5. The plugin POSTs the result, but if the POST takes >2s the restart's\nSIGTERM kills it mid-flight\n6. Command stays at `acked` forever\n7. 60s later, repeat from step 1\n\n## Fix (smallest blast radius — backend only)\n\n| | File | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `core-api/.../repositories/fleet_repository.py` | New\n`has_recent_in_flight_deploy` method — direct SQLAlchemy query |\n| 2 | `core-api/.../routes/fleet.py` | Import `fleet_repo`, define\n`DEPLOY_IN_FLIGHT_WINDOW = 10 min`, add a second gate check inside\n`_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade` AFTER the cheaper pending-list check, falls\nopen on repo exception |\n\nThe cheaper pending-list check still fires first (no DB roundtrip on the\nhappy path with a fresh pending deploy already in the list). The new DB\ncheck only runs when the auto-upgrade is otherwise eligible. The\n10-minute window means a genuinely-abandoned deploy auto-recovers\nwithout operator intervention.\n\n## What this PR explicitly does NOT do\n\n- **No plugin change.** The plugin's `setTimeout(systemctl restart,\n2000)` race with the result POST is a real bug that should be fixed in a\nfollow-up PR. But the backend gate makes the customer's loop bounded\nregardless of plugin version.\n- **No DB cleanup.** The 1,381 existing stuck-acked rows on the\ncustomer's prod will be naturally bypassed by the new gate (they're\noutside any future 10-min window). Optional follow-up: `UPDATE\nfleet_commands SET status='failed' WHERE status='acked' AND created_at <\nnow() - interval '1 hour'` if the customer wants the queue trimmed.\n- **No constant changes.** `MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION`, retry\nsemantics, ack timing — all unchanged.\n\n## Wet test (against real customer prod data)\n\nRead-only SQL simulation on `memclaw-postgres-1` (no writes; queries\nonly):\n\n```\ntotal_queued_deploys | would_have_been_blocked_by_new_gate | pct_blocked\n---------------------+-------------------------------------+-------------\n                1223 |                                1218 |       99.6\n```\n\nThe 5 unblocked are the **first** commands in the cycle (gate has\nnothing to see yet — first attempt must pass). After that the gate would\nhave suppressed every follow-up for 10 minutes. Result: 60s → 10min cap\non the SIGTERM cadence, AND zero runaway once a deploy completes\nsuccessfully.\n\n## Tests\n\n5 new in `tests/test_fleet_heartbeat_auto_upgrade.py`:\n- `test_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade_skips_when_acked_deploy_in_flight` —\nheadline behavior\n- `test_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade_queues_when_no_in_flight` — happy path\nunchanged\n- `test_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade_fails_open_on_repo_error` — DB hiccup\nsafety\n- `test_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade_skips_pending_before_querying_repo` —\ngate ordering (cheaper check first)\n- `test_deploy_in_flight_window_is_sensible` — pins the constant value\nrange\n\n| Test scope | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `test_fleet_heartbeat_auto_upgrade.py` (full file) | **51/51 pass**\n(was 46, +5) |\n| Broader `pytest -k \"fleet or heartbeat\" -m unit` | 24/24 pass, 0\nregressions |\n| `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` | clean |\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests: 51/51 pass in the auto-upgrade file\n- [x] Broader fleet/heartbeat sweep: 24/24 pass\n- [x] Wet test against customer prod data (read-only SQL): 1,218/1,223\n(99.6%) of past stuck commands would have been blocked\n- [ ] Customer redeploy: expect `[memclaw] command deploy reported` log\nlines to drop to ≤1 per 10 min on previously-stuck nodes;\n`[fleet.heartbeat] skipping auto-upgrade for node=...` INFO lines start\nappearing\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T14:20:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a94d0ab0664c4a1f36c28713b929e8489a5103cc","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a94d0ab0664c4a1f36c28713b929e8489a5103cc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a94d0ab0664c4a1f36c28713b929e8489a5103cc/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fe8ad26df789c60f65d38ea64b2fff5a3f82f210","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fe8ad26df789c60f65d38ea64b2fff5a3f82f210","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fe8ad26df789c60f65d38ea64b2fff5a3f82f210"}]},{"sha":"fe8ad26df789c60f65d38ea64b2fff5a3f82f210","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGZlOGFkMjZkZjc4OWM2MGY2NWQzOGVhNjRiMmZmZjVhM2Y4MmYyMTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-08T14:14:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T14:14:33Z"},"message":"fix(plugin): schedule restart AFTER result POST resolves (CAURA-000) (#306)\n\n## Summary\n\n`processCommand` was scheduling `setTimeout(systemctl --user restart,\n2000)` INSIDE the deploy/restart success branches, BEFORE awaiting the\nresult POST. If the POST took longer than ~2s (slow network, retried\nconnection, queued behind other heartbeat traffic), the systemctl\nSIGTERM killed it mid-flight and the backend never saw `status=\"done\"` —\nthe command stayed at `status=\"acked\"` forever.\n\nCombined with the backend's pending-only auto-upgrade gate (fixed\nseparately in #305 by adding an in-flight-deploy check), this race\nproduced the customer's observed \"SIGTERM every 60 seconds\" on one\ngateway. This PR removes the race at the source so new deploys don't\naccumulate in the first place; #305 handles cleanup/safety on\nalready-stuck-acked commands. Both together close the loop.\n\n## Mechanism\n\nBefore:\n```\ndeploy/restart branch:\n  setTimeout(systemctl restart, 2000)    ← T=0: scheduled\n  ...\n  // fall through to end of processCommand\n  await POST result                       ← T=X: depends on POST latency\n                                          ← T=2000: setTimeout fires → SIGTERM\n                                          // if X > 2000, POST is killed mid-flight\n```\n\nAfter:\n```\ndeploy/restart branch:\n  shouldRestart = true                    ← T=0: just a flag\n  ...\n  await POST result                       ← T=X: POST resolves (guaranteed done)\n  if (shouldRestart) _scheduleGracefulRestart()  ← T=X: setTimeout(2000) scheduled NOW\n                                          ← T=X+2000: systemctl fires\n```\n\nThe 2-second setTimeout is preserved as general post-POST drain\nheadroom, but it no longer competes with the POST.\n\n## Customer ground truth\n\n`134.98.155.239` postgres on 2026-06-08:\n- 1,381 deploy commands stuck at `status='acked'`\n- 1,223 on a single node, all `target_version: \"2.8.1\"`\n- Latest timestamps exactly 60s apart — matching the customer's\nheartbeat cadence (`HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS = 60_000`)\n- \"Removing memclaw plugin solved it\" because no plugin = no heartbeat =\nno restart trigger\n\n## Wet test (on openclaw-test-ran, OpenClaw 2026.6.1)\n\nThe probe spun up a fake backend that returns 200 on the result POST\nafter a configurable delay, and substituted `_scheduleGracefulRestart`\nwith an event recorder.\n\n| Scenario | POST delay | Order | Gap | Verdict |\n|---|---:|---|---:|---|\n| A. Normal POST | 30ms | post-resolved → restart-scheduled | 13ms | ✓ |\n| **B. SLOW POST** | **1500ms** | **post-resolved → restart-scheduled**\n| **3ms** | ✓ |\n| C. ping (no restart) | 30ms | post-resolved (only) | — | ✓ |\n\n**Scenario B is the headline**: with the 1500ms POST delay, the restart\nwas scheduled just 3ms AFTER the POST resolved. Pre-fix, the restart's\nsetTimeout would have been scheduled at t=0, fired at t=2000, and the\nPOST (still in flight at t=1500) would have continued momentarily before\nthe SIGTERM killed it. In real customer traffic with typical backend\nlatencies, the POST never completed → stuck-acked accumulation.\n\n## Tests (4 new in `plugin/src/heartbeat.test.ts`)\n\n- `processCommand POSTs result BEFORE scheduling systemctl` — pins the\nFIXED ordering using a 30ms POST delay to amplify the race. Pre-fix this\ntest fails; post-fix it passes deterministically.\n- `a non-restart command (ping) does NOT schedule a restart` — gate\ncheck on the `shouldRestart` flag\n- `unknown command does NOT schedule a restart` — fails-closed safety\n- `restart still fires when the result POST itself fails` — the\ndeploy/restart command completed; bookkeeping channel failure must not\nstrand the customer on the old binary\n\n## Risks\n\n- **The 2-second setTimeout is now redundant** since the POST is already\ndone. Considered shortening it; opted to preserve current behavior — the\nsmall extra grace period covers any tail post-POST tidy-up (e.g., log\nflush, file-write sync) without touching production-timing semantics.\nFuture cleanup PR can reduce/remove it.\n- **`__DEPLOY_INTERNALS__.processCommand` is now an exported test\nseam.** Gated to NODE_ENV=test for the restart override; the\nprocessCommand export itself is unprotected (it's already an internal\nhelper, the export just makes it directly invokable from tests).\n\n## Plan to ship\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Plugin version | 2.8.4 → 2.8.5 |\n| Backend dependency | none |\n| Customer deploy | refresh plugin on each gateway VM (existing flow) |\n| Expected impact | New deploy commands now correctly report\n`status=\"done\"` after `systemctl restart` lands the new gateway; no more\naccumulation of acked-stuck commands |\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests: 298/298 pass plugin-side (+4 new)\n- [x] Manifest drift: 11/11 pass\n- [x] tsc clean\n- [x] Wet test under OpenClaw 2026.6.1: all 3 scenarios PASS, including\nthe 1500ms-slow-POST race trigger\n- [ ] Customer redeploy: expect zero new stuck-acked commands after this\nplugin lands on goodclaw/yoniclaw/antclaw nodes\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ec52141aa80413168473607911c37cd0fec6cf5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/6ec52141aa80413168473607911c37cd0fec6cf5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/fe8ad26df789c60f65d38ea64b2fff5a3f82f210","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJs5JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwbMQAJxu6GjCGl3lfDzJDyoix0Qt\nu+VJ6HlgfK2dvqLHlvuS2Dwrb2qk5AGCEZhHyJuEq0PM7tKa/J0XmrwzeiI42UmV\n0t2veLsNiQ1LJUun75QT3CDhKUFfqBWpFhMVPZFQj2uwWUmOHGTeUhNEXzq4MmGw\nJnV1e9hCK3o/SS4gSqP7vH/ho1kNgY+KBcEKUe9PphiVSKmJQhsWV8irJdv54DpP\nl8kJg+zK7eEInpAn1txQ3CCFjDwSReoz6KWrflBsGi3vMBbSfFYrbKbdWiNfvLlk\neoqtskFeHhncPrUwB8ve0cmKTAavVZzMMXZFiQnRAfoImxSDeN0y6pGPFexNp61g\nk8YsuTzCgvzrEJxWF72uCYpG09LlEWTC/3baR9kTvWNVscwWrxpPmgZ18zeuCn8t\nysW5Wz/Ff3ZHeLZLrlhFNMpIKqjOZEmanXauMtfgAHwFjpea0mFrdk9myRDvEOis\n5J+jGLN8RcTpg/j+QVBNqiOEy3Bixy6FQDcuNEPZywpNdpkLXSTFa7bo/oLBrolU\nq9oKnWly4BWcAwI3hgZC1Zo4ShNiywiMcfyRwPXGCyetJykb37IANxaWKPTXmveu\n+HkDTNUlrEVBe5NpOYMBJnt+1GpyVjMY/+hAZJedgKLo6Bv+i5AGbNputwU6owbf\nqephKCSpkj8pQ4jDo5id\n=FRN1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6ec52141aa80413168473607911c37cd0fec6cf5\nparent f3a0f7c7084d2eef4fbe8d0484d53b2997f527c3\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780928073 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780928073 +0300\n\nfix(plugin): schedule restart AFTER result POST resolves (CAURA-000) (#306)\n\n## Summary\n\n`processCommand` was scheduling `setTimeout(systemctl --user restart,\n2000)` INSIDE the deploy/restart success branches, BEFORE awaiting the\nresult POST. If the POST took longer than ~2s (slow network, retried\nconnection, queued behind other heartbeat traffic), the systemctl\nSIGTERM killed it mid-flight and the backend never saw `status=\"done\"` —\nthe command stayed at `status=\"acked\"` forever.\n\nCombined with the backend's pending-only auto-upgrade gate (fixed\nseparately in #305 by adding an in-flight-deploy check), this race\nproduced the customer's observed \"SIGTERM every 60 seconds\" on one\ngateway. This PR removes the race at the source so new deploys don't\naccumulate in the first place; #305 handles cleanup/safety on\nalready-stuck-acked commands. Both together close the loop.\n\n## Mechanism\n\nBefore:\n```\ndeploy/restart branch:\n  setTimeout(systemctl restart, 2000)    ← T=0: scheduled\n  ...\n  // fall through to end of processCommand\n  await POST result                       ← T=X: depends on POST latency\n                                          ← T=2000: setTimeout fires → SIGTERM\n                                          // if X > 2000, POST is killed mid-flight\n```\n\nAfter:\n```\ndeploy/restart branch:\n  shouldRestart = true                    ← T=0: just a flag\n  ...\n  await POST result                       ← T=X: POST resolves (guaranteed done)\n  if (shouldRestart) _scheduleGracefulRestart()  ← T=X: setTimeout(2000) scheduled NOW\n                                          ← T=X+2000: systemctl fires\n```\n\nThe 2-second setTimeout is preserved as general post-POST drain\nheadroom, but it no longer competes with the POST.\n\n## Customer ground truth\n\n`134.98.155.239` postgres on 2026-06-08:\n- 1,381 deploy commands stuck at `status='acked'`\n- 1,223 on a single node, all `target_version: \"2.8.1\"`\n- Latest timestamps exactly 60s apart — matching the customer's\nheartbeat cadence (`HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS = 60_000`)\n- \"Removing memclaw plugin solved it\" because no plugin = no heartbeat =\nno restart trigger\n\n## Wet test (on openclaw-test-ran, OpenClaw 2026.6.1)\n\nThe probe spun up a fake backend that returns 200 on the result POST\nafter a configurable delay, and substituted `_scheduleGracefulRestart`\nwith an event recorder.\n\n| Scenario | POST delay | Order | Gap | Verdict |\n|---|---:|---|---:|---|\n| A. Normal POST | 30ms | post-resolved → restart-scheduled | 13ms | ✓ |\n| **B. SLOW POST** | **1500ms** | **post-resolved → restart-scheduled**\n| **3ms** | ✓ |\n| C. ping (no restart) | 30ms | post-resolved (only) | — | ✓ |\n\n**Scenario B is the headline**: with the 1500ms POST delay, the restart\nwas scheduled just 3ms AFTER the POST resolved. Pre-fix, the restart's\nsetTimeout would have been scheduled at t=0, fired at t=2000, and the\nPOST (still in flight at t=1500) would have continued momentarily before\nthe SIGTERM killed it. In real customer traffic with typical backend\nlatencies, the POST never completed → stuck-acked accumulation.\n\n## Tests (4 new in `plugin/src/heartbeat.test.ts`)\n\n- `processCommand POSTs result BEFORE scheduling systemctl` — pins the\nFIXED ordering using a 30ms POST delay to amplify the race. Pre-fix this\ntest fails; post-fix it passes deterministically.\n- `a non-restart command (ping) does NOT schedule a restart` — gate\ncheck on the `shouldRestart` flag\n- `unknown command does NOT schedule a restart` — fails-closed safety\n- `restart still fires when the result POST itself fails` — the\ndeploy/restart command completed; bookkeeping channel failure must not\nstrand the customer on the old binary\n\n## Risks\n\n- **The 2-second setTimeout is now redundant** since the POST is already\ndone. Considered shortening it; opted to preserve current behavior — the\nsmall extra grace period covers any tail post-POST tidy-up (e.g., log\nflush, file-write sync) without touching production-timing semantics.\nFuture cleanup PR can reduce/remove it.\n- **`__DEPLOY_INTERNALS__.processCommand` is now an exported test\nseam.** Gated to NODE_ENV=test for the restart override; the\nprocessCommand export itself is unprotected (it's already an internal\nhelper, the export just makes it directly invokable from tests).\n\n## Plan to ship\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Plugin version | 2.8.4 → 2.8.5 |\n| Backend dependency | none |\n| Customer deploy | refresh plugin on each gateway VM (existing flow) |\n| Expected impact | New deploy commands now correctly report\n`status=\"done\"` after `systemctl restart` lands the new gateway; no more\naccumulation of acked-stuck commands |\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests: 298/298 pass plugin-side (+4 new)\n- [x] Manifest drift: 11/11 pass\n- [x] tsc clean\n- [x] Wet test under OpenClaw 2026.6.1: all 3 scenarios PASS, including\nthe 1500ms-slow-POST race trigger\n- [ ] Customer redeploy: expect zero new stuck-acked commands after this\nplugin lands on goodclaw/yoniclaw/antclaw nodes\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T14:14:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fe8ad26df789c60f65d38ea64b2fff5a3f82f210","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fe8ad26df789c60f65d38ea64b2fff5a3f82f210","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fe8ad26df789c60f65d38ea64b2fff5a3f82f210/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f3a0f7c7084d2eef4fbe8d0484d53b2997f527c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f3a0f7c7084d2eef4fbe8d0484d53b2997f527c3","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f3a0f7c7084d2eef4fbe8d0484d53b2997f527c3"}]},{"sha":"f3a0f7c7084d2eef4fbe8d0484d53b2997f527c3","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGYzYTBmN2M3MDg0ZDJlZWY0ZmJlOGQwNDg0ZDUzYjI5OTdmNTI3YzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-08T13:30:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T13:30:47Z"},"message":"feat(graph-build): drop literal/attr entity nodes, block suffix-distinct merges, rerank entity_lookup by query overlap (#304)\n\n# feat(graph-build): fix entity_lookup recall collapse at scale\n(literal/attr nodes + suffix-merge)\n\n**Branch:** `feat/entity-graph-build-fix` (`6d9ce66`)\n**Files:** `core-api/src/core_api/services/entity_extraction_worker.py`,\n`core-api/src/core_api/pipeline/steps/search/classify_query.py`\n\n## Problem\n`entity_lookup` recall **collapses at scale**. On the S1 benchmark\n(entity-named attribute lookups):\n\n| scale | recall |\n|---|---|\n| K=100 | 22/25 |\n| **K≈1000** | **7/25 (≈0.28)** |\n\nThis is the bench's documented \"K-collapse\" (condition C → 0.31 at\nK≥1000). Root-caused to the **graph build**, not retrieval.\n\n## Root cause\nThe LLM entity-extraction over-populates the entity/relation graph two\nways:\n\n- **(A) Literal values and attribute names become entity NODES.** Dates\n(`2024-03-23`), percentages (`95.1%`), money, and attribute *names*\n(`sla_uptime`, `q3_revenue`) are extracted as entities (typed\n`identifier`/`concept`/`artifact`). Attribute names become **high-degree\nhubs** (`q3_revenue` deg 11, `sla_uptime` deg 9) that bridge every\nentity sharing an attribute.\n- **(B) Entity resolution merges suffix-distinct names.** Names\ndiffering only by a `#NNNN` suffix embed ≈identically → cosine ≥\n`ENTITY_RESOLUTION_THRESHOLD (0.85)` → merge (first-seen-wins). All\n`Comet #NNNN` collapse into one contaminated node carrying every Comet's\nedges.\n\n**Consequence:** in `entity_lookup`, 2–3 matched entities graph-expand\n(`_expand_per_fleet`, 3-hop union) through these hubs/merged-nodes to\n**~the entire corpus** (2 seeds → 51 entities/96 mems @K=100; 151/1041\n@K=1000), all at near-uniform hop-boost. The\n`GRAPH_MAX_BOOSTED_MEMORIES=50` cap then drops the exact entity\n**before** any ranking → miss. (Dump evidence: a single `Comet #0002`\nfact carried 5 edges incl. *other* Comets' launch_dates + a foreign\n`owns mark lin`.)\n\n## Fix\n**entity_extraction_worker.py**\n- **A** — `_is_valid_entity` now rejects literal-shaped names (ISO\ndates, numbers/money/percent) and snake_case attribute names, so they\nnever become nodes. Dropping the node **cascades to its edges**\n(relations require both endpoints to be persisted nodes). Shape-only →\npreserves legit named identifiers (`PR-2025-A`, `gpt-5.4-nano`).\n- **B** — before accepting a similarity-merge, require both names to\nshare the same digit-bearing identifier tokens\n(`_same_identifier_signature`). `#0002` vs `#0012` → don't merge.\n\n**classify_query.py**\n- **rerank (secondary)** — order `entity_lookup` candidates by\nquery-token overlap before trimming to `top_k`, so the exact entity\nisn't diluted below token-sharing siblings.\n\n## Evidence (local, full-stack wet test, S1 fixtures)\n| scale | before | **after** |\n|---|---|---|\n| K=100 | 22/25 | 22/25 |\n| **K≈1000 (clean 1000-fact corpus)** | **7/25** | **22/25 (0.88)** |\n\nGraph density (clean K=100 tenant, before→after A): **83 entities / 131\nrelations → 40 / 62**; literal/attribute nodes **many → 0**. `Comet\n#0002`: **5 edges → isolated → rank 1**.\n\n## NOT addressed (tracked as follow-ups)\n- **Person-hub expansion** — queries about person-valued attributes\n(`X's manager/ceo/team`) connect the subject to a person hub (`mark lin`\ndeg ~20) and still dilute (2 of 3 residual K=1000 misses).\n- **Semantic near-duplicate dilution** — at scale, near-identical facts\ndilute in *vector* space too (1 residual miss via `semantic_search`).\n- **Distractor abstention** — retrieval still returns sibling rows for\nnon-existent entities (no \"not found\" signal).\n- **Heuristic hardening** — the A regex misses `#`-prefixed bare\nsuffixes (`#0012` still node-ified); B is token-based. Consider moving B\nserver-side into resolution.\n\n## Testing\n- **Lint/type:** `ruff check` ✓, `ruff format --check` ✓, `mypy` ✓\n(changed files).\n- **Unit:** all relevant existing tests pass (193 across\n`test_entity_blocklist`, `test_p1_entity_extraction_bulk`,\n`test_entity_lookup_short_circuit`, `test_entity_linking_wiring`,\n`test_adaptive_fts_weight`, `test_a27_shared_tokenizer`, …) — **no\nbreakage** from A/B/rerank. New regression test\n`tests/test_graph_build_fix.py` locks in: literals/attrs not node-ified\n(A) + suffix-distinct not merged (B).\n- **End-to-end:** full-stack rebuild + S1 replay (K=100 and clean\nK=1000, 1001 facts); before/after Postgres graph dumps.\n- **Before merge:** wet test on memclaw.dev per workflow; full `pytest\ntests/` (incl. DB-integration suite) runs in CI.\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"81f8a4a5f39c5d614606bae842b50de774d62eae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/81f8a4a5f39c5d614606bae842b50de774d62eae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/f3a0f7c7084d2eef4fbe8d0484d53b2997f527c3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJsQHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEOcQAAgWTkAo9oogsf8quvOKJ0L0\nZ146eArikElD3Qj2dCKvvWnj/Wgjg0ujPsYscQBPEWwadJi0KjwRe1q+zbhJvTlA\ntft1NhKbKj+Ed3RB/6NT0NsJ80wqu+QnZHXWDKEmxim3Z9QrP6Q9DQx4a3wVunBy\n4HSNfj7IobNns3FjfuaolC8yMcm0n9PBExg59dWY5Y4BjMn8544nvtwA2UFLZm4U\n6Aa01b2pb/NjA6oUWEL5DYgBCjYZ6v/UW+zwLRpkP7hDxu2YSlcUwbZnhq9qvylv\nj79bNOA1uU1VDXf3HT/DysAaR4pnFBh2EAOlNaj6BcifEDA81x+F8v1cdRTv6gWW\nyNRT98AbTVRwuLuwfhhWhP1oH8Dblr2NFWd1dB+WwCffe+oXPRyURtDqUUlse2ZJ\naYs5pzsAj67JZhxDjhAZdu5+RFH1kUMHOveaJzsz4PvwHknbanT8ELch1ji89YGw\n1SM88Ng2a931G54dkukfhpZ3xnpwOIQV3Vx1iGjp0bKDLpoOzmVLkqdqz4V1jsF9\nB34bHSPYBnLtrYnh+mc86kR9WNshO6XJWCLf4LN4XdzA/BZkleeiPGITGyAfucbk\nziVHOmtvwPM18hdYIfYMQzXEMaltToeftX7HgAsYYJxyV00r8jKDUFZT/YAFZYhh\nVSkNmf0t64+wmZcG82DJ\n=PoFs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 81f8a4a5f39c5d614606bae842b50de774d62eae\nparent 3bbb559ea8cf397a0a49f3b00db37d5978e9b3df\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780925447 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780925447 +0300\n\nfeat(graph-build): drop literal/attr entity nodes, block suffix-distinct merges, rerank entity_lookup by query overlap (#304)\n\n# feat(graph-build): fix entity_lookup recall collapse at scale\n(literal/attr nodes + suffix-merge)\n\n**Branch:** `feat/entity-graph-build-fix` (`6d9ce66`)\n**Files:** `core-api/src/core_api/services/entity_extraction_worker.py`,\n`core-api/src/core_api/pipeline/steps/search/classify_query.py`\n\n## Problem\n`entity_lookup` recall **collapses at scale**. On the S1 benchmark\n(entity-named attribute lookups):\n\n| scale | recall |\n|---|---|\n| K=100 | 22/25 |\n| **K≈1000** | **7/25 (≈0.28)** |\n\nThis is the bench's documented \"K-collapse\" (condition C → 0.31 at\nK≥1000). Root-caused to the **graph build**, not retrieval.\n\n## Root cause\nThe LLM entity-extraction over-populates the entity/relation graph two\nways:\n\n- **(A) Literal values and attribute names become entity NODES.** Dates\n(`2024-03-23`), percentages (`95.1%`), money, and attribute *names*\n(`sla_uptime`, `q3_revenue`) are extracted as entities (typed\n`identifier`/`concept`/`artifact`). Attribute names become **high-degree\nhubs** (`q3_revenue` deg 11, `sla_uptime` deg 9) that bridge every\nentity sharing an attribute.\n- **(B) Entity resolution merges suffix-distinct names.** Names\ndiffering only by a `#NNNN` suffix embed ≈identically → cosine ≥\n`ENTITY_RESOLUTION_THRESHOLD (0.85)` → merge (first-seen-wins). All\n`Comet #NNNN` collapse into one contaminated node carrying every Comet's\nedges.\n\n**Consequence:** in `entity_lookup`, 2–3 matched entities graph-expand\n(`_expand_per_fleet`, 3-hop union) through these hubs/merged-nodes to\n**~the entire corpus** (2 seeds → 51 entities/96 mems @K=100; 151/1041\n@K=1000), all at near-uniform hop-boost. The\n`GRAPH_MAX_BOOSTED_MEMORIES=50` cap then drops the exact entity\n**before** any ranking → miss. (Dump evidence: a single `Comet #0002`\nfact carried 5 edges incl. *other* Comets' launch_dates + a foreign\n`owns mark lin`.)\n\n## Fix\n**entity_extraction_worker.py**\n- **A** — `_is_valid_entity` now rejects literal-shaped names (ISO\ndates, numbers/money/percent) and snake_case attribute names, so they\nnever become nodes. Dropping the node **cascades to its edges**\n(relations require both endpoints to be persisted nodes). Shape-only →\npreserves legit named identifiers (`PR-2025-A`, `gpt-5.4-nano`).\n- **B** — before accepting a similarity-merge, require both names to\nshare the same digit-bearing identifier tokens\n(`_same_identifier_signature`). `#0002` vs `#0012` → don't merge.\n\n**classify_query.py**\n- **rerank (secondary)** — order `entity_lookup` candidates by\nquery-token overlap before trimming to `top_k`, so the exact entity\nisn't diluted below token-sharing siblings.\n\n## Evidence (local, full-stack wet test, S1 fixtures)\n| scale | before | **after** |\n|---|---|---|\n| K=100 | 22/25 | 22/25 |\n| **K≈1000 (clean 1000-fact corpus)** | **7/25** | **22/25 (0.88)** |\n\nGraph density (clean K=100 tenant, before→after A): **83 entities / 131\nrelations → 40 / 62**; literal/attribute nodes **many → 0**. `Comet\n#0002`: **5 edges → isolated → rank 1**.\n\n## NOT addressed (tracked as follow-ups)\n- **Person-hub expansion** — queries about person-valued attributes\n(`X's manager/ceo/team`) connect the subject to a person hub (`mark lin`\ndeg ~20) and still dilute (2 of 3 residual K=1000 misses).\n- **Semantic near-duplicate dilution** — at scale, near-identical facts\ndilute in *vector* space too (1 residual miss via `semantic_search`).\n- **Distractor abstention** — retrieval still returns sibling rows for\nnon-existent entities (no \"not found\" signal).\n- **Heuristic hardening** — the A regex misses `#`-prefixed bare\nsuffixes (`#0012` still node-ified); B is token-based. Consider moving B\nserver-side into resolution.\n\n## Testing\n- **Lint/type:** `ruff check` ✓, `ruff format --check` ✓, `mypy` ✓\n(changed files).\n- **Unit:** all relevant existing tests pass (193 across\n`test_entity_blocklist`, `test_p1_entity_extraction_bulk`,\n`test_entity_lookup_short_circuit`, `test_entity_linking_wiring`,\n`test_adaptive_fts_weight`, `test_a27_shared_tokenizer`, …) — **no\nbreakage** from A/B/rerank. New regression test\n`tests/test_graph_build_fix.py` locks in: literals/attrs not node-ified\n(A) + suffix-distinct not merged (B).\n- **End-to-end:** full-stack rebuild + S1 replay (K=100 and clean\nK=1000, 1001 facts); before/after Postgres graph dumps.\n- **Before merge:** wet test on memclaw.dev per workflow; full `pytest\ntests/` (incl. DB-integration suite) runs in CI.\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T13:30:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f3a0f7c7084d2eef4fbe8d0484d53b2997f527c3","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f3a0f7c7084d2eef4fbe8d0484d53b2997f527c3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f3a0f7c7084d2eef4fbe8d0484d53b2997f527c3/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3bbb559ea8cf397a0a49f3b00db37d5978e9b3df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3bbb559ea8cf397a0a49f3b00db37d5978e9b3df","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3bbb559ea8cf397a0a49f3b00db37d5978e9b3df"}]},{"sha":"3bbb559ea8cf397a0a49f3b00db37d5978e9b3df","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDNiYmI1NTllYThjZjM5N2EwYTQ5ZjNiMDBkYjM3ZDU5NzhlOWIzZGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-08T13:15:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T13:15:19Z"},"message":"fix(plugin): memoize bootstrap at process level (CAURA-000) (#303)\n\n## Summary\n\nHoist the ContextEngine bootstrap (smoke-test) state from instance-level\nto module-level so it runs **once per Node process** instead of once per\nengine instance. OpenClaw's `resolveContextEngine` constructs a fresh\nengine every time any of ~7 subsystems needs one (no caching at\nOpenClaw's side), and each fresh instance was running its own\nwrite→search→delete smoke test.\n\n## Customer ground truth\n\nGoodclaw gateway, 31.4h window (2026-06-07 → 06-08):\n\n| | Count |\n|---|---:|\n| `ContextEngine bootstrap` log lines | 390 (12.4/hr) |\n| `Smoke test passed` | 388 |\n| `SMOKE TEST WARNING` (score < 0.7) | 0 |\n| `SMOKE TEST ERROR` (backend 5xx) | 2 (echoes of the 13:14-13:22\noutage; not new signal) |\n\nNet actionable signal from running the smoke test 388 times: **zero**.\nCost: ~37-62 backend ops/hour, ~25 embedding computations/hour,\n~500-1500ms latency tax on each fresh engine's first lifecycle hook, ~25\nlog lines/hour, and a fragility risk (the cleanup DELETE is\nfire-and-forget — if it ever 422s again as it did pre-PR-#274, smoke\nmemories leak into the tenant on every restart).\n\n## Mechanism (OpenClaw side)\n\n`/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/registry-CMq-i5MO.js`:\n\n```js\nengine = await entry.factory(factoryCtx);   // ← calls (config) => new MemClawContextEngine(config)\n```\n\nNo caching. Called from 7 OpenClaw subsystems: `embedded-agent-*.js`,\n`cli-compaction-*.js`, `init-*.js`, `openclaw-tools-*.js`,\n`prepare.runtime-*.js`, `subagent-registry-*.js`,\n`context-engine-host-compat-*.js`. Goodclaw observed ratio: ~1.93\nbootstraps per logical turn.\n\n## Fix\n\nReplace the per-instance state:\n\n```typescript\nprivate _bootstrapped = false;\nprivate _bootstrapPromise: Promise<void> | null = null;\n```\n\nwith a module-level promise:\n\n```typescript\nlet _processBootstrapPromise: Promise<void> | null = null;\n```\n\nThe `bootstrap()` method now reads/writes this single promise.\nConcurrent callers in the same engine OR across different engines all\n`await` the same in-flight promise. Retry-on-failure semantics\npreserved: the `.catch` resets the memo to `null` on rejection so the\nnext engine can retry.\n\nA test-only `_resetBootstrapForTests()` is exported so each test\nexercises the smoke path fresh.\n\n## Customer impact (post-deploy expectation)\n\n| Metric | Pre-fix (observed) | Post-fix (expected) |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `ContextEngine bootstrap` lines | 390 / 31.4h | 1 per gateway restart\n|\n| Smoke write RPS | 12.4/hr | ~0 |\n| Smoke search RPS | ~25/hr | ~0 |\n| Smoke delete RPS | 12.4/hr | ~0 |\n| Embedding compute (smoke) | ~25/hr | ~0 |\n| Latency on first-call after engine construction | +500-1500ms |\nunchanged for first engine of process; **eliminated for subsequent\nengines** |\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `plugin/src/bootstrap-memoization.test.ts` (4 cases):\n\n1. **Two engines share one smoke test** — the headline assertion\n2. **Ten concurrent engines share one smoke test** — race-safety pin\n(Node's single-threaded event loop guarantees the `if (!_x) _x = ...`\npattern is safe)\n3. **Subsequent bootstrap() calls are instant no-ops** — pins the cache\nhit path\n4. **Backend 500 doesn't reject bootstrap, AND memo holds on sick\nbackend** — pins the pre-existing \"swallow smoke errors internally\"\ncontract AND the new \"one error log per process, not per engine\"\nbehavior\n\nFull suite: 294/294 pass (was 290, +4 new). Manifest drift test: 11/11\npass.\n\n## Wet test\n\n`openclaw-test-ran` (GCE, OpenClaw 2026.6.1, plugin 2.8.4):\n\n```\n--- Wet test: 20 engines, sequential bootstrap() ---\n  smoke writes  : 1  (pre-fix would be 20)\n  smoke searches: 1  (pre-fix would be 20-60)\n  smoke deletes : 1  (pre-fix would be 20)\n  Verdict: PASS\n\n--- Race test: 10 concurrent bootstrap() on fresh engines ---\n  new HTTP requests: 0 (memoized → expect 0)\n  Verdict: PASS\n```\n\nThe probe spun up a real HTTP server on `127.0.0.1:<random>`, pointed\n`MEMCLAW_API_URL` at it, constructed 20 sequential + 10 concurrent\nengine instances, and counted requests by shape. Single `[memclaw]\nContextEngine bootstrap` log line across all 30 engines.\n\n## Plugin version\n\nBump `2.8.3 → 2.8.4`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests: 294/294 pass\n- [x] Manifest drift: 11/11 pass\n- [x] Wet test under OpenClaw 2026.6.1: PASS both scenarios\n- [ ] Customer push: refresh plugin on each gateway VM; expect\n`[memclaw] ContextEngine bootstrap` log count to drop from ~12/hr to ~0\n(once per gateway restart).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"472b1c584abfe6eccebf15338015db5a82b45443","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/472b1c584abfe6eccebf15338015db5a82b45443"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/3bbb559ea8cf397a0a49f3b00db37d5978e9b3df","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJsBnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxtEQAFqHmYkyCohzLa45GxUxtxb4\n8Vorlvw6TvdQJz0cgXRUWpzMeZrADy3v21MTIGtuH6uV2MEH9GG1yiKhOMqYruGs\ntXCfftH8LSz2AJ26sogs5bR4e1Khh5bfTXvdUolshN8kPOr89IIYrlLX1xIZv1Js\nh8IifM3ZJsvgOQho8Bn22dycyN4pYZa3ztEw01QW+EqVgaIkH0S6DCvlpdrwjYvk\nf7AWLEUmN9/ZvfU8d+78XzdLOZ34Du1U5RLnjWYpZAB+B3kTpdRAqJGGTM3QNc12\nlb7fjuEH00JAthVnH/2TaElW5CuW6B84uPFFtTqQa6g1ilvLGQAcXCMT6v17zMEd\niAnP4su0fgEFgpPBeXRy1ALUbpsZj+dIFnLWLRkxNZU94YPm39VkikiSOATn54UU\nlmP9cqNG9OTYgyBkcY4ksSWDRBLhrRqolpfC8TECtm21cjfHsboh4aD+fjFfKZoS\nh/rxSeuunZxF7FbU3U4k3GZaOyBHJKosUmE9fHH0DYU+2VChl2U30pgkd9NxbnhW\nMFQTjXJU+ON6MLf0vyEGMq0+3Y1DYMoxdtPjZCdmFUrdNkZcDM8vjTVA8udve7B4\n8sUeEkg0zCEhpc2EbdLYpm62urld4QzYnjhKZL7DSnKxUYltJiLA9F5nKoC5w+f3\nnbAMsygZ0XatBbXsOTWB\n=M//S\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 472b1c584abfe6eccebf15338015db5a82b45443\nparent d223b8af8df682bf4047326d9db694ad21d120de\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780924519 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780924519 +0300\n\nfix(plugin): memoize bootstrap at process level (CAURA-000) (#303)\n\n## Summary\n\nHoist the ContextEngine bootstrap (smoke-test) state from instance-level\nto module-level so it runs **once per Node process** instead of once per\nengine instance. OpenClaw's `resolveContextEngine` constructs a fresh\nengine every time any of ~7 subsystems needs one (no caching at\nOpenClaw's side), and each fresh instance was running its own\nwrite→search→delete smoke test.\n\n## Customer ground truth\n\nGoodclaw gateway, 31.4h window (2026-06-07 → 06-08):\n\n| | Count |\n|---|---:|\n| `ContextEngine bootstrap` log lines | 390 (12.4/hr) |\n| `Smoke test passed` | 388 |\n| `SMOKE TEST WARNING` (score < 0.7) | 0 |\n| `SMOKE TEST ERROR` (backend 5xx) | 2 (echoes of the 13:14-13:22\noutage; not new signal) |\n\nNet actionable signal from running the smoke test 388 times: **zero**.\nCost: ~37-62 backend ops/hour, ~25 embedding computations/hour,\n~500-1500ms latency tax on each fresh engine's first lifecycle hook, ~25\nlog lines/hour, and a fragility risk (the cleanup DELETE is\nfire-and-forget — if it ever 422s again as it did pre-PR-#274, smoke\nmemories leak into the tenant on every restart).\n\n## Mechanism (OpenClaw side)\n\n`/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/registry-CMq-i5MO.js`:\n\n```js\nengine = await entry.factory(factoryCtx);   // ← calls (config) => new MemClawContextEngine(config)\n```\n\nNo caching. Called from 7 OpenClaw subsystems: `embedded-agent-*.js`,\n`cli-compaction-*.js`, `init-*.js`, `openclaw-tools-*.js`,\n`prepare.runtime-*.js`, `subagent-registry-*.js`,\n`context-engine-host-compat-*.js`. Goodclaw observed ratio: ~1.93\nbootstraps per logical turn.\n\n## Fix\n\nReplace the per-instance state:\n\n```typescript\nprivate _bootstrapped = false;\nprivate _bootstrapPromise: Promise<void> | null = null;\n```\n\nwith a module-level promise:\n\n```typescript\nlet _processBootstrapPromise: Promise<void> | null = null;\n```\n\nThe `bootstrap()` method now reads/writes this single promise.\nConcurrent callers in the same engine OR across different engines all\n`await` the same in-flight promise. Retry-on-failure semantics\npreserved: the `.catch` resets the memo to `null` on rejection so the\nnext engine can retry.\n\nA test-only `_resetBootstrapForTests()` is exported so each test\nexercises the smoke path fresh.\n\n## Customer impact (post-deploy expectation)\n\n| Metric | Pre-fix (observed) | Post-fix (expected) |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `ContextEngine bootstrap` lines | 390 / 31.4h | 1 per gateway restart\n|\n| Smoke write RPS | 12.4/hr | ~0 |\n| Smoke search RPS | ~25/hr | ~0 |\n| Smoke delete RPS | 12.4/hr | ~0 |\n| Embedding compute (smoke) | ~25/hr | ~0 |\n| Latency on first-call after engine construction | +500-1500ms |\nunchanged for first engine of process; **eliminated for subsequent\nengines** |\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `plugin/src/bootstrap-memoization.test.ts` (4 cases):\n\n1. **Two engines share one smoke test** — the headline assertion\n2. **Ten concurrent engines share one smoke test** — race-safety pin\n(Node's single-threaded event loop guarantees the `if (!_x) _x = ...`\npattern is safe)\n3. **Subsequent bootstrap() calls are instant no-ops** — pins the cache\nhit path\n4. **Backend 500 doesn't reject bootstrap, AND memo holds on sick\nbackend** — pins the pre-existing \"swallow smoke errors internally\"\ncontract AND the new \"one error log per process, not per engine\"\nbehavior\n\nFull suite: 294/294 pass (was 290, +4 new). Manifest drift test: 11/11\npass.\n\n## Wet test\n\n`openclaw-test-ran` (GCE, OpenClaw 2026.6.1, plugin 2.8.4):\n\n```\n--- Wet test: 20 engines, sequential bootstrap() ---\n  smoke writes  : 1  (pre-fix would be 20)\n  smoke searches: 1  (pre-fix would be 20-60)\n  smoke deletes : 1  (pre-fix would be 20)\n  Verdict: PASS\n\n--- Race test: 10 concurrent bootstrap() on fresh engines ---\n  new HTTP requests: 0 (memoized → expect 0)\n  Verdict: PASS\n```\n\nThe probe spun up a real HTTP server on `127.0.0.1:<random>`, pointed\n`MEMCLAW_API_URL` at it, constructed 20 sequential + 10 concurrent\nengine instances, and counted requests by shape. Single `[memclaw]\nContextEngine bootstrap` log line across all 30 engines.\n\n## Plugin version\n\nBump `2.8.3 → 2.8.4`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests: 294/294 pass\n- [x] Manifest drift: 11/11 pass\n- [x] Wet test under OpenClaw 2026.6.1: PASS both scenarios\n- [ ] Customer push: refresh plugin on each gateway VM; expect\n`[memclaw] ContextEngine bootstrap` log count to drop from ~12/hr to ~0\n(once per gateway restart).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T13:15:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3bbb559ea8cf397a0a49f3b00db37d5978e9b3df","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3bbb559ea8cf397a0a49f3b00db37d5978e9b3df","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3bbb559ea8cf397a0a49f3b00db37d5978e9b3df/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d223b8af8df682bf4047326d9db694ad21d120de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d223b8af8df682bf4047326d9db694ad21d120de","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d223b8af8df682bf4047326d9db694ad21d120de"}]},{"sha":"d223b8af8df682bf4047326d9db694ad21d120de","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGQyMjNiOGFmOGRmNjgyYmY0MDQ3MzI2ZDlkYjY5NGFkMjFkMTIwZGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-08T12:50:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T12:50:00Z"},"message":"chore: add glama.json for Glama MCP registry claim (#302)\n\n## What\n\nAdds `glama.json` at the repo root to register/claim the MemClaw MCP\nserver on [glama.ai](https://glama.ai/mcp).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://glama.ai/mcp/schemas/server.json\",\n  \"maintainers\": [\n    \"yanki-m\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Why\n\nGlama's MCP registry requires a `glama.json` with a `maintainers` array\nto verify repository ownership before the server can be claimed. Lists\n`yanki-m` as the maintainer.\n\n## Next step\n\nAfter merge, claim the server via \"Login with GitHub to claim\" on Glama.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"90db8af31ad2562a615030c50428ff2d641e04d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/90db8af31ad2562a615030c50428ff2d641e04d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/d223b8af8df682bf4047326d9db694ad21d120de","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJrp4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAF3EQAIVDrIy65NsV1so74or0ZJHv\nlHPLntDiVwOhAKwj31Yg2s0+zGLgstGh9UOUY16KQyqYoLhWoh8NTjFpV9CtebnF\nGCpBq75uL2LSw6sqXHTSUwCTc3Yvmq67c6mpfPqr/7Ze2jkWq3btk+PmL0alJD6L\nMb5XssfJIu7/nnXbdqszBOxMMNWnN3K8AI5U88y7ErJvunHvDqDPrFStooZ5Ounk\ntQhZs1u8rKtYrLEV2iOHbnVPFuDLoQm3/PoTCfZSQw2wQV1DdpXZEow6YzG6z2yj\nLE+khLrz18vPdgS5xRxrmx0rC42OV8vdGnj4E7P2AU2ci8RXA9y35F/4BdZ6ohnw\nrblgkkK4aZLCfOPicU3u20IaIKCAhmXacJizjPdT0lE1vMU/kST0xqt4TUNkHiRD\n5PHAWQW4eoyDKRn4VVV1BoimNnfrvDfRMrE8YIu4YhJHLyvZb8Q8jUSaiGFv3G8j\ndpjLjIHaq82mOtVf6KS0FiDfkigk1x3HBzWr6Yh4l9Zy63JCb21636cnvEtHDcOk\nCO9g9T++PXh7BxhazynIPdFA6y/2X9qixqC5Z7Mthn62/locfKVgsN+e3GDjLRxk\nZc2XsXv3XaQDM6RyKfN/wxB3RadV/8n94rtxJ6udHO/9jAJi5zxmDcrgUkEvpEX9\n2C6R9oDDGm94QMhXGtTf\n=MzP9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 90db8af31ad2562a615030c50428ff2d641e04d6\nparent b7d73d4465ee01ca9360728c44b68925c58648e6\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780923000 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780923000 +0300\n\nchore: add glama.json for Glama MCP registry claim (#302)\n\n## What\n\nAdds `glama.json` at the repo root to register/claim the MemClaw MCP\nserver on [glama.ai](https://glama.ai/mcp).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://glama.ai/mcp/schemas/server.json\",\n  \"maintainers\": [\n    \"yanki-m\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Why\n\nGlama's MCP registry requires a `glama.json` with a `maintainers` array\nto verify repository ownership before the server can be claimed. Lists\n`yanki-m` as the maintainer.\n\n## Next step\n\nAfter merge, claim the server via \"Login with GitHub to claim\" on Glama.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T12:50:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d223b8af8df682bf4047326d9db694ad21d120de","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d223b8af8df682bf4047326d9db694ad21d120de","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d223b8af8df682bf4047326d9db694ad21d120de/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b7d73d4465ee01ca9360728c44b68925c58648e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b7d73d4465ee01ca9360728c44b68925c58648e6","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b7d73d4465ee01ca9360728c44b68925c58648e6"}]},{"sha":"b7d73d4465ee01ca9360728c44b68925c58648e6","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGI3ZDczZDQ0NjVlZTAxY2E5MzYwNzI4YzQ0YjY4OTI1YzU4NjQ4ZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-08T11:45:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T11:45:54Z"},"message":"fix(search): bound graph BFS frontier to prevent unbounded IN-clause (CAURA-000 F4) (#301)\n\n## Summary\n\nServer-side fix for the F4 root cause identified during the customer-log\ninvestigation. F3 already landed via PR #298, so this PR is **F4-only**.\n\n## Root cause (proven, not inferred)\n\nCustomer log capture (read-only ssh, `core-storage-api` container,\ntenant `etoro0-40f488`, 2026-06-07T16:52:05Z):\n\n```\nWHERE relations.tenant_id = $1::VARCHAR\n  AND (relations.fleet_id = $4::VARCHAR OR relations.fleet_id IS NULL)\n  AND relations.from_entity_id IN ($5::UUID, $6::UUID, ..., $42146::UUID)\n[parameters: ('etoro0-40f488', 'yoniclaw-fleet', ..., 42046 parameters truncated ...)]\n(Background on this error at: https://sqlalche.me/e/20/rvf5)\n\"severity\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": \"Exception in ASGI application\\n\"\n```\n\n→ **42,146 bind parameters in a single statement** — well past asyncpg's\nsafe window. Manifests upstream as 7 `recall failed: MemClaw API 500`\nand 3 `SMOKE TEST ERROR` events in the gateway log over a 2-day capture.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n`entity_expand_graph` (`postgres_service.py:3089`) does BFS over the\nrelations graph:\n\n```python\nfrontier = set(seed_entity_ids)\nfor hop in range(1, max_hops + 1):\n    fwd = select(...).where(Relation.from_entity_id.in_(frontier))   # ← N bind params\n    rev = select(...).where(Relation.to_entity_id.in_(frontier))\n    ...\n    frontier = neighbor_weights.keys() - ...   # ← unbounded growth\n```\n\nA `GRAPH_MAX_EXPANDED_ENTITIES = 200` constant existed but was **applied\nin the wrong place**: only the OUTPUT of `entity_expand_graph` was\ncapped (in `classify_query.py:287-291`), not the FRONTIER inside the\nBFS. By the time we got to the truncation, the giant SQL had already\nfired. And the *other* search path that consumes the BFS output\n(`parallel_embed_entity_boost.py:91-94`) had no cap at all.\n\n## Fix\n\nTwo-site fix, one logical change:\n\n1. **`entity_expand_graph`** (core-storage-api): cap the frontier at\n`GRAPH_MAX_EXPANDED_ENTITIES` BEFORE building the per-hop `IN (...)`\nquery. Order by `(weight desc, id asc)` so the cap keeps the\nhighest-weighted edges deterministically; ID tiebreak makes selection\nstable.\n\n2. **`parallel_embed_entity_boost`** (core-api): apply the same cap\ndefensively at the call boundary BEFORE `get_memory_ids_by_entity_ids`.\nMirrors the existing cap in `classify_query._load_graph_memories` so\nboth search paths behave consistently. Order by `(hop asc, weight desc)`\n— closest entities win.\n\nBoth sites log `INFO` when the cap fires so we get operator visibility\non hot-tenant cap rates.\n\n## Numbers\n\n| | Bind params | Outcome |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Customer's failing query, before fix | 42,151 | crashed (`Exception in\nASGI application`) |\n| Same query, after fix | 205 | safe (≪ asyncpg ~32K ceiling) |\n\n## Risks & trade-offs\n\n- **Truncation can drop low-weight edges.** Since we order by weight,\ndropped edges are the lowest-relevance ones. The other search path\nalready does this and we have no recall-regression evidence; this PR\nbrings the second path in line.\n- **No schema change, no migration, no constant change.**\n`GRAPH_MAX_EXPANDED_ENTITIES = 200` was already in\n`common/constants.py`. We just apply it at the right places.\n- **Doesn't migrate to recursive CTE.** That's the architecturally\ncleaner fix (single round-trip, no parameter explosion possible) but a\nbigger change. Deferred to a follow-up; will re-evaluate based on\npost-deploy cap-fire rates.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `tests/test_caura_000_graph_frontier_cap.py` (8 unit tests):\n\n- Constant sanity (cap below asyncpg window, above realistic seed\ncounts)\n- `parallel_embed_entity_boost` cap applied when entity_hops > cap\n- `parallel_embed_entity_boost` no-op when within cap\n- `parallel_embed_entity_boost` ordering keeps closer hops (regression\nguard: a sort-key inversion would silently drop seed-hop entities)\n- `entity_expand_graph` cap keeps highest-weight edges\n- `entity_expand_graph` cap is deterministic across calls (ID tiebreak)\n- `entity_expand_graph` no-op when within cap\n\nRegression sweep across neighboring suites: 37/37 pass (D7 + P3-3 + P3-2\n+ new file).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests: 8/8 pass\n- [x] Regression sweep: 37/37 pass\n- [x] Customer-scenario simulation: 42,151 → 205 bind params\n- [ ] Customer rollout: ship via next on-prem release; expect `recall\nfailed: MemClaw API 500` (search pipeline) count to drop to near-zero.\nWatch the new `entity_expand_graph: frontier capped at 200` INFO lines —\nif they fire >5/sec in steady state we should reconsider the cap or move\nto a CTE traversal.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"28658835be38abf9a3277d4cdd896e9f1508721b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/28658835be38abf9a3277d4cdd896e9f1508721b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b7d73d4465ee01ca9360728c44b68925c58648e6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJqtyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8cgQACEaabD4FLuFvdSn4xAM696J\nhYb2CyhYzDk7mzmk6NzaJD6DcFLq4Z+KJbh9Z+QHPQYA4quNqmfTZdi+7bc5qPaM\nxJgJ5Fb0eWf3ueCnsk2Q6PzHHOAM9p/4hwfQiJQiLBzop5ydmEf7Fd42jgezHNTT\nxo6zAHSadCypTpfGyiQvO1fRMZ8zIePZmjsUKMx8AFROufYXajfr2oDAnObXp0EZ\nWzTP4gHWmdwOmmWaZvKpaQJozifIXcZxTyKf76aGVTUHPD3bbM5RYxt1NVyS0RaL\nzfAGU3JXapw5CRMBMHh0CpC2F179oOuQHi3A6RodFkQ7mG1NzoB6MAun+f1NIS7B\nJdBbnORUR0p6rrDSiIU2xGARSQOqJplnBcZuVe2GtWQYGlC6Q7vRB3O/K3nCw5kA\nK7GepgB3QXbIapqbSJ+R8oKKBB+Axe2TrpPqpTIv2tT54IKoENLtgUfnHAxDY/aD\nLBSFgt/yx5qlGNVeOJQJvaNyM2o5zY5nJBC34rhbtpa8/y/RAiQC/UBrqYriTReM\nuHKkMUrhyy0qeKtfwDJLKO77CVt0NLKrQqN24OW1Z8lyGWhqU11jg1UiZT2mEv3h\n3gS28ox1VqzoMmeX6AfuJ9rrdYMBTP8FfTgtU2rFyUTtS9Huz00BxZ6p3+OR76H4\nb2c6+zPoE77iWiRSXjm6\n=uxoV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 28658835be38abf9a3277d4cdd896e9f1508721b\nparent 67053152428d55d2e93f9a552ddd0724d1a73393\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780919154 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780919154 +0300\n\nfix(search): bound graph BFS frontier to prevent unbounded IN-clause (CAURA-000 F4) (#301)\n\n## Summary\n\nServer-side fix for the F4 root cause identified during the customer-log\ninvestigation. F3 already landed via PR #298, so this PR is **F4-only**.\n\n## Root cause (proven, not inferred)\n\nCustomer log capture (read-only ssh, `core-storage-api` container,\ntenant `etoro0-40f488`, 2026-06-07T16:52:05Z):\n\n```\nWHERE relations.tenant_id = $1::VARCHAR\n  AND (relations.fleet_id = $4::VARCHAR OR relations.fleet_id IS NULL)\n  AND relations.from_entity_id IN ($5::UUID, $6::UUID, ..., $42146::UUID)\n[parameters: ('etoro0-40f488', 'yoniclaw-fleet', ..., 42046 parameters truncated ...)]\n(Background on this error at: https://sqlalche.me/e/20/rvf5)\n\"severity\": \"ERROR\", \"message\": \"Exception in ASGI application\\n\"\n```\n\n→ **42,146 bind parameters in a single statement** — well past asyncpg's\nsafe window. Manifests upstream as 7 `recall failed: MemClaw API 500`\nand 3 `SMOKE TEST ERROR` events in the gateway log over a 2-day capture.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n`entity_expand_graph` (`postgres_service.py:3089`) does BFS over the\nrelations graph:\n\n```python\nfrontier = set(seed_entity_ids)\nfor hop in range(1, max_hops + 1):\n    fwd = select(...).where(Relation.from_entity_id.in_(frontier))   # ← N bind params\n    rev = select(...).where(Relation.to_entity_id.in_(frontier))\n    ...\n    frontier = neighbor_weights.keys() - ...   # ← unbounded growth\n```\n\nA `GRAPH_MAX_EXPANDED_ENTITIES = 200` constant existed but was **applied\nin the wrong place**: only the OUTPUT of `entity_expand_graph` was\ncapped (in `classify_query.py:287-291`), not the FRONTIER inside the\nBFS. By the time we got to the truncation, the giant SQL had already\nfired. And the *other* search path that consumes the BFS output\n(`parallel_embed_entity_boost.py:91-94`) had no cap at all.\n\n## Fix\n\nTwo-site fix, one logical change:\n\n1. **`entity_expand_graph`** (core-storage-api): cap the frontier at\n`GRAPH_MAX_EXPANDED_ENTITIES` BEFORE building the per-hop `IN (...)`\nquery. Order by `(weight desc, id asc)` so the cap keeps the\nhighest-weighted edges deterministically; ID tiebreak makes selection\nstable.\n\n2. **`parallel_embed_entity_boost`** (core-api): apply the same cap\ndefensively at the call boundary BEFORE `get_memory_ids_by_entity_ids`.\nMirrors the existing cap in `classify_query._load_graph_memories` so\nboth search paths behave consistently. Order by `(hop asc, weight desc)`\n— closest entities win.\n\nBoth sites log `INFO` when the cap fires so we get operator visibility\non hot-tenant cap rates.\n\n## Numbers\n\n| | Bind params | Outcome |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Customer's failing query, before fix | 42,151 | crashed (`Exception in\nASGI application`) |\n| Same query, after fix | 205 | safe (≪ asyncpg ~32K ceiling) |\n\n## Risks & trade-offs\n\n- **Truncation can drop low-weight edges.** Since we order by weight,\ndropped edges are the lowest-relevance ones. The other search path\nalready does this and we have no recall-regression evidence; this PR\nbrings the second path in line.\n- **No schema change, no migration, no constant change.**\n`GRAPH_MAX_EXPANDED_ENTITIES = 200` was already in\n`common/constants.py`. We just apply it at the right places.\n- **Doesn't migrate to recursive CTE.** That's the architecturally\ncleaner fix (single round-trip, no parameter explosion possible) but a\nbigger change. Deferred to a follow-up; will re-evaluate based on\npost-deploy cap-fire rates.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `tests/test_caura_000_graph_frontier_cap.py` (8 unit tests):\n\n- Constant sanity (cap below asyncpg window, above realistic seed\ncounts)\n- `parallel_embed_entity_boost` cap applied when entity_hops > cap\n- `parallel_embed_entity_boost` no-op when within cap\n- `parallel_embed_entity_boost` ordering keeps closer hops (regression\nguard: a sort-key inversion would silently drop seed-hop entities)\n- `entity_expand_graph` cap keeps highest-weight edges\n- `entity_expand_graph` cap is deterministic across calls (ID tiebreak)\n- `entity_expand_graph` no-op when within cap\n\nRegression sweep across neighboring suites: 37/37 pass (D7 + P3-3 + P3-2\n+ new file).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests: 8/8 pass\n- [x] Regression sweep: 37/37 pass\n- [x] Customer-scenario simulation: 42,151 → 205 bind params\n- [ ] Customer rollout: ship via next on-prem release; expect `recall\nfailed: MemClaw API 500` (search pipeline) count to drop to near-zero.\nWatch the new `entity_expand_graph: frontier capped at 200` INFO lines —\nif they fire >5/sec in steady state we should reconsider the cap or move\nto a CTE traversal.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T11:45:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b7d73d4465ee01ca9360728c44b68925c58648e6","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b7d73d4465ee01ca9360728c44b68925c58648e6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b7d73d4465ee01ca9360728c44b68925c58648e6/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"67053152428d55d2e93f9a552ddd0724d1a73393","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/67053152428d55d2e93f9a552ddd0724d1a73393","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/67053152428d55d2e93f9a552ddd0724d1a73393"}]},{"sha":"67053152428d55d2e93f9a552ddd0724d1a73393","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDY3MDUzMTUyNDI4ZDU1ZDJlOTNmOWE1NTJkZGQwNzI0ZDFhNzMzOTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-08T10:35:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T10:35:39Z"},"message":"fix(plugin): suppress bootstrap agent-id warn + swallow afterTurn 409 (CAURA-000) (#300)\n\n## Summary\n\nTwo noise-reduction changes targeting the exact warn floor observed in\nthe customer's goodclaw 2.8.1 window (2026-06-07T13:23 → 06-08T07:26,\n18h):\n\n| Pre-fix observed | Source | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 227 \\`Could not resolve agent ID\\` warns | Bootstrap call site only\n(\\`_doBootstrap\\`) — 1.00 per bootstrap, 100% of residual noise | New\n\\`resolveAgentIdQuiet\\` variant; bootstrap is the only caller |\n| 296 \\`Failed to persist turn summary: MemClaw API 409\\` warns (~5/hr)\n| \\`afterTurn\\` dedup rejection from identical replies (\"ok\", \"Got it.\")\n| New \\`isDuplicateMemoryError\\` gate; non-409 still logs |\n\nBoth are pure operator-log signal-to-noise improvements. No behavior\nchange to the write/read paths themselves — the dedup is already working\ncorrectly server-side; the plugin just stops complaining about it.\n\n### Why split the warn (loud/quiet) instead of just lowering severity\n\nThe per-turn paths (\\`ingest\\` / \\`assemble\\` / \\`afterTurn\\` /\n\\`prepareSubagentSpawn\\`) MUST keep warning loudly if agent_id falls\nthrough — that's the next-regression signal for PR #286. Silencing\nglobally would mask real bugs. The bootstrap fallback is by design (no\nper-call context at construction); silencing **only that one call site**\npreserves the diagnostic for per-turn drift.\n\n### Tests\n\nNew \\`resolve-agent.test.ts\\` (5 cases) pins:\n- \\`resolveAgentId({}) \\` emits 1 warn, returns \\`main-<id>\\`\n- \\`resolveAgentIdQuiet({})\\` emits 0 warns, returns \\`main-<id>\\`\n- Successful resolves (sessionKey parsed) emit 0 warns from either\nvariant\n- Multi-source precedence is preserved\n\nNew describe block in \\`context-engine.test.ts\\` (4 cases) pins:\n- 409 dedup error matches\n- 400/401/403/404/422/500/502/503 do NOT match\n- Non-Error inputs / null / undefined do NOT match\n- Word-boundary regex rejects \\`new Error(\"something else 409\")\\`\n\n### Validation\n\n- \\`npm test\\` in \\`plugin/\\`: **290/290 pass** (was 281, +9 new tests)\n- \\`pytest tests/test_plugin_source_manifest.py\\`: 11/11 pass\n- Wet test on \\`openclaw-test-ran\\` (GCE, OpenClaw 2026.6.1, plugin\n2.8.3): **15/15 pass**, including PR #286 (sessionKey parsing) and PR\n#292 (AbortSignal threading) regression guards\n\n### Version\n\nBumps \\`2.8.2 → 2.8.3\\` across \\`package.json\\`,\n\\`openclaw.plugin.json\\`, \\`src/version.ts\\` (auto-regenerated by\n\\`gen-version.sh\\` prebuild).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests pass\n- [x] Wet-tested on GCE VM under OpenClaw 2026.6.1\n- [ ] Customer push: \\`memclaw.allowlist.fix\\` to refresh plugin on each\ngoodclaw/yoniclaw/antclaw VM; expect bootstrap warn count drop from\n227/18h to 0 and \\`Failed to persist turn summary\\` count from 296/2d to\n0\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"76a5ab73e85ec760f081d8447f1f0113a74095b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/76a5ab73e85ec760f081d8447f1f0113a74095b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/67053152428d55d2e93f9a552ddd0724d1a73393","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJpr7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfnoQAJxT/dMAtYtlOU1b2f5VJPYl\naoLmSQiXHqVTid/eWG7VhDJ5WtJ3BFdkcctSDV6h1kWB8kWVhG7rwtyq29EXK/KF\nnreyIITMF+SrnwEin5vuJ1J5QjxySMupjOZBthKpnxAxt07f6icq1XMi4tHF9cDG\npethVDbNDAs2WToy4CD5b9ZdLC08d/nRAOM88auIeFcICaXdekuVsZR2dT3PnSoV\n24P/sZHU2UgC5oCr4oZGo+6x5lU4smm+X0IVxgWp23MABs5Tw/mAVsSzWJ0xvLPw\nYpwr4A87J3RwEbWavU8QRuXr4X7szzNhdsLTE+rjU+UqXZYMJUBvMszxD7ApmGMJ\nDN1WOF2xUkNmsYdm9/rGfS50s65utCxCZOl6+dC2q3hNFciIIzex6oNYN9xbhQQo\n8njuwvRSyl3jI2nW+8vnrvcVoxgPcVYwrDYj4+skuO4laromuKe5XCIfqL89Qw2C\nS831AKv0VVJGp9apUZeLGVDAR4iUIdebyOlrJYHZcJNBpYgQaM9NH7iAmitMeveF\nS4ytJiGLTSGAfud4Cli3ahsWF+1k1HCXlWGLBVHUT1VPF7Wcc0e+uD3w0B0OZ3JV\nG7hWCii1p/r+JmDk5U+7efDk1aG7P6AntRXNa9Kognv9Fjso5nJ/JMEu69miBSvh\n4M9sVwb7RZPxLzDju0TZ\n=EALh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 76a5ab73e85ec760f081d8447f1f0113a74095b6\nparent b7d0f2f864eee3e16f3df40c10b71c7f2e3c0dc9\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780914939 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780914939 +0300\n\nfix(plugin): suppress bootstrap agent-id warn + swallow afterTurn 409 (CAURA-000) (#300)\n\n## Summary\n\nTwo noise-reduction changes targeting the exact warn floor observed in\nthe customer's goodclaw 2.8.1 window (2026-06-07T13:23 → 06-08T07:26,\n18h):\n\n| Pre-fix observed | Source | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 227 \\`Could not resolve agent ID\\` warns | Bootstrap call site only\n(\\`_doBootstrap\\`) — 1.00 per bootstrap, 100% of residual noise | New\n\\`resolveAgentIdQuiet\\` variant; bootstrap is the only caller |\n| 296 \\`Failed to persist turn summary: MemClaw API 409\\` warns (~5/hr)\n| \\`afterTurn\\` dedup rejection from identical replies (\"ok\", \"Got it.\")\n| New \\`isDuplicateMemoryError\\` gate; non-409 still logs |\n\nBoth are pure operator-log signal-to-noise improvements. No behavior\nchange to the write/read paths themselves — the dedup is already working\ncorrectly server-side; the plugin just stops complaining about it.\n\n### Why split the warn (loud/quiet) instead of just lowering severity\n\nThe per-turn paths (\\`ingest\\` / \\`assemble\\` / \\`afterTurn\\` /\n\\`prepareSubagentSpawn\\`) MUST keep warning loudly if agent_id falls\nthrough — that's the next-regression signal for PR #286. Silencing\nglobally would mask real bugs. The bootstrap fallback is by design (no\nper-call context at construction); silencing **only that one call site**\npreserves the diagnostic for per-turn drift.\n\n### Tests\n\nNew \\`resolve-agent.test.ts\\` (5 cases) pins:\n- \\`resolveAgentId({}) \\` emits 1 warn, returns \\`main-<id>\\`\n- \\`resolveAgentIdQuiet({})\\` emits 0 warns, returns \\`main-<id>\\`\n- Successful resolves (sessionKey parsed) emit 0 warns from either\nvariant\n- Multi-source precedence is preserved\n\nNew describe block in \\`context-engine.test.ts\\` (4 cases) pins:\n- 409 dedup error matches\n- 400/401/403/404/422/500/502/503 do NOT match\n- Non-Error inputs / null / undefined do NOT match\n- Word-boundary regex rejects \\`new Error(\"something else 409\")\\`\n\n### Validation\n\n- \\`npm test\\` in \\`plugin/\\`: **290/290 pass** (was 281, +9 new tests)\n- \\`pytest tests/test_plugin_source_manifest.py\\`: 11/11 pass\n- Wet test on \\`openclaw-test-ran\\` (GCE, OpenClaw 2026.6.1, plugin\n2.8.3): **15/15 pass**, including PR #286 (sessionKey parsing) and PR\n#292 (AbortSignal threading) regression guards\n\n### Version\n\nBumps \\`2.8.2 → 2.8.3\\` across \\`package.json\\`,\n\\`openclaw.plugin.json\\`, \\`src/version.ts\\` (auto-regenerated by\n\\`gen-version.sh\\` prebuild).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests pass\n- [x] Wet-tested on GCE VM under OpenClaw 2026.6.1\n- [ ] Customer push: \\`memclaw.allowlist.fix\\` to refresh plugin on each\ngoodclaw/yoniclaw/antclaw VM; expect bootstrap warn count drop from\n227/18h to 0 and \\`Failed to persist turn summary\\` count from 296/2d to\n0\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T10:35:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/67053152428d55d2e93f9a552ddd0724d1a73393","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/67053152428d55d2e93f9a552ddd0724d1a73393","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/67053152428d55d2e93f9a552ddd0724d1a73393/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b7d0f2f864eee3e16f3df40c10b71c7f2e3c0dc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b7d0f2f864eee3e16f3df40c10b71c7f2e3c0dc9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b7d0f2f864eee3e16f3df40c10b71c7f2e3c0dc9"}]},{"sha":"b7d0f2f864eee3e16f3df40c10b71c7f2e3c0dc9","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGI3ZDBmMmY4NjRlZWUzZTE2ZjNkZjQwYzEwYjcxYzdmMmUzYzBkYzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-08T08:09:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T08:09:32Z"},"message":"fix(evolve): pass weight_adjustment_skipped_reason from MCP evolve path (#299)\n\n## The error (prod)\n\n```\nUnhandled error in memclaw_evolve\nTypeError: _apply_outcome_to_db() missing 1 required keyword-only argument:\n'weight_adjustment_skipped_reason'\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe A15 work added `weight_adjustment_skipped_reason` as a **required**\nkeyword-only arg of `_apply_outcome_to_db` and updated the REST\n`report_outcome` caller (`evolve_service.py:744-811`) — but the **MCP\n`memclaw_evolve` caller** (`mcp_server.py`) was never updated. It ran\nits scope filter but neither computed the slug nor passed it, so every\nwrite-path evolve through MCP raised the `TypeError`.\n\nSame class as the recent cross-link fix: a required arg added, one call\nsite missed.\n\n## Fix\n\nReplicate the REST A15 slug logic in the MCP scope block and pass it\nthrough:\n- `no_related_ids` when there are no related ids\n- `agent_id_mismatch` / `fleet_id_mismatch` / `all_out_of_scope` when\nthe scope filter drops everything\n- pass `weight_adjustment_skipped_reason=` into `_apply_outcome_to_db`\n\n## Why CI didn't catch it\n\nThe existing `test_mcp_evolve_session_split.py` tests patch\n`_apply_outcome_to_db` with an `AsyncMock`, which **accepts any\nsignature** — so the missing required kwarg never surfaced. This PR adds\na regression test that captures the kwargs the handler actually passes\nand **binds them against the real `_apply_outcome_to_db` signature**, so\na missing required kwarg fails the test. Plus slug-value tests for the\n`no_related_ids` and all-out-of-scope cases.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ruff check` clean ✅\n- `pytest tests/test_mcp_evolve_session_split.py` → 5 passed ✅\n- **Red/green proven:** the new bind guard *fails* when the pass-through\nis removed (reproduces the prod `TypeError`) and *passes* with the fix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"8e1ff56f448e8bb13c4fe4bac95c4383de369c0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/8e1ff56f448e8bb13c4fe4bac95c4383de369c0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b7d0f2f864eee3e16f3df40c10b71c7f2e3c0dc9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJni8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7O4QAIjp28TfN91YbNPI+XuxgnOR\nklXqG3kKPKgI/PT4iR7biATsNP0OxMyTKWCKx0tPW2uq5NEtGr+hIhvl2dxPcYgr\nwgxbVs03P+gzhathboJHuHI+zPDHgAeJkjbyYki1pvYHVp0qD26rCqk7tBEgDc1u\nyt0oSrcGOwOcyZVKvXOZYZZoAnJT5nWptrfmoEHz3jIUtvRr2CbudfGdlx6Attk1\nLP+YZ9fuuPaeYDSdD2z7Xwf9SKjH5yfrC3MjPX4iQfPB47hlwgPSFonCI2KVouxR\nwu2hozgy+75Q2cx0xFTYbjgW1VpKIucL7vzhIxLXX+YSp8nAiYOnzXNlXrIXfHiJ\n/rRnudFC0YXPUpI14rJuNiEyahQESJI5s0X6X4IwPaWt8f5DOnC9nw1uKDR0arlY\n2PIZA8SUmIIKiEJhHIkh8BTN+oOZL8bWZQNeku+HO2GOhhpxY9szp99+FXLPR/o7\n20uNo404qOWCqF00pc2+FDwLAhcghYLMYyNaVFqFR0OaWnyERh8XOWiGiTMT79ae\nFNKvXYNQ27+F8HPy+b3a95AJrFMwl0LSyGTNYC6K8gNogA4yhtPvNrcVoke/Apvq\nLt8P6VQeoFsADOrakoX0f8aCnmZIqgz4trSwV/eeIMsDMiROR9wruVF6K/X2KZVA\nbOT+Edsye4f2+MpyT4hX\n=c8Dn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8e1ff56f448e8bb13c4fe4bac95c4383de369c0d\nparent 086427407b08df8475a29927882b01c5c76cb026\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780906172 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780906172 +0300\n\nfix(evolve): pass weight_adjustment_skipped_reason from MCP evolve path (#299)\n\n## The error (prod)\n\n```\nUnhandled error in memclaw_evolve\nTypeError: _apply_outcome_to_db() missing 1 required keyword-only argument:\n'weight_adjustment_skipped_reason'\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe A15 work added `weight_adjustment_skipped_reason` as a **required**\nkeyword-only arg of `_apply_outcome_to_db` and updated the REST\n`report_outcome` caller (`evolve_service.py:744-811`) — but the **MCP\n`memclaw_evolve` caller** (`mcp_server.py`) was never updated. It ran\nits scope filter but neither computed the slug nor passed it, so every\nwrite-path evolve through MCP raised the `TypeError`.\n\nSame class as the recent cross-link fix: a required arg added, one call\nsite missed.\n\n## Fix\n\nReplicate the REST A15 slug logic in the MCP scope block and pass it\nthrough:\n- `no_related_ids` when there are no related ids\n- `agent_id_mismatch` / `fleet_id_mismatch` / `all_out_of_scope` when\nthe scope filter drops everything\n- pass `weight_adjustment_skipped_reason=` into `_apply_outcome_to_db`\n\n## Why CI didn't catch it\n\nThe existing `test_mcp_evolve_session_split.py` tests patch\n`_apply_outcome_to_db` with an `AsyncMock`, which **accepts any\nsignature** — so the missing required kwarg never surfaced. This PR adds\na regression test that captures the kwargs the handler actually passes\nand **binds them against the real `_apply_outcome_to_db` signature**, so\na missing required kwarg fails the test. Plus slug-value tests for the\n`no_related_ids` and all-out-of-scope cases.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ruff check` clean ✅\n- `pytest tests/test_mcp_evolve_session_split.py` → 5 passed ✅\n- **Red/green proven:** the new bind guard *fails* when the pass-through\nis removed (reproduces the prod `TypeError`) and *passes* with the fix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T08:09:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b7d0f2f864eee3e16f3df40c10b71c7f2e3c0dc9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b7d0f2f864eee3e16f3df40c10b71c7f2e3c0dc9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b7d0f2f864eee3e16f3df40c10b71c7f2e3c0dc9/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"086427407b08df8475a29927882b01c5c76cb026","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/086427407b08df8475a29927882b01c5c76cb026","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/086427407b08df8475a29927882b01c5c76cb026"}]},{"sha":"086427407b08df8475a29927882b01c5c76cb026","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDA4NjQyNzQwN2IwOGRmODQ3NWEyOTkyNzg4MmIwMWM1Yzc2Y2IwMjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-08T07:46:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T07:46:39Z"},"message":"fix(events): env-scoped topic prefix for PubSubEventBus (no-op default) (#295)\n\n## What\nCross-env Pub/Sub **fan-out**: prod + staging share one GCP project\n(`alpine-theory-469016-c8`) and publish/subscribe against the **same\nnon-env-scoped topics** (`memclaw.memory.*`, `lifecycle.*`, `audit.*`,\n…), so every event is delivered to **both** envs' workers — the foreign\nenv logs `target row missing; ack-dropping`. The EventBus already\nenv-scopes **subscriptions** (`EVENT_BUS_SUBSCRIPTION_PREFIX`) but **not\ntopics** — that asymmetry is the root cause. (Filed as the P0\ncross-env-leakage report; verified real but ~P2 — no data loss, since\neach env has its own subscription and processes its own copy; the\nforeign env just wastes work + logs noise + is a latent cross-env-write\nrisk.)\n\n## This PR — the safe enabling primitive only (strict no-op)\nA `_topic_name()` helper that prefixes the topic id with an env-scoped\n`EVENT_BUS_TOPIC_PREFIX`, applied at **both** the publish (`topic_path`)\nand subscribe (`sub_name`) call sites so an env's publishers and\nsubscribers always agree. **Default (unset/empty) returns the raw topic\nname — byte-identical to today.** `topics.py`, terraform, and the events\nmanifest are untouched, so **this changes nothing in prod on its own**\n(the cross-repo `pubsub-provisioning` validator is unaffected).\n\n- `common/events/pubsub.py` — `topic_prefix` ctor kwarg +\n`_topic_name()` + both call sites.\n- `common/events/factory.py` — read `EVENT_BUS_TOPIC_PREFIX` (empty\ndefault ⇒ no-op).\n- `tests/test_events/test_pubsub_bus.py` — prefixed + no-op coverage\n(`40 passed`; ruff clean).\n\n## Deferred — the actual cutover (NOT in this PR)\nActivating cross-env isolation is a **staged terraform cutover**: create\nper-env topics (`{prefix}--<topic>` + DLQs) in each env's terraform,\ndual-publish, drain, set `EVENT_BUS_TOPIC_PREFIX` per env, flip all\nconsumers (core-api, core-worker, platform-audit-api,\nplatform-admin-api), then delete the old shared topics. Renaming\nterraform topics is destroy-recreate, so it must be phased (big-bang\nwould crash consumers + lose in-flight messages). The terraform topic\nname **must** equal this helper's `{prefix}--{topic}` format.\n\n@erni-a — over to you. This PR is intentionally a no-op until the\ncutover wires `EVENT_BUS_TOPIC_PREFIX`; it just lands the primitive so\nthe cutover is a config/terraform change, not a code change under time\npressure.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f30d6440ee9a0b951565011a39ed24edc1f0e74b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f30d6440ee9a0b951565011a39ed24edc1f0e74b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/086427407b08df8475a29927882b01c5c76cb026","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJnNfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABUoQADrePRsM1o/VNHX+vEckf2dB\nTtk3l7N3l1yVgyLwV4oRZIvh/UHGvMLTyZWtlLDc2HpdTM3M80BhrWyPGiQm4cR9\nTgWzXkSbgHk+lY6Lj/MO6X3fCs16g+NJCJZ0OWFnB2FED3M+f0M42kC7bkA894+Y\nYMNJKSq7z0s2+kHNhhl0mcUGdRvjXiQvNsUHng+seo0AdxBNk6bnzYzM9qrj3kH1\nIKcILZA1smg0QshNnNMXoiK5WiDYJ6N+z6g9yocdvlP9+Jyfm4cBjSWBnOnmlVJa\nMkiTsiVZvAL+69aWe8ZWElqv7E22NVEtZyekT6AnLxLc+uRTh5Q+EAaboWCn6xaW\ns9/S+XjjV0E6mvSuJwlLY3X0qBQRs8Z4jDpxROQ3ZEQ0CF3vx5qmu+A+yasmOjDC\n5zTfkxpaqFLl39psz+Z/nbes/+0kHfcEoHqEL7ys7If4klFqtxhXzpsi+F4lK3pd\nZ0Oy8B55jGBy3NLpykVZyDWmlHp3VbIxL7qRqzQg3OLSlUOeZvQ1ulTIV65F9GnS\n9NGJrFkqgTs3CT8qX4pmg49oGQu8S8FQxhUQyNtd8J/RGG099uIOHXCtjanJNub/\nzuKY59Vy7w5wTo21KWHnFlofvPF6t+8MB8owbbrQ4JPhKYAR1WjrEkKbsrtDoppl\nLFmceHIeYyz0mE7oWY3G\n=/XuE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f30d6440ee9a0b951565011a39ed24edc1f0e74b\nparent 7ddb78b20de6a3f111e935f888a186ff1fa9b880\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1780904799 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780904799 +0300\n\nfix(events): env-scoped topic prefix for PubSubEventBus (no-op default) (#295)\n\n## What\nCross-env Pub/Sub **fan-out**: prod + staging share one GCP project\n(`alpine-theory-469016-c8`) and publish/subscribe against the **same\nnon-env-scoped topics** (`memclaw.memory.*`, `lifecycle.*`, `audit.*`,\n…), so every event is delivered to **both** envs' workers — the foreign\nenv logs `target row missing; ack-dropping`. The EventBus already\nenv-scopes **subscriptions** (`EVENT_BUS_SUBSCRIPTION_PREFIX`) but **not\ntopics** — that asymmetry is the root cause. (Filed as the P0\ncross-env-leakage report; verified real but ~P2 — no data loss, since\neach env has its own subscription and processes its own copy; the\nforeign env just wastes work + logs noise + is a latent cross-env-write\nrisk.)\n\n## This PR — the safe enabling primitive only (strict no-op)\nA `_topic_name()` helper that prefixes the topic id with an env-scoped\n`EVENT_BUS_TOPIC_PREFIX`, applied at **both** the publish (`topic_path`)\nand subscribe (`sub_name`) call sites so an env's publishers and\nsubscribers always agree. **Default (unset/empty) returns the raw topic\nname — byte-identical to today.** `topics.py`, terraform, and the events\nmanifest are untouched, so **this changes nothing in prod on its own**\n(the cross-repo `pubsub-provisioning` validator is unaffected).\n\n- `common/events/pubsub.py` — `topic_prefix` ctor kwarg +\n`_topic_name()` + both call sites.\n- `common/events/factory.py` — read `EVENT_BUS_TOPIC_PREFIX` (empty\ndefault ⇒ no-op).\n- `tests/test_events/test_pubsub_bus.py` — prefixed + no-op coverage\n(`40 passed`; ruff clean).\n\n## Deferred — the actual cutover (NOT in this PR)\nActivating cross-env isolation is a **staged terraform cutover**: create\nper-env topics (`{prefix}--<topic>` + DLQs) in each env's terraform,\ndual-publish, drain, set `EVENT_BUS_TOPIC_PREFIX` per env, flip all\nconsumers (core-api, core-worker, platform-audit-api,\nplatform-admin-api), then delete the old shared topics. Renaming\nterraform topics is destroy-recreate, so it must be phased (big-bang\nwould crash consumers + lose in-flight messages). The terraform topic\nname **must** equal this helper's `{prefix}--{topic}` format.\n\n@erni-a — over to you. This PR is intentionally a no-op until the\ncutover wires `EVENT_BUS_TOPIC_PREFIX`; it just lands the primitive so\nthe cutover is a config/terraform change, not a code change under time\npressure.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T07:46:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/086427407b08df8475a29927882b01c5c76cb026","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/086427407b08df8475a29927882b01c5c76cb026","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/086427407b08df8475a29927882b01c5c76cb026/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7ddb78b20de6a3f111e935f888a186ff1fa9b880","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7ddb78b20de6a3f111e935f888a186ff1fa9b880","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/7ddb78b20de6a3f111e935f888a186ff1fa9b880"}]},{"sha":"7ddb78b20de6a3f111e935f888a186ff1fa9b880","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDdkZGI3OGIyMGRlNmEzZjExMWU5MzVmODg4YTE4NmZmMWZhOWI4ODA","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-08T07:34:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T07:34:30Z"},"message":"fix: return real columns from cross-link insert instead of nonexistent id (#298)\n\n## The error (prod)\n\n```\nError bulk-inserting 1 cross-links for tenant olivier-obuchowski-3d53f3\nasyncpg.exceptions.UndefinedColumnError: column \"id\" does not exist\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\n`DiscoverCrossLinks` inserts into `memory_entity_links` with `RETURNING\nid`, but that table is a **pure junction table** — composite PK\n`(memory_id, entity_id)`, no surrogate `id` column\n(`common/models/entity.py:53-62`). So `RETURNING id` references a column\nthat doesn't exist and Postgres rejects the statement.\n\n**Latent since v1.0.0** (`7456e23`), not a regression. It only surfaced\nnow because (1) the insert branch only fires when a memory has <3 entity\nlinks *and* a similar entity clears the 0.75 threshold *and* text-verify\npasses, and (2) the existing tests mock the DB, so the invalid SQL was\nnever validated against a real schema. Tenant\n`olivier-obuchowski-3d53f3` is the first prod write to reach the branch.\n\n**Blast radius:** non-fatal. The step catches the exception and returns\n`FAILED`; the parent memory write still succeeds. Effect = degraded\ncross-link discovery, no data loss.\n\n## Fix\n\n```diff\n-                    RETURNING id\n+                    RETURNING memory_id, entity_id\n```\n\nBehaviour-preserving for the count: with `ON CONFLICT … DO NOTHING`,\n`RETURNING` only emits actually-inserted rows, so `links_created` stays\naccurate — it just selects columns that exist.\n\n## Test\n\nMock-based tests can't catch a bad column name, so this adds a SQL-shape\nregression test (`test_discover_insert_returns_real_columns_not_id`)\nasserting the INSERT returns `memory_id, entity_id` and never `RETURNING\nid` again — mirroring the existing CAURA-675 guard in the same file.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ruff check` clean ✅\n- `pytest tests/pipeline/test_entity_linking.py\ntests/test_entity_linking_wiring.py` → 10 passed ✅\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"c6d50c3975244d9dab8f23028380b63cd6bfa1f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/c6d50c3975244d9dab8f23028380b63cd6bfa1f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/7ddb78b20de6a3f111e935f888a186ff1fa9b880","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJnCGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYMgQABvlaMz6/g5KIxL8i+LfWNbP\nWXgNBTNQielSPVsVSaedRVecX8bFI5pPx2vdH3EXXg4MOsO+izGiRDC1ypx7iqbK\nfkKbCZyD6nJ2nN+iWLug6rF4oKu+GFK2clHRrrnO984Qx+2xHB/O1D/zWe4JP7Qf\na9o7a+BQ2E1jIxvBE8gdsfuayGz7E70R7jN+5us8RB0RZWI+zo9yP3x20Mpj8yyD\no3E5TV/nF903UhUHcLkBw24QIm3Q/Ep5BIWxSG6ZYMzKEu6EI8OVvocDzuWWFBt5\nMB5BGxx4gwqdWOYHO5A9dNngYVew4dXfF536uD4eKOg3hk8sTQiSy0LRyPYjpYTl\nexhRMw+r1d+56CxwqO0wA8ooAa4g4svxfA+9CJeraQcEL2O92f4gRFxap3FCu8b3\nVMBNyF0Dq4O4VHm+te+enBg/rWv8Ia96yDGnwaTURuHGPPA8NFOifcogRUv/HkyM\nhfRttho0WzquEIRath165tV02aUKq7sB4akYULAKHu0WZUcEgdyQtpMWE1NmDmpv\niKT7IB2JwJZNcYt6OwTXrJTT00192OuQfKbmAH2V9XVsdytsQka10Wmp8T9KBkA3\nCuzpMdx5Br8cGIAbEDGP9e6cVhH7hUAG3fHQGSuPG/6ZXQpY9xV5L2twLFYMthvx\nr/8WaOj8eEXUT1f04eDW\n=qU45\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c6d50c3975244d9dab8f23028380b63cd6bfa1f6\nparent 4f03679ef389c7c31e1ef6c3d31792881eccb600\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780904070 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780904070 +0300\n\nfix: return real columns from cross-link insert instead of nonexistent id (#298)\n\n## The error (prod)\n\n```\nError bulk-inserting 1 cross-links for tenant olivier-obuchowski-3d53f3\nasyncpg.exceptions.UndefinedColumnError: column \"id\" does not exist\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\n`DiscoverCrossLinks` inserts into `memory_entity_links` with `RETURNING\nid`, but that table is a **pure junction table** — composite PK\n`(memory_id, entity_id)`, no surrogate `id` column\n(`common/models/entity.py:53-62`). So `RETURNING id` references a column\nthat doesn't exist and Postgres rejects the statement.\n\n**Latent since v1.0.0** (`7456e23`), not a regression. It only surfaced\nnow because (1) the insert branch only fires when a memory has <3 entity\nlinks *and* a similar entity clears the 0.75 threshold *and* text-verify\npasses, and (2) the existing tests mock the DB, so the invalid SQL was\nnever validated against a real schema. Tenant\n`olivier-obuchowski-3d53f3` is the first prod write to reach the branch.\n\n**Blast radius:** non-fatal. The step catches the exception and returns\n`FAILED`; the parent memory write still succeeds. Effect = degraded\ncross-link discovery, no data loss.\n\n## Fix\n\n```diff\n-                    RETURNING id\n+                    RETURNING memory_id, entity_id\n```\n\nBehaviour-preserving for the count: with `ON CONFLICT … DO NOTHING`,\n`RETURNING` only emits actually-inserted rows, so `links_created` stays\naccurate — it just selects columns that exist.\n\n## Test\n\nMock-based tests can't catch a bad column name, so this adds a SQL-shape\nregression test (`test_discover_insert_returns_real_columns_not_id`)\nasserting the INSERT returns `memory_id, entity_id` and never `RETURNING\nid` again — mirroring the existing CAURA-675 guard in the same file.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ruff check` clean ✅\n- `pytest tests/pipeline/test_entity_linking.py\ntests/test_entity_linking_wiring.py` → 10 passed ✅\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T07:34:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7ddb78b20de6a3f111e935f888a186ff1fa9b880","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/7ddb78b20de6a3f111e935f888a186ff1fa9b880","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7ddb78b20de6a3f111e935f888a186ff1fa9b880/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4f03679ef389c7c31e1ef6c3d31792881eccb600","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4f03679ef389c7c31e1ef6c3d31792881eccb600","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4f03679ef389c7c31e1ef6c3d31792881eccb600"}]},{"sha":"4f03679ef389c7c31e1ef6c3d31792881eccb600","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDRmMDM2NzllZjM4OWM3YzMxZTFlZjZjM2QzMTc5Mjg4MWVjY2I2MDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-08T07:23:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T07:23:26Z"},"message":"fix(events): drop cross-environment Pub/Sub fan-out messages (#297)\n\n## Problem\n\nWhen two environments share one GCP project, they also share its Pub/Sub\ntopic namespace — topic names are not env-scoped\n(`topic_path(project_id, topic)` uses bare names). Each topic has a\nseparate subscription per environment, so Pub/Sub **fans every published\nmessage out to both environments**.\n\nThe foreign-env subscriber then does real work: the core-worker's\n`handle_embed_request` / `handle_enrich_request` call\n`provider.embed(...)` / `enrich_memory(...)` on the **payload content**\n*before* the DB write, then the tenant-scoped `UPDATE … WHERE\ntenant_id/id` no-ops against a row that doesn't exist in that env's\ndatabase. The result is wasted embedding/LLM spend, doubled compute, and\na flood of `target row missing; ack-dropping` logs across the memory,\nlifecycle, audit and suppression topics.\n\n**No data is lost** — each environment has its own subscription and\nsuccessfully processes its own copy; the foreign copy is a duplicate\nthat gets dropped.\n\n## Fix\n\nMake the event bus environment-aware:\n\n- `publish()` stamps every message with a `source_env` Pub/Sub\n**attribute** (an attribute, not a body field, so a later subscription\n`filter` can match it server-side).\n- `_pull_loop` ack-drops any message whose `source_env` differs from\nthis process's env **before decode/dispatch**, so the foreign-env\nhandler — and its provider call — never runs.\n- Env identity resolves from `EVENT_BUS_ENV`, falling back to\n`ENVIRONMENT` (already set per service) → **activates with no infra\nchange**.\n\nThe guard lives in the bus, so it covers **every** topic, not just the\nmemory ones.\n\n### Backward-compatible / safe rollout in any order\nA message with **no** `source_env` attribute is processed exactly as\ntoday. Until every publisher stamps the attribute, unstamped messages\nkeep their current fan-out behaviour rather than being dropped — so\nthere is no data-loss window regardless of deploy order. If neither env\nvar is set the guard is disabled (fail-soft) with a startup warning.\n\n## Verification\n- New tests in `tests/test_events/test_pubsub_bus.py`: attribute\nstamping (+ omission when env unset), env normalization, the foreign-env\ndecision matrix, and `_pull_loop` behaviour (foreign\ndropped+acked+not-dispatched / same-env processed / no-attribute\nbackward-compat).\n- `tests/test_events/` — 78 passed; `mypy` clean on both changed files.\n\n## Follow-up (separate, infra-only)\nOnce `source_env` is confirmed flowing on both envs, recreate each\nsubscription with a server-side `filter` on `attributes.source_env`.\nThat moves the drop server-side (eliminates even the wasted pull) and\nmakes this code guard defense-in-depth. **Must land after this is fully\ndeployed** — adding the filter before publishers stamp the attribute\nwould drop everything.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"f1112bd8a59c7884e452d80a0121dea8c6086357","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f1112bd8a59c7884e452d80a0121dea8c6086357"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/4f03679ef389c7c31e1ef6c3d31792881eccb600","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJm3uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhe8QAGqoxvTcl2ESAP/AYvhpofh9\nkIDp8pbq9/LikW9gMm62cYqEhQBVihcunws9T3kpvP+7dis6FLecbvFIYFtb1ksf\nuhTFgXTcvJfIkEANuh7Lpv+gkO6Aa2gydhyTv4LTtidjbMnu48bdQGQKffYSIYfW\n4kaxDsP9Tpbs5gDI0ThjUsBRKACtgz6ywQM34D1I+hdt7ddWu3EeAoaIcS94RMUr\nOnxBjl9kORJWSbDCcQX+b19+1wBJnH5XnWHnFwEUC6tJxHu1DjowYGo8XCo2APRi\ncH0r0nW5EoKDsva48yDuDHPb5kwFRIrapA5tBK9kT3+UiEiQKB+LaA9HNtiq87JP\ng7rJR8IUvWy164iHAEzySmbCECFP7TT2Fn/y5AskhcKj5VNeGAil74+kYBryy4+B\nhFKcIHC7FqGSGE9isHH+SKaIlgDV5iSv6NzQc2E2jTKZaneHE9Nrt/yZmYEYuh2i\nCgkpjtdVjcvR7F9vw8yRIk//P2mJOzvjEcj4FikkKU8oqntKENfeWebGxo6eauI/\nwtcmvflbwSuZ9qBkhI6Q8ieiyAXUMQEK3LQIvUwsk5GETzbm1SbGm6vCM2SLzy4a\nEFdTJw11d7oNNIFOK5kFNTp/YLYYV/1bq6DJFIAHAf9rmWqPiXA2T23DYrEdrZR9\njJmQqkvL7jtBNwF6yAxw\n=35GP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f1112bd8a59c7884e452d80a0121dea8c6086357\nparent a3532a433ab4ef5032304a2c125251c7c4bfdea5\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1780903406 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780903406 +0300\n\nfix(events): drop cross-environment Pub/Sub fan-out messages (#297)\n\n## Problem\n\nWhen two environments share one GCP project, they also share its Pub/Sub\ntopic namespace — topic names are not env-scoped\n(`topic_path(project_id, topic)` uses bare names). Each topic has a\nseparate subscription per environment, so Pub/Sub **fans every published\nmessage out to both environments**.\n\nThe foreign-env subscriber then does real work: the core-worker's\n`handle_embed_request` / `handle_enrich_request` call\n`provider.embed(...)` / `enrich_memory(...)` on the **payload content**\n*before* the DB write, then the tenant-scoped `UPDATE … WHERE\ntenant_id/id` no-ops against a row that doesn't exist in that env's\ndatabase. The result is wasted embedding/LLM spend, doubled compute, and\na flood of `target row missing; ack-dropping` logs across the memory,\nlifecycle, audit and suppression topics.\n\n**No data is lost** — each environment has its own subscription and\nsuccessfully processes its own copy; the foreign copy is a duplicate\nthat gets dropped.\n\n## Fix\n\nMake the event bus environment-aware:\n\n- `publish()` stamps every message with a `source_env` Pub/Sub\n**attribute** (an attribute, not a body field, so a later subscription\n`filter` can match it server-side).\n- `_pull_loop` ack-drops any message whose `source_env` differs from\nthis process's env **before decode/dispatch**, so the foreign-env\nhandler — and its provider call — never runs.\n- Env identity resolves from `EVENT_BUS_ENV`, falling back to\n`ENVIRONMENT` (already set per service) → **activates with no infra\nchange**.\n\nThe guard lives in the bus, so it covers **every** topic, not just the\nmemory ones.\n\n### Backward-compatible / safe rollout in any order\nA message with **no** `source_env` attribute is processed exactly as\ntoday. Until every publisher stamps the attribute, unstamped messages\nkeep their current fan-out behaviour rather than being dropped — so\nthere is no data-loss window regardless of deploy order. If neither env\nvar is set the guard is disabled (fail-soft) with a startup warning.\n\n## Verification\n- New tests in `tests/test_events/test_pubsub_bus.py`: attribute\nstamping (+ omission when env unset), env normalization, the foreign-env\ndecision matrix, and `_pull_loop` behaviour (foreign\ndropped+acked+not-dispatched / same-env processed / no-attribute\nbackward-compat).\n- `tests/test_events/` — 78 passed; `mypy` clean on both changed files.\n\n## Follow-up (separate, infra-only)\nOnce `source_env` is confirmed flowing on both envs, recreate each\nsubscription with a server-side `filter` on `attributes.source_env`.\nThat moves the drop server-side (eliminates even the wasted pull) and\nmakes this code guard defense-in-depth. **Must land after this is fully\ndeployed** — adding the filter before publishers stamp the attribute\nwould drop everything.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T07:23:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4f03679ef389c7c31e1ef6c3d31792881eccb600","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4f03679ef389c7c31e1ef6c3d31792881eccb600","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4f03679ef389c7c31e1ef6c3d31792881eccb600/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a3532a433ab4ef5032304a2c125251c7c4bfdea5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a3532a433ab4ef5032304a2c125251c7c4bfdea5","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a3532a433ab4ef5032304a2c125251c7c4bfdea5"}]},{"sha":"a3532a433ab4ef5032304a2c125251c7c4bfdea5","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGEzNTMyYTQzM2FiNGVmNTAzMjMwNGEyYzEyNTI1MWM3YzRiZmRlYTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-07T19:25:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-07T19:25:41Z"},"message":"fix(plugin): bound resolveTenantId fetch with AbortSignal timeout (CAURA-000) (#292)\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Root cause**: `resolveTenantId` (`plugin/src/env.ts:85`) calls\n`fetch(/auth/verify)` with no signal. When the backend accepts the TCP\nconnection but never replies (slow proxy, half-open conn, etc.), the\nfetch hangs indefinitely. The `TypeError` short-circuit only catches DNS\n/ ECONNREFUSED (undici's \"fetch failed\" shape) — it does NOT catch\naccepted-but-unanswered connections.\n- **Why it stalls everything**: `ensureTenantId` is on the hot path of\nevery lifecycle hook (`ingest` / `assemble` / `afterTurn`) and the\nresult is memoized via `_tenantPromise`. So every concurrent caller\nstalls behind the one in-flight hung fetch. Observed downstream as an\nOpenClaw `stalled_agent_run` diagnostic (`embedded_run age=156s,\nqueueDepth=4`) in a customer install.\n- **Fix**: Add `signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10_000)` to the fetch —\nmatching the plugin's other raw-fetch sites (`agent-auth.ts`,\n`heartbeat.ts`) for a consistent worst-case per-attempt latency. Same\nfix applied to `fetchToolDescriptions` for hygiene (cold path, less\nimpact, but a hung registration still blocks plugin load).\n- **Log clarity**: `AbortError` is now distinguished from generic errors\nin the warn/error lines — operators can tell \"backend slow\" from\n\"backend unreachable\" without a code review.\n- Plugin version bumped 2.8.1 → 2.8.2.\n\n## Customer impact\n\nReplaces an unbounded stall (observed: 156s+) with a bounded retry\nsequence: worst-case ~44s (3 retries × 10s timeout + 2/4/8s backoff),\nafter which `ensureTenantId` throws and the lifecycle hook returns\ncleanly. The customer's hung sessions will no longer pile up behind a\nhung tenant resolution.\n\nThis does NOT fix the underlying network/backend issue that triggered\nthe hang — but it converts an unrecoverable stall into a normal error\npath that OpenClaw can surface and recover from.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` in `plugin/` — 281/281 pass (was 280, +1 for the new\nstructural test pinning that fetch is invoked with an AbortSignal)\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_plugin_source_manifest.py` — 11/11 pass (no new\nfiles, manifest unchanged)\n- [x] `tsc` clean (run via `npm test`'s `tsc &&` prefix)\n- [ ] Customer redeploy: pull `core-api:v2.12.2` (when release-please\ncuts it), reinstall plugin on each agent VM, restart gateway\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"349397c4995457e208385a44d6f9597b8174b98a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/349397c4995457e208385a44d6f9597b8174b98a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/a3532a433ab4ef5032304a2c125251c7c4bfdea5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJcW1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASQkQAH+JAKs59aVMfiRSwg9urW1Z\ncCDsFTvDEP1g7HrZewp0UAfQaiwSYRJ1P1Mf/hDI8dLMNaCvFxnCO80qr3syme/l\nC+qPolfUQcZI5e2u4KdolEKyU2JHWkjiE0Io7hsxyhGfM2QUddTEoz4o8/kWoEac\n2ey6uT++aihpD6OcV3BcQLXvQI5fH83TquoTHTwA805geH2TUu4l0QXiMYQpJI6X\nLxj0SQLE2Uf/Iv8klSXIZe9OEFEjUSsThIyt6qd2o7DqoS4p4B74zJo2IsfUdGsd\n6ZkAKuXEynK3f1WId6vSaC/BVk4tmU6E8OpW3R5QXg/CJm8ynk4ifMKmZXxKpRFE\nYnf3+h6EBOR44+QNM8qDZa63rAS0ql2l9BjS5deGhzDUiiPubr9VQSOLH7xmKZcw\n26mTzVpm6NtXQH0mqm2odqLD52vlcieMuBNuxkq8pHt2LBFtsHL2lJG6umObuAIu\nzr8MeOAINwdl7bJKoKI4hN9+MPDeyNl2YY04wUVkgAIshmiaOHlxrt35cjhjm1GP\nROSZnin4ZqoZtt7R8fIo7TqrwNLH8bmYSzqqKHOnyuLZz7+afdu2mnACu1h8ZObZ\n1dxbCS3EXizH80JdfFmDfXTrvlk31NVSF94xxhJZH+YegpmZBmDeGat7zOvVIBKt\n3LbmeLj4RhZPm2DfS6h2\n=GJNr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 349397c4995457e208385a44d6f9597b8174b98a\nparent 0991cef1c9aa001af6557d38ee7098e3b9f20b5a\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780860341 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780860341 +0300\n\nfix(plugin): bound resolveTenantId fetch with AbortSignal timeout (CAURA-000) (#292)\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Root cause**: `resolveTenantId` (`plugin/src/env.ts:85`) calls\n`fetch(/auth/verify)` with no signal. When the backend accepts the TCP\nconnection but never replies (slow proxy, half-open conn, etc.), the\nfetch hangs indefinitely. The `TypeError` short-circuit only catches DNS\n/ ECONNREFUSED (undici's \"fetch failed\" shape) — it does NOT catch\naccepted-but-unanswered connections.\n- **Why it stalls everything**: `ensureTenantId` is on the hot path of\nevery lifecycle hook (`ingest` / `assemble` / `afterTurn`) and the\nresult is memoized via `_tenantPromise`. So every concurrent caller\nstalls behind the one in-flight hung fetch. Observed downstream as an\nOpenClaw `stalled_agent_run` diagnostic (`embedded_run age=156s,\nqueueDepth=4`) in a customer install.\n- **Fix**: Add `signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10_000)` to the fetch —\nmatching the plugin's other raw-fetch sites (`agent-auth.ts`,\n`heartbeat.ts`) for a consistent worst-case per-attempt latency. Same\nfix applied to `fetchToolDescriptions` for hygiene (cold path, less\nimpact, but a hung registration still blocks plugin load).\n- **Log clarity**: `AbortError` is now distinguished from generic errors\nin the warn/error lines — operators can tell \"backend slow\" from\n\"backend unreachable\" without a code review.\n- Plugin version bumped 2.8.1 → 2.8.2.\n\n## Customer impact\n\nReplaces an unbounded stall (observed: 156s+) with a bounded retry\nsequence: worst-case ~44s (3 retries × 10s timeout + 2/4/8s backoff),\nafter which `ensureTenantId` throws and the lifecycle hook returns\ncleanly. The customer's hung sessions will no longer pile up behind a\nhung tenant resolution.\n\nThis does NOT fix the underlying network/backend issue that triggered\nthe hang — but it converts an unrecoverable stall into a normal error\npath that OpenClaw can surface and recover from.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` in `plugin/` — 281/281 pass (was 280, +1 for the new\nstructural test pinning that fetch is invoked with an AbortSignal)\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_plugin_source_manifest.py` — 11/11 pass (no new\nfiles, manifest unchanged)\n- [x] `tsc` clean (run via `npm test`'s `tsc &&` prefix)\n- [ ] Customer redeploy: pull `core-api:v2.12.2` (when release-please\ncuts it), reinstall plugin on each agent VM, restart gateway\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-07T19:25:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a3532a433ab4ef5032304a2c125251c7c4bfdea5","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a3532a433ab4ef5032304a2c125251c7c4bfdea5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a3532a433ab4ef5032304a2c125251c7c4bfdea5/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0991cef1c9aa001af6557d38ee7098e3b9f20b5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0991cef1c9aa001af6557d38ee7098e3b9f20b5a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0991cef1c9aa001af6557d38ee7098e3b9f20b5a"}]},{"sha":"0991cef1c9aa001af6557d38ee7098e3b9f20b5a","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDA5OTFjZWYxYzlhYTAwMWFmNjU1N2QzOGVlNzA5OGUzYjlmMjBiNWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-07T17:38:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-07T17:38:50Z"},"message":"feat(embedding): let the platform singleton target a self-hosted endpoint (#291)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe core-worker embeds documents **exclusively** through the platform\nembedding singleton (`core_worker/consumer.py::handle_embed_request` →\n`get_platform_embedding`), never the registry. `init_platform_embedding`\nbuilt `OpenAIEmbeddingProvider(api_key, model)` with **no `base_url`**,\nso the worker write path could only ever reach `api.openai.com` — there\nwas no env var to point it at a self-hosted OpenAI-compatible endpoint\n(TEI, vLLM).\n\nThis is the gap behind a subtle failure mode: pointing core-api at TEI\nvia the registry's `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL` moves only the **query**\npath. The **write** path (and thus the stored corpus) silently stays on\nthe old vendor — and cross-vendor cosine is ~random, so search recall\ncollapses.\n\n## Change\n\n`init_platform_embedding` now also reads `PLATFORM_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL`,\n`PLATFORM_EMBEDDING_SEND_DIMENSIONS`, and\n`PLATFORM_EMBEDDING_TRUNCATE_TO_DIM` and threads them into the provider,\nwith the same two fail-loud guards the registry uses (the `base_url` ⊕\n`send_dimensions` misconfigurations). A small `_reject_openai_config`\nhelper single-sources the `openai-embedding-config` error tag across the\nrejection arms.\n\n**Backward compatible:** with `PLATFORM_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL` unset,\nbehaviour is identical to today (hosted OpenAI, `dimensions=` enabled).\n\n## Why\n\nUnblocks pointing the platform/worker embedding tier at a self-hosted\nTEI/bge-m3 endpoint — the staging local-embedder rollout (Cloud Run GPU)\nneeds this before a coherent query+write cutover. Same knobs the\nregistry already exposes, so both tiers can target the same endpoint.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- New `TestPlatformEmbeddingSelfHosted` group in\n`tests/test_platform_providers.py`: TEI provider built with `base_url` +\n`send_dimensions=false`; hosted-OpenAI default unchanged; and the four\nreject paths (base_url+send_dimensions,\nsend_dimensions-false-without-base_url, invalid bool, non-int truncate).\n- `tests/test_platform_providers.py` — **32 passed**. Embedding test\nsurface (platform + service + stampede + cache + qemb) — **54 passed**.\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean on changed files; `mypy`\nintroduces 0 new errors in `_platform.py`.\n- Note: full repo suite / CI not run locally — CI is the gate here.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2dafc62c70e11fc1a6c743c3cb284b94fda55f0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/2dafc62c70e11fc1a6c743c3cb284b94fda55f0b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/0991cef1c9aa001af6557d38ee7098e3b9f20b5a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJayqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwmUQAD7zYBGeHjFnvsLxZfNEQmvU\nufiPmiHloh2VhBqSOAL4xUAB3Dj82bLmiLKtc+X6VnkeETX/pGarw88uOMzIayiV\nBJO5nKjMmC84/8wD1vOxw/V6uOcIbWJrvboEBXH5c0tU2m/01cOAf9zEHWs0tzdx\naIYf5DyoWAV/AAN4nw6cZgInM8iu3o4AzPS3+pjD1MsF1s0epJQ40JcGcn1OYxmu\n0iBEG1J3EMlH5QJd+mCzfmQvq97cl5dvwe05N/ncfuNqnSYpw5ObhVuFWgwf2C/5\ntABXi0mS56WCmUqOuOZ1esSl1z73gm30wCmNRD8kxW1Hcjr23nW8HBk7u2Hs+6Uy\nLfInJ65MHLEAkcoegQZs/KF7bd+ukPipsQKFussz2ExMa+Q1EtyRUMS2PaIAiY4z\nS0Ia57IX0mwX5LDo3S41pfOWUcrP/grhKRXtP9uB/5oIPcYqq38/snefiTm0ZvJI\nwAeGFalKFp4oN2o4srftjm0w72K4nb52SExy+LA2uQ0H3MxsRSPb9cTYlp7EEF5l\nrzIydUMfnfbZTgYCWYEsorTio+N2/RIk/r0uZs0UiOJhx78WGjHvAlgQKcXplCxs\nERkyQ9d1x07sxG+A5OSyGCteFhKaSLBG3VS9AeK2QAGqW0tchebBIrARDnWlQwNU\n5qXjFLm7s2NEBoVf5AFb\n=tA08\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2dafc62c70e11fc1a6c743c3cb284b94fda55f0b\nparent b61a4159f816a9cf4a26495adc133e89300ea98e\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1780853930 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780853930 +0300\n\nfeat(embedding): let the platform singleton target a self-hosted endpoint (#291)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe core-worker embeds documents **exclusively** through the platform\nembedding singleton (`core_worker/consumer.py::handle_embed_request` →\n`get_platform_embedding`), never the registry. `init_platform_embedding`\nbuilt `OpenAIEmbeddingProvider(api_key, model)` with **no `base_url`**,\nso the worker write path could only ever reach `api.openai.com` — there\nwas no env var to point it at a self-hosted OpenAI-compatible endpoint\n(TEI, vLLM).\n\nThis is the gap behind a subtle failure mode: pointing core-api at TEI\nvia the registry's `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL` moves only the **query**\npath. The **write** path (and thus the stored corpus) silently stays on\nthe old vendor — and cross-vendor cosine is ~random, so search recall\ncollapses.\n\n## Change\n\n`init_platform_embedding` now also reads `PLATFORM_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL`,\n`PLATFORM_EMBEDDING_SEND_DIMENSIONS`, and\n`PLATFORM_EMBEDDING_TRUNCATE_TO_DIM` and threads them into the provider,\nwith the same two fail-loud guards the registry uses (the `base_url` ⊕\n`send_dimensions` misconfigurations). A small `_reject_openai_config`\nhelper single-sources the `openai-embedding-config` error tag across the\nrejection arms.\n\n**Backward compatible:** with `PLATFORM_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL` unset,\nbehaviour is identical to today (hosted OpenAI, `dimensions=` enabled).\n\n## Why\n\nUnblocks pointing the platform/worker embedding tier at a self-hosted\nTEI/bge-m3 endpoint — the staging local-embedder rollout (Cloud Run GPU)\nneeds this before a coherent query+write cutover. Same knobs the\nregistry already exposes, so both tiers can target the same endpoint.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- New `TestPlatformEmbeddingSelfHosted` group in\n`tests/test_platform_providers.py`: TEI provider built with `base_url` +\n`send_dimensions=false`; hosted-OpenAI default unchanged; and the four\nreject paths (base_url+send_dimensions,\nsend_dimensions-false-without-base_url, invalid bool, non-int truncate).\n- `tests/test_platform_providers.py` — **32 passed**. Embedding test\nsurface (platform + service + stampede + cache + qemb) — **54 passed**.\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean on changed files; `mypy`\nintroduces 0 new errors in `_platform.py`.\n- Note: full repo suite / CI not run locally — CI is the gate here.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-07T17:38:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0991cef1c9aa001af6557d38ee7098e3b9f20b5a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0991cef1c9aa001af6557d38ee7098e3b9f20b5a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0991cef1c9aa001af6557d38ee7098e3b9f20b5a/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b61a4159f816a9cf4a26495adc133e89300ea98e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b61a4159f816a9cf4a26495adc133e89300ea98e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b61a4159f816a9cf4a26495adc133e89300ea98e"}]},{"sha":"b61a4159f816a9cf4a26495adc133e89300ea98e","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGI2MWE0MTU5ZjgxNmE5Y2Y0YTI2NDk1YWRjMTMzZTg5MzAwZWE5OGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-07T12:29:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-07T12:29:12Z"},"message":"chore(plugin): reconcile release-please manifest to 2.8.1 + bump auto-upgrade floor (#289)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #288 (`chore: release main`, merged today) cut **backend-v2.12.1**,\nbut the **plugin release state drifted**:\n\n| Source | Plugin version |\n|--------|---------------|\n| `plugin/package.json`, `openclaw.plugin.json`, `src/version.ts` (on\n`main`) | **2.8.1** |\n| `.release-please-manifest.json` | **2.8.0** |\n| Latest tag / GitHub release | **2.8.0** |\n| `plugin-v2.8.1` tag | ❌ does not exist |\n\nThe served plugin version was bumped to **2.8.1** out-of-band inside\n#286 (`fix(plugin): thread per-call session context into\nresolveAgentId`) rather than via a release-please PR, so the manifest\nnever advanced and no `plugin-v2.8.1` was tagged.\n\nAdditionally the plugin-release **floor invariant is violated**:\n`MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION = 2.7.0` while the served plugin on\n`main` is `2.8.1`. Per the invariant the served version must equal the\nfloor, or manifest-aware fleet nodes don't converge on the intended\nversion.\n\n## What\n\n- `.release-please-manifest.json`: `plugin` **2.8.0 → 2.8.1** (align\nrelease-please state with the already-bumped files)\n- `core-api/src/core_api/version_compat.py`:\n`MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION` **2.7.0 → 2.8.1** (floor companion,\nmoves in lockstep)\n- `MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY_PLUGIN_VERSION` (2.6.0) unchanged.\n\nEnd state is internally consistent: served files == manifest == floor ==\n**2.8.1**.\n\n## Reviewer decision — two valid reconciliations\n\nThis PR takes **Option A (reconcile manifest forward to 2.8.1)**.\nTrade-off: release-please then treats 2.8.1 as already released, so **no\n`plugin-v2.8.1` tag / changelog entry** is produced for the #286 fix.\n\n**Option B** (not taken): revert the three plugin files back to `2.8.0`,\nlet release-please open a normal plugin release PR (2.8.0 → 2.8.1) so a\nreal `plugin-v2.8.1` tag + changelog is cut on merge; the floor bump\nhere still applies. Choose B if you want the tagged release/changelog.\n\n## Not for auto-merge\nPer repo workflow, leaving the merge decision to a human. CI (incl.\n`check:version` = version.ts ↔ package.json, both already 2.8.1) should\npass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a3422a305cfedc37ef1604d6b68dedf94522a418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a3422a305cfedc37ef1604d6b68dedf94522a418"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b61a4159f816a9cf4a26495adc133e89300ea98e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJWQYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARxUQAA+wCw969pahZV8WPU/PRZAH\nn3X2AWm1OL2L2JX3rTleYDwEJ+epDQAqUp7pqpkXMRsqEESBLFn8zdVEgUvE+Zwb\nJ2zwuatC5FJJsme/A3rcCXPo6SwuAah86oVZfDy7Saz+Hf5lLzhptzsT57RLDBkN\naMtmyApaxk7YkhX8NtvtsMU4mykETNg9GfO6CG0O5X5jo5u41On56kf5rNja4JJ7\n2lTXxaoLN1cZo2xeFDey/TxOzliZxqoUdCHhwv8KjWC6npSZfVBY+b5BCcTaG2SM\nLTavX0YMwl/p1HqIzlNvHfie5T3AzP2JlBhZmpUobWbeXRYEeRtz5a0NJVjx8HHj\n+90xYh81XoxL0EervPzWxCIZ6l4AdoapemfdFuVcmCV4a2b63rKgqz1COggXXhpH\nAccFUscRniO9pbdwQ6RSj6xehf9ozHVP9LMUn0hVpsh8+H9x8H6h211V7v/MwrQ7\nTINlvs2QtajBK8t4xYOKqJoV+WadSLBvNfb95qHKaUVWW3msbGRAx1C7D7qvZo4o\nnthtj9fV+z8xuAbWSalm8AZ3ruRawvZOTW/CTWr1f1u7+vZdKrswRKHj9tT4Hk9N\ntbGuFrtrSJ0PFz4inRwAg7486CHgdZnHHkwNLbbnBLcdTNkKQn7l2wO6Hh6JZYLD\nplRtiqGdfL8isW+MYkF4\n=im5z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a3422a305cfedc37ef1604d6b68dedf94522a418\nparent c49203bc8f5bf617b6785ce1f45396c610b28988\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780835352 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780835352 +0300\n\nchore(plugin): reconcile release-please manifest to 2.8.1 + bump auto-upgrade floor (#289)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #288 (`chore: release main`, merged today) cut **backend-v2.12.1**,\nbut the **plugin release state drifted**:\n\n| Source | Plugin version |\n|--------|---------------|\n| `plugin/package.json`, `openclaw.plugin.json`, `src/version.ts` (on\n`main`) | **2.8.1** |\n| `.release-please-manifest.json` | **2.8.0** |\n| Latest tag / GitHub release | **2.8.0** |\n| `plugin-v2.8.1` tag | ❌ does not exist |\n\nThe served plugin version was bumped to **2.8.1** out-of-band inside\n#286 (`fix(plugin): thread per-call session context into\nresolveAgentId`) rather than via a release-please PR, so the manifest\nnever advanced and no `plugin-v2.8.1` was tagged.\n\nAdditionally the plugin-release **floor invariant is violated**:\n`MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION = 2.7.0` while the served plugin on\n`main` is `2.8.1`. Per the invariant the served version must equal the\nfloor, or manifest-aware fleet nodes don't converge on the intended\nversion.\n\n## What\n\n- `.release-please-manifest.json`: `plugin` **2.8.0 → 2.8.1** (align\nrelease-please state with the already-bumped files)\n- `core-api/src/core_api/version_compat.py`:\n`MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION` **2.7.0 → 2.8.1** (floor companion,\nmoves in lockstep)\n- `MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY_PLUGIN_VERSION` (2.6.0) unchanged.\n\nEnd state is internally consistent: served files == manifest == floor ==\n**2.8.1**.\n\n## Reviewer decision — two valid reconciliations\n\nThis PR takes **Option A (reconcile manifest forward to 2.8.1)**.\nTrade-off: release-please then treats 2.8.1 as already released, so **no\n`plugin-v2.8.1` tag / changelog entry** is produced for the #286 fix.\n\n**Option B** (not taken): revert the three plugin files back to `2.8.0`,\nlet release-please open a normal plugin release PR (2.8.0 → 2.8.1) so a\nreal `plugin-v2.8.1` tag + changelog is cut on merge; the floor bump\nhere still applies. Choose B if you want the tagged release/changelog.\n\n## Not for auto-merge\nPer repo workflow, leaving the merge decision to a human. CI (incl.\n`check:version` = version.ts ↔ package.json, both already 2.8.1) should\npass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-07T12:29:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b61a4159f816a9cf4a26495adc133e89300ea98e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b61a4159f816a9cf4a26495adc133e89300ea98e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b61a4159f816a9cf4a26495adc133e89300ea98e/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c49203bc8f5bf617b6785ce1f45396c610b28988","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c49203bc8f5bf617b6785ce1f45396c610b28988","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c49203bc8f5bf617b6785ce1f45396c610b28988"}]},{"sha":"c49203bc8f5bf617b6785ce1f45396c610b28988","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGM0OTIwM2JjOGY1YmY2MTdiNjc4NWNlMWY0NTM5NmM2MTBiMjg5ODg","commit":{"author":{"name":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","email":"265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-07T11:38:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-07T11:38:22Z"},"message":"chore: release main (#288)\n\n:robot: I have created a release *beep* *boop*\n---\n\n\n<details><summary>backend: 2.12.1</summary>\n\n##\n[2.12.1](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/backend-v2.12.0...backend-v2.12.1)\n(2026-06-07)\n\n\n### Documentation\n\n* **contributing:** warn about commit subjects that break release-please\n([#285](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/285))\n([ea829db](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ea829db0bd8d21b359c418d14b43e3ea0e29d5c3))\n\n\n### Code Refactoring\n\n* rename cryptic sp to search_params in ClassifyQuery\n([#287](https://github.c