ve created a release *beep* *boop*\n---\n\n\n<details><summary>backend: 2.12.1</summary>\n\n##\n[2.12.1](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/backend-v2.12.0...backend-v2.12.1)\n(2026-06-07)\n\n\n### Documentation\n\n* **contributing:** warn about commit subjects that break release-please\n([#285](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/285))\n([ea829db](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ea829db0bd8d21b359c418d14b43e3ea0e29d5c3))\n\n\n### Code Refactoring\n\n* rename cryptic sp to search_params in ClassifyQuery\n([#287](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/287))\n([bad3109](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/bad3109da265f13507532484f2c9dd892f8dd8af))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-07T11:38:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c49203bc8f5bf617b6785ce1f45396c610b28988","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c49203bc8f5bf617b6785ce1f45396c610b28988","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c49203bc8f5bf617b6785ce1f45396c610b28988/comments","author":{"login":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","id":265395343,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9Gcjw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229147182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/caura-deploy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ea829db0bd8d21b359c418d14b43e3ea0e29d5c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ea829db0bd8d21b359c418d14b43e3ea0e29d5c3","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ea829db0bd8d21b359c418d14b43e3ea0e29d5c3"}]},{"sha":"ea829db0bd8d21b359c418d14b43e3ea0e29d5c3","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGVhODI5ZGIwYmQ4ZDIxYjM1OWM0MThkMTRiNDNlM2VhMGUyOWQ1YzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-07T11:34:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-07T11:34:40Z"},"message":"docs(contributing): warn about commit subjects that break release-please (#285)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a 'Common parser breakers' subsection to `CONTRIBUTING.md`'s\ncommit-messages guidance. Documents three real failure modes that have\ncaused release-please to skip commits — including one that **currently\nblocks the next release PR from being opened**.\n\n## Context\n\nAfter `backend-v2.12.0` (May 28), three commits landed on `main`:\n\n| SHA | Title | Why release-please skipped it |\n|---|---|---|\n| 094b9594 | `CAURA-699 fix(enrichment): … …` | Leading ticket id +\nUnicode ellipsis |\n| 7e1bcde1 | `CAURA-132 chore(contradiction): …` | Leading ticket id;\n`chore:` also doesn't trigger |\n| ea039109 | `Reword fleet-scope 403s …` | No conventional prefix |\n\nResult: `release-please` ran on every push and reported `Considering: 0\ncommits` → no release PR opened → CAURA-132 diagnostic logs sit\nunreleased → wet-test verification of CAURA-128/129/130/131 stays\nblocked.\n\nThis PR is the unblocker: a clean `docs:` commit that release-please\nWILL parse, sweeping the post-v2.12.0 SHA range into the next release\nPR. The actual content (warning about the three parser breakers) means\nthe failure class is documented for everyone going forward.\n\n## What the new subsection covers\n\n1. **Leading ticket identifier** (`CAURA-NNN feat(scope): …`) — the\ndominant pattern in recent PRs and the proximate cause of the current\nrelease-please block.\n2. **Unicode ellipsis (`…`, U+2026)** — GitHub's squash-merge UI can\nintroduce this on long titles. Bit us on CAURA-699.\n3. **Non-ASCII punctuation generally** (em-dashes, smart quotes) —\nadjacent failure class, already flagged by `ruff` in code comments. Adds\nconsistency.\n\nPlus a small strengthening of the existing squash-merge note: a single\nun-parseable subject in the post-tag window can block the whole next\nrelease.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] `CONTRIBUTING.md` renders cleanly in GitHub's markdown preview.\n- [x] No code touched.\n- [x] DCO sign-off.\n\n## Rollback\n\nSingle `git revert`. Pure docs.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"ef4eb5c84f411a327e5246f00a811cbac080898d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ef4eb5c84f411a327e5246f00a811cbac080898d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ea829db0bd8d21b359c418d14b43e3ea0e29d5c3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJVdQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABUwQABYBn/9zD33bPyk+EEYjZ2gs\nqUEF1VusSanNq3DHqYri6LP6aZt+S4NnpXbQJVF006POmIy2nGV8YL+vILtKEOCC\nMEbH4wpQK/cWP/ZnXPabX8Ctvt4c0b5+KeBWiKGxbC+CZUfw6P/DV+QNUYnE2RE/\nBMIVy8IYAgAQunuPzcZLJETTSq+hUvpGKUxcRIsYEKnCbozZh3UdyMav8baGXjZf\nfheb/TDppwAu2NWD7xy9zkI1WZOhotmAB+3xP4/wmm0xcENO169AvzIFGR4EFGlq\nt9DmUw+tZq2B+AIgEJaqCXrFuoBQUlg9tQQQMCCQwnQvHJrPwA58ZlqFRRqHDiP2\n1IRpTcK9A8UQBDbKzXql9d5twqUfIMBtyS2Jgd8OY70aNZ7NvhH4E6mphLHJMD1+\nB4C5RV4T+/0qH1HbpaPGKGCoQQbDyt3+wUb7gWpHjg8y7h3rwJHMkUCv2Qz4Q2t5\nHtnGZsvLnHK7o9Wu6vE+KVPiKuywIXGXygtibjGqIQ1OUaV9AkTtitYuZNMhxAhB\naAMC/xQUvqJ6B9QCwTDGpLwlIy+zZ88IDlWMhIg9Nki8XTDvfS2eRLLkixZluj9k\nLgGjQtlPNvxT2gk5AWOZz+alz+n33Q1pZLBFT5nTn1PUZ9w5RG6qZkaeG9mJtUbA\na6/TLbQHD3pSX9VePPPu\n=vig2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ef4eb5c84f411a327e5246f00a811cbac080898d\nparent e2a8d1ea8e1d32206ec1769c20c9bfc7334540dd\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780832080 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780832080 +0300\n\ndocs(contributing): warn about commit subjects that break release-please (#285)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a 'Common parser breakers' subsection to `CONTRIBUTING.md`'s\ncommit-messages guidance. Documents three real failure modes that have\ncaused release-please to skip commits — including one that **currently\nblocks the next release PR from being opened**.\n\n## Context\n\nAfter `backend-v2.12.0` (May 28), three commits landed on `main`:\n\n| SHA | Title | Why release-please skipped it |\n|---|---|---|\n| 094b9594 | `CAURA-699 fix(enrichment): … …` | Leading ticket id +\nUnicode ellipsis |\n| 7e1bcde1 | `CAURA-132 chore(contradiction): …` | Leading ticket id;\n`chore:` also doesn't trigger |\n| ea039109 | `Reword fleet-scope 403s …` | No conventional prefix |\n\nResult: `release-please` ran on every push and reported `Considering: 0\ncommits` → no release PR opened → CAURA-132 diagnostic logs sit\nunreleased → wet-test verification of CAURA-128/129/130/131 stays\nblocked.\n\nThis PR is the unblocker: a clean `docs:` commit that release-please\nWILL parse, sweeping the post-v2.12.0 SHA range into the next release\nPR. The actual content (warning about the three parser breakers) means\nthe failure class is documented for everyone going forward.\n\n## What the new subsection covers\n\n1. **Leading ticket identifier** (`CAURA-NNN feat(scope): …`) — the\ndominant pattern in recent PRs and the proximate cause of the current\nrelease-please block.\n2. **Unicode ellipsis (`…`, U+2026)** — GitHub's squash-merge UI can\nintroduce this on long titles. Bit us on CAURA-699.\n3. **Non-ASCII punctuation generally** (em-dashes, smart quotes) —\nadjacent failure class, already flagged by `ruff` in code comments. Adds\nconsistency.\n\nPlus a small strengthening of the existing squash-merge note: a single\nun-parseable subject in the post-tag window can block the whole next\nrelease.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] `CONTRIBUTING.md` renders cleanly in GitHub's markdown preview.\n- [x] No code touched.\n- [x] DCO sign-off.\n\n## Rollback\n\nSingle `git revert`. Pure docs.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-07T11:34:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ea829db0bd8d21b359c418d14b43e3ea0e29d5c3","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ea829db0bd8d21b359c418d14b43e3ea0e29d5c3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ea829db0bd8d21b359c418d14b43e3ea0e29d5c3/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e2a8d1ea8e1d32206ec1769c20c9bfc7334540dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e2a8d1ea8e1d32206ec1769c20c9bfc7334540dd","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e2a8d1ea8e1d32206ec1769c20c9bfc7334540dd"}]},{"sha":"e2a8d1ea8e1d32206ec1769c20c9bfc7334540dd","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGUyYThkMWVhOGUxZDMyMjA2ZWMxNzY5YzIwYzliZmM3MzM0NTQwZGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-07T11:31:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-07T11:31:17Z"},"message":"fix(plugin): thread per-call session context into resolveAgentId (CAURA-000) (#286)\n\n## Summary\n\nCustomer report 2026-06-02: `webclaw` agent gateway emitting `[memclaw]\nCould not resolve agent ID — using install-default 'main-e5366d79a926'`\n4-5 times per turn. Resolver was falling back to install-default on\nevery per-turn `assemble` call (and `ingest`), not just at bootstrap.\n\n**Root cause:** OpenClaw 2026.5.4 invokes\n`contextEngine.assemble({sessionId, sessionKey, messages, tokenBudget,\nmodel})` with `sessionKey` in the canonical `\"agent:NAME:CHANNEL:...\"`\nform. Our `resolveAgentId` helper parses `parts[1]` to recover the agent\nname. But 3 of our 6 `resolveAgentId` call sites passed only\n`this.config` (the factory-time `factoryCtx` wrapper — `{config,\nagentDir, workspaceDir}`, no `sessionKey`). The per-call `params` was\ndropped on the floor.\n\n**User-visible effect:** `assemble`'s identity block (`**Your\nidentity**: agent_id=\\`...\\``) carried `main-<installId>` instead of the\nreal agent name. The LLM saw the wrong `agent_id` every turn and\npropagated it into downstream `memclaw_write` / `memclaw_recall` tool\ncalls, scoping memory under a phantom agent. Cross-session recall\nsilently broke.\n\n## Fix\n\n3 surgical edits to `plugin/src/context-engine.ts`:\n\n1. **`getSessionKey(config, perCall?)`** — widened signature; reads\nsessionKey/sessionId from `perCall` first.\n2. **`ingest(message)`** — passes `message` to both `getSessionKey` and\n`resolveAgentId`.\n3. **`_assembleInner(params, ...)`** — passes `params` to both\n`getSessionKey` and `resolveAgentId`. Load-bearing fix.\n\nThe 3 existing-correct sites (`compact`, `afterTurn`,\n`prepareSubagentSpawn`) are untouched. Bootstrap intentionally still\npasses only `this.config` — no per-call context yet.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `ContextEngine.assemble agent-id resolution` describe block with 4\n**positive-content** tests:\n- sessionKey `\"agent:bankingclaw:...\"` → `agent_id=\\`bankingclaw\\``\n- Explicit `agentId` on params → takes precedence\n- No per-call context → install-default (regression guard)\n- Malformed sessionKey → clean fall-through\n\nThese assert **semantic content**, not just structural shape. The\nearlier wet test missed the bug because it only checked structural\nfields; the new tests close that gap.\n\n## Wet-test verification\n\nRan against the built dist on the GCE test VM (OpenClaw 2026.5.4):\n\n```\nTEST 1: sessionKey 'agent:bankingclaw-test:whatsapp:...'  → bankingclaw-test     ✓\nTEST 2: explicit agentId 'explicit-name-here'             → explicit-name-here   ✓\nTEST 3: no per-call context (fallback)                    → main-464841c00a47   ✓\nTEST 4: sessionKey 'agent:webclaw-second:slack:dm'        → webclaw-second       ✓\nPASSED: 4/4\n```\n\nTESTS 1, 2, 4 emitted ZERO `Could not resolve agent ID` warnings. Only\nTEST 3 (the fallback case) emitted the warning — matching expected\nbehavior.\n\nVM restored to v2.6.4 post-test.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] 278/278 plugin tests pass (274 prior + 4 new).\n- [x] `tsc --noEmit` clean.\n- [x] Compiled dist verified.\n- [x] Wet-test on real OpenClaw 2026.5.4 against built dist.\n- [ ] Customer post-deploy: grep `journalctl --user | grep \"Could not\nresolve agent ID\"` — bootstrap-time warn still expected (one per gateway\nstart); zero per-turn warns after the first turn lands. Customer's\nidentity block in agent's prompt shows the real agent name.\n\n## Version\n\n2.8.0 → 2.8.1.\n\n## Out-of-scope for this PR (deliberate)\n\n- The 409 `Duplicate memory exists` cascade (separate dedup-design\ndiscussion).\n- The 90% entity_lookup over-routing on the customer's deployment\n(separate design — requires backend changes to `classify_query`).\n- The `parallel_embed_entity_boost` 32767-parameter asyncpg limit\n(separate PR — was planned).\n\nEach tracked in earlier investigation threads.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4dd80fbb62b0bbd9a87269f5309f19060e950fd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4dd80fbb62b0bbd9a87269f5309f19060e950fd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/e2a8d1ea8e1d32206ec1769c20c9bfc7334540dd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJVaFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnjAQACAXeEdq/2hwmYkSBAvA0C4K\nl+AevW0wleZ8HgLZFqw0rn5a2o5Yyw9jCZ2j2TuDWU7ZX1rPfAIg3Q69POUmmrOT\nPzV7+yMAA0pQ0V3YjmgpFSf+KAKCtr0bHCF23WxKWir7fHZJYGIeBUyydl5a0yoJ\nSN/6xUi0P28jBGeSOCJYZGSDHlZ6EJoX9jhS/dZkZ7jCOvXP8EzSDRnmCKE+z6xQ\nHt8tpE9zVb+au8c/dFv6fG6pBM1Fm/cpuQ9O53W7Wf2umQLXYKCTEgTO4aMXevuD\nmCD3CpS19IY+Eg9q5453zpAlcrES9ymkLqPX2Prs3pJdYYvjMQcR1La8qMmIrc10\nKgTMdsdBk27GmVgxoTecCdw2VJQFB2OgEpQNwFqBjY+I3dZs+309STkaI4X3TTcp\n1Ze/pw6Ya5CL1RE7i7dcn89vb8J4EyF744Pr3lLHQnfDNNwEUZxKcZmB3Cur6kH3\nUQS8Bjm8Msw8mRefcQs7ThWT83Q2bXqUlYZY3ss/5SWA1LvNe7J3YgN794BZPQgq\njajgN1t/FjAd6u2ea/NhAwwety4nVwffqnn1ptfBuoqkII0LzV0KCL3/FQjOs8oE\nMzw/+1+PabXVtRTeS9ZNXTP2sYBFGwsI3uz1eWWue0Sy5RoVoFDMUHgHf3VPittV\nxoSueldcpkLmtp2E035A\n=kIh5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4dd80fbb62b0bbd9a87269f5309f19060e950fd0\nparent bad3109da265f13507532484f2c9dd892f8dd8af\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780831877 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780831877 +0300\n\nfix(plugin): thread per-call session context into resolveAgentId (CAURA-000) (#286)\n\n## Summary\n\nCustomer report 2026-06-02: `webclaw` agent gateway emitting `[memclaw]\nCould not resolve agent ID — using install-default 'main-e5366d79a926'`\n4-5 times per turn. Resolver was falling back to install-default on\nevery per-turn `assemble` call (and `ingest`), not just at bootstrap.\n\n**Root cause:** OpenClaw 2026.5.4 invokes\n`contextEngine.assemble({sessionId, sessionKey, messages, tokenBudget,\nmodel})` with `sessionKey` in the canonical `\"agent:NAME:CHANNEL:...\"`\nform. Our `resolveAgentId` helper parses `parts[1]` to recover the agent\nname. But 3 of our 6 `resolveAgentId` call sites passed only\n`this.config` (the factory-time `factoryCtx` wrapper — `{config,\nagentDir, workspaceDir}`, no `sessionKey`). The per-call `params` was\ndropped on the floor.\n\n**User-visible effect:** `assemble`'s identity block (`**Your\nidentity**: agent_id=\\`...\\``) carried `main-<installId>` instead of the\nreal agent name. The LLM saw the wrong `agent_id` every turn and\npropagated it into downstream `memclaw_write` / `memclaw_recall` tool\ncalls, scoping memory under a phantom agent. Cross-session recall\nsilently broke.\n\n## Fix\n\n3 surgical edits to `plugin/src/context-engine.ts`:\n\n1. **`getSessionKey(config, perCall?)`** — widened signature; reads\nsessionKey/sessionId from `perCall` first.\n2. **`ingest(message)`** — passes `message` to both `getSessionKey` and\n`resolveAgentId`.\n3. **`_assembleInner(params, ...)`** — passes `params` to both\n`getSessionKey` and `resolveAgentId`. Load-bearing fix.\n\nThe 3 existing-correct sites (`compact`, `afterTurn`,\n`prepareSubagentSpawn`) are untouched. Bootstrap intentionally still\npasses only `this.config` — no per-call context yet.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `ContextEngine.assemble agent-id resolution` describe block with 4\n**positive-content** tests:\n- sessionKey `\"agent:bankingclaw:...\"` → `agent_id=\\`bankingclaw\\``\n- Explicit `agentId` on params → takes precedence\n- No per-call context → install-default (regression guard)\n- Malformed sessionKey → clean fall-through\n\nThese assert **semantic content**, not just structural shape. The\nearlier wet test missed the bug because it only checked structural\nfields; the new tests close that gap.\n\n## Wet-test verification\n\nRan against the built dist on the GCE test VM (OpenClaw 2026.5.4):\n\n```\nTEST 1: sessionKey 'agent:bankingclaw-test:whatsapp:...'  → bankingclaw-test     ✓\nTEST 2: explicit agentId 'explicit-name-here'             → explicit-name-here   ✓\nTEST 3: no per-call context (fallback)                    → main-464841c00a47   ✓\nTEST 4: sessionKey 'agent:webclaw-second:slack:dm'        → webclaw-second       ✓\nPASSED: 4/4\n```\n\nTESTS 1, 2, 4 emitted ZERO `Could not resolve agent ID` warnings. Only\nTEST 3 (the fallback case) emitted the warning — matching expected\nbehavior.\n\nVM restored to v2.6.4 post-test.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] 278/278 plugin tests pass (274 prior + 4 new).\n- [x] `tsc --noEmit` clean.\n- [x] Compiled dist verified.\n- [x] Wet-test on real OpenClaw 2026.5.4 against built dist.\n- [ ] Customer post-deploy: grep `journalctl --user | grep \"Could not\nresolve agent ID\"` — bootstrap-time warn still expected (one per gateway\nstart); zero per-turn warns after the first turn lands. Customer's\nidentity block in agent's prompt shows the real agent name.\n\n## Version\n\n2.8.0 → 2.8.1.\n\n## Out-of-scope for this PR (deliberate)\n\n- The 409 `Duplicate memory exists` cascade (separate dedup-design\ndiscussion).\n- The 90% entity_lookup over-routing on the customer's deployment\n(separate design — requires backend changes to `classify_query`).\n- The `parallel_embed_entity_boost` 32767-parameter asyncpg limit\n(separate PR — was planned).\n\nEach tracked in earlier investigation threads.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-07T11:31:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e2a8d1ea8e1d32206ec1769c20c9bfc7334540dd","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e2a8d1ea8e1d32206ec1769c20c9bfc7334540dd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e2a8d1ea8e1d32206ec1769c20c9bfc7334540dd/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bad3109da265f13507532484f2c9dd892f8dd8af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bad3109da265f13507532484f2c9dd892f8dd8af","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bad3109da265f13507532484f2c9dd892f8dd8af"}]},{"sha":"bad3109da265f13507532484f2c9dd892f8dd8af","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGJhZDMxMDlkYTI2NWYxMzUwNzUzMjQ4NGYyYzlkZDg5MmY4ZGQ4YWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-07T11:09:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-07T11:09:39Z"},"message":"refactor: rename cryptic sp to search_params in ClassifyQuery (#287)\n\n## What\n\nRename the local variable `sp` → `search_params` in\n`ClassifyQuery.execute()`\n(`core-api/.../pipeline/steps/search/classify_query.py`).\n\n## Why\n\n`sp` is a cryptic two-letter abbreviation that breaks the file's own\nconvention — every other local binding in `execute()` uses a full\ndescriptive name (`query`, `tenant_id`, `fleet_ids`, `caller_agent_id`,\n…). The dict it holds is literally `ctx.data[\"search_params\"]`, so\nthat's the natural name.\n\n## Scope\n\nPure variable rename within a single function — **no behavior change**.\n7 occurrences updated (7 insertions / 7 deletions).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `grep \\bsp\\b` → 0 hits; `grep \\bsearch_params\\b` → 7 ✅\n- `ruff check` → clean ✅\n- `pytest tests/pipeline/test_classify_query.py\ntests/test_adaptive_fts_weight.py` → **83 passed** ✅\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"e91fbedf077e8b91c3504fea30c2c80ee3682c5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/e91fbedf077e8b91c3504fea30c2c80ee3682c5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/bad3109da265f13507532484f2c9dd892f8dd8af","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJVFzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6iwQAJVMHbf1/cB9Xp3vAKcJiT7g\ndUhqcbZ9cuL94DQAknAtgpgOn31zL8D16GkAyZRTNI1KREG3OffC8j9UwegSePD4\nzxL54qGwK9BZDHrRG1vrJkjdDbSqTdvAu/ft3laaKBWW8BOMy0pxQKzNJEGshpjZ\nyE2FkknvtynwPSUGRjkKdkZEtFWDtelNOgWjHhZ8hPkt+0gU3I74FmLeBpDdJKAB\ncIc37Ldpxw2meBDJ0qF/AciFHoHzzRyMCff3kiC7/eTEGfgQnDHeXHxmAt9cCbSM\nRr/9Ew2jTEEQusSW5i2nK5exFtuVNkFfLmgcGn88CfI9CnD6hnCJo4+AF5PCrr1M\nWcHxEYC0JgD2l0482WaSWlAbT1jTvHuvjy5NPVCGTu7rrKsFj10DL/hRST7PWO+V\n4JWQKfNx8xvLO0upbSR4lj3hqwCcztEejpb4sHGZPil7pICoTd2a7B9m4LgBNJPi\ncWt4uhOeUdHqi+znC8eZcIMy8yo8tsSftiL5ye/EMF6KHgAiNfZDwj8qjw2fMRM6\ngBeT+pvgqRzbc15HupFTxw/12kryqp6ValsFFaxOlv0ay/YYx84lTtOFwUfH22N9\naNg7ChT+hdDF8pEQX3mawUBqjcoeguWFZXiDOvF1aywSQQdFQmO/7PsL5XF1NW0v\ncFfsnzEbeNv2AcXm5iku\n=szgF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e91fbedf077e8b91c3504fea30c2c80ee3682c5e\nparent ea0391096270fd4189d6bb755edb9e9aea2154d1\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780830579 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780830579 +0300\n\nrefactor: rename cryptic sp to search_params in ClassifyQuery (#287)\n\n## What\n\nRename the local variable `sp` → `search_params` in\n`ClassifyQuery.execute()`\n(`core-api/.../pipeline/steps/search/classify_query.py`).\n\n## Why\n\n`sp` is a cryptic two-letter abbreviation that breaks the file's own\nconvention — every other local binding in `execute()` uses a full\ndescriptive name (`query`, `tenant_id`, `fleet_ids`, `caller_agent_id`,\n…). The dict it holds is literally `ctx.data[\"search_params\"]`, so\nthat's the natural name.\n\n## Scope\n\nPure variable rename within a single function — **no behavior change**.\n7 occurrences updated (7 insertions / 7 deletions).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `grep \\bsp\\b` → 0 hits; `grep \\bsearch_params\\b` → 7 ✅\n- `ruff check` → clean ✅\n- `pytest tests/pipeline/test_classify_query.py\ntests/test_adaptive_fts_weight.py` → **83 passed** ✅\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-07T11:09:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bad3109da265f13507532484f2c9dd892f8dd8af","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bad3109da265f13507532484f2c9dd892f8dd8af","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bad3109da265f13507532484f2c9dd892f8dd8af/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ea0391096270fd4189d6bb755edb9e9aea2154d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ea0391096270fd4189d6bb755edb9e9aea2154d1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ea0391096270fd4189d6bb755edb9e9aea2154d1"}]},{"sha":"ea0391096270fd4189d6bb755edb9e9aea2154d1","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGVhMDM5MTA5NjI3MGZkNDE4OWQ2YmI3NTVlZGI5ZTlhZWEyMTU0ZDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-05T06:28:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T06:28:07Z"},"message":"Reword fleet-scope 403s as policy, not trust levels (#283)\n\nCross-fleet read/write and delete/update denials now read as access\npolicy (`fleet 'legal' is not readable by principals of fleet 'rnd'`)\ninstead of exposing the internal `trust_level >= N` ladder. The 403 body\nis API copy that gets quoted/screenshotted; this matches how the\nboundary is described externally. Enforcement unchanged — message\nstrings only in `core-api/src/core_api/services/agent_service.py` (5\nmessages). No tests assert them.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f25e6f3a491a30da354e1b2cb89612db3e7aaab6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f25e6f3a491a30da354e1b2cb89612db3e7aaab6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ea0391096270fd4189d6bb755edb9e9aea2154d1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqImx3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWi8QAJWjMtH5ArhAHCUUGFLsfPAQ\nToq2rziHKeIj+QmW/1n3jwTY3Vma09vSsDSCCoTYPgBpN44ZRR6ZHy1xCCds1jmZ\nisiJo4PG/U7dFpJiEIfDx/CigHAcmg5ddmG+JKcmDzTxu9eBHqUsdv0WZmGJb+EW\nIs9j1eS9qSRWCq/sAHGTARUIxScdAgTZkDGCeaKFdvMM+DK2Y6jAR2d3zPhhyvaQ\np15RWM9QlliHOhae0ux+Vk9rKII0Kw+jO0bQ2u5xf1sYCike+rtSO7RfJ14y4ov4\nTsj+fIbew+/5uBlNPkDzsCOkRGuEgBzGNd1rOk6PNlDJfZygjfP7ww/h8aY9zWJN\nw5vUjbTqEGEO0tVDYGqDVLsff4zv+2kw7nKJ4BFPaaLgPQVNvvKbhYBJ1sfo7geJ\nLkzq/jwNjPmIlbWEWyoM+fQ3Y5/meEyynGqm3ieZxfsFZ3GB2o0Mylbr8ulfs0me\nzJROrzWg1M6L3zzvNQdKXyoNM2N0OfaMFiPAVNAphnQc5PddPQ2SQJpODx+i3G6H\n01DrvJ6+IWC5rMhmydl5hdKn9BQVgyhM9FItDLXoDn6DsrkHskrMpFE+TB5OkkzM\n8PdPz5UPsswoYFjyEbomnGIT1QKVEFIiLbtM1ksDgTML95iK3sg8mbMYlvwiiUZe\n4hWu5I2UxltJuSX0kY06\n=0Rt8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f25e6f3a491a30da354e1b2cb89612db3e7aaab6\nparent 7e1bcde19d7b56aa2d169908688a992468d9f3a9\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1780640887 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780640887 +0300\n\nReword fleet-scope 403s as policy, not trust levels (#283)\n\nCross-fleet read/write and delete/update denials now read as access\npolicy (`fleet 'legal' is not readable by principals of fleet 'rnd'`)\ninstead of exposing the internal `trust_level >= N` ladder. The 403 body\nis API copy that gets quoted/screenshotted; this matches how the\nboundary is described externally. Enforcement unchanged — message\nstrings only in `core-api/src/core_api/services/agent_service.py` (5\nmessages). No tests assert them.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-05T06:28:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ea0391096270fd4189d6bb755edb9e9aea2154d1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ea0391096270fd4189d6bb755edb9e9aea2154d1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ea0391096270fd4189d6bb755edb9e9aea2154d1/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7e1bcde19d7b56aa2d169908688a992468d9f3a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7e1bcde19d7b56aa2d169908688a992468d9f3a9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/7e1bcde19d7b56aa2d169908688a992468d9f3a9"}]},{"sha":"7e1bcde19d7b56aa2d169908688a992468d9f3a9","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDdlMWJjZGUxOWQ3YjU2YWEyZDE2OTkwODY4OGE5OTI0NjhkOWYzYTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-04T09:26:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T09:26:00Z"},"message":"CAURA-132 chore(contradiction): diagnostic logging for Path A + Path C (#282)\n\n## Summary\n\nPure-observability PR. No behavior change. Adds INFO logs at the\ndecision points in `contradiction_detector.py` so we can pinpoint why\nthe wet-test miss class isn't being flagged on v2.12.0 even though\nCAURA-128/129/130/131 are deployed.\n\n## Motivation\n\n33-trial race probe on v2.12.0 returned **90%/92%** for gap=0/100ms —\n**statistically indistinguishable from the v2.11.0 baseline\n(80%/100%)**. Repeated priya-collision probes still silent. All misses\nshare the exact same shape: `status=active/active`, `entity_links=2/2`,\nno contradiction surfaced.\n\nWithout per-call observability, we can't tell whether:\n- (a) Path C entity-aware judge wasn't invoked (context empty /\ncandidate not returned),\n- (b) It WAS invoked but returned `verdict=False` despite the\n\"AUTHORITATIVE entities\" framing,\n- (c) Path A semantic ran and declined first.\n\n## Log surface\n\nAll `logger.info` with `PATH_A_SEMANTIC` / `PATH_C_DETECTION` prefixes\nfor easy grep:\n\n| Line | What it tells us |\n|---|---|\n| `PATH_A_SEMANTIC entry memory=… candidates_initial=N` | Path A\nreached, vector-sim found N candidates |\n| `PATH_A_SEMANTIC verdict memory=… candidate=… verdict=… confidence=…`\n| Base judge result per candidate |\n| `PATH_C_DETECTION entry memory=… candidates_initial=N` | Path C\nreached, entity-overlap query found N |\n| `PATH_C_DETECTION after_a1_17 …preflight_skipped=… remaining=…` | A1\n#17 outcome |\n| `PATH_C_DETECTION context_fetched … new_ctx_size=… cand_ctx_sizes={…}`\n| Context-fetch outcome per candidate |\n| `PATH_C_DETECTION judge_selection … entity_aware=K base=M` | Which\njudge selected per candidate |\n| `PATH_C_DETECTION verdict … judge=… verdict=… confidence=…` | **Key\nforensic line** — judge result tagged with kind |\n\n## Decision matrix for the forensic analysis\n\n| Observed log pattern | Diagnosis |\n|---|---|\n| No `PATH_C_DETECTION entry` for memory | Path C wasn't enqueued\n(worker bug) |\n| `candidates_initial=0` | Storage entity-overlap query miss (indexing\nbug) |\n| `judge_selection entity_aware=0` | Contexts weren't populated when\nPath C ran (timing bug) |\n| `verdict judge=entity_aware verdict=False` | Prompt doesn't convince\nLLM (prompt bug) |\n| `verdict … verdict=True` but `status=active` | Status-write race (P2\nbatch-update interaction) |\n\n## Out of scope (intentionally)\n\n- Retraction path — already logs sufficient signal from\nCAURA-128/129/130.\n- Path A RDF path — short, deterministic, not implicated by wet tests.\n- DEBUG-level traces — INFO is enough; downgrade later if volume becomes\nan issue in production.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] `python -m py_compile` clean.\n- [x] `uv run ruff format` (1 file reformatted; cosmetic).\n- [x] `uv run ruff check` clean.\n- No new tests — logging-only change, no behavior to assert.\n\n## Post-merge wet-test plan\n\n1. Wait for next release (release-please will cut v2.13.0).\n2. Re-run `scripts/repro_contradictions_collision.py` on the priya\nshape.\n3. Read dev logs for `PATH_C_DETECTION verdict` lines on the\nmissed-contradiction memory IDs.\n4. Conclude per the decision matrix above, then file the actual fix as\nCAURA-133.\n\n## Rollback\n\nSingle `git revert`. Pure log lines, zero risk surface.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"62c60a863b51c8f4836b3f2b596ac25295c65ebe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/62c60a863b51c8f4836b3f2b596ac25295c65ebe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/7e1bcde19d7b56aa2d169908688a992468d9f3a9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIUSoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMigQAHC5KWddldU7nPakbVYFNc1n\nNuxBvn+okyaagTLl+zl4R/tD+y4f8vdiNcHYCohMTQ9s69p2O2IP71L5psRsM2V0\n6HKWlZXX5EXV6VYKkhH5ikDVxz1iW4eQ3rW3XPSc0xkdoxW3XH95+Qql/0PgKfrj\nB7BOUm7u+qlObVPZ4GJtPt9C6EJ0g+eyyK03ylKOmjK8Cne9/5g4E3VI1cYOhH5b\nyIMOuHqTXOWpTZiiVZm2XhwFMrRYTHIhUZhNTaBw1ozp+98+0YKw5xSKHhcPnHHi\ny/yW8plaugJswgQV2lXhRi0P2qxaCvMvTMFDAbR9pcNl98L98QNhi3oe9iODPOhH\nn2SfjyNJPDxV9awKzzMNmSwxvfF450gLrMIlH/6AlaxoCqCqOvC0N6XhAG3rY254\nm+dJJKQ9d/cPT6qI95QFuQ2ZDcFG8l3oT3XGouYbgMLHR5nQioMGeJUHqHM8rRlE\nch7tOAibFziB6VqpxDU+Rfcy4JPNokQY8SdcaiWqrvWicU5X0cQdjv5Evx6t9EHF\nO+ulZMbtiMr/ahJmmewbaBdbhHpm/PVFexaBs00+hGjsv0uCZA6qrgiNfc/Rc/qC\n5XwqeRyZqF/lRTMJolaNIoit6r68Pe6gI9lp52aRgAI8gmiYYD66SuLg0+gjOKqD\nXEfRT1dckPc2sjBJWCr3\n=n006\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 62c60a863b51c8f4836b3f2b596ac25295c65ebe\nparent 094b9594265b190e6be8136e66eb339c392de073\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780565160 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780565160 +0300\n\nCAURA-132 chore(contradiction): diagnostic logging for Path A + Path C (#282)\n\n## Summary\n\nPure-observability PR. No behavior change. Adds INFO logs at the\ndecision points in `contradiction_detector.py` so we can pinpoint why\nthe wet-test miss class isn't being flagged on v2.12.0 even though\nCAURA-128/129/130/131 are deployed.\n\n## Motivation\n\n33-trial race probe on v2.12.0 returned **90%/92%** for gap=0/100ms —\n**statistically indistinguishable from the v2.11.0 baseline\n(80%/100%)**. Repeated priya-collision probes still silent. All misses\nshare the exact same shape: `status=active/active`, `entity_links=2/2`,\nno contradiction surfaced.\n\nWithout per-call observability, we can't tell whether:\n- (a) Path C entity-aware judge wasn't invoked (context empty /\ncandidate not returned),\n- (b) It WAS invoked but returned `verdict=False` despite the\n\"AUTHORITATIVE entities\" framing,\n- (c) Path A semantic ran and declined first.\n\n## Log surface\n\nAll `logger.info` with `PATH_A_SEMANTIC` / `PATH_C_DETECTION` prefixes\nfor easy grep:\n\n| Line | What it tells us |\n|---|---|\n| `PATH_A_SEMANTIC entry memory=… candidates_initial=N` | Path A\nreached, vector-sim found N candidates |\n| `PATH_A_SEMANTIC verdict memory=… candidate=… verdict=… confidence=…`\n| Base judge result per candidate |\n| `PATH_C_DETECTION entry memory=… candidates_initial=N` | Path C\nreached, entity-overlap query found N |\n| `PATH_C_DETECTION after_a1_17 …preflight_skipped=… remaining=…` | A1\n#17 outcome |\n| `PATH_C_DETECTION context_fetched … new_ctx_size=… cand_ctx_sizes={…}`\n| Context-fetch outcome per candidate |\n| `PATH_C_DETECTION judge_selection … entity_aware=K base=M` | Which\njudge selected per candidate |\n| `PATH_C_DETECTION verdict … judge=… verdict=… confidence=…` | **Key\nforensic line** — judge result tagged with kind |\n\n## Decision matrix for the forensic analysis\n\n| Observed log pattern | Diagnosis |\n|---|---|\n| No `PATH_C_DETECTION entry` for memory | Path C wasn't enqueued\n(worker bug) |\n| `candidates_initial=0` | Storage entity-overlap query miss (indexing\nbug) |\n| `judge_selection entity_aware=0` | Contexts weren't populated when\nPath C ran (timing bug) |\n| `verdict judge=entity_aware verdict=False` | Prompt doesn't convince\nLLM (prompt bug) |\n| `verdict … verdict=True` but `status=active` | Status-write race (P2\nbatch-update interaction) |\n\n## Out of scope (intentionally)\n\n- Retraction path — already logs sufficient signal from\nCAURA-128/129/130.\n- Path A RDF path — short, deterministic, not implicated by wet tests.\n- DEBUG-level traces — INFO is enough; downgrade later if volume becomes\nan issue in production.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] `python -m py_compile` clean.\n- [x] `uv run ruff format` (1 file reformatted; cosmetic).\n- [x] `uv run ruff check` clean.\n- No new tests — logging-only change, no behavior to assert.\n\n## Post-merge wet-test plan\n\n1. Wait for next release (release-please will cut v2.13.0).\n2. Re-run `scripts/repro_contradictions_collision.py` on the priya\nshape.\n3. Read dev logs for `PATH_C_DETECTION verdict` lines on the\nmissed-contradiction memory IDs.\n4. Conclude per the decision matrix above, then file the actual fix as\nCAURA-133.\n\n## Rollback\n\nSingle `git revert`. Pure log lines, zero risk surface.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-04T09:26:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7e1bcde19d7b56aa2d169908688a992468d9f3a9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/7e1bcde19d7b56aa2d169908688a992468d9f3a9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7e1bcde19d7b56aa2d169908688a992468d9f3a9/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"094b9594265b190e6be8136e66eb339c392de073","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/094b9594265b190e6be8136e66eb339c392de073","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/094b9594265b190e6be8136e66eb339c392de073"}]},{"sha":"094b9594265b190e6be8136e66eb339c392de073","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDA5NGI5NTk0MjY1YjE5MGU2YmU4MTM2ZTY2ZWIzMzljMzkyZGUwNzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"eyal-bl","email":"eyal.b@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-03T14:34:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T14:34:19Z"},"message":"CAURA-699 fix(enrichment): stop the auto-classifier minting reserved … (#281)\n\n…types\n\nThe internal insights flow is the only intended author of insight-type\nmemories — reports, supersession, and the lifecycle activity gate all\nassume every insight row is server-generated. External agents were\npolluting that space: the enrichment prompt offered the LLM the full\ntype vocabulary (insight/outcome/rule included) and _validate_enrichment\naccepted those values, so an agent write that merely *looked* insight-/\nrule-/outcome-shaped got auto-classified into a server-reserved type.\nExplicit agent-supplied reserved types were already rejected at the\nMCP/REST boundary (C3/C8); the auto-classification path was the open\ndoor.\n\nFix, in two layers:\n- Don't offer them. The classifier prompt vocabulary is now rendered\nfrom MEMORY_TYPES minus SERVER_RESERVED_MEMORY_TYPES, so the LLM never\nsees insight/outcome/rule as choices.\n- Demote any that slip through. _validate_enrichment maps a reserved\ntop-level type (and any reserved atomic-fact suggested_type) to\nDEFAULT_MEMORY_TYPE, and enrich_memory applies the same guard to the\nkeyword-heuristic fallback. The fake_enrich primitive is left unchanged\n(still reusable); the policy is enforced at the enrich_memory boundary.\n\nInternal flows are unaffected: insights_service / evolve_service set\nmemory_type explicitly and bypass the classifier path entirely.\n\nDocs: the SKILL.md write sections now state insight/outcome/rule are\nserver-generated only and never auto-assigned; the misleading\n\"intentionally allowed\" note on SERVER_RESERVED_MEMORY_TYPES is\ncorrected.\n\n<!-- Thanks for the contribution! Please fill in this template so we can\nreview quickly. -->\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What does this PR do? One or two sentences. -->\n\n## Related Issue\n\n<!-- Link the issue this PR addresses, e.g. `Closes #123`. Delete if\nN/A. -->\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing behavior)\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Refactor / internal cleanup\n- [ ] Other:\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n<!-- Describe the tests you ran. Include commands if possible. -->\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] I have added tests that cover my changes (or explained why none\nare needed)\n- [ ] `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass\n- [ ] `mypy` passes\n- [ ] `pytest` passes locally\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation (README,\nARCHITECTURE_REVIEW, etc.)\n- [ ] I have updated `CHANGELOG.md` under the `Unreleased` section (if\nuser-facing)\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n<!-- Anything reviewers should know — tradeoffs, follow-up work, open\nquestions. -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Eyal Blyachman <eyal.b@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aa8e4768fb15e814edf0f94046c2d9ab9ea89888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/aa8e4768fb15e814edf0f94046c2d9ab9ea89888"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/094b9594265b190e6be8136e66eb339c392de073","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIDtrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1/gQAIuFpcTf18j9D2Xx61lMlUux\niQUgrxkATj5FKMkgKfR+Io+92/lWRZoxAjpP/73c8RuQA39YvJ3a6dYfQl0jhOpb\nDrS5KWj+c4NwaJ6yr0WePeAe3X7sv09NfDTrbxrXLXyKWm5dIoy5uijhJ5tsfGXp\ne8r+qFUrZPIcb/ycBTHgwVOkouLkZq7sUGWHoZMxHWQinh0oEDc7alfQ4iRfxZzJ\nDyo+zgxbkekhXYnVi4LSI5O9bnz2q34cnWOs9pfXWHCmA+2hiUDiYn+BXxXafk1k\nWZGxYenMbLD8dzAG4JmS7nqU4onxlk4yV3bBw0x0sUYqHy9zGYPdWFpavAWgHXU2\n28jeDPZupwd4ZD6l2RphSRyV7JTBrW5XNj/oa0Fx8uHlKtTGY4/3OUY4T0AS7k6/\nL2xMCseRzx/SytzPQX1ObYA94kKxRlzs5SekOM7i3TF4YfybiVp6CVWJTysd5a7H\nOfgfeoiw9uR0DogRMm4Fb75UlOIcxaDG1xK/hB9T0k5/9pyURd55SwiV4SDHo4oW\nwli0G1zIELSuHFMVsMrUB4dYwYlvXZiAGlKSvpCXwKqQFVEoN4HrWoUSWeogtTX0\n1cO6Z0kiitQipNQBZqyhccFoSvzpZEfvI4rKu/fPyDVU1z3ahqKvmJ8t3XiI8Mxc\n2ddrx14xgdbUHjlZTAvh\n=C9HM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aa8e4768fb15e814edf0f94046c2d9ab9ea89888\nparent b23a75471af2d7e6238f96dcb47ae2bcf940485d\nauthor eyal-bl <eyal.b@caura.ai> 1780497259 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780497259 +0300\n\nCAURA-699 fix(enrichment): stop the auto-classifier minting reserved … (#281)\n\n…types\n\nThe internal insights flow is the only intended author of insight-type\nmemories — reports, supersession, and the lifecycle activity gate all\nassume every insight row is server-generated. External agents were\npolluting that space: the enrichment prompt offered the LLM the full\ntype vocabulary (insight/outcome/rule included) and _validate_enrichment\naccepted those values, so an agent write that merely *looked* insight-/\nrule-/outcome-shaped got auto-classified into a server-reserved type.\nExplicit agent-supplied reserved types were already rejected at the\nMCP/REST boundary (C3/C8); the auto-classification path was the open\ndoor.\n\nFix, in two layers:\n- Don't offer them. The classifier prompt vocabulary is now rendered\nfrom MEMORY_TYPES minus SERVER_RESERVED_MEMORY_TYPES, so the LLM never\nsees insight/outcome/rule as choices.\n- Demote any that slip through. _validate_enrichment maps a reserved\ntop-level type (and any reserved atomic-fact suggested_type) to\nDEFAULT_MEMORY_TYPE, and enrich_memory applies the same guard to the\nkeyword-heuristic fallback. The fake_enrich primitive is left unchanged\n(still reusable); the policy is enforced at the enrich_memory boundary.\n\nInternal flows are unaffected: insights_service / evolve_service set\nmemory_type explicitly and bypass the classifier path entirely.\n\nDocs: the SKILL.md write sections now state insight/outcome/rule are\nserver-generated only and never auto-assigned; the misleading\n\"intentionally allowed\" note on SERVER_RESERVED_MEMORY_TYPES is\ncorrected.\n\n<!-- Thanks for the contribution! Please fill in this template so we can\nreview quickly. -->\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What does this PR do? One or two sentences. -->\n\n## Related Issue\n\n<!-- Link the issue this PR addresses, e.g. `Closes #123`. Delete if\nN/A. -->\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing behavior)\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Refactor / internal cleanup\n- [ ] Other:\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n<!-- Describe the tests you ran. Include commands if possible. -->\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] I have added tests that cover my changes (or explained why none\nare needed)\n- [ ] `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass\n- [ ] `mypy` passes\n- [ ] `pytest` passes locally\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation (README,\nARCHITECTURE_REVIEW, etc.)\n- [ ] I have updated `CHANGELOG.md` under the `Unreleased` section (if\nuser-facing)\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n<!-- Anything reviewers should know — tradeoffs, follow-up work, open\nquestions. -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Eyal Blyachman <eyal.b@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-03T14:34:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/094b9594265b190e6be8136e66eb339c392de073","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/094b9594265b190e6be8136e66eb339c392de073","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/094b9594265b190e6be8136e66eb339c392de073/comments","author":{"login":"eyal-bl","id":262085605,"node_id":"U_kgDOD58b5Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262085605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl","html_url":"https://github.com/eyal-bl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b23a75471af2d7e6238f96dcb47ae2bcf940485d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b23a75471af2d7e6238f96dcb47ae2bcf940485d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b23a75471af2d7e6238f96dcb47ae2bcf940485d"}]},{"sha":"b23a75471af2d7e6238f96dcb47ae2bcf940485d","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGIyM2E3NTQ3MWFmMmQ3ZTYyMzhmOTZkY2I0N2FlMmJjZjk0MDQ4NWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","email":"265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-03T12:34:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T12:34:02Z"},"message":"chore: release main (#243)\n\n:robot: I have created a release *beep* *boop*\n---\n\n\n<details><summary>backend: 2.12.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.12.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/backend-v2.11.0...backend-v2.12.0)\n(2026-06-03)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **api:** reject server-reserved memory_types at write boundary (C3,\nC8) ([#261](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/261))\n([0abd727](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/0abd727f31b53430519054cc339c238f319489ba))\n* **api:** surface near_duplicate_of in default-mode write metadata\n(A21) ([#266](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/266))\n([e7f9bc8](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/e7f9bc8de184a99f3b97d0d17d54cd3094a28574))\n* **core-api:** add fleet-scoped hard-purge endpoint\n([#275](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/275))\n([cd9e2a6](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/cd9e2a6a5a63e03f404797944d056025f8e53df0))\n* **core:** deletion-preview counts (CAURA-696 PR A — OSS half)\n([#246](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/246))\n([454a233](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/454a233d6fdbaaad67053bf40e3e7b584c956f52))\n* **core:** OSS suppression mirror + boundary guard (CAURA-694)\n([#244](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/244))\n([64cf3e4](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/64cf3e446cf26b634e3dee39197f2fcc76affe88))\n* **evolve:** surface weight-adjustment skip reason (A15)\n([#257](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/257))\n([5f314d9](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/5f314d90c8e847b874a7d5fcd2c9e5218a4c0e1c))\n* **lifecycle:** align all lifecycle crons to a fixed UTC hour, not\nboot-relative intervals\n([#278](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/278))\n([6b73bba](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/6b73bba5e95769247101a02a788f3e8de6ee7819))\n* **lifecycle:** run insights cron at a fixed UTC hour, not a\nboot-relative interval\n([#277](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/277))\n([bca3ddd](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/bca3dddadf5f439ce00585c2df23a992b39f550e))\n* **plugin:** bump MEMCLAW_KEYSTONES_TOKEN_CAP default 500 → 1500\n(CAURA-000)\n([#249](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/249))\n([6c3b021](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/6c3b021e4e011e1d1ada5e811b4e3ca68065e615))\n* **storage:** purge_org_data primitive for org hard-delete (CAURA-689)\n([#241](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/241))\n([f3d896b](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/f3d896b1890e5e2e46e166afdf225d475046ebf0))\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **api:** accept metadata_mode as a query param on PATCH /memories/{id}\n(C7) ([#265](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/265))\n([808f4c5](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/808f4c564e413ee9822fad08acf1cc2b72c02727))\n* **mcp:** extend mcp-agent default refusal to all read tools (A29)\n([#263](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/263))\n([1cccbe3](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1cccbe37a1c312978085fecf59a1753b5eb06b4b))\n* **mcp:** extend mcp-agent default refusal to all write tools (A14)\n([#256](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/256))\n([887c702](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/887c7021d6e00bab844a893005f723cda55f96c0))\n* **plugin:** context-engine auto-recall, smoke cleanup & post-upgrade\nallowlist drift\n([#274](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/274))\n([573857c](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/573857c70867541069d4f8e8157864b19372f5d1))\n* **plugin:** tolerate undefined config in ContextEngine constructor\n(CAURA-000)\n([#247](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/247))\n([78e10fb](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/78e10fb3cc21021883798d43d8e09f55bb33890d))\n* **recall:** add items alias key to /recall response (C4)\n([#262](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/262))\n([88ca5a8](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/88ca5a8f33008370bfb720695582c190c39c1207))\n* **search:** dedup per-tenant storage_search slot on entity-lookup\nfall-through (C10)\n([#264](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/264))\n([905db5c](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/905db5c6874a5dbcaa1a387d3730caca87da0656))\n* **search:** include EMBEDDING_QUERY_INSTRUCTION in embedding cache key\n(C9) ([#259](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/259))\n([595300a](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/595300aae3e51d14d183a1f52a6461e3244e98ec))\n* **search:** per-task timeout for parallel_embed_entity_boost (D7)\n([#260](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/260))\n([68f1977](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/68f19773ecd0d840048b046071e42a813eb68d50))\n* **search:** share entity tokenizer between FTS-weight + entity-FTS\ngates (A27)\n([#258](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/258))\n([71fd841](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/71fd8412086f426519a401038f9954242c41e120))\n* **security:** block agent credentials from agent-management & settings\n(trust self-escalation)\n([#252](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/252))\n([8475901](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/8475901603d52438638bb890c562017d3ea42fa1))\n* **security:** enforce fleet/agent scope on by-id memory access\n([#250](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/250))\n([fde5ceb](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/fde5cebe569e1fdb5c7cab101d60a4bc857719a8))\n* **security:** enforce fleet/agent scope on entity reads + document\ndeletes ([#253](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/253))\n([dab6b71](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/dab6b711921a5bba568a083eb6d8c09b2545870a))\n* **security:** gateway-shared-secret gate on the X-Tenant-ID auth path\n(CRITICAL-1, app side)\n([#254](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/254))\n([045039f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/045039f341ba54fe080d0e83f04e84fdc961750b))\n* **security:** require admin-trust for bulk/whole-tenant memory deletes\n([#251](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/251))\n([9fcac01](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/9fcac01685dee45072b809cb45d9366e63898e13))\n* **version-compat:** bump MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION to 2.7.0\n([#279](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/279))\n([7238180](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/7238180a4f451838e3e4e7c71c85609d08aa58b3))\n\n\n### Performance\n\n* **entity-extraction:** collapse worker N+1 storage HTTPs (P1)\n([#245](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/245))\n([e2d805e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/e2d805e8b80aa24ba22312e4c9ee35b6381c56ce))\n\n\n### Documentation\n\n* fix stale API paths, tool counts, and version references\n([#255](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/255))\n([496717e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/496717eeeb28cabdf07d8b690c07e2d03ac7aa2f))\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>plugin: 2.8.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.8.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/plugin-v2.7.0...plugin-v2.8.0)\n(2026-06-03)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **plugin:** bump MEMCLAW_KEYSTONES_TOKEN_CAP default 500 → 1500\n(CAURA-000)\n([#249](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/249))\n([6c3b021](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/6c3b021e4e011e1d1ada5e811b4e3ca68065e615))\n* **plugin:** decouple plugin release cadence from backend\n([#131](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/131))\n([ac6c0f2](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ac6c0f2ec05a020b0acb27b6ec7b92a0be338d73))\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **plugin:** close install-script alsoAllow drift + manifest version\ndrift (CAURA-444)\n([#181](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/181))\n([28f22aa](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/28f22aa72b0ca306b5f1a7e25a6005ead484db02))\n* **plugin:** conform to OpenClaw MemoryFlushPlan contract (CAURA-000)\n([#191](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/191))\n([ea750c7](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ea750c7abea37cbce21fef85ffe21db830bb5f07))\n* **plugin:** context-engine auto-recall, smoke cleanup & post-upgrade\nallowlist drift\n([#274](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/274))\n([573857c](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/573857c70867541069d4f8e8157864b19372f5d1))\n* **plugin:** delegate compaction to OpenClaw runtime SDK to unwedge\nover-budget groups (CAURA-000)\n([#234](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/234))\n([6e70d3f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/6e70d3f677cfec4029edbada88fe4f1e88cd4732))\n* **plugin:** tolerate undefined config in ContextEngine constructor\n(CAURA-000)\n([#247](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/247))\n([78e10fb](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/78e10fb3cc21021883798d43d8e09f55bb33890d))\n* **plugin:** wire keystones into WhatsApp system prompts end-to-end\n(CAURA-000)\n([#212](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/212))\n([cb54bda](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/cb54bda929e9f45744c6baea485e00aede9c682e))\n\n\n### Documentation\n\n* fix stale API paths, tool counts, and version references\n([#255](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/255))\n([496717e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/496717eeeb28cabdf07d8b690c07e2d03ac7aa2f))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <releas