TU4YjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-03T08:51:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T08:51:43Z"},"message":"fix(version-compat): bump MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION to 2.7.0 (#279)\n\nCompanion to the plugin **2.7.0** release (#243). Bumps the auto-upgrade\nfloor so manifest-aware nodes (plugin >= 2.6.0) auto-upgrade to 2.7.0\nonce the server runs the `onprem-v2.9.0` image set. Nodes below 2.6.0\n(`MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY_PLUGIN_VERSION`) still require manual re-install.\n\nMerge alongside #243, then `onprem-v2.9.0` is cut from the result.\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"a3480413e32cc551f68b60002ad754426eb251e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a3480413e32cc551f68b60002ad754426eb251e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/7238180a4f451838e3e4e7c71c85609d08aa58b3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH+sfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVo0QAEYfeLcOo9air+usuzFRVCt3\nxCxXc9f6G9qVhsayr8EeRlUdJABsI+N/nTaPbGX3CijEu2TnFLQ63Xdr3lnahGhD\nBZMysSzGzgTwS12dQyieqOLai1uZfdNeu3RCLzpzMKvVPbIB+p1mBWoPdoD6EAx+\nCtVhaVZwLvClp7qACQnmqGyRi9eA+MNPZlj2nGrMY2V8OMa8mPV4LGxT/UymPCRd\nUysMGAnGAuVGYogp6v8LfCg4caTRVcNxyA9EANeiqCREpJB/nrOO3j0OpyZYr3An\nHDy1ewxbMosOrVW9QYkRj/SkAztBGn5pS+7OYrfYYxnmt+te8cjqvEi0VHmZ5GU6\nrvx1nBR/jhUsEFdQ+ynREQU6ZGbjXR/Ra6zCf33gGLoKvFKSufbEcylMnQsH1Zro\nyqPoJXz9nLc5H8e2tzEKAW+UwXs0cMnxYVI5OtRyKuuHtmxaxoh91+OFpUNVVVm7\nJsoaeeGfHkdmR7eSE9KYmADiq0AVkzFIw7S5+Kxr+cdlAViic3AUbQOV+xUJvSsC\nPw+mDneaWL1L6/4OS0fzApmQyvhhTxhpDj6iRGsF3aCyxKnBl4YUedSUv174RU2H\n/vnFuj2zMcQVEJ7mwiel34k1xl6gdrfLDro0/HLwJN8Jb83BXOAB9u3p6hQhkIoi\nt9nA0SoKn4CsqaJzbIqd\n=ezqQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a3480413e32cc551f68b60002ad754426eb251e8\nparent 439fec2fd8fcccb837e5e33a5ab4803e2aedb80b\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1780476703 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780476703 +0300\n\nfix(version-compat): bump MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION to 2.7.0 (#279)\n\nCompanion to the plugin **2.7.0** release (#243). Bumps the auto-upgrade\nfloor so manifest-aware nodes (plugin >= 2.6.0) auto-upgrade to 2.7.0\nonce the server runs the `onprem-v2.9.0` image set. Nodes below 2.6.0\n(`MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY_PLUGIN_VERSION`) still require manual re-install.\n\nMerge alongside #243, then `onprem-v2.9.0` is cut from the result.\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-03T08:51:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7238180a4f451838e3e4e7c71c85609d08aa58b3","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/7238180a4f451838e3e4e7c71c85609d08aa58b3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7238180a4f451838e3e4e7c71c85609d08aa58b3/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"439fec2fd8fcccb837e5e33a5ab4803e2aedb80b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/439fec2fd8fcccb837e5e33a5ab4803e2aedb80b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/439fec2fd8fcccb837e5e33a5ab4803e2aedb80b"}]},{"sha":"439fec2fd8fcccb837e5e33a5ab4803e2aedb80b","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQzOWZlYzJmZDhmY2NjYjgzN2U1ZTMzYTVhYjQ4MDNlMmFlZGI4MGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-03T08:33:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T08:33:41Z"},"message":"CAURA-131 feat(contradiction): entity-aware Path C detection (close priya silence) (#276)\n\n## Summary\n\nSymmetric mirror of CAURA-129. There, Path C's **retraction** judge ran\nthe same LLM call as Path A and got stochastic disagreement. Here, Path\nC's **forward detection** judge runs the same base call and inherits its\nsurface-qualifier blindness — failing to flag genuine within-subject\ncontradictions when the entity extractor has correctly merged the\nsubjects.\n\nWet-tested case (`scripts/repro_contradictions_collision.py` on dev,\n2026-06-02):\n\n```\nMemory A: \"Priya from AcmeCorp lives in Tel Aviv.\"\nMemory B: \"Priya from BetaIndustries lives in Haifa.\"\n```\n\nEntity extractor merged both `Priya` to entity `b5aca002-…`.\n`find_entity_overlap_candidates` returned the pair (entities match →\ncandidate). Then the LLM call extracted `subject_a=\"Priya from\nAcmeCorp\"` / `subject_b=\"Priya from BetaIndustries\"` →\n`same_subject=false` → silent. **The data was one variable away from the\nprompt.**\n\n## What changed\n\n| Change | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Lifted entity-context fetch above the L3.4 preflight |\n`_fetch_entity_context` runs once for `new_memory + all post-A1#17\ncandidates`, parallel `asyncio.gather` under 5s `wait_for`. Stored in\n`contexts: dict[memory_id, list[dict]]`. |\n| L3.4 preflight now reads from `contexts` | Cheap dict lookup; same\ncanonical-subject-mismatch drop semantics. |\n| Detection LLM call selects per-candidate | Both contexts non-empty →\n`_llm_entity_aware_contradiction_check` (CAURA-129's entity-aware\njudge). Either empty / fetch failed / cap exceeded → fallback to base\n`_llm_contradiction_check`. |\n| Cap reused | `_ENTITY_LINKS_PREFLIGHT_MAX_CANDIDATES = 20` bounds the\nfull candidate-set fetch (was: fall-through-set only). |\n\n## Tests (32 collected across 4 files)\n\n**`tests/test_caura_131_entity_aware_path_c_detection.py`** *(new, 6\ntests)*:\n\n| Test | Asserts |\n|---|---|\n| Entity-aware judge used when both contexts present |\n`entity_aware_judge.assert_called_once()` + `base.assert_not_called()` +\nentity_ids in call args. The priya-shape repro. |\n| Fallback when new memory has empty context | Base judge runs |\n| Fallback when candidate has empty context | Base judge runs |\n| Fallback when context fetch fails | Base judge runs (fail-open) |\n| Fallback when candidate count > cap | Fetch NOT called; base judge\nruns N times |\n| L3.4 collision still drops (regression guard) | Neither judge runs\n(preflight dropped) |\n\nExisting CAURA-128/129/130 tests preserved unchanged.\n\n## Wet-test artifacts committed\n\n- `scripts/repro_contradictions_race.py` — adds `--trials N` for\nvariance measurement. Pre-128/129/130 ~50% detection on net;\npost-128/129/130 90% on dev (5×4 trials).\n- `scripts/repro_contradictions_collision.py` — new probe for the\npriya-shape. Pre-merge silent; expected post-merge to fire.\n- `scripts/repro_contradictions_proper_noun.py` — minor lint cleanup\ncarried over from S1 session.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] `python -m py_compile` clean on all changed files.\n- [x] `uv run ruff check core-api/src/ scripts/ tests/...` clean.\n- [x] `uv run ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `pytest --collect-only` collects 32 tests across all 4\ncontradiction test files.\n- [ ] CI runs full pytest (Postgres autouse fixture).\n- [ ] **Post-merge wet test on dev**:\n- `scripts/repro_contradictions_collision.py` — expect contradiction to\nfire when extractor merges subjects.\n- `scripts/repro_contradictions_race.py --trials 5` — expect ≥95% (was\n90%).\n\n## Cost analysis\n\nZero new round-trips on the happy path — the L3.4 preflight already\nfetched `new_memory`'s context. CAURA-131 just extends the same\n`asyncio.gather` to all surviving candidates instead of only the\nfall-through set. On the post-A1-#17 candidate list, fetch is `1 + N`\nparallel storage calls, bounded by the existing cap (20).\n\n## Rollback\n\nSingle `git revert`. No DB migration, no schema change, no flag flip.\n\n## What's left (deferred)\n\n- Path A **semantic** detection — runs PRE-entity-extraction, so\n`entity_links` typically empty. Fixing it requires a defer-and-retry\npattern (significant refactor). Path C entity-aware should catch most of\nwhat Path A misses anyway.\n- L3.2 object normalization, L3.5 N>2 transitive, L3.6 MCP coverage,\nL3.7 cross-tenant.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"5d31fb03dccacde73425c68b6d0d5fd4534d020c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/5d31fb03dccacde73425c68b6d0d5fd4534d020c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/439fec2fd8fcccb837e5e33a5ab4803e2aedb80b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH+blCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM48QAEYjJ1U8oTlmQ5sGrCixUfI1\nvZAbJIz/Ou+o0Tpj/IFU897FFnXyK6GsU/OyXv/iRsEhtWp/siE0zGFcPqfQUHPq\nhVMyssfVnpv4zcG944XUUoQuu84TrfLR1fdjc53cZjlrInvx0kc850Thszrzy6fo\n7gAeDGmF2f7aNOk6uSaNFF++ysMh1/iB4UprWrOLoRzrl8GOpG+N0uUqMueruBNZ\ntvsiPfZwp6QySUtrUlELpQw4jwzq33xAwslQKYsLWPcN79oSUb/Tkn+55z3VpA7v\n1PT0n/dqeVseCFZgW4mtr+rtdgKjz7yX6Hq+knyFD9nv3cGwIgoNtfeHnQ4VaKx9\nbVweWSwJ3TG7R3jM/bgPijSOfNUZt+d2BfTxjAOVXIrPiEYBBEc2yJ7HBCNELcZn\niOlQhFJtxzmHfMUs+HjPaAV35G/Q4gJZAiF3wDVVukumsryZ4kEJuoXuThDxj9Rz\nb+mwXWsD1cvEFv4RoUoaMbQDCRNCzMYbggsbb9ruk+7bLk7usuDnZ3MkIs6agkUV\nHtdQtxP+/hae24Qg9PrDdMhV2k6RuFh/eoZp+N97AI4a+BVgpPwQAZVfwe19qUAl\nQXBOxUdq5mxWERiYBtrAV5sxtZqf9ws1Rug2Ao/g19kUXFuukz3SDOBgAO2DXeO6\nh7f1HjiRgEPcnfTQlheD\n=wZrL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5d31fb03dccacde73425c68b6d0d5fd4534d020c\nparent 6b73bba5e95769247101a02a788f3e8de6ee7819\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780475621 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780475621 +0300\n\nCAURA-131 feat(contradiction): entity-aware Path C detection (close priya silence) (#276)\n\n## Summary\n\nSymmetric mirror of CAURA-129. There, Path C's **retraction** judge ran\nthe same LLM call as Path A and got stochastic disagreement. Here, Path\nC's **forward detection** judge runs the same base call and inherits its\nsurface-qualifier blindness — failing to flag genuine within-subject\ncontradictions when the entity extractor has correctly merged the\nsubjects.\n\nWet-tested case (`scripts/repro_contradictions_collision.py` on dev,\n2026-06-02):\n\n```\nMemory A: \"Priya from AcmeCorp lives in Tel Aviv.\"\nMemory B: \"Priya from BetaIndustries lives in Haifa.\"\n```\n\nEntity extractor merged both `Priya` to entity `b5aca002-…`.\n`find_entity_overlap_candidates` returned the pair (entities match →\ncandidate). Then the LLM call extracted `subject_a=\"Priya from\nAcmeCorp\"` / `subject_b=\"Priya from BetaIndustries\"` →\n`same_subject=false` → silent. **The data was one variable away from the\nprompt.**\n\n## What changed\n\n| Change | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Lifted entity-context fetch above the L3.4 preflight |\n`_fetch_entity_context` runs once for `new_memory + all post-A1#17\ncandidates`, parallel `asyncio.gather` under 5s `wait_for`. Stored in\n`contexts: dict[memory_id, list[dict]]`. |\n| L3.4 preflight now reads from `contexts` | Cheap dict lookup; same\ncanonical-subject-mismatch drop semantics. |\n| Detection LLM call selects per-candidate | Both contexts non-empty →\n`_llm_entity_aware_contradiction_check` (CAURA-129's entity-aware\njudge). Either empty / fetch failed / cap exceeded → fallback to base\n`_llm_contradiction_check`. |\n| Cap reused | `_ENTITY_LINKS_PREFLIGHT_MAX_CANDIDATES = 20` bounds the\nfull candidate-set fetch (was: fall-through-set only). |\n\n## Tests (32 collected across 4 files)\n\n**`tests/test_caura_131_entity_aware_path_c_detection.py`** *(new, 6\ntests)*:\n\n| Test | Asserts |\n|---|---|\n| Entity-aware judge used when both contexts present |\n`entity_aware_judge.assert_called_once()` + `base.assert_not_called()` +\nentity_ids in call args. The priya-shape repro. |\n| Fallback when new memory has empty context | Base judge runs |\n| Fallback when candidate has empty context | Base judge runs |\n| Fallback when context fetch fails | Base judge runs (fail-open) |\n| Fallback when candidate count > cap | Fetch NOT called; base judge\nruns N times |\n| L3.4 collision still drops (regression guard) | Neither judge runs\n(preflight dropped) |\n\nExisting CAURA-128/129/130 tests preserved unchanged.\n\n## Wet-test artifacts committed\n\n- `scripts/repro_contradictions_race.py` — adds `--trials N` for\nvariance measurement. Pre-128/129/130 ~50% detection on net;\npost-128/129/130 90% on dev (5×4 trials).\n- `scripts/repro_contradictions_collision.py` — new probe for the\npriya-shape. Pre-merge silent; expected post-merge to fire.\n- `scripts/repro_contradictions_proper_noun.py` — minor lint cleanup\ncarried over from S1 session.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] `python -m py_compile` clean on all changed files.\n- [x] `uv run ruff check core-api/src/ scripts/ tests/...` clean.\n- [x] `uv run ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `pytest --collect-only` collects 32 tests across all 4\ncontradiction test files.\n- [ ] CI runs full pytest (Postgres autouse fixture).\n- [ ] **Post-merge wet test on dev**:\n- `scripts/repro_contradictions_collision.py` — expect contradiction to\nfire when extractor merges subjects.\n- `scripts/repro_contradictions_race.py --trials 5` — expect ≥95% (was\n90%).\n\n## Cost analysis\n\nZero new round-trips on the happy path — the L3.4 preflight already\nfetched `new_memory`'s context. CAURA-131 just extends the same\n`asyncio.gather` to all surviving candidates instead of only the\nfall-through set. On the post-A1-#17 candidate list, fetch is `1 + N`\nparallel storage calls, bounded by the existing cap (20).\n\n## Rollback\n\nSingle `git revert`. No DB migration, no schema change, no flag flip.\n\n## What's left (deferred)\n\n- Path A **semantic** detection — runs PRE-entity-extraction, so\n`entity_links` typically empty. Fixing it requires a defer-and-retry\npattern (significant refactor). Path C entity-aware should catch most of\nwhat Path A misses anyway.\n- L3.2 object normalization, L3.5 N>2 transitive, L3.6 MCP coverage,\nL3.7 cross-tenant.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-03T08:33:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/439fec2fd8fcccb837e5e33a5ab4803e2aedb80b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/439fec2fd8fcccb837e5e33a5ab4803e2aedb80b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/439fec2fd8fcccb837e5e33a5ab4803e2aedb80b/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6b73bba5e95769247101a02a788f3e8de6ee7819","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6b73bba5e95769247101a02a788f3e8de6ee7819","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6b73bba5e95769247101a02a788f3e8de6ee7819"}]},{"sha":"6b73bba5e95769247101a02a788f3e8de6ee7819","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDZiNzNiYmE1ZTk1NzY5MjQ3MTAxYTAyYTc4OGYzZThkZTZlZTc4MTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-03T08:22:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T08:22:29Z"},"message":"feat(lifecycle): align all lifecycle crons to a fixed UTC hour, not boot-relative intervals (#278)\n\n## What\n\nFollow-up to #277. That PR moved the **insights** cron to a fixed UTC\nhour; this extends the same wall-clock alignment to **all**\n`core-operations` lifecycle crons:\n\n`lifecycle-archive-expired`, `lifecycle-archive-stale`,\n`lifecycle-purge-soft-deleted`, `lifecycle-crystallize`,\n`lifecycle-entity-link` (insights already landed in #277).\n\nEach now fires **once a day at a configurable UTC hour** (default\n**02:00 UTC**) via the scheduler's `delay_provider`, instead of a\nrun-then-sleep interval that fired at startup and drifted by each tick's\nduration from the last deploy.\n\n## How\n\n- **config**: replace the three interval knobs\n(`lifecycle_{archive,purge,pipeline}_interval_seconds`) with per-job\nhour knobs (`lifecycle_{archive,purge,pipeline,insights}_run_at_hour`,\nint `0..23`, default `2`), validated by one shared `field_validator`.\nHours are independent so operators can **stagger** the jobs across the\nnight.\n- **app**: every job registered with a `delay_provider`;\narchive-expired/stale share the archive hour, crystallize/entity-link\nshare the pipeline hour.\n\nThe `delay_provider` mechanism and `seconds_until_next_utc_hour` helper\nalready landed in #277 — this PR just wires the remaining five jobs to\nthem.\n\nNo change to any consumer-side gate (`auto_*_enabled`, the insights\nactivity gate, crystallize's >1000-active-memory threshold) — only\n**when** each daily tick fires.\n\n## Behavior note\n\nThe boot-time tick is gone, so after a deploy a job won't run until the\nnext occurrence of its hour (≤24h later) rather than immediately — the\nintended trade for predictable off-peak scheduling.\n\n## Test\n\n- `ruff check` ✓ · `ruff format --check` ✓ · `mypy src/` ✓ · `pytest` ✓\n(34 passed)\n- New `test_app.py`: all six jobs registered + wall-clock aligned (no\nboot tick), `*_run_at_hour` overrides thread through to the scheduler,\nconfig validator rejects out-of-range hours.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ed0e8161874cb1193828de5246244a9c4471bf1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ed0e8161874cb1193828de5246244a9c4471bf1b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/6b73bba5e95769247101a02a788f3e8de6ee7819","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH+RFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEt0QACeVXZZ6IIdcZTyl/z+JqBj2\nhErYed5SDbeRsBpmG7CQK23Q64JNl+6WbHojgqsDvSbs+Gx2P3N6BZJdug4H5MUB\nUF+r3g6AERsPO4FvCcC/tLCLB6evPdJIKpyHZRn59tV+gN9AAqc/hTczpjxFzkkI\npn3daGnpWvrKl2cgwDcOX0fP/UCcYbLI87T2rQjbnHjrEJQkkCz5/ugZCHleiUqs\n6Cxpo6FUwNLkqg5ZccSWuMlb1hN1URqyw3jnVeSUYdbWSDY83F+9HFZGeqdkn2TO\njgVB+lc5E3Vx+I2dvBP0wEQsTsfFvdRE6l8FlVFIpGqBmtFR4jhWHmpux755qjvE\nuJkOCW4BM65T8U3NUzSiD8dVIaM446Z3adEDyEx+JHtwF+PFTgwUVGxXn9FslGAo\nDQkeG1i6BXIzCYoQpDbIzk1d4NHGYOO+pIS5XKCpQwwEoEKS3vJHnOqLTICMxJjc\nQSL32dg4hp76moxdtvmx1XSBERSrLZ93ynN0Igmx28I3E3rhKdiURtraKsamUH3n\ncPKj8JmPyXg7Ctde+XRiDAY3mf/YALP0GPaK3Pm8tdjAfajaYtH70ze8oYEuIXUn\nUa0Kw+HV3sbbjfYl/XUZCtHxdrZiDOZX+PQpg29VCd7Zgg+dZhF1shWNfp/OwjLb\ncXhLauqLglZ1kDniWPEK\n=oKXc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ed0e8161874cb1193828de5246244a9c4471bf1b\nparent bca3dddadf5f439ce00585c2df23a992b39f550e\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780474949 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780474949 +0300\n\nfeat(lifecycle): align all lifecycle crons to a fixed UTC hour, not boot-relative intervals (#278)\n\n## What\n\nFollow-up to #277. That PR moved the **insights** cron to a fixed UTC\nhour; this extends the same wall-clock alignment to **all**\n`core-operations` lifecycle crons:\n\n`lifecycle-archive-expired`, `lifecycle-archive-stale`,\n`lifecycle-purge-soft-deleted`, `lifecycle-crystallize`,\n`lifecycle-entity-link` (insights already landed in #277).\n\nEach now fires **once a day at a configurable UTC hour** (default\n**02:00 UTC**) via the scheduler's `delay_provider`, instead of a\nrun-then-sleep interval that fired at startup and drifted by each tick's\nduration from the last deploy.\n\n## How\n\n- **config**: replace the three interval knobs\n(`lifecycle_{archive,purge,pipeline}_interval_seconds`) with per-job\nhour knobs (`lifecycle_{archive,purge,pipeline,insights}_run_at_hour`,\nint `0..23`, default `2`), validated by one shared `field_validator`.\nHours are independent so operators can **stagger** the jobs across the\nnight.\n- **app**: every job registered with a `delay_provider`;\narchive-expired/stale share the archive hour, crystallize/entity-link\nshare the pipeline hour.\n\nThe `delay_provider` mechanism and `seconds_until_next_utc_hour` helper\nalready landed in #277 — this PR just wires the remaining five jobs to\nthem.\n\nNo change to any consumer-side gate (`auto_*_enabled`, the insights\nactivity gate, crystallize's >1000-active-memory threshold) — only\n**when** each daily tick fires.\n\n## Behavior note\n\nThe boot-time tick is gone, so after a deploy a job won't run until the\nnext occurrence of its hour (≤24h later) rather than immediately — the\nintended trade for predictable off-peak scheduling.\n\n## Test\n\n- `ruff check` ✓ · `ruff format --check` ✓ · `mypy src/` ✓ · `pytest` ✓\n(34 passed)\n- New `test_app.py`: all six jobs registered + wall-clock aligned (no\nboot tick), `*_run_at_hour` overrides thread through to the scheduler,\nconfig validator rejects out-of-range hours.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-03T08:22:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6b73bba5e95769247101a02a788f3e8de6ee7819","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6b73bba5e95769247101a02a788f3e8de6ee7819","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6b73bba5e95769247101a02a788f3e8de6ee7819/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bca3dddadf5f439ce00585c2df23a992b39f550e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bca3dddadf5f439ce00585c2df23a992b39f550e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bca3dddadf5f439ce00585c2df23a992b39f550e"}]},{"sha":"bca3dddadf5f439ce00585c2df23a992b39f550e","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGJjYTNkZGRhZGY1ZjQzOWNlMDA1ODVjMmRmMjNhOTkyYjM5ZjU1MGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-03T08:04:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T08:04:07Z"},"message":"feat(lifecycle): run insights cron at a fixed UTC hour, not a boot-relative interval (#277)\n\n## What\n\nThe `lifecycle-insights` cron (PR #238) currently uses the generic\nrun-then-sleep interval cadence: it fires **once immediately at\ncore-operations startup**, then every ~24h *after the previous tick\nfinishes*. That anchors the run to whenever the service last deployed\nand **drifts** by each tick's duration — so insights can land at any\nhour and move around over time.\n\nThis pins it to a **configurable off-peak wall-clock hour** (default\n**02:00 UTC**).\n\n## How\n\n- **scheduler**: optional `delay_provider` on `register()`. When set,\nthe loop sleeps `delay_provider()` (recomputed every cycle → drift-free)\n*before* each run and **skips the boot-time tick**. Interval mode is\nunchanged and remains the default — fully backward compatible.\n- **`seconds_until_next_utc_hour(hour)`** helper: strictly-future, ≤24h.\nThe strict-future guarantee also means an aligned task can't hot-loop\nafter a fast failure (next slot is a full day out once the hour passes).\n- **config**: `lifecycle_insights_interval_seconds` →\n`lifecycle_insights_run_at_hour` (int `0..23`, default `2`), validated\nat startup.\n- **app**: `lifecycle-insights` registered with the `delay_provider`;\nthe other five lifecycle ops keep their interval cadence.\n\nNo change to the opt-in (`auto_insights_enabled`, default off) or the\nconsumer-side activity gate — only **when** the daily tick fires.\n\n## Test\n\n- `ruff check` ✓ · `ruff format --check` ✓ · `mypy src/` ✓ · `pytest` ✓\n(28 passed)\n- New tests: helper math (same-day / rollover / exact-boundary / bounds\n/ out-of-range), aligned task does **not** fire at boot, aligned task\nsleeps-then-runs each cycle (drift-free), aligned failing tick recovers\nwithout killing the loop.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9475230aeecf1445acd942525c2f2f6adc846f4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9475230aeecf1445acd942525c2f2f6adc846f4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/bca3dddadf5f439ce00585c2df23a992b39f550e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH9/3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHqQQAImR/WO0BJLXzLj3YV4aBafp\nI5RJIGG30Jh42NQr3nUQfg2s0mcKTJNKOqHK5w4PepR6BjoGXYGRVmEie+CjRYgw\nNEnlCm2DcGdp7uJOIV1Qrw5fANzRdRg2M3Aw9LJQHrQLztk8KfdmdJFF6ScgDtKg\n9JiPyhnLSTjhR0JrAIIEmXk8xkVeIpnaWclbxrh4DOWRWTljh1qQb24bjqN8Bpvy\nCxWbpeVRiAMu9lGZEWIYArnYm3aXjUgHvi9AnfQGq1do2llePbUNrTT6pce5Fo5W\ni8BW6GUo/XlKqq2ShPeDIcsbYJzF44SLhAycZ0lxsaRxU1vujnK+8lzITeen4xU+\nvJwFZBO9v7lBGdbQCOxia4AbMHXgSJH50jww+TY/4mdAogpaygHhkxFjxJM5YeiR\ndOdnfq5krbmjNEjC1WMBIQHk7yRcC661wrZYp4Yn+378m8ClKQFzZZ9R/pj6WdT6\nXr1e6TtZC0mB/8RyVpM7IIHMltrQ/NGGIFYyEnO29gqLnUgVKrUXbojKCvgTwwnr\n6oNoreD4hmivYtpVzmn/43/xp2rfV1M6ZBdeF/v7Gwdq6i4lDc0Rqx1JLF5WOgb3\nPPFYpV35Leq8u62a9AIp95LO3lvUPoysksP/sTS/2r6AljTwe2yVWsg1A4Hz8wUq\n6RYM/7iknsxJ7g0Rn4RR\n=IZ6/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9475230aeecf1445acd942525c2f2f6adc846f4e\nparent cd9e2a6a5a63e03f404797944d056025f8e53df0\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780473847 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780473847 +0300\n\nfeat(lifecycle): run insights cron at a fixed UTC hour, not a boot-relative interval (#277)\n\n## What\n\nThe `lifecycle-insights` cron (PR #238) currently uses the generic\nrun-then-sleep interval cadence: it fires **once immediately at\ncore-operations startup**, then every ~24h *after the previous tick\nfinishes*. That anchors the run to whenever the service last deployed\nand **drifts** by each tick's duration — so insights can land at any\nhour and move around over time.\n\nThis pins it to a **configurable off-peak wall-clock hour** (default\n**02:00 UTC**).\n\n## How\n\n- **scheduler**: optional `delay_provider` on `register()`. When set,\nthe loop sleeps `delay_provider()` (recomputed every cycle → drift-free)\n*before* each run and **skips the boot-time tick**. Interval mode is\nunchanged and remains the default — fully backward compatible.\n- **`seconds_until_next_utc_hour(hour)`** helper: strictly-future, ≤24h.\nThe strict-future guarantee also means an aligned task can't hot-loop\nafter a fast failure (next slot is a full day out once the hour passes).\n- **config**: `lifecycle_insights_interval_seconds` →\n`lifecycle_insights_run_at_hour` (int `0..23`, default `2`), validated\nat startup.\n- **app**: `lifecycle-insights` registered with the `delay_provider`;\nthe other five lifecycle ops keep their interval cadence.\n\nNo change to the opt-in (`auto_insights_enabled`, default off) or the\nconsumer-side activity gate — only **when** the daily tick fires.\n\n## Test\n\n- `ruff check` ✓ · `ruff format --check` ✓ · `mypy src/` ✓ · `pytest` ✓\n(28 passed)\n- New tests: helper math (same-day / rollover / exact-boundary / bounds\n/ out-of-range), aligned task does **not** fire at boot, aligned task\nsleeps-then-runs each cycle (drift-free), aligned failing tick recovers\nwithout killing the loop.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-03T08:04:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bca3dddadf5f439ce00585c2df23a992b39f550e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bca3dddadf5f439ce00585c2df23a992b39f550e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bca3dddadf5f439ce00585c2df23a992b39f550e/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cd9e2a6a5a63e03f404797944d056025f8e53df0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cd9e2a6a5a63e03f404797944d056025f8e53df0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/cd9e2a6a5a63e03f404797944d056025f8e53df0"}]},{"sha":"cd9e2a6a5a63e03f404797944d056025f8e53df0","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGNkOWUyYTZhNWE2M2UwM2Y0MDQ3OTc5NDRkMDU2MDI1ZjhlNTNkZjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-02T19:10:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:10:34Z"},"message":"feat(core-api): add fleet-scoped hard-purge endpoint (#275)\n\n## What\n\nAdds `POST /api/v1/fleet/{fleet_id}/purge` — a **hard purge** of a\nsingle fleet's entire footprint within a tenant: memories, entities,\nrelations, agents, documents, analysis/dedup rows, nodes, and commands.\nIt's the per-fleet analogue of the org-delete tenant purge\n(`purge_tenant_data`).\n\nContrast with the existing `DELETE /api/v1/fleet/{fleet_id}`, which\nremoves only the fleet's **nodes + commands** and intentionally keeps\nmemories for history. This new route HARD-deletes the fleet's\nmemories/agents too.\n\n## Why\n\nThe OpenClaw fleet-tester (`caura-ai/openclaw-fleet-tester`) creates\nrun-scoped fleets named `nightly-<run_id>-fleet-NN` on every nightly\nrun, but teardown only deletes the GCP VMs — it never removes the\nfleet's data from the shared dev tenant. That tenant accumulates\nnodes/memories/entities across runs, which confounds the isolation/trust\nprobes (org-wide recall returns every prior run's memories) and bloats\nthe tenant.\n\nA follow-up PR on the fleet-tester will call this endpoint at teardown\n(scoped strictly to its own `nightly-<run_id>-fleet-NN` ids), and a\none-time backfill will clear the already-accumulated stale fleets.\n\n## How\n\n**core-storage-api**\n- `PostgresService.purge_fleet_data(tenant_id, fleet_id)` — one\ntransaction, children-before-parents. `fleet_commands` (no `fleet_id`\ncolumn) is deleted by the fleet's node ids first so its count is\nexplicit rather than hidden in the `fleet_nodes` `ON DELETE CASCADE`;\n`memory_entity_links` rides the CASCADE from `memories`/`entities`.\nTables are schema-qualified (`public.`) with bound params, mirroring\n`purge_tenant_data`. `audit_log` + tenant-wide settings are untouched.\nIdempotent (zeros on a clean fleet).\n- `POST /purge/fleet-data` (VPC-trusted, no router auth — same trust\nmodel as `/purge/tenant-data`).\n\n**core-api**\n- Public `POST /fleet/{fleet_id}/purge`, gated by a write-capable\n**tenant-owner key**. Agent-scoped credentials are blocked\n(`enforce_not_agent_credential`) — a hard fleet purge is an admin-plane\noperation, on par with bulk memory delete and agent deletion. Writes an\naudit row. Idempotent (no 404 on a missing fleet, so a retried teardown\nis safe).\n- `storage_client.purge_fleet_data`.\n\n## Tests\n- `core-storage-api/tests/test_purge.py::TestPurgeFleetData` — scoped\ndeletion + per-table counts, idempotency, fleet-isolation within a\ntenant, cross-tenant safety, required-field + malformed-body validation.\n-\n`tests/test_api_fleet.py::test_purge_fleet_hard_deletes_nodes_and_memories`\n— node + memory hard-deleted through the public route.\n- `tests/test_agent_admin_authz.py` — agent credential is 403'd on the\npurge route (BFLA).\n\nLocal gate green: `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` (src), `mypy\ncore-api/src core-storage-api/src`, and the new tests pass against a\npgvector Postgres.\n\n## Notes\n- Irreversible by design (hard delete). The blast radius is bounded to\n`(tenant_id, fleet_id)` and the caller's own tenant.\n- First of a small cross-repo series (fleet-tester teardown integration\n+ one-time backfill follow).\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c06942aa95172c93571c1d3e61ecd0f9bd849d35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/c06942aa95172c93571c1d3e61ecd0f9bd849d35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/cd9e2a6a5a63e03f404797944d056025f8e53df0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHyqqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcH8QAFbg8mIe3tDYlAVQBhYe7KxY\nX4hpI5l5+QmDJyOeXKljFtnXvQDLlGB2szV+W2Xjso/kSNp1VChSR/VfS++crwBF\nBE7NC28IYLUeybIWiMECdwXlb6T4qwYChWAx+i/6/Sn01G0Jn5ODLrmfpfpW+YU9\niLySTSkY+ayW+Xuu4ezJb/tzcJnXyfqDrUcuEUBqlr5BWx2XIrv/Y2hjjlW8bxDq\n+1tzpg/vD2TaHkUl9iSXzLSCnZSroUG+mbQoDfTWNc17wOjgkzz86qK0tncspphF\nZfHqc/isyvmeyv/22Pk65Gv4NRN3JCuhh8xruVWhihm2oOfBHaz21qFFJy6tdI1A\njvkOpqeosNXw6PPW2sZ5nysLVxc1EglNw9AKog0BaqJZ8e7NRr5SXvM9havxUjeW\nljWUxWONSRae2wCvv21p5M9Y2JgTZV1YiwBFHJ2pdTPtZJxVC+JadT4hCxTE2BsT\n8gLPs0JviDRw0U1qRkEmczl5mPpZqnJQ5vvZBk5cY0ZLU/t7gTUsYJZVOWHbQPK0\n1OnojltuS6wYsAAxANN3tz/0uua3E1B/Mu3/w5aAObB2rOmV2GioIcfQPLOYCocX\n0HVl84bqKLW1gRfPHf6KGtFIFRq8ISgeJAJB/f50PdeBZt6o97Ql8KBQVE+CRwGI\nQSjeXnEgXzPjQowJlmlf\n=XnhZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c06942aa95172c93571c1d3e61ecd0f9bd849d35\nparent 573857c70867541069d4f8e8157864b19372f5d1\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1780427434 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780427434 +0300\n\nfeat(core-api): add fleet-scoped hard-purge endpoint (#275)\n\n## What\n\nAdds `POST /api/v1/fleet/{fleet_id}/purge` — a **hard purge** of a\nsingle fleet's entire footprint within a tenant: memories, entities,\nrelations, agents, documents, analysis/dedup rows, nodes, and commands.\nIt's the per-fleet analogue of the org-delete tenant purge\n(`purge_tenant_data`).\n\nContrast with the existing `DELETE /api/v1/fleet/{fleet_id}`, which\nremoves only the fleet's **nodes + commands** and intentionally keeps\nmemories for history. This new route HARD-deletes the fleet's\nmemories/agents too.\n\n## Why\n\nThe OpenClaw fleet-tester (`caura-ai/openclaw-fleet-tester`) creates\nrun-scoped fleets named `nightly-<run_id>-fleet-NN` on every nightly\nrun, but teardown only deletes the GCP VMs — it never removes the\nfleet's data from the shared dev tenant. That tenant accumulates\nnodes/memories/entities across runs, which confounds the isolation/trust\nprobes (org-wide recall returns every prior run's memories) and bloats\nthe tenant.\n\nA follow-up PR on the fleet-tester will call this endpoint at teardown\n(scoped strictly to its own `nightly-<run_id>-fleet-NN` ids), and a\none-time backfill will clear the already-accumulated stale fleets.\n\n## How\n\n**core-storage-api**\n- `PostgresService.purge_fleet_data(tenant_id, fleet_id)` — one\ntransaction, children-before-parents. `fleet_commands` (no `fleet_id`\ncolumn) is deleted by the fleet's node ids first so its count is\nexplicit rather than hidden in the `fleet_nodes` `ON DELETE CASCADE`;\n`memory_entity_links` rides the CASCADE from `memories`/`entities`.\nTables are schema-qualified (`public.`) with bound params, mirroring\n`purge_tenant_data`. `audit_log` + tenant-wide settings are untouched.\nIdempotent (zeros on a clean fleet).\n- `POST /purge/fleet-data` (VPC-trusted, no router auth — same trust\nmodel as `/purge/tenant-data`).\n\n**core-api**\n- Public `POST /fleet/{fleet_id}/purge`, gated by a write-capable\n**tenant-owner key**. Agent-scoped credentials are blocked\n(`enforce_not_agent_credential`) — a hard fleet purge is an admin-plane\noperation, on par with bulk memory delete and agent deletion. Writes an\naudit row. Idempotent (no 404 on a missing fleet, so a retried teardown\nis safe).\n- `storage_client.purge_fleet_data`.\n\n## Tests\n- `core-storage-api/tests/test_purge.py::TestPurgeFleetData` — scoped\ndeletion + per-table counts, idempotency, fleet-isolation within a\ntenant, cross-tenant safety, required-field + malformed-body validation.\n-\n`tests/test_api_fleet.py::test_purge_fleet_hard_deletes_nodes_and_memories`\n— node + memory hard-deleted through the public route.\n- `tests/test_agent_admin_authz.py` — agent credential is 403'd on the\npurge route (BFLA).\n\nLocal gate green: `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` (src), `mypy\ncore-api/src core-storage-api/src`, and the new tests pass against a\npgvector Postgres.\n\n## Notes\n- Irreversible by design (hard delete). The blast radius is bounded to\n`(tenant_id, fleet_id)` and the caller's own tenant.\n- First of a small cross-repo series (fleet-tester teardown integration\n+ one-time backfill follow).\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-02T19:10:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cd9e2a6a5a63e03f404797944d056025f8e53df0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/cd9e2a6a5a63e03f404797944d056025f8e53df0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cd9e2a6a5a63e03f404797944d056025f8e53df0/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"573857c70867541069d4f8e8157864b19372f5d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/573857c70867541069d4f8e8157864b19372f5d1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/573857c70867541069d4f8e8157864b19372f5d1"}]},{"sha":"573857c70867541069d4f8e8157864b19372f5d1","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU3Mzg1N2M3MDg2NzU0MTA2OWQ0ZjhlODE1Nzg2NGIxOTM3MmY1ZDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-02T15:01:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T15:01:40Z"},"message":"fix(plugin): context-engine auto-recall, smoke cleanup & post-upgrade allowlist drift (#274)\n\n## Summary\n\nThree independent plugin defects surfaced while validating the MemClaw\nplugin against **OpenClaw 2026.5.28** on a wet-test VM\n(`openclaw-test-ran`). All three are verified — #1 and #2 live against\n`memclaw.net`, #3 via unit tests.\n\n### 1. Auto-recall injected nothing (high impact)\nThe REST `POST /api/v1/search` endpoint returns `{ items: [...] }`\n(core-api `SearchResponse(items=...)`), but `assemble()` and\n`searchMemories` parsed **`.results`** → always `[]`. Context-engine\nauto-recall has therefore been silently empty (masked because the\nexplicit `memclaw_recall` *tool* uses the MCP path, which does return\n`results`). The bootstrap smoke test parsed `.results` too, so it also\nmisfired (`SMOKE TEST FAILED: … check EMBEDDING_PROVIDER`).\n- New `parseSearchItems()` helper: `items` → `results` → bare-array\nfallback, never throws.\n- Applied at all three `/search` consumers: recall, smoke test,\nmemory-runtime search.\n- **Verified live:** recall block now injects the matching memory\n(`RECALL block present: true`).\n\n### 2. Smoke-test memory leaked on every restart\nBootstrap cleanup `DELETE /memories/{id}` omitted the required\n`tenant_id` query param → 422 (swallowed by `.catch(()=>{})`) → a\n`__health_check__` memory accumulated on each start. Hoist `tid` out of\nthe `try` and pass `{ tenant_id }`.\n- **Verified live:** 0 leaked memories after bootstrap (was: one per\nrestart).\n\n### 3. Tools dropped from `tools.alsoAllow` after a plugin upgrade\n`autoFixAllowlist` already adds all `MEMCLAW_TOOLS`, but the gate ran it\n**once** (`.allowlist-applied` flag). So a tool added in a later plugin\nversion (`memclaw_keystones`) never landed in `alsoAllow` on existing\ninstalls — and OpenClaw 2026.5.28's new `tools.profile` (grants core\ntools + `alsoAllow` only) then **stripped it**. Extracted pure\n`shouldRunAutoFix()` that also re-runs on drift (a missing tool, or an\nunclaimed contextEngine slot); `autoFixAllowlist` is idempotent so clean\ninstalls still no-op. Also added `memclaw_keystones` to the wet-test\ninstaller's tool list.\n\n## Tests\n- `parseSearchItems` — 5 cases (items / results / both / bare array /\nempty·null·primitive).\n- `shouldRunAutoFix` — truth table (force / opt-out / first-run /\nmissing-tool / unclaimed-slot / clean).\n- Full plugin suite green: **273 passing**.\n\n## Scope / non-goals\n- The **compaction SDK-bridge** and **`assemble` contract** were\nverified *unaffected* by 2026.5.28 (runtime still calls `assemble()` and\ninjects `systemPromptAddition`) — not touched here.\n- **Skills-discovery truncation** (new 300/200 caps) is intentionally\n**out of scope**.\n- `plugin/dist` is gitignored; build artifacts not committed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1b897594b748ab29d3f37f4eaac7fb881934f250","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/1b897594b748ab29d3f37f4eaac7fb881934f250"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/573857c70867541069d4f8e8157864b19372f5d1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHvBUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxyIQAIiagJqIVSytvxjiT/iBveWa\nLMn8eYijexGU7W78ObNPyUDCtm3yfmC52G+KWcS4Chi5Bp3mXTpQYe9jcAwKzr8M\nqgExXGFb1TrJMzSFO01L9yjijXr+6oUwM7B6jrWzHz3p2jhRLTgtn7A/kSAT//Mi\n7d65B8+FgGtMESNOXCmI8/GT76dqwg+E+27/lS1jMk5zgKjiUohnsfGpxL3aUYq/\nHCNg9uk41DD5wgVQYDP2QC1hqx98Rs7eoZj6mfrIA03VKKrmFFUlm+z0JAihOQai\nhoADeqflsh3dJe5zNMxJK8+U2GU8szCztRF75C1kgtLBf88jfpSid02aWW4nX1cC\nvcO809gg9qPt4dm6qfc/HwbKjZg7r5Z7Sc44aJE5l7S0PLS5p9YPXMc8EWZZCswh\npnnnV6JFdp9Q0pemYImc8m3mJBEvT0jRnw9EOMlyHBF3E06tzuw80FQedES8gvSO\n7xgpDlKqoW9d2vvSY3j61VIPQfjjDVTz8htboDwX8XVw/IMpuEVPWKRBGTWcufGq\nQPU0ZutST3IWojs6GeuR/GWEp5DwbDyiGECe9/IRG/2EECnfU1GG3D7ECWE+fdTg\nMd9/3ndzULT9MFo3crVQw9NLrJfHy34GYkaPhGXIYj0ms8nCsd0+OFGvP/2N5FgL\nNtmGuaiHZSMJ2EC5BQx4\n=AbEG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1b897594b748ab29d3f37f4eaac7fb881934f250\nparent 45f83d6199c744ae5aab7a2b95dd230f85cc00e0\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780412500 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780412500 +0300\n\nfix(plugin): context-engine auto-recall, smoke cleanup & post-upgrade allowlist drift (#274)\n\n## Summary\n\nThree independent plugin defects surfaced while validating the MemClaw\nplugin against **OpenClaw 2026.5.28** on a wet-test VM\n(`openclaw-test-ran`). All three are verified — #1 and #2 live against\n`memclaw.net`, #3 via unit tests.\n\n### 1. Auto-recall injected nothing (high impact)\nThe REST `POST /api/v1/search` endpoint returns `{ items: [...] }`\n(core-api `SearchResponse(items=...)`), but `assemble()` and\n`searchMemories` parsed **`.results`** → always `[]`. Context-engine\nauto-recall has therefore been silently empty (masked because the\nexplicit `memclaw_recall` *tool* uses the MCP path, which does return\n`results`). The bootstrap smoke test parsed `.results` too, so it also\nmisfired (`SMOKE TEST FAILED: … check EMBEDDING_PROVIDER`).\n- New `parseSearchItems()` helper: `items` → `results` → bare-array\nfallback, never throws.\n- Applied at all three `/search` consumers: recall, smoke test,\nmemory-runtime search.\n- **Verified live:** recall block now injects the matching memory\n(`RECALL block present: true`).\n\n### 2. Smoke-test memory leaked on every restart\nBootstrap cleanup `DELETE /memories/{id}` omitted the required\n`tenant_id` query param → 422 (swallowed by `.catch(()=>{})`) → a\n`__health_check__` memory accumulated on each start. Hoist `tid` out of\nthe `try` and pass `{ tenant_id }`.\n- **Verified live:** 0 leaked memories after bootstrap (was: one per\nrestart).\n\n### 3. Tools dropped from `tools.alsoAllow` after a plugin upgrade\n`autoFixAllowlist` already adds all `MEMCLAW_TOOLS`, but the gate ran it\n**once** (`.allowlist-applied` flag). So a tool added in a later plugin\nversion (`memclaw_keystones`) never landed in `alsoAllow` on existing\ninstalls — and OpenClaw 2026.5.28's new `tools.profile` (grants core\ntools + `alsoAllow` only) then **stripped it**. Extracted pure\n`shouldRunAutoFix()` that also re-runs on drift (a missing tool, or an\nunclaimed contextEngine slot); `autoFixAllowlist` is idempotent so clean\ninstalls still no-op. Also added `memclaw_keystones` to the wet-test\ninstaller's tool list.\n\n## Tests\n- `parseSearchItems` — 5 cases (items / results / both / bare array /\nempty·null·primitive).\n- `shouldRunAutoFix` — truth table (force / opt-out / first-run /\nmissing-tool / unclaimed-slot / clean).\n- Full plugin suite green: **273 passing**.\n\n## Scope / non-goals\n- The **compaction SDK-bridge** and **`assemble` contract** were\nverified *unaffected* by 2026.5.28 (runtime still calls `assemble()` and\ninjects `systemPromptAddition`) — not touched here.\n- **Skills-discovery truncation** (new 300/200 caps) is intentionally\n**out of scope**.\n- `plugin/dist` is gitignored; build artifacts not committed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-02T15:01:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/573857c70867541069d4f8e8157864b19372f5d1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/573857c70867541069d4f8e8157864b19372f5d1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/573857c70867541069d4f8e8157864b19372f5d1/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"45f83d6199c744ae5aab7a2b95dd230f85cc00e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/45f83d6199c744ae5aab7a2b95dd230f85cc00e0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/45f83d6199c744ae5aab7a2b95dd230f85cc00e0"}]},{"sha":"45f83d6199c744ae5aab7a2b95dd230f85cc00e0","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQ1ZjgzZDYxOTljNzQ0YWU1YWFiN2EyYjk1ZGQyMzBmODVjYzAwZTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"eyal-bl","email":"eyal.b@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-02T14:01:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T14:01:38Z"},"message":"CAURA-698 feat(search): decline ENTITY_LOOKUP short-circuit on over-broad FTS matches (#273)\n\n## Summary\n\nEtoro prod data (6h sample, 2026-06-02) showed the now-working\nENTITY_LOOKUP short-circuit firing on **89.8%** of all `/search` calls —\nmedian 41 matched entities, max 5,415. The path is designed for *\"user\nnamed a specific entity\"* queries, not for narrative queries that\nincidentally match many entities. Once the count is high enough the\nshort-circuit returns 50 hop-proximate-but-low-relevance memories and\nskips the rest of the pipeline (vector scoring, FTS rank, freshness), so\nthe noise can't be re-filtered downstream.\n\nAdds a count threshold gate: when entity FTS returns more than\n`ENTITY_LOOKUP_MAX_MATCHES = 100`, log + decline the short-circuit and\nfall through to the keyword/semantic cascade.\n\n## Threshold choice\n\n| Threshold | Caught (% of legit queries from etoro 6h CSV) | Tradeoff |\n|---|---|---|\n| 50 | ~58% redirect | Aggressive, risk of false fallthroughs in 50-100\nzone |\n| **100** | ~37% redirect | Sits well above legit median (41), catches\nover-broad tail |\n| 200 | ~32% redirect | Conservative; medium-broad 100-200 zone stays\nmisclassified |\n\n100 chosen for first-pass — easy to tune from the constant later.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `test_entity_lookup_fires_when_match_count_at_threshold` —\nboundary case; exactly `ENTITY_LOOKUP_MAX_MATCHES` allowed through (gate\nis `>`, not `>=`).\n- [x]\n`test_entity_lookup_falls_through_when_match_count_exceeds_threshold` —\none over; downstream storage calls (`_expand_per_fleet`,\n`get_memory_ids_by_entity_ids`, `load_memories_by_ids`) MUST NOT\nexecute; decision logged at INFO for ops visibility.\n- [x] Negative control: both tests fail when the gate is stashed\n(ImportError on the new constant).\n- [x] 32 targeted tests pass with the change in place.\n\n## What this doesn't do\n\n- Doesn't fix the \"100 matches but all weak FTS rank\" middle zone —\nthat's gate 2 from the design discussion (surface `ts_rank_cd` from\nstorage, threshold on best rank). Separate ticket if numbers still look\nbad after deploy.\n- Doesn't fix the upstream OR-vs-AND tsquery semantics that produce the\nhigh match counts in the first place — separate consideration.\n- Doesn't tighten the broad `except Exception:` at\n`classify_query.py:123`. Still a tracked follow-up.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Eyal Blyachman <eyal.b@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"6d52d306741f05c603f3778a5ed4defa45a51a40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/6d52d306741f05c603f3778a5ed4defa45a51a40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/45f83d6199c744ae5aab7a2b95dd230f85cc00e0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHuJCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACcIQAEP6bhRkvJZd2A3K2+ypEjjD\nIsI0W/62UiVnKLpuvZ4Q6aY87OVb5Wxj4F3LHH4vp+wFCK5j0fujI166t7iCZNE+\n2x2FKJeCnMNwLKvUkKXquGjvLlzXarU3NGOyCwaof84qux/qG5j1YAZwzIstLZPc\nq9530VBZwKyQD4S0sHJH5Tjl5e1Bd/X3jocsaqiTa1zpG6jTDsiQXnEWPyYrAF+2\ncjyXyvnEGZdHOyjDLO87x0iomyohG1UqZliyYrPPmGPU2Kp+ZEW6AURrb0bn7PAc\npru0Cb86BvSfFIUwTZy6/xhcXugKLiG5Jpfvv2dVQsN5sLrF++C6qrw/oxhMT3f7\nIzrmOmvI8gnExfJcPAHfI9s9ND6qmDrDRAcrQ9QdR5lxghjq7JMwGA3SqXFLubW9\nBWGTP/rq5NpzXsHDtnAIct9fOM2jsfoSGOORnFA4saQUDFY5Pbgfg0fSC2MwXDcw\neAtV61QW6ZRXJwRhUlqiZVZXgOAOFxqkI02JTso1WI1dHr87T6krmUauFucK5dtB\nr4wN4UJ2+9w4E7dDQETWlcETLRXIWUjf/xmZH1gfk4nWNQBLpNESerV/qREnp3pL\n3ejdQju6YiaU0lpyZHuYjmKPNHvSEWGcWRc+3JK5+0Nj8BULNKED5TgzR577HoEu\nqkBjmh2XtK9ZwL3N+19+\n=VzIX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6d52d306741f05c603f3778a5ed4defa45a51a40\nparent 7c911638eadfefb806166a8dac4ab92277c9de81\nauthor eyal-bl <eyal.b@caura.ai> 1780408898 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780408898 +0300\n\nCAURA-698 feat(search): decline ENTITY_LOOKUP short-circuit on over-broad FTS matches (#273)\n\n## Summary\n\nEtoro prod data (6h sample, 2026-06-02) showed the now-working\nENTITY_LOOKUP short-circuit firing on **89.8%** of all `/search` calls —\nmedian 41 matched entities, max 5,415. The path is designed for *\"user\nnamed a specific entity\"* queries, not for narrative queries that\nincidentally match many entities. Once the count is high enough the\nshort-circuit returns 50 hop-proximate-but-low-relevance memories and\nskips the rest of the pipeline (vector scoring, FTS rank, freshness), so\nthe noise can't be re-filtered downstream.\n\nAdds a count threshold gate: when entity FTS returns more than\n`ENTITY_LOOKUP_MAX_MATCHES = 100`, log + decline the short-circuit and\nfall through to the keyword/semantic cascade.\n\n## Threshold choice\n\n| Threshold | Caught (% of legit queries from etoro 6h CSV) | Tradeoff |\n|---|---|---|\n| 50 | ~58% redirect | Aggressive, risk of false fallthroughs in 50-100\nzone |\n| **100** | ~37% redirect | Sits well above legit median (41), catches\nover-broad tail |\n| 200 | ~32% redirect | Conservative; medium-broad 100-200 zone stays\nmisclassified |\n\n100 chosen for first-pass — easy to tune from the constant later.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `test_entity_lookup_fires_when_match_count_at_threshold` —\nboundary case; exactly `ENTITY_LOOKUP_MAX_MATCHES` allowed through (gate\nis `>`, not `>=`).\n- [x]\n`test_entity_lookup_falls_through_when_match_count_exceeds_threshold` —\none over; downstream storage calls (`_expand_per_fleet`,\n`get_memory_ids_by_entity_ids`, `load_memories_by_ids`) MUST NOT\nexecute; decision logged at INFO for ops visibility.\n- [x] Negative control: both tests fail when the gate is stashed\n(ImportError on the new constant).\n- [x] 32 targeted tests pass with the change in place.\n\n## What this doesn't do\n\n- Doesn't fix the \"100 matches but all weak FTS rank\" middle zone —\nthat's gate 2 from the design discussion (surface `ts_rank_cd` from\nstorage, threshold on best rank). Separate ticket if numbers still look\nbad after deploy.\n- Doesn't fix the upstream OR-vs-AND tsquery semantics that produce the\nhigh match counts in the first place — separate consideration.\n- Doesn't tighten the broad `except Exception:` at\n`classify_query.py:123`. Still a tracked follow-up.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Eyal Blyachman <eyal.b@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-02T14:01:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/45f83d6199c744ae5aab7a2b95dd230f85cc00e0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/45f83d6199c744ae5aab7a2b95dd230f85cc00e0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/45f83d6199c744ae5aab7a2b95dd230f85cc00e0/comments","author":{"login":"eyal-bl","id":262085605,"node_id":"U_kgDOD58b5Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262085605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl","html_url":"https://github.com/eyal-bl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7c911638eadfefb806166a8dac4ab92277c9de81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7c911638eadfefb806166a8dac4ab92277c9de81","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/7c911638eadfefb806166a8dac4ab92277c9de81"}]},{"sha":"7c911638eadfefb806166a8dac4ab92277c9de81","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDdjOTExNjM4ZWFkZmVmYjgwNjE2NmE4ZGFjNGFiOTIyNzdjOWRlODE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-02T11:36:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T11:36:53Z"},"message":"CAURA-130 feat(contradiction): Path C kill-switch + entity-links preflight (#272)\n\n## Summary\n\nTwo safety controls on Path C contradiction detection, bundled because\nthey touch the same code path and share testing infrastructure.\n\n### L3.8 — Per-tenant retraction kill-switch\n\nCAURA-128/129 tightened the retraction judge but left no operational\nescape valve. This PR adds `ResolvedConfig.retraction_enabled` (default\n`True`) backed by\n`organization_settings.settings[\"write\"][\"retraction_enabled\"]`. Ops can\nflip per-tenant in the JSONB blob without a deploy.\n\nMirrors the existing `triple_emission_enabled` pattern (CAURA-123):\n- `DEFAULT_SETTINGS[\"write\"][\"retraction_enabled\"]` — `None`\nplaceholder; resolver returns `True` when None/absent.\n- `_LEAF_TYPES[\"write.retraction_enabled\"] = bool` — type validation on\nPATCH.\n- `ResolvedConfig.retraction_enabled` — property reading the blob with\nTrue default.\n- Early-return at the top of `_attempt_path_c_retraction` with INFO log.\n\n### L3.4 — Entity-links subject preflight (forward Path C)\n\nThe A1 #17 subject preflight only fires when **both** memories have\nnon-NULL `subject_entity_id`. When one side is NULL (heuristic missed\nbut entity-extraction populated `entity_links` with a subject-role\nentity), same-canonical-name distinct-entity pairs — the\n**`priya`-collision case** from the inline TODO at\n`contradiction_detector.py:1100` — silently fell through to the LLM\njudge, which mis-classified them as contradictions.\n\nNew plumbing:\n- `_extract_subject_canonical_identity(entities)` — pure helper\nreturning `(canonical_name, entity_type, entity_id)` of the first\nsubject-role entity, or `None`. Identity keyed on `entity_id`.\n- `_fetch_entity_context`'s hydrated row now includes `entity_id`\n(additive; doesn't break CAURA-129 consumers).\n- Forward Path C preflight (post A1 #17 filter): fetches entity context\nfor the fall-through set (candidates where `subject_entity_id` is NULL\non at least one side), compares canonical identity by `entity_id`, drops\non mismatch.\n\n### Cost guards (per D3 in the plan)\n\n| Case | Behaviour |\n|---|---|\n| Both `subject_entity_id` non-NULL | L3.4 stage **skips entirely** —\nlegacy A1 #17 already covered it. Zero new round-trips. |\n| At least one side NULL | Fetch via parallel `gather` wrapped in\n`asyncio.wait_for(timeout=5.0)`. 1 RT for new_memory + N RTs for\nfall-through candidates. |\n| Storage error / timeout / missing subject identity | **Fail-open** —\nkeep candidates, let the LLM judge decide. Conservative against losing\nreal contradictions on a transient hiccup. |\n\n## Tests (25 collected across both files)\n\n**`tests/test_a4_13_path_c_retraction.py`** — 2 new kill-switch tests:\n- `test_kill_switch_disabled_skips_retraction`\n- `test_kill_switch_enabled_default_allows_retraction`\n\n**`tests/test_caura_130_path_c_safety.py`** *(new — 14 tests)*:\n- **6** `_extract_subject_canonical_identity` helper tests\n(first-subject-role, empty, no-subject, name fallback, skip missing\nentity_id, role match case-insensitive).\n- **4** `ResolvedConfig.retraction_enabled` resolver tests (defaults,\nexplicit True/False).\n- **4** forward-path preflight tests:\n  - Drops collision when `subject_entity_id` NULL on either side.\n  - Keeps candidate when subjects truly match (same entity_id).\n- Skipped entirely when both subject_entity_id non-NULL (zero RT cost).\n  - Fails open on storage error.\n\nAll CAURA-128/129 tests preserved unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] `python -m py_compile` clean.\n- [x] `uv run ruff check core-api/src/` clean.\n- [x] `uv run ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `pytest --collect-only` collects 25 tests.\n- [ ] CI runs full pytest (Postgres required for autouse fixture).\n- [ ] Post-merge wet test:\n- Re-run `scripts/repro_contradictions_race.py` on dev → expect ≥95%\ndetection across all gaps.\n- Optional: build a synthetic ``priya``-collision repro to confirm L3.4\ndrops the false-positive.\n\n## Rollback\n\nSingle `git revert` of the merged squash. No DB migration, no schema\nchange. Per-tenant kill-switch state lives in JSONB; clearing the key\nrestores default-ON behaviour.\n\n## Follow-ups (not in this PR)\n\n- L3.4 in retraction path — already handled by CAURA-129's entity-aware\njudge; no change needed.\n- Per-fleet kill-switch granularity — defer until tenant-level proves\ninsufficient.\n- Tier-3 `disputed` status + tiebreaker.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"58856edbd704056dd12792d12819272e4092bb4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/58856edbd704056dd12792d12819272e4092bb4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/7c911638eadfefb806166a8dac4ab92277c9de81","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHsBVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFIUQAB/ALXkUXciYs6gaoDt5TAy5\n4iBUzxN0S2UUX0xofWJdylS+dq5BoX16aByOvRtj9DLXrJVM9wauKXLODSlODbIX\nGETzeOaOTctHF6nMvjXrEF+L5gPci0w83Io/cIyQdPGzlt/KNMEiYPUqbcEj96MP\n6qBf46AIx8tkxjVhCvncKILRIK0miAtCbB08SRXFKkPODj20txqB5fohR/CjimIk\nwFWtVKyjeBFh93bLViB2SvWLU1EiR8IdBAdqZsowxYfSkRpznIsDcu9nEmzXwoPg\nga+XrZXS4ZbF5puK7wyCLbvmblQhL4QhhGWCjFhke6yWmZHJZCFRcb/LhwtfG3vi\nHiDzW2S1AzwXwu8ammFJo4NGXUArvEMRy636OQoN4cszGOdbCXnNVZKiFB2or7so\nwZgAJJLqdd9dV+xnLgPBpRZvx9K7O3z97KveIdupayCoQ4CGBX2rhdgUXNU1SvQ/\nuz/zWFMbfbVZrxFogCTCGitMFZPClPFX3PqtbtSy5GyO7mWjJodSHn3ScuF//VRy\nZmOPgTmcyuV8I/4z4+CTkdLD40/EIaErvqirb7tuz01Gvt+MB0RSFgckS30TGcUH\nHYuoQycw3H/f9Ouy9uvewrNXrGs9QETSF11Qc1ryIMzzXd28mcMMNw5o0qGQQ4XP\navJTed7chFZ3EYZZ0uSP\n=oyW6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 58856edbd704056dd12792d12819272e4092bb4a\nparent 07661c55cf3d21fbb4349d9c342d7fdf036a7483\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780400213 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780400213 +0300\n\nCAURA-130 feat(contradiction): Path C kill-switch + entity-links preflight (#272)\n\n## Summary\n\nTwo safety controls on Path C contradiction detection, bundled because\nthey touch the same code path and share testing infrastructure.\n\n### L3.8 — Per-tenant retraction kill-switch\n\nCAURA-128/129 tightened the retraction judge but left no operational\nescape valve. This PR adds `ResolvedConfig.retraction_enabled` (default\n`True`) backed by\n`organization_settings.settings[\"write\"][\"retraction_enabled\"]`. Ops can\nflip per-tenant in the JSONB blob without a deploy.\n\nMirrors the existing `triple_emission_enabled` pattern (CAURA-123):\n- `DEFAULT_SETTINGS[\"write\"][\"retraction_enabled\"]` — `None`\nplaceholder; resolver returns `True` when None/absent.\n- `_LEAF_TYPES[\"write.retraction_enabled\"] = bool` — type validation on\nPATCH.\n- `ResolvedConfig.retraction_enabled` — property reading the blob with\nTrue default.\n- Early-return at the top of `_attempt_path_c_retraction` with INFO log.\n\n### L3.4 — Entity-links subject preflight (forward Path C)\n\nThe A1 #17 subject preflight only fires when **both** memories have\nnon-NULL `subject_entity_id`. When one side is NULL (heuristic missed\nbut entity-extraction populated `entity_links` with a subject-role\nentity), same-canonical-name distinct-entity pairs — the\n**`priya`-collision case** from the inline TODO at\n`contradiction_detector.py:1100` — silently fell through to the LLM\njudge, which mis-classified them as contradictions.\n\nNew plumbing:\n- `_extract_subject_canonical_identity(entities)` — pure helper\nreturning `(canonical_name, entity_type, entity_id)` of the first\nsubject-role entity, or `None`. Identity keyed on `entity_id`.\n- `_fetch_entity_context`'s hydrated row now includes `entity_id`\n(additive; doesn't break CAURA-129 consumers).\n- Forward Path C preflight (post A1 #17 filter): fetches entity context\nfor the fall-through set (candidates where `subject_entity_id` is NULL\non at least one side), compares canonical identity by `entity_id`, drops\non mismatch.\n\n### Cost guards (per D3 in the plan)\n\n| Case | Behaviour |\n|---|---|\n| Both `subject_entity_id` non-NULL | L3.4 stage **skips entirely** —\nlegacy A1 #17 already covered it. Zero new round-trips. |\n| At least one side NULL | Fetch via parallel `gather` wrapped in\n`asyncio.wait_for(timeout=5.0)`. 1 RT for new_memory + N RTs for\nfall-through candidates. |\n| Storage error / timeout / missing subject identity | **Fail-open** —\nkeep candidates, let the LLM judge decide. Conservative against losing\nreal contradictions on a transient hiccup. |\n\n## Tests (25 collected across both files)\n\n**`tests/test_a4_13_path_c_retraction.py`** — 2 new kill-switch tests:\n- `test_kill_switch_disabled_skips_retraction`\n- `test_kill_switch_enabled_default_allows_retraction`\n\n**`tests/test_caura_130_path_c_safety.py`** *(new — 14 tests)*:\n- **6** `_extract_subject_canonical_identity` helper tests\n(first-subject-role, empty, no-subject, name fallback, skip missing\nentity_id, role match case-insensitive).\n- **4** `ResolvedConfig.retraction_enabled` resolver tests (defaults,\nexplicit True/False).\n- **4** forward-path preflight tests:\n  - Drops collision when `subject_entity_id` NULL on either side.\n  - Keeps candidate when subjects truly match (same entity_id).\n- Skipped entirely when both subject_entity_id non-NULL (zero RT cost).\n  - Fails open on storage error.\n\nAll CAURA-128/129 tests preserved unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] `python -m py_compile` clean.\n- [x] `uv run ruff check core-api/src/` clean.\n- [x] `uv run ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `pytest --collect-only` collects 25 tests.\n- [ ] CI runs full pytest (Postgres required for autouse fixture).\n- [ ] Post-merge wet test:\n- Re-run `scripts/repro_contradictions_race.py` on dev → expect ≥95%\ndetection across all gaps.\n- Optional: build a synthetic ``priya``-collision repro to confirm L3.4\ndrops the false-positive.\n\n## Rollback\n\nSingle `git revert` of the merged squash. No DB migration, no schema\nchange. Per-tenant kill-switch state lives in JSONB; clearing the key\nrestores default-ON behaviour.\n\n## Follow-ups (not in this PR)\n\n- L3.4 in retraction path — already handled by CAURA-129's entity-aware\njudge; no change needed.\n- Per-fleet kill-switch granularity — defer until tenant-level proves\ninsufficient.\n- Tier-3 `disputed` status + tiebreaker.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-02T11:36:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7c911638eadfefb806166a8dac4ab92277c9de81","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/7c911638eadfefb806166a8dac4ab92277c9de81","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7c911638eadfefb806166a8dac4ab92277c9de81/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"07661c55cf3d21fbb4349d9c342d7fdf036a7483","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/07661c55cf3d21fbb4349d9c342d7fdf036a7483","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/07661c55cf3d21fbb4349d9c342d7fdf036a7483"}]},{"sha":"07661c55cf3d21fbb4349d9c342d7fdf036a7483","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDA3NjYxYzU1Y2YzZDIxZmJiNDM0OWQ5YzM0MmQ3ZmRmMDM2YTc0ODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-02T06:27:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T06:27:33Z"},"message":"CAURA-129 feat(contradiction): entity-aware Path C retraction judge (#271)\n\n## Summary\n\nTier-2 fix for the Path C retraction non-determinism class. CAURA-128\n(PR #267) raised the confidence floor 0.60 → 0.90 to mitigate the\nstochastic-flip case. This PR delivers the deeper fix the original\ndocstring at `contradiction_detector.py:898-901` promised but never\nimplemented: **Path C now asks a structurally different question than\nPath A**, grounded on resolved entities rather than raw-text NER.\n\nStatus report L3.1:\n`docs/contradiction-detection-status-2026-05-26.html`.\n\n## Architecture diff\n\n**Before (CAURA-128):**\n```\n_attempt_path_c_retraction\n  └─ _llm_contradiction_check(new_content, old_content, ...)   ← same prompt as Path A\n                                                                  same inputs as Path A\n                                                                  → stochastic flip\n```\n\n**After (CAURA-129):**\n```\n_attempt_path_c_retraction\n  ├─ _fetch_entity_context(new_memory)   ── get_entity_links_for_memories + get_entity ×N\n  ├─ _fetch_entity_context(candidate)    ── (gather'd in parallel)\n  ├─ if either empty → log + skip       ── guard against degenerate inputs\n  └─ _llm_entity_aware_contradiction_check(\n        new_content, old_content,\n        new_entities, old_entities,      ← AUTHORITATIVE entity context\n        tenant_config\n     )                                    → ENTITY_AWARE_CONTRADICTION_PROMPT\n                                           same JSON schema → _judge_contradiction reused\n```\n\n## What ships\n\n| Component | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `ENTITY_AWARE_CONTRADICTION_PROMPT` | New template; identical JSON\nschema to `CONTRADICTION_PROMPT` so the parser is reused. Explicitly\nframes resolved entities as authoritative. |\n| `_format_entity_context(entities)` | Render `{name, entity_type,\nrole}` dicts as a bulleted block for the prompt. |\n| `_fetch_entity_context(sc, memory_id)` | Compose\n`get_entity_links_for_memories` (1 RT, batch) + per-entity `get_entity`\n(gather'd). Errors swallowed → returns `[]`. |\n| `_llm_entity_aware_contradiction_check(...)` | Same fallback chain,\nsame 10s timeout, same parser. Service label\n`contradiction-entity-aware`. |\n| Rewired `_attempt_path_c_retraction` | Fetch both contexts in\nparallel; skip retraction (log INFO) when either side empty; otherwise\ncall new judge. |\n\nThreshold stays at `_CONF_CLEAN = 0.90` for this PR — we want production\nsignal that the new judge is genuinely more deterministic before\nlowering it. A follow-up can drop to `_CONF_GATE2` after data.\n\n## Tests (25 collected across both files)\n\n**`tests/test_a4_13_path_c_retraction.py`** — 9 tests, all 7 originals\npreserve their semantics; patch target updated to the new judge. Default\nmock now returns one resolved subject per memory. 2 new guard tests:\n- `test_no_retraction_when_new_memory_has_no_entity_links`\n- `test_no_retraction_when_candidate_has_no_entity_links`\n\n**`tests/test_caura_129_entity_aware_retraction_prompt.py`** *(new)* —\n16 direct tests:\n- Prompt: required placeholders, JSON schema for parser reuse,\nauthoritative-entity framing, end-to-end `.format()` with realistic\ninputs.\n- `_format_entity_context`: bullets, empty sentinel, missing-field\ndefaults.\n- `_fetch_entity_context`: two-round-trip composition,\ncanonical_name/name fallback, links-lookup error swallow, per-entity\nerror tolerance.\n- `_llm_entity_aware_contradiction_check`: `call_with_fallback` wiring\n(service label, timeout, model_attr), prompt payload carries both entity\nblocks, 500-char truncation per side.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] `python -m py_compile` clean on production + both test files.\n- [x] `pytest --collect-only` collects 25 tests with no errors.\n- [ ] CI runs pytest with Postgres (local environment unavailable).\n- [ ] Post-merge wet test: `scripts/repro_contradictions_race.py` on\ndev. Expect detection rate ≥ 95% across all gaps.\n\n## Cost analysis\n\nPath C is post-commit async (no user is waiting). The new fetch adds\n**3-4 storage round-trips per retraction attempt**:\n\n- 1 round-trip: batch `get_entity_links_for_memories([new_id, cand_id])`\n— wait, currently we pass one memory_id at a time per\n`_fetch_entity_context` call. *Could* be optimised in a follow-up to one\nbatch call covering both memories; not done here to keep diff surgical.\n- N round-trips: per-entity `get_entity` calls, parallelised via\n`asyncio.gather`. Typical N = 2–5 per memory.\n\nTotal latency: roughly the slowest `get_entity` call ≈ 50–150ms p95.\nInvisible to the write path.\n\n## Rollback\n\nSingle `git revert` of the merged squash fully restores the\npost-CAURA-128 state. No DB migration, no schema change, no flag flip.\n\n## Follow-ups (not in this PR)\n\n1. Tier-3 belt-and-suspenders: replace silent retract with `disputed`\nstatus + tiebreaker (separate ticket).\n2. Per-tenant retraction kill-switch (L3.8).\n3. Optional storage micro-opt: one round-trip per retraction via a\n`get_memory_with_entity_details(memory_id)` endpoint (file as P3 if\nprofiling warrants).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"4ebd76a7ff8e864e2c07a0399980a205aa8e54bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4ebd76a7ff8e864e2c07a0399980a205aa8e54bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/07661c55cf3d21fbb4349d9c342d7fdf036a7483","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHnfVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2CMQAKWjvRkwjOR9Kls69VCoGkaa\nd28IIr1s8J6FccrnuBeQiLS+lIu8x3nqk/s4uMao8+qPRLxDfnXkhyVBLBZKX08t\nixmiLnOdgQdcnNnntkhAlXejffq7tRhBqNVBXFzFFTfKxD3U+x5U/4oW1taSnNvO\nImcSA7aypRKlSS81rdtElYGpKXLbDBXD01d7wanLnkW+INaj2kIewEV+yQKuHdlj\nFZDC/Iz0c0BFoTBJ/o8GnuTYhiw4UYE1LPLUxU6mkmQbgK90RWEROD6fdEJv4btX\nqN7xVJ6+AyOqshGY6BTSzAMM2lgz/GdOJVQ9tnlfCGBmWc5UbkVFj2IKLUWhw7L5\n/6r1Zpe9U8Wt+MQ/tw1ppY1ol8xpTkAJrNP97f1MXPE1BmxIlB1Cv1HS2MspPo3f\noAWnmlAw+Xpoxt26wxBo13kJJZxSEhPhrLd1ume2NqXHa4zc0iGZUQxblwsdwQRo\nzzt/WKm+Es5/da1G6jPiYvJSX7D5SmkDX3yPpL810v8hUhVVRm1Whj2dsh5l1H2N\n18Kr5FCqxpskFQkCxYLRlPxQ3UGTuO8SXOEDURsXwj8KfivMvsFFtpxmngDTC18m\nwI1vw+3lozUEfsDHMK+C/d91b1mjGcgdMSt1CTSV329mVrhqozXs8N1vwHcq06sG\n6kINRRFD41Rio6TlJK98\n=lZ3r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4ebd76a7ff8e864e2c07a0399980a205aa8e54bb\nparent c48611bfa0fbe28046197a08f45c83daf98d17e2\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780381653 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780381653 +0300\n\nCAURA-129 feat(contradiction): entity-aware Path C retraction judge (#271)\n\n## Summary\n\nTier-2 fix for the Path C retraction non-determinism class. CAURA-128\n(PR #267) raised the confidence floor 0.60 → 0.90 to mitigate the\nstochastic-flip case. This PR delivers the deeper fix the original\ndocstring at `contradiction_detector.py:898-901` promised but never\nimplemented: **Path C now asks a structurally different question than\nPath A**, grounded on resolved entities rather than raw-text NER.\n\nStatus report L3.1:\n`docs/contradiction-detection-status-2026-05-26.html`.\n\n## Architecture diff\n\n**Before (CAURA-128):**\n```\n_attempt_path_c_retraction\n  └─ _llm_contradiction_check(new_content, old_content, ...)   ← same prompt as Path A\n                                                                  same inputs as Path A\n                                                                  → stochastic flip\n```\n\n**After (CAURA-129):**\n```\n_attempt_path_c_retraction\n  ├─ _fetch_entity_context(new_memory)   ── get_entity_links_for_memories + get_entity ×N\n  ├─ _fetch_entity_context(candidate)    ── (gather'd in parallel)\n  ├─ if either empty → log + skip       ── guard against degenerate inputs\n  └─ _llm_entity_aware_contradiction_check(\n        new_content, old_content,\n        new_entities, old_entities,      ← AUTHORITATIVE entity context\n        tenant_config\n     )                                    → ENTITY_AWARE_CONTRADICTION_PROMPT\n                                           same JSON schema → _judge_contradiction reused\n```\n\n## What ships\n\n| Component | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `ENTITY_AWARE_CONTRADICTION_PROMPT` | New template; identical JSON\nschema to `CONTRADICTION_PROMPT` so the parser is reused. Explicitly\nframes resolved entities as authoritative. |\n| `_format_entity_context(entities)` | Render `{name, entity_type,\nrole}` dicts as a bulleted block for the prompt. |\n| `_fetch_entity_context(sc, memory_id)` | Compose\n`get_entity_links_for_memories` (1 RT, batch) + per-entity `get_entity`\n(gather'd). Errors swallowed → returns `[]`. |\n| `_llm_entity_aware_contradiction_check(...)` | Same fallback chain,\nsame 10s timeout, same parser. Service label\n`contradiction-entity-aware`. |\n| Rewired `_attempt_path_c_retraction` | Fetch both contexts in\nparallel; skip retraction (log INFO) when either side empty; otherwise\ncall new judge. |\n\nThreshold stays at `_CONF_CLEAN = 0.90` for this PR — we want production\nsignal that the new judge is genuinely more deterministic before\nlowering it. A follow-up can drop to `_CONF_GATE2` after data.\n\n## Tests (25 collected across both files)\n\n**`tests/test_a4_13_path_c_retraction.py`** — 9 tests, all 7 originals\npreserve their semantics; patch target updated to the new judge. Default\nmock now returns one resolved subject per memory. 2 new guard tests:\n- `test_no_retraction_when_new_memory_has_no_entity_links`\n- `test_no_retraction_when_candidate_has_no_entity_links`\n\n**`tests/test_caura_129_entity_aware_retraction_prompt.py`** *(new)* —\n16 direct tests:\n- Prompt: required placeholders, JSON schema for parser reuse,\nauthoritative-entity framing, end-to-end `.format()` with realistic\ninputs.\n- `_format_entity_context`: bullets, empty sentinel, missing-field\ndefaults.\n- `_fetch_entity_context`: two-round-trip composition,\ncanonical_name/name fallback, links-lookup error swallow, per-entity\nerror tolerance.\n- `_llm_entity_aware_contradiction_check`: `call_with_fallback` wiring\n(service label, timeout, model_attr), prompt payload carries both entity\nblocks, 500-char truncation per side.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] `python -m py_compile` clean on production + both test files.\n- [x] `pytest --collect-only` collects 25 tests with no errors.\n- [ ] CI runs pytest with Postgres (local environment unavailable).\n- [ ] Post-merge wet test: `scripts/repro_contradictions_race.py` on\ndev. Expect detection rate ≥ 95% across all gaps.\n\n## Cost analysis\n\nPath C is post-commit async (no user is waiting). The new fetch adds\n**3-4 storage round-trips per retraction attempt**:\n\n- 1 round-trip: batch `get_entity_links_for_memories([new_id, cand_id])`\n— wait, currently we pass one memory_id at a time per\n`_fetch_entity_context` call. *Could* be optimised in a follow-up to one\nbatch call covering both memories; not done here to keep diff surgical.\n- N round-trips: per-entity `get_entity` calls, parallelised via\n`asyncio.gather`. Typical N = 2–5 per memory.\n\nTotal latency: roughly the slowest `get_entity` call ≈ 50–150ms p95.\nInvisible to the write path.\n\n## Rollback\n\nSingle `git revert` of the merged squash fully restores the\npost-CAURA-128 state. No DB migration, no schema change, no flag flip.\n\n## Follow-ups (not in this PR)\n\n1. Tier-3 belt-and-suspenders: replace silent retract with `disputed`\nstatus + tiebreaker (separate ticket).\n2. Per-tenant retraction kill-switch (L3.8).\n3. Optional storage micro-opt: one round-trip per retraction via a\n`get_memory_with_entity_details(memory_id)` endpoint (file as P3 if\nprofiling warrants).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-02T06:27:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/07661c55cf3d21fbb4349d9c342d7fdf036a7483","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/07661c55cf3d21fbb4349d9c342d7fdf036a7483","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/07661c55cf3d21fbb4349d9c342d7fdf036a7483/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c48611bfa0fbe28046197a08f45c83daf98d17e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c48611bfa0fbe28046197a08f45c83daf98d17e2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c48611bfa0fbe28046197a08f45c83daf98d17e2"}]},{"sha":"c48611bfa0fbe28046197a08f45c83daf98d17e2","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGM0ODYxMWJmYTBmYmUyODA0NjE5N2EwOGY0NWM4M2RhZjk4ZDE3ZTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-02T06:02:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T06:02:25Z"},"message":"test(search): pin fleet-less visibility contract for fleet-scoped search (A13) (#268)\n\n## Summary\n- **A13 does NOT reproduce on current main.** Storage-api\n`scored_search` already widens fleet filtering to `fleet_id IN (...) OR\nfleet_id IS NULL OR visibility == \"scope_org\"`\n(`core-storage-api/.../postgres_service.py:1090-1097`), shipped in\nv1.0.0.\n- Wet-tested on local stack: a fleet-less write IS visible to a\nfleet-scoped `/search` call.\n- This PR adds **no production code changes** — only a blackbox\nregression test that pins the four contract clauses so the widening\ncan't be silently refactored away.\n\n## What the test verifies\n1. `fleet-less write → fleet-scoped search visible` (the original A13\nsymptom — not reproducible)\n2. `fleet=X write → fleet=X search visible` (sanity)\n3. `fleet=X write → fleet=Y search NOT visible` (isolation must still\nhold; guards against accidental `OR TRUE`)\n4. `fleet-less write → unscoped search visible` (sanity)\n5. `fleet=X + visibility=scope_org → fleet=Y search visible` (the third\nOR clause)\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Blackbox subagent wrote the test (no implementation access — only\nneighbor test files for fixture style)\n- [x] `pytest\ntests/test_a13_fleet_less_visible_to_fleet_scoped_search.py -q` → 5\npassed\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: 2672 passed (was 2667 + 5 new)\n- [x] `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean\n\nCloses A13 on the V4 task checklist.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"3124175f0eb5ce1cdd65b22d247fa18f7baec376","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/3124175f0eb5ce1cdd65b22d247fa18f7baec376"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/c48611bfa0fbe28046197a08f45c83daf98d17e2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHnHxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUNYQAA5ztOwoDZy3Fa/p8KS7+ErX\nvV1mnpJWGxxF7SDSb3lBHzY6gAASXmkm/ss2NRTcZVY36INjFl/HRRHiiUIu0GGp\nHGmLc03srPPQ8aA/z9LMwrcn2+gQn7GDyAFCwU2dNlV7D9C17wQOhKZfK4ktyVvF\nr2RuE2NaNcjGt5eToa6Q50cux+EpCFVp1M9xPzfnUjauAH43i1M3L7jfyjF1xYJV\nknp6LAK8ViYRWi2ZWRhsqARHVD9ZseJldMYZ7aDHYEPwrA++YS59pqsY4dqjUpBd\nCczN/LO4k4f/xC7ZGaVJWWVjMtCtOQxuqd47u5Hyr6tx+VYuQKIuvOxRR+aMpJOo\nx6oSrhmSf+uF2ymOpUxKSxn50qOWRY1yTJP/F+W1SQsiM77ZmvEmId8qD+QajDku\nUnsN+LR+yJkplf3z0U3d0iT/GvIrEPYftaOVPpDZRpBTboCMkT/5dVg4AIVkHdHW\nAZaTHO77TOfwb8PC3FL2NZRfnoyy9Da+7paXiDBAYh8cIoQTPrUTdX41qYhT7xHD\nGxMmBpKP+pNNJWAHNKE9aOpUzDSpM88Lp88kW8qZwi5TWElXMWKvqqrXWeQMK+km\nJDkReMksGcS88iTa8637LlQpw1ZpntVgc5miW5XDfDSbkZfbtY5y4Z0WlcQme3UX\n/VZA1x4RMgRZfKAuNGHF\n=8SZg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3124175f0eb5ce1cdd65b22d247fa18f7baec376\nparent a22c30bea2dcd61f7bc35d74e48ce96b26ff89d1\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780380145 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780380145 +0300\n\ntest(search): pin fleet-less visibility contract for fleet-scoped search (A13) (#268)\n\n## Summary\n- **A13 does NOT reproduce on current main.** Storage-api\n`scored_search` already widens fleet filtering to `fleet_id IN (...) OR\nfleet_id IS NULL OR visibility == \"scope_org\"`\n(`core-storage-api/.../postgres_service.py:1090-1097`), shipped in\nv1.0.0.\n- Wet-tested on local stack: a fleet-less write IS visible to a\nfleet-scoped `/search` call.\n- This PR adds **no production code changes** — only a blackbox\nregression test that pins the four contract clauses so the widening\ncan't be silently refactored away.\n\n## What the test verifies\n1. `fleet-less write → fleet-scoped search visible` (the original A13\nsymptom — not reproducible)\n2. `fleet=X write → fleet=X search visible` (sanity)\n3. `fleet=X write → fleet=Y search NOT visible` (isolation must still\nhold; guards against accidental `OR TRUE`)\n4. `fleet-less write → unscoped search visible` (sanity)\n5. `fleet=X + visibility=scope_org → fleet=Y search visible` (the third\nOR clause)\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Blackbox subagent wrote the test (no implementation access — only\nneighbor test files for fixture style)\n- [x] `pytest\ntests/test_a13_fleet_less_visible_to_fleet_scoped_search.py -q` → 5\npassed\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: 2672 passed (was 2667 + 5 new)\n- [x] `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean\n\nCloses A13 on the V4 task checklist.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-02T06:02:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c48611bfa0fbe28046197a08f45c83daf98d17e2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c48611bfa0fbe28046197a08f45c83daf98d17e2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c48611bfa0fbe28046197a08f45c83daf98d17e2/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a22c30bea2dcd61f7bc35d74e48ce96b26ff89d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a22c30bea2dcd61f7bc35d74e48ce96b26ff89d1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a22c30bea2dcd61f7bc35d74e48ce96b26ff89d1"}]},{"sha":"a22c30bea2dcd61f7bc35d74e48ce96b26ff89d1","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGEyMmMzMGJlYTJkY2Q2MWY3YmMzNWQ3NGU0OGNlOTZiMjZmZjg5ZDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-01T19:01:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T19:01:18Z"},"message":"ci: harden the shared review script (#270)\n\nHardens the shared review script (`.github/scripts/claude_pr_review.sh`)\n— follow-ups surfaced by the **enterprise repo's self-test review** of\nthe identical script (the on-open review working as intended caught\nthese):\n\n- **Medium — jq silent-exit:** under `set -euo pipefail`, a non-JSON\nresponse from `claude` (warning banner, rate-limit HTML) made `jq` fail\nand killed the script *before* the empty-result guard, posting no error.\nNow guarded → posts a visible parse-error instead.\n- **Low — 65 536-char comment limit:** a very large review would 422 on\n`gh api` then silently exit. Now truncated with a `_[truncated]_`\nmarker.\n- **Low — job-summary cost table:** restored the cost +\ninput/output-token table to `$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY` (alongside the\ncomment footer).\n\nDeclined (with reasoning, documented): the \"PR-branch checkout runs the\nPR's script with secrets\" finding — pinning to base would kill the\nself-test that *caught these very issues*; the real mitigation is the\nrepo's \"require approval for workflow runs\" setting, not workflow code.\n\nKeeps the script byte-identical across all three repos. This PR\nself-tests on open (it's a `.sh` change).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f2c274634342938086e2fa54e71a6634b153d936","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f2c274634342938086e2fa54e71a6634b153d936"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/a22c30bea2dcd61f7bc35d74e48ce96b26ff89d1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHdb+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfZwQAF9ZBjHwGbMDkeZVxcXrVQ46\nkSXWzXQ272ecy8aN4W6SDBabVt3s9GedJEeNUwLvMaiQf+67FCeXpv5uAfoUBOzg\no5uNbDBnl+yqXvePSFLddhMpKwuVAXJUXIV+DUjXiutYpGlDU+jO7x8fs0HE0WCo\nqSMwk8fCyl31bvTmO1gS6yskQkr4iwUtIO593yHWlw0JhMDm1fcxgAFZxF1/Uuvx\nmD2IV1u7vfNLzZhckBgt3J/vEq+R6oqQAM2ZYhcXaHNRLH6+qUAqtr4+5E445rKT\nAdH1cnluthwDeB/2ACqj+ZQ7wjkdsnFqHuI8sgcLO1r3u6CYeXM9h+0Jjwg1Lyqz\nLDyAh4FLhLvwlZIDPQEb7Ar9UlAdNtBjx0n5W8PPDELX9GAV/ERsgVKrp2IveEAN\ntEyL1PfAI89yTfloY6cbMzXnZHfrnOVO0JOUK4op9sHoybLsbym6id2xuyatCo/l\n5V6btVnULDC/dyRZE/+kVfyllufM/i+DJwguTjylIBdtN/IyHU+aad5zfy1vTNa5\n5VKIUYpyFLdGSOoNt5956uzm1ckhZSdlqCltQVsndZxPLYDsOuyi/gxIW8WbQil0\nAVDSd4avLWkL3QZ6Zofyy1DEZyuQlByxsqQGCpIa8Ema0jzdonzVNPWBdYoKplPl\nLk/vkH27gjj0t1FUm28C\n=DjbT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f2c274634342938086e2fa54e71a6634b153d936\nparent 5a0aa5f4218c7d79b9cff2c81aa41438940a86ee\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1780340478 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780340478 +0300\n\nci: harden the shared review script (#270)\n\nHardens the shared review script (`.github/scripts/claude_pr_review.sh`)\n— follow-ups surfaced by the **enterprise repo's self-test review** of\nthe identical script (the on-open review working as intended caught\nthese):\n\n- **Medium — jq silent-exit:** under `set -euo pipefail`, a non-JSON\nresponse from `claude` (warning banner, rate-limit HTML) made `jq` fail\nand killed the script *before* the empty-result guard, posting no error.\nNow guarded → posts a visible parse-error instead.\n- **Low — 65 536-char comment limit:** a very large review would 422 on\n`gh api` then silently exit. Now truncated with a `_[truncated]_`\nmarker.\n- **Low — job-summary cost table:** restored the cost +\ninput/output-token table to `$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY` (alongside the\ncomment footer).\n\nDeclined (with reasoning, documented): the \"PR-branch checkout runs the\nPR's script with secrets\" finding — pinning to base would kill the\nself-test that *caught these very issues*; the real mitigation is the\nrepo's \"require approval for workflow runs\" setting, not workflow code.\n\nKeeps the script byte-identical across all three repos. This PR\nself-tests on open (it's a `.sh` change).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-01T19:01:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a22c30bea2dcd61f7bc35d74e48ce96b26ff89d1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a22c30bea2dcd61f7bc35d74e48ce96b26ff89d1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a22c30bea2dcd61f7bc35d74e48ce96b26ff89d1/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5a0aa5f4218c7d79b9cff2c81aa41438940a86ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5a0aa5f4218c7d79b9cff2c81aa41438940a86ee","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5a0aa5f4218c7d79b9cff2c81aa41438940a86ee"}]},{"sha":"5a0aa5f4218c7d79b9cff2c81aa41438940a86ee","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDVhMGFhNWY0MjE4YzdkNzliOWNmZjJjODFhYTQxNDM4OTQwYTg2ZWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-01T18:23:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:23:56Z"},"message":"ci: make the on-open review actually review the diff (#269)\n\n## Problem\nThe on-open `claude-review` job used `anthropics/claude-code-action@v1`,\nwhich never actually received the PR diff — in the headless runner the\nagent tried to fetch the PR via `gh`, hit the permission wall, and the\nfallback step stamped **\"✅ No issues found.\"** So a green on-open review\nmeant *nothing was reviewed*. (The `@claude` retrigger path already\nworked, because it pipes the real diff to `claude --print`.)\n\n## Fix\nRoute **both** jobs through one shared script —\n[`.github/scripts/claude_pr_review.sh`](.github/scripts/claude_pr_review.sh)\n— that feeds the real PR diff to `claude --print`. Now:\n- On-open and `@claude` are **byte-for-byte identical** (no more\ndivergence).\n- Each review posts a **cost footer** (`*Reviewed by <model> · cost\n$X*`), which also distinguishes a real review from the old fake stamp.\n- Dropped the dead top-level `id-token: write` and the\n`claude-code-action` dependency; pinned the CLI (`@2.1.159`) for\nreproducible reviews.\n- Preserved everything repo-specific: the org-membership pre-check gate,\nthe `MEMBER`/`OWNER` `@claude` gate, and the prompts.\n\nThis mirrors a fix already validated end-to-end in a sibling repo.\n\n## Self-test\nThis PR includes a `.sh` source file, so `pre-checks` won't skip it —\n**the new on-open review runs on this very PR.** Watch for a substantive\nreview below (with the cost footer), not a rubber-stamp.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8cbfa6ee353aa807aaf1d536e82be1cee2a2b2ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/8cbfa6ee353aa807aaf1d536e82be1cee2a2b2ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5a0aa5f4218c7d79b9cff2c81aa41438940a86ee","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHc48CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/AgQAIaYAtqnTU5+Vl8vSD9ou/FL\nd2nIY4qUL8vV8+YO2kIwMguxku22no0m2sSCwfe4guikcjKdmuNA8Su4DeRo5cYH\nR5TxWQYdZDXkswr+IoeIhat0AbIfRUvXA4Y5fYbeVAiUYFnUapqMvaCjbSWvNsdo\nh3Zf9fyxEOYPnIjrpmTCdk37Uce0DpNQKNYAQ84gAGq04j0ma0FPAJqYUdQCkbOT\nRnpPnortdc1cKxsyV5XDMIWdOKT97YvVA41vfaZqYDaqQJkODx12d+/rzK/sV8Dv\n5VxHoxmaX/4speCcAi6NOepowSMugSCKgqV1AF0tEom7F7XWexoFPdekaChjAfV7\nBmbvoM8reEedNrryBFKsbsYgthjUAcreJEx0Jt+mhNmj+kVK1GhM37ozq9r+s5P0\nqcchJiSIGL7WkyemEaDpn0QQEqYTHyCLCQflvsBzzR56eQf+KEaleJ3aAH0Xmo89\njn1IS8HzK4zgSn5dv+8w+F677JmZE02AQ8I8XH3mEJmUCVd/Iq8th3I3umQNVY3P\n6HoNfRdbHgjcyuv9ooXfGxk2QzU15kGteVq0epkqjmCg92QN3xuC4Pa2AgTTqc2v\nMQ5EsZbL/e4V9ABwEsMyyUNM6GtLZsLqxGWCpDV0Gw1BGuU1QlDJjE+s3hEH2QII\n7hwKtpovBl2+NOg0H/Tu\n=0wtt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8cbfa6ee353aa807aaf1d536e82be1cee2a2b2ef\nparent 7d18bcbb0f69187d328ac83d9228ac4f77a67454\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1780338236 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780338236 +0300\n\nci: make the on-open review actually review the diff (#269)\n\n## Problem\nThe on-open `claude-review` job used `anthropics/claude-code-action@v1`,\nwhich never actually received the PR diff — in the headless runner the\nagent tried to fetch the PR via `gh`, hit the permission wall, and the\nfallback step stamped **\"✅ No issues found.\"** So a green on-open review\nmeant *nothing was reviewed*. (The `@claude` retrigger path already\nworked, because it pipes the real diff to `claude --print`.)\n\n## Fix\nRoute **both** jobs through one shared script —\n[`.github/scripts/claude_pr_review.sh`](.github/scripts/claude_pr_review.sh)\n— that feeds the real PR diff to `claude --print`. Now:\n- On-open and `@claude` are **byte-for-byte identical** (no more\ndivergence).\n- Each review posts a **cost footer** (`*Reviewed by <model> · cost\n$X*`), which also distinguishes a real review from the old fake stamp.\n- Dropped the dead top-level `id-token: write` and the\n`claude-code-action` dependency; pinned the CLI (`@2.1.159`) for\nreproducible reviews.\n- Preserved everything repo-specific: the org-membership pre-check gate,\nthe `MEMBER`/`OWNER` `@claude` gate, and the prompts.\n\nThis mirrors a fix already validated end-to-end in a sibling repo.\n\n## Self-test\nThis PR includes a `.sh` source file, so `pre-checks` won't skip it —\n**the new on-open review runs on this very PR.** Watch for a substantive\nreview below (with the cost footer), not a rubber-stamp.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-01T18:23:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5a0aa5f4218c7d79b9cff2c81aa41438940a86ee","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5a0aa5f4218c7d79b9cff2c81aa41438940a86ee","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5a0aa5f4218c7d79b9cff2c81aa41438940a86ee/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7d18bcbb0f69187d328ac83d9228ac4f77a67454","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7d18bcbb0f69187d328ac83d9228ac4f77a67454","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/7d18bcbb0f69187d328ac83d9228ac4f77a67454"}]},{"sha":"7d18bcbb0f69187d328ac83d9228ac4f77a67454","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDdkMThiY2JiMGY2OTE4N2QzMjhhYzgzZDkyMjhhYzRmNzdhNjc0NTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-01T13:41:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T13:41:33Z"},"message":"CAURA-128 fix(contradiction): tighten Path C retraction threshold 0.60 → 0.90 (#267)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe A4 #13 retraction was designed to *re-judge a Path A verdict with\nfull entity context*. In practice `_attempt_path_c_retraction` calls\n`_llm_contradiction_check(new_content, old_content, tenant_config)` with\nthe **same prompt and same inputs** as Path A's semantic judge. No\nentity context is passed in — it's the same LLM call rolled twice.\n\nLLMs are non-deterministic. Independent rolls disagree some fraction of\nthe time. Under the original 0.60 floor, gate-1 (`verdict=False` after a\n`contradicts=True same_subject=False` parser override — confidence 0.60)\nwas sufficient to silently retract a genuine Path A flag.\n\nThis PR raises `RETRACTION_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD` from `0.60` → `0.90`.\nRetraction now fires only on clean LLM agreement (both gates aligned\nwith no parser override).\n\n## Wet-test evidence (memclaw.net, 2026-05-26)\n\nProbe: `scripts/repro_contradictions_race.py` — two memories with\ndirectly conflicting release dates about a synthetic proper-noun\nsubject.\n\n| gap_ms | detected | status A / B | entity_links A / B | interpretation\n|\n\n|-------:|:--------:|:----------------------|:-------------------|:----------------------------------------------------------|\n| 0 | **No** | confirmed / active | 2 / 0 | Path A flagged → Path C\nretracted on stochastic 0.60 roll |\n| 100 | Yes | conflicted / confirmed| 0 / 0 | polled before Path C ran |\n| 500 | Yes | conflicted / confirmed| 0 / 0 | same — caught the window |\n| 2000 | **No** | confirmed / confirmed | 2 / 0 | Path C ran and\nretracted |\n\nThe \"race\" is not between inter-write gaps — it is between the client's\nread and Path C's wall-clock. Production clients reading\n`/contradictions` after Path C completes see the retraction.\n\nFull architecture map and prioritised gap list:\n`docs/contradiction-detection-status-2026-05-26.html`.\n\n## Why this is the *quick* fix tier\n\nThree options were laid out in the status report. This PR is option 1:\n\n1. **Quick** (this PR): raise the floor so single-gate signals can't\nretract; only clean agreement (0.90) is strong enough.\n2. **Real** (follow-up): pass `entity_links` + canonical names into a\ndistinct entity-aware prompt that asks a *different* question than Path\nA. The comment block at line 899 promises this; the code never\nimplemented it.\n3. **Belt-and-suspenders** (future): replace silent revert with a\n`disputed` status + tiebreaker pass.\n\n## Test changes\n\n| Test | Before | After |\n\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------|------------------------------------------------|\n| `…_clean_confidence` (0.90) | retracts ✓ | retracts ✓ (unchanged —\nclean agreement) |\n| `…_gate2_confidence` (0.85) | retracts | renamed →\n`test_no_retraction_at_gate2_below_threshold` — asserts NO retract |\n| `test_retracts_on_gate1_confidence_canonical_case` (0.60) | retracts\n(THE BUG) | renamed → `test_no_retraction_on_gate1_stochastic_signal` —\nasserts NO retract |\n| `…_malformed_fallback` (0.50) | no retract ✓ | no retract ✓\n(unchanged) |\n| `…_judge_confirms_contradiction` (True, 0.90) | no retract ✓ | no\nretract ✓ (unchanged) |\n| 2× precondition tests (no `supersedes_id`, already active) | no\nretract ✓ | no retract ✓ (unchanged) |\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Syntax + AST + pytest collection clean in local worktree.\n- [ ] CI runs the unit tests (Postgres-backed conftest needed; local pg\n:5432 unavailable here).\n- [ ] After merge → deploy to `dev` → re-run\n`scripts/repro_contradictions_race.py` against `memclaw.dev` to confirm\ntrials are no longer retracted.\n- [ ] After dev confirms → soak on `net` via next nightly loadtest.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"06cc60beef8217e8fcc620be93f9b4c9f80fcda2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/06cc60beef8217e8fcc620be93f9b4c9f80fcda2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/7d18bcbb0f69187d328ac83d9228ac4f77a67454","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHYwNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABTIQAFFHrgEFPZfd5LKdzTy7NyHU\n/LLJutcGkaVMyVpTH6QHBL2Vm4m2EeQTxLMrqJdjppzmbPeZY/vePQuCDIf8P5G4\ndd+0l9kbcl/0q0kNic0MY5LZpsczL2ixyaAM+DyaIGpVZrP+t+2b8ZYNmsqwFBTS\nxvalymgOMSaPXfDQOSKrekadaoKOqnYhpnN1nNlEwZn315GD9m4SWLnvIB5RP8Qt\nZIsYV1b8Upzmu+F54B93jbMV6cMnzKcy1SpXwTRDVhPhzq3PA4AVL7gHG8IrmxMO\nCNUdlwfsPhP/zoJ6sMlknGKFYU6ag0rRKVnjb5oPdbA02YIfntVPZ/VjO2xUORTn\nb3xiJ+3VKo6a26SwiTCiZF7EEkE9AUkSIOu1VaZkfVkjjhsbMHalGJU7DdJf/Ti5\nbUnLVhaF9Dt/9COe+FYjQnZd1lHpimq5Gd2TVXoiBRfK3v8XTKF0UK2LVDBuw2Jr\nDYjSwvTfjBN+apVH7NjbCalIaXwdaHdRoNksy4WrU//hqLMbWVad7xC6EY72Mfu+\nX8NWzADKxzpGT99glx6Xn3bDvAqHA/8ncaCqE/VYDiff+/gaCLQpZTMcRtmbw+SX\nt4L3juXHy2XXKiUfL+s7cUYOWR3Rrr8sX4yNqvABriyhKKOEev6nzXRcqOKyl5vf\n+GXLA1U6r8kbfAwcw1EJ\n=bLbG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 06cc60beef8217e8fcc620be93f9b4c9f80fcda2\nparent e7f9bc8de184a99f3b97d0d17d54cd3094a28574\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1780321293 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780321293 +0300\n\nCAURA-128 fix(contradiction): tighten Path C retraction threshold 0.60 → 0.90 (#267)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe A4 #13 retraction was designed to *re-judge a Path A verdict with\nfull entity context*. In practice `_attempt_path_c_retraction` calls\n`_llm_contradiction_check(new_content, old_content, tenant_config)` with\nthe **same prompt and same inputs** as Path A's semantic judge. No\nentity context is passed in — it's the same LLM call rolled twice.\n\nLLMs are non-deterministic. Independent rolls disagree some fraction of\nthe time. Under the original 0.60 floor, gate-1 (`verdict=False` after a\n`contradicts=True same_subject=False` parser override — confidence 0.60)\nwas sufficient to silently retract a genuine Path A flag.\n\nThis PR raises `RETRACTION_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD` from `0.60` → `0.90`.\nRetraction now fires only on clean LLM agreement (both gates aligned\nwith no parser override).\n\n## Wet-test evidence (memclaw.net, 2026-05-26)\n\nProbe: `scripts/repro_contradictions_race.py` — two memories with\ndirectly conflicting release dates about a synthetic proper-noun\nsubject.\n\n| gap_ms | detected | status A / B | entity_links A / B | interpretation\n|\n\n|-------:|:--------:|:----------------------|:-------------------|:----------------------------------------------------------|\n| 0 | **No** | confirmed / active | 2 / 0 | Path A flagged → Path C\nretracted on stochastic 0.60 roll |\n| 100 | Yes | conflicted / confirmed| 0 / 0 | polled before Path C ran |\n| 500 | Yes | conflicted / confirmed| 0 / 0 | same — caught the window |\n| 2000 | **No** | confirmed / confirmed | 2 / 0 | Path C ran and\nretracted |\n\nThe \"race\" is not between inter-write gaps — it is between the client's\nread and Path C's wall-clock. Production clients reading\n`/contradictions` after Path C completes see the retraction.\n\nFull architecture map and prioritised gap list:\n`docs/contradiction-detection-status-2026-05-26.html`.\n\n## Why this is the *quick* fix tier\n\nThree options were laid out in the status report. This PR is option 1:\n\n1. **Quick** (this PR): raise the floor so single-gate signals can't\nretract; only clean agreement (0.90) is strong enough.\n2. **Real** (follow-up): pass `entity_links` + canonical names into a\ndistinct entity-aware prompt that asks a *different* question than Path\nA. The comment block at line 899 promises this; the code never\nimplemented it.\n3. **Belt-and-suspenders** (future): replace silent revert with a\n`disputed` status + tiebreaker pass.\n\n## Test changes\n\n| Test | Before | After |\n\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------|------------------------------------------------|\n| `…_clean_confidence` (0.90) | retracts ✓ | retracts ✓ (unchanged —\nclean agreement) |\n| `…_gate2_confidence` (0.85) | retracts | renamed →\n`test_no_retraction_at_gate2_below_threshold` — asserts NO retract |\n| `test_retracts_on_gate1_confidence_canonical_case` (0.60) | retracts\n(THE BUG) | renamed → `test_no_retraction_on_gate1_stochastic_signal` —\nasserts NO retract |\n| `…_malformed_fallback` (0.50) | no retract ✓ | no retract ✓\n(unchanged) |\n| `…_judge_confirms_contradiction` (True, 0.90) | no retract ✓ | no\nretract ✓ (unchanged) |\n| 2× precondition tests (no `supersedes_id`, already active) | no\nretract ✓ | no retract ✓ (unchanged) |\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Syntax + AST + pytest collection clean in local worktree.\n- [ ] CI runs the unit tests (Postgres-backed conftest needed; local pg\n:5432 unavailable here).\n- [ ] After merge → deploy to `dev` → re-run\n`scripts/repro_contradictions_race.py` against `memclaw.dev` to confirm\ntrials are no longer retracted.\n- [ ] After dev confirms → soak on `net` via next nightly loadtest.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-01T13:41:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7d18bcbb0f69187d328ac83d9228ac4f77a67454","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/7d18bcbb0f69187d328ac83d9228ac4f77a67454","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7d18bcbb0f69187d328ac83d9228ac4f77a67454/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e7f9bc8de184a99f3b97d0d17d54cd3094a28574","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e7f9bc8de184a99f3b97d0d17d54cd3094a28574","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e7f9bc8de184a99f3b97d0d17d54cd3094a28574"}]},{"sha":"e7f9bc8de184a99f3b97d0d17d54cd3094a28574","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGU3ZjliYzhkZTE4NGE5OWYzYjk3ZDBkMTdkNTRjZDMwOTRhMjg1NzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-01T12:30:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T12:30:58Z"},"message":"feat(api): surface near_duplicate_of in default-mode write metadata (A21) (#266)\n\n## Summary\n- Adds `DetectNearDuplicate`, an advisory twin of\n`CheckSemanticDuplicate`, wired into the fast write pipeline between\n`CheckExactDuplicate` and `WriteMemoryRow`. On a high-similarity hit it\nstashes `metadata[\"near_duplicate_of\"]`,\n`metadata[\"near_duplicate_similarity\"]`, and\n`metadata[\"near_dup_check_ms\"]` on the write response — **never\n409-rejects** (strong-mode keeps that contract via\n`CheckSemanticDuplicate`).\n- Uses the JUDGE threshold (`SEMANTIC_DEDUP_JUDGE_THRESHOLD = 0.85`),\nnot AUTO (0.97). Wider band catches real paraphrases that sit at cosine\n0.85–0.94; we skip the LLM-judge call the strong path makes above this\nthreshold (advisory ≠ rejection, so false-positives are tolerable). Same\nA1 identifier-bearing pre-filter + same `semantic_dedup_enabled` tenant\ngate as the strong-side step.\n- Closes A21 from the V4 task checklist: closes the asymmetry where\ndefault-mode agents could re-state the same fact and get two rows with\nno signal a near-duplicate already exists.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] 14 blackbox unit tests in\n`tests/test_a21_detect_near_duplicate.py` (subagent-written, no\nimplementation access — verifies: gate behavior, metadata key contract,\nembedding/visibility plumbing, identifier-prefilter skip,\nJUDGE-threshold pin, non-blocking semantics, latency-record contract)\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite (`pytest tests/ -x -q`): 2667 passed\n- [x] `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean on the four touched\nfiles\n- [x] Local wet test against `localhost` gateway: two\nsemantically-equivalent writes (\"Dana likes her tea steeped for exactly\n3 minutes\" → \"Dana prefers her tea steeped for 3 minutes\", 15s gap, both\n`write_mode=fast`) — second response carries `near_duplicate_of`\npointing at the first id, `similarity=0.9766`, `check_ms=3.6`. Both\nwrites accepted (201, as designed).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"f929486314b8fec7febd83dcdfe79298e964c30f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f929486314b8fec7febd83dcdfe79298e964c30f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/e7f9bc8de184a99f3b97d0d17d54cd3094a28574","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHXuCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0mIQAFioRM6f0pmDUZxpQ3nR+eQC\nt7mB8TSYYBYLkEESsJoeXhqbZ9JFjZmaeqlMPPwabadBBG3+Xao3/UwG+1go3TKm\nqHuq4kOVE15nKf6f5ac3bVrZozo5t1n3+lS9+x04Xu4vYwzjAZvhgGl/PME3kYoR\niTDbk/F9Rdtrit9hoho2KJjGnHsY540TsvPxnJwGAADyypZ7qYbtX0Wp3NI/2U6M\nzSiSmPhTjx/KTnqNU7FgjZNBPHmcjU1wA1ky8foujppMH+Heq6w4BHOlSX0NeOKQ\nd5tUfHEhoFllaCCmLrZ0x0ePQUQCAz8Y2NFHH3iSv6qXr8DYc9BwyVQPzJL4d9us\n4O3DDu6WEO77WxucJQ20OhLBEtQFO5lrpjKviEAhmMV1geUPfv2LBaklxAlmXSQe\n9UY8F3iSy6vaIohaFxkctGOhvbvYTXQjrB3oDaP2ZOpzdHjvtdfy0RNk/mmHTqmp\n93KLFnOc9bu+OiAvBRnakY0ldi2AHFrlvTXPp/4orjYF6PpegWPUXDJnc0Go3jqb\nGgTePrSInjP8ffxQRhRVgmOtrP1gkoDZn8MfJM/i8nNAPog+80YTGK9mNgPAcPF+\nfI6sSLyDR4VXMcsG+WiYKftcTs6KGY8W8DER2Wnh2Yxnul0ox0posrlVqSj5RB99\nuY4piJr055wWZtse2p9C\n=BfR2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f929486314b8fec7febd83dcdfe79298e964c30f\nparent 808f4c564e413ee9822fad08acf1cc2b72c02727\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780317058 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780317058 +0300\n\nfeat(api): surface near_duplicate_of in default-mode write metadata (A21) (#266)\n\n## Summary\n- Adds `DetectNearDuplicate`, an advisory twin of\n`CheckSemanticDuplicate`, wired into the fast write pipeline between\n`CheckExactDuplicate` and `WriteMemoryRow`. On a high-similarity hit it\nstashes `metadata[\"near_duplicate_of\"]`,\n`metadata[\"near_duplicate_similarity\"]`, and\n`metadata[\"near_dup_check_ms\"]` on the write response — **never\n409-rejects** (strong-mode keeps that contract via\n`CheckSemanticDuplicate`).\n- Uses the JUDGE threshold (`SEMANTIC_DEDUP_JUDGE_THRESHOLD = 0.85`),\nnot AUTO (0.97). Wider band catches real paraphrases that sit at cosine\n0.85–0.94; we skip the LLM-judge call the strong path makes above this\nthreshold (advisory ≠ rejection, so false-positives are tolerable). Same\nA1 identifier-bearing pre-filter + same `semantic_dedup_enabled` tenant\ngate as the strong-side step.\n- Closes A21 from the V4 task checklist: closes the asymmetry where\ndefault-mode agents could re-state the same fact and get two rows with\nno signal a near-duplicate already exists.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] 14 blackbox unit tests in\n`tests/test_a21_detect_near_duplicate.py` (subagent-written, no\nimplementation access — verifies: gate behavior, metadata key contract,\nembedding/visibility plumbing, identifier-prefilter skip,\nJUDGE-threshold pin, non-blocking semantics, latency-record contract)\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite (`pytest tests/ -x -q`): 2667 passed\n- [x] `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean on the four touched\nfiles\n- [x] Local wet test against `localhost` gateway: two\nsemantically-equivalent writes (\"Dana likes her tea steeped for exactly\n3 minutes\" → \"Dana prefers her tea steeped for 3 minutes\", 15s gap, both\n`write_mode=fast`) — second response carries `near_duplicate_of`\npointing at the first id, `similarity=0.9766`, `check_ms=3.6`. Both\nwrites accepted (201, as designed).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-01T12:30:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e7f9bc8de184a99f3b97d0d17d54cd3094a28574","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e7f9bc8de184a99f3b97d0d17d54cd3094a28574","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e7f9bc8de184a99f3b97d0d17d54cd3094a28574/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"808f4c564e413ee9822fad08acf1cc2b72c02727","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/808f4c564e413ee9822fad08acf1cc2b72c02727","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/808f4c564e413ee9822fad08acf1cc2b72c02727"}]},{"sha":"808f4c564e413ee9822fad08acf1cc2b72c02727","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDgwOGY0YzU2NGU0MTNlZTk4MjJmYWQwOGFjZjFjYzJiNzJjMDI3Mjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-01T09:29:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T09:29:19Z"},"message":"fix(api): accept metadata_mode as a query param on PATCH /memories/{id} (C7) (#265)\n\n## Summary\n\n\\`PATCH /api/v1/memories/{memory_id}\\` read \\`metadata_mode\\` only from\nthe request body. A caller sending \\`?metadata_mode=replace\\` as a query\nstring got the default merge behaviour silently — FastAPI drops unknown\nquery params on the floor, and the body-side validator never sees the\nvalue.\n\nC7 asked for either (a) accept it as a documented query param, OR (b)\nreturn 422 on unknown query params on PATCH. This PR picks (a) —\ntargeted to the one endpoint, no behaviour change for callers who\nalready use the body field.\n\n## Changes\n\n- \\`update_memory_endpoint\\` gains an optional \\`metadata_mode\\` query\nparam with the same \\`^(merge|replace)$\\` pattern as the body field.\n- **Body wins on conflict.** When body did NOT set \\`metadata_mode\\` and\nthe query param IS set, the query value applies (and the body field is\npatched in place before the service call).\n- Mirror the body-side \\`metadata_mode_requires_metadata\\` validator: if\nthe caller supplies the query param without a matching \\`metadata\\`\nfield in the body, return 422 with the same message. Sending only the\nmode flag is a no-op the existing validator already rejects on the body\nside; this PR makes the query-side symmetric.\n\n## Truth table\n\n| body \\`metadata_mode\\` | query \\`metadata_mode\\` | body \\`metadata\\` |\noutcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| no | no | yes | merge (default) — unchanged |\n| no | yes (\\`replace\\`) | yes | **REPLACE via query** (new C7) |\n| yes (\\`replace\\`) | no | yes | replace (existing) |\n| yes (\\`merge\\`) | yes (\\`replace\\`) | yes | **merge — body wins** |\n| no | yes (\\`replace\\`) | no | **422 — query-side mirror of body\nvalidator** |\n| no | yes (\\`bogus\\`) | yes | 422 — FastAPI regex validation |\n\n## Tests — black-box by a subagent\n\nI implemented the fix, then briefed a subagent on the behavioural\ncontract only (no access to \\`routes/memories.py\\`). It produced\n\\`tests/test_c7_metadata_mode_query_param.py\\` with 8 cases — one per\nrow of the truth table plus an idempotency check.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] \\`tests/test_c7_metadata_mode_query_param.py\\`: 8 tests, 1.14s,\nall pass.\n- [x] Existing body-side tests (\\`tests/test_api_memories.py\\`)\npreserved.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2653 passed** (+8), 0 regressions.\n- [x] \\`ruff check\\` + \\`ruff format --check\\` clean.\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh core-api build on local-dev:\n- PATCH \\`?metadata_mode=replace\\` + body \\`{metadata:{c:3}}\\` →\nresulting metadata = \\`{\\\"c\\\": 3}\\` (replace applied via query).\n- PATCH \\`?metadata_mode=replace\\` + body \\`{title:\\\"renamed\\\"}\\` (no\nmetadata) → 422 with expected message.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes C7 in the canonical task list.\n- Doesn't broaden to 422-on-unknown-query-params (the alternative C7\noption) — that would touch every PATCH and risk breaking clients that\nsend tracking query params. Targeted accept is the minimal change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"922925f75b578329094df810c56144050777699a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/922925f75b578329094df810c56144050777699a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/808f4c564e413ee9822fad08acf1cc2b72c02727","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHVDvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe3wQAIySFUmwI8K1mczAvPqhxY2R\n3cRaq+a0dytmdfNcPQmL17hF+WkC+NYOhZGC2uhnH8sFZJG7HU265PDchPBODd0m\n1zVGHGKQbodg8v+cZ4kqs2JFU37+DTrOIB3NVWulNvzzVHi7kEvsYRtPAYyB5YN8\nXeWOxceQZcqGVf967rXPHaN8s76+IfYepwzKK0R4pkiwWlp5hhwmG5VuC+wz2L+x\nW4/t8LQG85X3kKfnd0gVQcXzuavM+A7bdYQtIWCkunnGBEC1JgKF3+PXAAwXAllh\nbUQ2vG3DaZRFIuQo2qmtWyF/uMh0k4YcSRq/grxrl+rywQG1aT5w/3SHKkh/XqHT\n5QR9jcgJMQhfXQV6MZcE5zbcI6QLsCpkYZj132VxNOhEYD9qY3eiLtQLTfF+ETug\nyCf5hBpPyhyN3pslPunora2U9galwEwaQQZH4EZqLMxBIBWtf8qYpIRSZVOirRzL\n5Fm1pDN8+skuLZmr6Ql6vNKeObUx5Devubpm3xUR7LmpBHHoVeYXNhHTz6CR+6Ru\ncf4q7CN8D+f2SLcAJVytwEytC+LDXtJOcFAZhq5QgBxfRLZ7ZOPiJ5s3FSIOGIfA\ni7f/ul2xEp/h/lBa3VZIyaNHQBZ/8PFs95gbQ8Fn3LZcf6glLt6YyxK+7ElGwI02\n2t43dVTuS3xtF+UqLSIu\n=sXxM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 922925f75b578329094df810c56144050777699a\nparent 905db5c6874a5dbcaa1a387d3730caca87da0656\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780306159 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780306159 +0300\n\nfix(api): accept metadata_mode as a query param on PATCH /memories/{id} (C7) (#265)\n\n## Summary\n\n\\`PATCH /api/v1/memories/{memory_id}\\` read \\`metadata_mode\\` only from\nthe request body. A caller sending \\`?metadata_mode=replace\\` as a query\nstring got the default merge behaviour silently — FastAPI drops unknown\nquery params on the floor, and the body-side validator never sees the\nvalue.\n\nC7 asked for either (a) accept it as a documented query param, OR (b)\nreturn 422 on unknown query params on PATCH. This PR picks (a) —\ntargeted to the one endpoint, no behaviour change for callers who\nalready use the body field.\n\n## Changes\n\n- \\`update_memory_endpoint\\` gains an optional \\`metadata_mode\\` query\nparam with the same \\`^(merge|replace)$\\` pattern as the body field.\n- **Body wins on conflict.** When body did NOT set \\`metadata_mode\\` and\nthe query param IS set, the query value applies (and the body field is\npatched in place before the service call).\n- Mirror the body-side \\`metadata_mode_requires_metadata\\` validator: if\nthe caller supplies the query param without a matching \\`metadata\\`\nfield in the body, return 422 with the same message. Sending only the\nmode flag is a no-op the existing validator already rejects on the body\nside; this PR makes the query-side symmetric.\n\n## Truth table\n\n| body \\`metadata_mode\\` | query \\`metadata_mode\\` | body \\`metadata\\` |\noutcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| no | no | yes | merge (default) — unchanged |\n| no | yes (\\`replace\\`) | yes | **REPLACE via query** (new C7) |\n| yes (\\`replace\\`) | no | yes | replace (existing) |\n| yes (\\`merge\\`) | yes (\\`replace\\`) | yes | **merge — body wins** |\n| no | yes (\\`replace\\`) | no | **422 — query-side mirror of body\nvalidator** |\n| no | yes (\\`bogus\\`) | yes | 422 — FastAPI regex validation |\n\n## Tests — black-box by a subagent\n\nI implemented the fix, then briefed a subagent on the behavioural\ncontract only (no access to \\`routes/memories.py\\`). It produced\n\\`tests/test_c7_metadata_mode_query_param.py\\` with 8 cases — one per\nrow of the truth table plus an idempotency check.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] \\`tests/test_c7_metadata_mode_query_param.py\\`: 8 tests, 1.14s,\nall pass.\n- [x] Existing body-side tests (\\`tests/test_api_memories.py\\`)\npreserved.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2653 passed** (+8), 0 regressions.\n- [x] \\`ruff check\\` + \\`ruff format --check\\` clean.\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh core-api build on local-dev:\n- PATCH \\`?metadata_mode=replace\\` + body \\`{metadata:{c:3}}\\` →\nresulting metadata = \\`{\\\"c\\\": 3}\\` (replace applied via query).\n- PATCH \\`?metadata_mode=replace\\` + body \\`{title:\\\"renamed\\\"}\\` (no\nmetadata) → 422 with expected message.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes C7 in the canonical task list.\n- Doesn't broaden to 422-on-unknown-query-params (the alternative C7\noption) — that would touch every PATCH and risk breaking clients that\nsend tracking query params. Targeted accept is the minimal change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-01T09:29:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/808f4c564e413ee9822fad08acf1cc2b72c02727","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/808f4c564e413ee9822fad08acf1cc2b72c02727","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/808f4c564e413ee9822fad08acf1cc2b72c02727/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"905db5c6874a5dbcaa1a387d3730caca87da0656","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/905db5c6874a5dbcaa1a387d3730caca87da0656","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/905db5c6874a5dbcaa1a387d3730caca87da0656"}]},{"sha":"905db5c6874a5dbcaa1a387d3730caca87da0656","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDkwNWRiNWM2ODc0YTVkYmNhYTFhMzg3ZDM3MzBjYWNhODdkYTA2NTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-01T08:36:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T08:36:28Z"},"message":"fix(search): dedup per-tenant storage_search slot on entity-lookup fall-through (C10) (#264)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe search pipeline has two storage round-trips that both acquired\n\\`per_tenant_storage_slot(\\\"storage_search\\\", tenant_id)\\`:\n\n1. \\`ClassifyQuery._collect_memories\\` for the entity-lookup\nshort-circuit's \\`load_memories_by_ids\\` call.\n2. \\`ExecuteScoredSearch\\` for the \\`scored_search\\` call.\n\nWhen the entity-lookup short-circuit **succeeds** (\\`filtered_rows\\`\nnon-empty), the resulting plan sets \\`skip_scored_search=True\\`,\nExecuteScoredSearch skips, and the request consumes 1 slot.\n\nWhen the short-circuit **fails** (matched entities but their linked\nmemories all got filtered out), classify falls through to keyword /\nsemantic and ExecuteScoredSearch runs — at which point the request\nconsumed **2 slots** against the same per-tenant bucket. That's the\n\\\"doubles queueing latency\\\" C10 named, now visible since A23 fixed the\nclassify load.\n\nThe gap list called out two fix options: a sentinel through the pipeline\ncontext, or refactoring scored_search to take an outer slot. This PR\ntakes the **sentinel route** — minimal scope, no API change.\n\n## Changes\n\n- \\`ClassifyQuery._collect_memories\\` gains a \\`slot_acquired_marker:\ndict | None\\` parameter. After the \\`per_tenant_storage_slot\\` \\`async\nwith\\` returns successfully, it writes\n\\`slot_acquired_marker[\\\"_storage_slot_acquired\\\"] = True\\`. The\n\\`execute\\` site passes \\`ctx.data\\` as the marker.\n- \\`ExecuteScoredSearch.execute\\` reads\n\\`data.get(\\\"_storage_slot_acquired\\\")\\`; when truthy, it calls\n\\`scored_search\\` directly without re-acquiring the slot. When falsy, it\nacquires as before.\n- The sentinel is set ONLY after a successful \\`load_memories_by_ids\\`.\nIf the load raises (caught by classify's outer try/except),\n\\`_storage_slot_acquired\\` stays unset and ExecuteScoredSearch acquires\nthe slot normally on the fall-through.\n\nNet effect: one logical search counts once against the per-tenant\n\\`storage_search\\` bucket, regardless of which path it took.\n\n## Tests — black-box by a subagent\n\nI implemented the fix, then briefed a subagent on the behavioural\ncontract only (no access to the two pipeline-step files or\n\\`per_tenant_concurrency.py\\`). It produced\n\\`tests/test_c10_storage_slot_dedup.py\\` with 7 cases:\n\n1. Entity-lookup SUCCESS path → classify acquires 1 slot, execute skips.\nSentinel set.\n2. Entity-lookup FALL-THROUGH → classify acquires 1, sentinel set,\nexecute calls scored_search without re-acquiring.\n3. Non-entity-lookup path → classify never enters \\`_collect_memories\\`,\nsentinel absent, execute acquires normally.\n4. Sentinel suppresses only the slot, not the scored_search call.\n5. Sentinel doesn't leak across requests (two ctx objects).\n6. \\`load_memories_by_ids\\` failure does NOT mark the sentinel — execute\nre-acquires.\n7. Plan-says-skip wins regardless of sentinel (defensive).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] \\`tests/test_c10_storage_slot_dedup.py\\`: 7 tests, 0.50s, all\npass.\n- [x] Pipeline-tagged tests (40 across classify_query / scored_search /\nsearch_pipeline): all pass.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2645 passed** (+7), 0 regressions.\n- [x] \\`ruff check\\` + \\`ruff format --check\\` clean.\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh core-api build on local-dev: both\n\\`POST /api/v1/search\\` and \\`POST /api/v1/recall\\` return 200 — no\nregression on the normal (sentinel-absent) path.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes C10 in the canonical task list.\n- Subagent caught an ASGI-bridge subtlety in the conftest\n(\\`get_storage_client\\` resolves to a real in-process bridge by default)\nand patched both step modules' bindings consistently. One iteration loop\non the first run, all green on the second.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"7a8584f2186783b5153282c879e2c9923d32270d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/7a8584f2186783b5153282c879e2c9923d32270d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/905db5c6874a5dbcaa1a387d3730caca87da0656","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHUSMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiEEQAInTyduG7q0TUOLz3SbTLNx4\n8AKI6aV4Ll9HYQWbO/qdcWIB1ztBx9NmJKsXoiTnYMHhjbhjdHMo+q6gsuCk61km\nIWZ5E7j8H/cY3OGRcKTsmUO/QwzBwLG6tDkCneI+JLzv9df0G9oQbe3XjAuGaWct\nEA0oZtW3aCfQ+FODW8zL1QrMcsBHQ1v7UH1XGd2uGug1wxiMVjrd0tZBbKZiy2BR\nXPzW37PFS6Fy6T43RAX8GmXdTqDU/d7yCUAqRFHBrF/JA8yrKIENHH1i/zZ1UB5/\njXQgcgEP9KsEQzkMNJdARBU9w8groMF3EsMyJj2J+my2kNlSlwTA5kGXdeguLbD2\nLHMFOFWeItPixkpsyF5jPk9mDobsaosoiJMUN15zp/RGe+Ur9qS+iCppG9VPjaT8\nhy47LeoMyNvbt0KvFTTIcFViEVlQG/+jrx3Vz0xVzsFsi625TQDjyZmAimttb/ni\nDVCNOv0bxE+h35/2n6jiDRhSwIBTXDeTOOpE3J4P75l6VY0voe8zmg2LokZtCXet\nvw4phBSOg6bx58CRA1kYxo90yM1Rw5KZ4hUauZpa5Z5VPXnIRHwMoK4q3sVzm67j\n9UxLjh1LPP+UKOvTkqqpSGwiU6rQQ7gUH5Dn5LYmwD0CmtjlfrAudmdfmoF8iPQJ\novDEi+gZngyduzXD0Pjo\n=zKrW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7a8584f2186783b5153282c879e2c9923d32270d\nparent 1cccbe37a1c312978085fecf59a1753b5eb06b4b\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780302988 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780302988 +0300\n\nfix(search): dedup per-tenant storage_search slot on entity-lookup fall-through (C10) (#264)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe search pipeline has two storage round-trips that both acquired\n\\`per_tenant_storage_slot(\\\"storage_search\\\", tenant_id)\\`:\n\n1. \\`ClassifyQuery._collect_memories\\` for the entity-lookup\nshort-circuit's \\`load_memories_by_ids\\` call.\n2. \\`ExecuteScoredSearch\\` for the \\`scored_search\\` call.\n\nWhen the entity-lookup short-circuit **succeeds** (\\`filtered_rows\\`\nnon-empty), the resulting plan sets \\`skip_scored_search=True\\`,\nExecuteScoredSearch skips, and the request consumes 1 slot.\n\nWhen the short-circuit **fails** (matched entities but their linked\nmemories all got filtered out), classify falls through to keyword /\nsemantic and ExecuteScoredSearch runs — at which point the request\nconsumed **2 slots** against the same per-tenant bucket. That's the\n\\\"doubles queueing latency\\\" C10 named, now visible since A23 fixed the\nclassify load.\n\nThe gap list called out two fix options: a sentinel through the pipeline\ncontext, or refactoring scored_search to take an outer slot. This PR\ntakes the **sentinel route** — minimal scope, no API change.\n\n## Changes\n\n- \\`ClassifyQuery._collect_memories\\` gains a \\`slot_acquired_marker:\ndict | None\\` parameter. After the \\`per_tenant_storage_slot\\` \\`async\nwith\\` returns successfully, it writes\n\\`slot_acquired_marker[\\\"_storage_slot_acquired\\\"] = True\\`. The\n\\`execute\\` site passes \\`ctx.data\\` as the marker.\n- \\`ExecuteScoredSearch.execute\\` reads\n\\`data.get(\\\"_storage_slot_acquired\\\")\\`; when truthy, it calls\n\\`scored_search\\` directly without re-acquiring the slot. When falsy, it\nacquires as before.\n- The sentinel is set ONLY after a successful \\`load_memories_by_ids\\`.\nIf the load raises (caught by classify's outer try/except),\n\\`_storage_slot_acquired\\` stays unset and ExecuteScoredSearch acquires\nthe slot normally on the fall-through.\n\nNet effect: one logical search counts once against the per-tenant\n\\`storage_search\\` bucket, regardless of which path it took.\n\n## Tests — black-box by a subagent\n\nI implemented the fix, then briefed a subagent on the behavioural\ncontract only (no access to the two pipeline-step files or\n\\`per_tenant_concurrency.py\\`). It produced\n\\`tests/test_c10_storage_slot_dedup.py\\` with 7 cases:\n\n1. Entity-lookup SUCCESS path → classify acquires 1 slot, execute skips.\nSentinel set.\n2. Entity-lookup FALL-THROUGH → classify acquires 1, sentinel set,\nexecute calls scored_search without re-acquiring.\n3. Non-entity-lookup path → classify never enters \\`_collect_memories\\`,\nsentinel absent, execute acquires normally.\n4. Sentinel suppresses only the slot, not the scored_search call.\n5. Sentinel doesn't leak across requests (two ctx objects).\n6. \\`load_memories_by_ids\\` failure does NOT mark the sentinel — execute\nre-acquires.\n7. Plan-says-skip wins regardless of sentinel (defensive).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] \\`tests/test_c10_storage_slot_dedup.py\\`: 7 tests, 0.50s, all\npass.\n- [x] Pipeline-tagged tests (40 across classify_query / scored_search /\nsearch_pipeline): all pass.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2645 passed** (+7), 0 regressions.\n- [x] \\`ruff check\\` + \\`ruff format --check\\` clean.\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh core-api build on local-dev: both\n\\`POST /api/v1/search\\` and \\`POST /api/v1/recall\\` return 200 — no\nregression on the normal (sentinel-absent) path.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes C10 in the canonical task list.\n- Subagent caught an ASGI-bridge subtlety in the conftest\n(\\`get_storage_client\\` resolves to a real in-process bridge by default)\nand patched both step modules' bindings consistently. One iteration loop\non the first run, all green on the second.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-01T08:36:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/905db5c6874a5dbcaa1a387d3730caca87da0656","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/905db5c6874a5dbcaa1a387d3730caca87da0656","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/905db5c6874a5dbcaa1a387d3730caca87da0656/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1cccbe37a1c312978085fecf59a1753b5eb06b4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1cccbe37a1c312978085fecf59a1753b5eb06b4b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1cccbe37a1c312978085fecf59a1753b5eb06b4b"}]},{"sha":"1cccbe37a1c312978085fecf59a1753b5eb06b4b","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDFjY2NiZTM3YTFjMzEyOTc4MDg1ZmVjZjU5YTE3NTNiNWViMDZiNGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-01T07:27:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T07:27:59Z"},"message":"fix(mcp): extend mcp-agent default refusal to all read tools (A29) (#263)\n\n## Summary\n\nA14 ([#256](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/256)) closed\nthe destructive class of the silent \\`mcp-agent\\` default failure by\nguarding the write surfaces. **A29 extends the same\n\\`_refuse_default_agent_on_gateway\\` guard to the read surfaces** — and\ncloses a small gap on \\`memclaw_doc\\` where the destructive \\`delete\\`\nop was inadvertently un-guarded under the earlier write-only scope.\n\nThe read-side failure mode A29 closes: a gateway-routed tenant-key\nholder calling a read tool without an explicit \\`agent_id\\` was silently\nscoped to the reserved \\`mcp-agent\\` identity. Reads returned empty\n(nothing was ever written under that identity), looking like a data-loss\nbug. Now the caller gets a clear \\`MISSING_AGENT_ID\\` envelope.\n\n## Tools newly guarded\n\n| Tool | Notes |\n|---|---|\n| \\`memclaw_recall\\` | always |\n| \\`memclaw_list\\` | always |\n| \\`memclaw_stats\\` | always |\n| \\`memclaw_insights\\` | always |\n| \\`memclaw_keystones\\` | always |\n| \\`memclaw_doc\\` | extended from \\`op=write\\` only → every op\n(\\`read\\`/\\`query\\`/\\`search\\`/\\`list_collections\\`/\\`write\\`/\\`delete\\`)\n|\n\n## Intentionally NOT extended\n\n- \\`memclaw_manage\\` op ∈ {\\`read\\`, \\`lineage\\`}. A14 scoped manage to\nits write ops; manage's reads stay un-guarded. The new test file pins\nthis intentional gap so a future refactor doesn't silently start\nrefusing manage reads.\n\n## Tests — black-box by a subagent\n\nBriefed an agent on the behavioural contract only (no access to\n\\`mcp_server.py\\`). It produced\n\\`tests/test_mcp_default_agent_guard_a29.py\\` with 15 cases:\n\n- 5 simple read tools refuse (parametrized).\n- \\`memclaw_doc\\` refuses on every op (6 parametrizations including the\nA14-covered \\`write\\` as a regression guard, and the A29 gap-closer\n\\`delete\\`).\n- Standalone path keeps default-identity ergonomics.\n- Explicit \\`agent_id\\` bypasses the guard on a read.\n- \\`memclaw_write\\` still refuses (A14 regression).\n- \\`memclaw_manage op=lineage\\` stays un-guarded (intentional gap\npinned).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] \\`tests/test_mcp_default_agent_guard_a29.py\\`: 15 tests, 0.69s.\n- [x] Existing A14 tests (\\`test_mcp_default_agent_guard_a14.py\\`) +\n\\`test_mcp_write.py\\` still pass.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2638 passed** (+15), 0 regressions.\n- [x] \\`ruff check\\` + \\`ruff format --check\\` clean.\n- [x] \\`mypy\\`: 5 new errors of the systemic \\`_with_latency\\` \\`str |\nCallToolResult\\` shape — same class as 182 pre-existing, out of scope.\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh \\`core-api\\` build on local-dev:\n\n\\`\\`\\`\nA29 reads (expect MISSING_AGENT_ID):\n  recall             → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  list               → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  stats              → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  insights           → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  keystones          → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  doc-read           → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  doc-search         → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  doc-list_coll      → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  doc-delete         → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n\nmanage_lineage (expect NOT MISSING_AGENT_ID): NOT_FOUND\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes A29 in the canonical task list.\n- A14 + A29 together close the \\`mcp-agent\\` silent-default class across\nevery MCP tool except \\`memclaw_manage\\` reads.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"f27da67da65ce790732734db0daed3d59edcc8ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f27da67da65ce790732734db0daed3d59edcc8ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/1cccbe37a1c312978085fecf59a1753b5eb06b4b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHTR/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd58QAKxf0UhvCXbH/hShAbQtyJPA\nvCxv5oHB9saqAgZT63Yq5kgX5wJMqd4MeBQE58cG8Keidq0U7xSXDvwFQ/wl3qtz\nwEupxInfP439kaGOzAmsID7XdO7+gdacx4sKtiKX9rJT4PhF4tS7Pray3/jyeiRf\ndY0wFv7GLB3fuz0+7hasqG1maGBwTEZcaZ5G9/S2ngx6HJxZPXk5Pre/uvauo6Tt\nThRmZ+O6oRt4pwWsuJ54q4Fl6IolvcfVWbyPI658C7yPw2WonM83O09Hlnqlxza2\njrHE0sFxmh6kBLkbmZube8/d42s8JTU1oGhWybmYG+7Ohz5MM6Jfof0Hqn/GKsLp\nHCKmCLYfhNQeOQOMzao65WDseGmbR8vtPed6oBuXR0+decIrPz+08wVpD/ir0/QB\n9P7cMrZgWzXIO8g3lUcM49QzpT+qCcx/dZPOzxDzJj4P4uQn5X2Llbr+gpC9G2GP\nTXcJ+6DHr6eNc+fEYYQCvCtlns9Xh/rWsvCENWclc+5WUhJYdHu94ej96pFTZZMf\nlMEMUyaG8TDY66ypZzD2wbeOrk3rMVcJmQDV9ndV7nIPZNDIQ0IM0xC0hYdLSjGG\nlJ+Ij3gNWN4Achb/4q4bfEzIB5zmFwYKB4UpK+3Yu5znOT8RuIB8UNEYrUXTtjF/\n0+tS1TgAkTdOL7P/x9/N\n=GGMd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f27da67da65ce790732734db0daed3d59edcc8ec\nparent 88ca5a8f33008370bfb720695582c190c39c1207\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780298879 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780298879 +0300\n\nfix(mcp): extend mcp-agent default refusal to all read tools (A29) (#263)\n\n## Summary\n\nA14 ([#256](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/256)) closed\nthe destructive class of the silent \\`mcp-agent\\` default failure by\nguarding the write surfaces. **A29 extends the same\n\\`_refuse_default_agent_on_gateway\\` guard to the read surfaces** — and\ncloses a small gap on \\`memclaw_doc\\` where the destructive \\`delete\\`\nop was inadvertently un-guarded under the earlier write-only scope.\n\nThe read-side failure mode A29 closes: a gateway-routed tenant-key\nholder calling a read tool without an explicit \\`agent_id\\` was silently\nscoped to the reserved \\`mcp-agent\\` identity. Reads returned empty\n(nothing was ever written under that identity), looking like a data-loss\nbug. Now the caller gets a clear \\`MISSING_AGENT_ID\\` envelope.\n\n## Tools newly guarded\n\n| Tool | Notes |\n|---|---|\n| \\`memclaw_recall\\` | always |\n| \\`memclaw_list\\` | always |\n| \\`memclaw_stats\\` | always |\n| \\`memclaw_insights\\` | always |\n| \\`memclaw_keystones\\` | always |\n| \\`memclaw_doc\\` | extended from \\`op=write\\` only → every op\n(\\`read\\`/\\`query\\`/\\`search\\`/\\`list_collections\\`/\\`write\\`/\\`delete\\`)\n|\n\n## Intentionally NOT extended\n\n- \\`memclaw_manage\\` op ∈ {\\`read\\`, \\`lineage\\`}. A14 scoped manage to\nits write ops; manage's reads stay un-guarded. The new test file pins\nthis intentional gap so a future refactor doesn't silently start\nrefusing manage reads.\n\n## Tests — black-box by a subagent\n\nBriefed an agent on the behavioural contract only (no access to\n\\`mcp_server.py\\`). It produced\n\\`tests/test_mcp_default_agent_guard_a29.py\\` with 15 cases:\n\n- 5 simple read tools refuse (parametrized).\n- \\`memclaw_doc\\` refuses on every op (6 parametrizations including the\nA14-covered \\`write\\` as a regression guard, and the A29 gap-closer\n\\`delete\\`).\n- Standalone path keeps default-identity ergonomics.\n- Explicit \\`agent_id\\` bypasses the guard on a read.\n- \\`memclaw_write\\` still refuses (A14 regression).\n- \\`memclaw_manage op=lineage\\` stays un-guarded (intentional gap\npinned).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] \\`tests/test_mcp_default_agent_guard_a29.py\\`: 15 tests, 0.69s.\n- [x] Existing A14 tests (\\`test_mcp_default_agent_guard_a14.py\\`) +\n\\`test_mcp_write.py\\` still pass.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2638 passed** (+15), 0 regressions.\n- [x] \\`ruff check\\` + \\`ruff format --check\\` clean.\n- [x] \\`mypy\\`: 5 new errors of the systemic \\`_with_latency\\` \\`str |\nCallToolResult\\` shape — same class as 182 pre-existing, out of scope.\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh \\`core-api\\` build on local-dev:\n\n\\`\\`\\`\nA29 reads (expect MISSING_AGENT_ID):\n  recall             → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  list               → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  stats              → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  insights           → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  keystones          → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  doc-read           → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  doc-search         → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  doc-list_coll      → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n  doc-delete         → MISSING_AGENT_ID\n\nmanage_lineage (expect NOT MISSING_AGENT_ID): NOT_FOUND\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes A29 in the canonical task list.\n- A14 + A29 together close the \\`mcp-agent\\` silent-default class across\nevery MCP tool except \\`memclaw_manage\\` reads.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-01T07:27:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1cccbe37a1c312978085fecf59a1753b5eb06b4b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1cccbe37a1c312978085fecf59a1753b5eb06b4b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1cccbe37a1c312978085fecf59a1753b5eb06b4b/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"88ca5a8f33008370bfb720695582c190c39c1207","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/88ca5a8f33008370bfb720695582c190c39c1207","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/88ca5a8f33008370bfb720695582c190c39c1207"}]},{"sha":"88ca5a8f33008370bfb720695582c190c39c1207","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDg4Y2E1YThmMzMwMDgzNzBiZmI3MjA2OTU1ODJjMTkwYzM5YzEyMDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-01T06:56:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T06:56:18Z"},"message":"fix(recall): add items alias key to /recall response (C4) (#262)\n\n## Summary\n\n\\`/search\\` returns \\`{\\\"items\\\": [...], ...}\\`; \\`/recall\\` returned\n\\`{\\\"memories\\\": [...], ...}\\`. Consumers pattern-matching on\n\\`/search\\`'s shape silently got zero results when hitting \\`/recall\\`\ninstead. **C4** asks for one of: unify the response models, or add an\n\\`items\\` alias key. The alias is the smaller / safer move — no contract\nbreak for legacy \\`memories\\` readers.\n\n## Changes\n\n- \\`services.recall_service.summarize_memories\\` now emits an \\`items\\`\nkey alongside \\`memories\\` at all three return sites (empty /\nrecall-disabled / normal-brief). Both keys carry the same list of memory\ndumps. The non-empty branches materialise the \\`[m.model_dump() ...]\\`\nlist once so the alias doesn't double-cost.\n- Docstring updated to advertise both keys.\n\nBecause every consumer (REST \\`/recall\\`, MCP\n\\`memclaw_recall(include_brief=True)\\`) goes through\n\\`summarize_memories\\`, the alias surfaces at every layer:\n\n| Surface | Path | Where the alias lands |\n|---|---|---|\n| REST | \\`POST /api/v1/recall\\` | top-level \\`body[\\\"items\\\"]\\`\n(alongside \\`body[\\\"memories\\\"]\\`) |\n| MCP | \\`memclaw_recall(include_brief=True)\\` |\n\\`payload[\\\"brief\\\"][\\\"items\\\"]\\` |\n\n## Tests — black-box by a subagent\n\nI implemented the fix, then briefed a subagent on the behavioural\ncontract only (no access to \\`recall_service.py\\` or\n\\`routes/memories.py\\`). It produced\n\\`tests/test_c4_recall_items_alias.py\\` with 10 cases:\n\n- Empty-input branch (parametrized × \\`recall_enabled\\`)\n- Recall-disabled branch — equal content + matching \\`memory_count\\`\n- Normal-brief branch — equal content + full expected key-set\n- Element-equality deep check\n- Parametrized \"other-keys-still-present\" across all three branches\n- REST wire-level: \\`POST /api/v1/recall\\` body carries both keys\n- MCP wire-level: \\`payload[\\\"brief\\\"]\\` carries both keys\n\nI rewrote the MCP test after the agent first stubbed\n\\`summarize_memories\\` to return a hand-rolled dict (tautology — would\nhave passed without the C4 fix). The replacement lets the real helper\nrun via the empty-memories branch so the alias has to come out of actual\ncode.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] \\`tests/test_c4_recall_items_alias.py\\`: **10 tests, 0.73s**, all\npass.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2623 passed** (+10), 0 regressions.\n- [x] \\`ruff check\\` + \\`ruff format --check\\` clean.\n- [x] \\`mypy\\`: 0 new errors (14 → 14 on \\`recall_service.py\\`).\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh core-api build on local-dev: \\`POST\n/api/v1/recall\\` returns both \\`memories\\` and \\`items\\` keys, equal\ncontent, all other keys preserved.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes C4 in the canonical task list.\n- Doesn't unify the Pydantic response models — alias is enough for the\ncited use case. A future cleanup could merge \\`SearchResponse\\` + the\nrecall dict into one model and drop the alias.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"1ceb9a05896f96a1bb29fb440dc67682d5de70a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/1ceb9a05896f96a1bb29fb440dc67682d5de70a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/88ca5a8f33008370bfb720695582c190c39c1207","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHS0SCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAihMQAH/XUcIsJwUXROERnjZHCJ0M\nKxnNpdPb/ljvI2oTm4FYbQXqSlP5g+EI9NJI7WcltAsip8S4ZElxpedypJmOct6J\nszl6PdNbaCk7oLb+r0vqtc2uW2d7zuO/DrYulLDanNXuJdPO8iAZJhhs5qYqNSup\nPxPZJVSZr2aqzX0xAeVlRqIKfNIS2XxmcSIMgp+tsTlMoJDy+jdR69Uu78NAJw6m\n+I+ahln/HgPpQYjw6BKC5oO/b9jzdWOJHqPPcDgBwWDFCve+hkPoWJ79mIv2OAc7\n0TxWNtSTRh9Je23snY4CB0OF04FJD3TfZJHPOFa4s1k6bbtbyJ8pxpKO4WE/0Jir\n0q4cXShA/Y0dFgwt8X7zAebyBDNHYQOsJaCZIYswzbkEuN51UNjopkUCesWLHTwb\neCx5zzIDtK878yqPV67uwCzySF4U1dL2KQDMJhDhn5wuxsTBIiM91ouztJNcSSgh\nk8W2/D+vVPeox/0Yw7RVCye2YWPFLeEneuURgDFh5uXBXkFLgaebugeAJnzgFcQc\n7CSdZtc+Ee6GQ+GT8G4uxcDKonf87GeQ5lOqDEyD76CuFjC8nXk2ZKM/FH4/5HL8\nsQC8B6GeSMtfIfNGohBUHl+IAMdLRq43XmmQb7hSGZD5cFqn7uy2mZvowC45KyTQ\nYKnxGM+WzvMEEd3f/A5a\n=gWAo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1ceb9a05896f96a1bb29fb440dc67682d5de70a7\nparent 0abd727f31b53430519054cc339c238f319489ba\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780296978 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780296978 +0300\n\nfix(recall): add items alias key to /recall response (C4) (#262)\n\n## Summary\n\n\\`/search\\` returns \\`{\\\"items\\\": [...], ...}\\`; \\`/recall\\` returned\n\\`{\\\"memories\\\": [...], ...}\\`. Consumers pattern-matching on\n\\`/search\\`'s shape silently got zero results when hitting \\`/recall\\`\ninstead. **C4** asks for one of: unify the response models, or add an\n\\`items\\` alias key. The alias is the smaller / safer move — no contract\nbreak for legacy \\`memories\\` readers.\n\n## Changes\n\n- \\`services.recall_service.summarize_memories\\` now emits an \\`items\\`\nkey alongside \\`memories\\` at all three return sites (empty /\nrecall-disabled / normal-brief). Both keys carry the same list of memory\ndumps. The non-empty branches materialise the \\`[m.model_dump() ...]\\`\nlist once so the alias doesn't double-cost.\n- Docstring updated to advertise both keys.\n\nBecause every consumer (REST \\`/recall\\`, MCP\n\\`memclaw_recall(include_brief=True)\\`) goes through\n\\`summarize_memories\\`, the alias surfaces at every layer:\n\n| Surface | Path | Where the alias lands |\n|---|---|---|\n| REST | \\`POST /api/v1/recall\\` | top-level \\`body[\\\"items\\\"]\\`\n(alongside \\`body[\\\"memories\\\"]\\`) |\n| MCP | \\`memclaw_recall(include_brief=True)\\` |\n\\`payload[\\\"brief\\\"][\\\"items\\\"]\\` |\n\n## Tests — black-box by a subagent\n\nI implemented the fix, then briefed a subagent on the behavioural\ncontract only (no access to \\`recall_service.py\\` or\n\\`routes/memories.py\\`). It produced\n\\`tests/test_c4_recall_items_alias.py\\` with 10 cases:\n\n- Empty-input branch (parametrized × \\`recall_enabled\\`)\n- Recall-disabled branch — equal content + matching \\`memory_count\\`\n- Normal-brief branch — equal content + full expected key-set\n- Element-equality deep check\n- Parametrized \"other-keys-still-present\" across all three branches\n- REST wire-level: \\`POST /api/v1/recall\\` body carries both keys\n- MCP wire-level: \\`payload[\\\"brief\\\"]\\` carries both keys\n\nI rewrote the MCP test after the agent first stubbed\n\\`summarize_memories\\` to return a hand-rolled dict (tautology — would\nhave passed without the C4 fix). The replacement lets the real helper\nrun via the empty-memories branch so the alias has to come out of actual\ncode.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] \\`tests/test_c4_recall_items_alias.py\\`: **10 tests, 0.73s**, all\npass.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2623 passed** (+10), 0 regressions.\n- [x] \\`ruff check\\` + \\`ruff format --check\\` clean.\n- [x] \\`mypy\\`: 0 new errors (14 → 14 on \\`recall_service.py\\`).\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh core-api build on local-dev: \\`POST\n/api/v1/recall\\` returns both \\`memories\\` and \\`items\\` keys, equal\ncontent, all other keys preserved.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes C4 in the canonical task list.\n- Doesn't unify the Pydantic response models — alias is enough for the\ncited use case. A future cleanup could merge \\`SearchResponse\\` + the\nrecall dict into one model and drop the alias.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-01T06:56:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/88ca5a8f33008370bfb720695582c190c39c1207","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/88ca5a8f33008370bfb720695582c190c39c1207","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/88ca5a8f33008370bfb720695582c190c39c1207/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0abd727f31b53430519054cc339c238f319489ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0abd727f31b53430519054cc339c238f319489ba","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0abd727f31b53430519054cc339c238f319489ba"}]},{"sha":"0abd727f31b53430519054cc339c238f319489ba","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDBhYmQ3MjdmMzFiNTM0MzA1MTkwNTRjYzMzOWMyMzhmMzE5NDg5YmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-01T06:34:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T06:34:20Z"},"message":"feat(api): reject server-reserved memory_types at write boundary (C3, C8) (#261)\n\n## Summary\n\nCloses **C3** and **C8** in the canonical task list.\n\n`outcome`, `rule`, and `insight` are emitted by internal services\n(evolve_service for outcome+rule, insights_service for insight). Letting\nagents write them explicitly produces rows that downstream queries treat\nas system-generated — RL signals and insights surfaces get polluted by\nagent-authored content.\n\n**C8 specifically documented the .net + .dev behaviour** where agents\nbelieved `insight` was a legit write target because the type description\nliterally said \"persist results of reflection/analysis steps here.\" Now\nthey're told to use `semantic` / `fact` instead.\n\n## Changes\n\n- New `common.enrichment.constants.SERVER_RESERVED_MEMORY_TYPES =\nfrozenset({\"outcome\", \"rule\", \"insight\"})`. Import-time guard asserts\nevery reserved slug is in the enum so a misspelling raises loudly rather\nthan letting the gate reference a phantom type.\n- REST: `_reject_reserved_memory_type` helper raises `HTTPException(422,\n…)` naming the offending slug; the bulk path includes `items[<idx>]: …`\nso callers can locate the bad row. Wired into `POST /memories` and `POST\n/memories/bulk`.\n- MCP: `_refuse_reserved_memory_type` helper returns the standard\n`INVALID_ARGUMENTS` envelope. Wired into both\n`memclaw_write(content=...)` and `memclaw_write(items=[...])` paths.\n- `MEMORY_TYPE_DESCRIPTIONS` rewritten for the three reserved types so\nthe LLM-facing enrichment prompt also tells agents NOT to set them\nexplicitly. `rule`'s original signal-phrase guidance (`\"always\"`,\n`\"never\"`, `\"must\"`…) is preserved — the existing\n`test_enrichment_prompt` suite locks it.\n\nInternal callers are unaffected: `evolve_service` and `insights_service`\nbuild `MemoryCreate` objects and pass them to\n`services.memory_service.create_memory` directly. The boundary lives at\nthe route + MCP layer; the service layer never sees the helper.\n\n## Tests — black-box by a subagent\n\nI implemented the fix, then briefed a subagent on the behavioural\ncontract only (no access to `routes/memories.py`, `mcp_server.py`, or\n`common/enrichment/constants.py`). It produced\n`tests/test_c3_c8_reserved_memory_types.py` with 15 cases:\n\n- REST single rejects each of `outcome` / `rule` / `insight`\n(parametrized).\n- REST single accepts `fact` + `None` memory_type.\n- REST bulk rejects when any item carries a reserved type, names the\noffending index.\n- REST bulk accepts when every item is allowed.\n- MCP single rejects each reserved type (parametrized).\n- MCP single accepts `fact`.\n- MCP batch rejects the first reserved item, names the index.\n- MCP batch accepts when all items are allowed.\n- `SERVER_RESERVED_MEMORY_TYPES` shape (frozenset of the three slugs).\n- **Service-layer-doesn't-gate guard via `inspect.getsource`** —\nregression-proofs the internal-bypass contract (a future refactor that\nmoves the check down into `create_memory` would break evolve/insights\nsilently; this test fails loudly instead).\n\nPlus an existing regression test `test_memory_type_insight_accepted` was\nrenamed + rewritten — enum-sync coverage now lives in a schema-level\n`MemoryCreate(...)` instantiation, while the route-level rejection is\nasserted alongside it.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `tests/test_c3_c8_reserved_memory_types.py` — 15 tests, all\npassing, <1s.\n- [x] Existing `test_enrichment_prompt.py` (20 tests) preserved — `rule`\nsignal phrases unchanged.\n- [x] Existing `test_memory_type_insight_accepted` updated to match the\nnew contract.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2613 passed** (+15), 0 regressions.\n- [x] `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `mypy`: 2 new errors of the systemic `_with_latency` `str |\nCallToolResult` shape — same class as 197 pre-existing in the file, out\nof scope.\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh `core-api` build on local-dev:\n`insight` / `outcome` / `rule` → 422 with clean `memory_type='<slug>'`\nin the message; `fact` → 201.\n\n```\n=== insight (expect 422) ===\n{\"detail\":\"memory_type='insight' is server-reserved and cannot be supplied on writes...\"}  HTTP 422\n=== outcome (expect 422) ===\n{\"detail\":\"memory_type='outcome' is server-reserved and cannot be supplied on writes...\"}  HTTP 422\n=== rule (expect 422) ===\n{\"detail\":\"memory_type='rule' is server-reserved and cannot be supplied on writes...\"}     HTTP 422\n=== fact (expect 201) ===\n{\"id\":\"f50b9503-...\",\"memory_type\":\"fact\",...}                                              HTTP 201\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- Cosmetic: the first wet-test pass surfaced `<MemoryType.INSIGHT:\n'insight'>` in error messages (the helper used `!r` on a str-Enum).\nFixed to use `.value` so the message is operator-friendly.\n- Closes C3 + C8 in one PR — they were two views of the same underlying\nboundary gap.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a6fc92dd1b58558aa3cdd5e39a615046082247f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/2a6fc92dd1b58558aa3cdd5e39a615046082247f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/0abd727f31b53430519054cc339c238f319489ba","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHSfsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsSgQAEOndRKrYViYX54ZMSyRV+K+\n+Iy5ZMWq1Fu8j1ugLRrTxHGWO+F5alhvttDEXYuFelaguPxdCvv3/oPqF7FwFXk0\no6EbaFUhtbm87FK1LQEOnu4K0WrmC8ttH+jXw+yqkTMt2roryvDfkLvVwBld8cBl\nxFNu6pndsMiYAhMZLcjQL5YKIACO4+9jz0Q3PqAPYWz6Qe5BzjGlqGBSwccXJPnU\n0PtT3N60w7Lq7pnC6PERVQf8lEMTQXGU2BzfeaMqrxfOTJ9aliEBGgMqHxkS3fKM\nJVbPhKqCszDqC1yD2apikDo4am4rZdF2F76Fmyu2EW0hQcyoKyXmEJCKWQ370LHN\nZRMYvCt4jKbHR/IJ/kmq4sF4nF0TshG1Xsdn6Nlk8N2XS+e5g1zJMTGraJknFA89\nQCaQ0HIYIO8RuH3Nysp63dmsulXbAh+4hq1D8+79msU20flVk2JO4tujlybAsOrs\nQjJrYyo/WTvinLNeKpbvVNPHFeZCOznwdmEvO3AisuX0V1i3bXDj2lCsDLaHENjG\niaZv/qSI18gzvQawTwOKwn2cwsqe947Z8cGVj7CSPmZXY+wRaCF0Sj8VsFiTRwyt\n0msouWk8ET8Db1fqDAIKJShhmsR4yuIhPgqQ9yUi242uS+jF7k9VLU6f6saVGurT\n83nu9m7X7joRH5ynAAeT\n=m2Pj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2a6fc92dd1b58558aa3cdd5e39a615046082247f\nparent 68f19773ecd0d840048b046071e42a813eb68d50\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780295660 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780295660 +0300\n\nfeat(api): reject server-reserved memory_types at write boundary (C3, C8) (#261)\n\n## Summary\n\nCloses **C3** and **C8** in the canonical task list.\n\n`outcome`, `rule`, and `insight` are emitted by internal services\n(evolve_service for outcome+rule, insights_service for insight). Letting\nagents write them explicitly produces rows that downstream queries treat\nas system-generated — RL signals and insights surfaces get polluted by\nagent-authored content.\n\n**C8 specifically documented the .net + .dev behaviour** where agents\nbelieved `insight` was a legit write target because the type description\nliterally said \"persist results of reflection/analysis steps here.\" Now\nthey're told to use `semantic` / `fact` instead.\n\n## Changes\n\n- New `common.enrichment.constants.SERVER_RESERVED_MEMORY_TYPES =\nfrozenset({\"outcome\", \"rule\", \"insight\"})`. Import-time guard asserts\nevery reserved slug is in the enum so a misspelling raises loudly rather\nthan letting the gate reference a phantom type.\n- REST: `_reject_reserved_memory_type` helper raises `HTTPException(422,\n…)` naming the offending slug; the bulk path includes `items[<idx>]: …`\nso callers can locate the bad row. Wired into `POST /memories` and `POST\n/memories/bulk`.\n- MCP: `_refuse_reserved_memory_type` helper returns the standard\n`INVALID_ARGUMENTS` envelope. Wired into both\n`memclaw_write(content=...)` and `memclaw_write(items=[...])` paths.\n- `MEMORY_TYPE_DESCRIPTIONS` rewritten for the three reserved types so\nthe LLM-facing enrichment prompt also tells agents NOT to set them\nexplicitly. `rule`'s original signal-phrase guidance (`\"always\"`,\n`\"never\"`, `\"must\"`…) is preserved — the existing\n`test_enrichment_prompt` suite locks it.\n\nInternal callers are unaffected: `evolve_service` and `insights_service`\nbuild `MemoryCreate` objects and pass them to\n`services.memory_service.create_memory` directly. The boundary lives at\nthe route + MCP layer; the service layer never sees the helper.\n\n## Tests — black-box by a subagent\n\nI implemented the fix, then briefed a subagent on the behavioural\ncontract only (no access to `routes/memories.py`, `mcp_server.py`, or\n`common/enrichment/constants.py`). It produced\n`tests/test_c3_c8_reserved_memory_types.py` with 15 cases:\n\n- REST single rejects each of `outcome` / `rule` / `insight`\n(parametrized).\n- REST single accepts `fact` + `None` memory_type.\n- REST bulk rejects when any item carries a reserved type, names the\noffending index.\n- REST bulk accepts when every item is allowed.\n- MCP single rejects each reserved type (parametrized).\n- MCP single accepts `fact`.\n- MCP batch rejects the first reserved item, names the index.\n- MCP batch accepts when all items are allowed.\n- `SERVER_RESERVED_MEMORY_TYPES` shape (frozenset of the three slugs).\n- **Service-layer-doesn't-gate guard via `inspect.getsource`** —\nregression-proofs the internal-bypass contract (a future refactor that\nmoves the check down into `create_memory` would break evolve/insights\nsilently; this test fails loudly instead).\n\nPlus an existing regression test `test_memory_type_insight_accepted` was\nrenamed + rewritten — enum-sync coverage now lives in a schema-level\n`MemoryCreate(...)` instantiation, while the route-level rejection is\nasserted alongside it.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `tests/test_c3_c8_reserved_memory_types.py` — 15 tests, all\npassing, <1s.\n- [x] Existing `test_enrichment_prompt.py` (20 tests) preserved — `rule`\nsignal phrases unchanged.\n- [x] Existing `test_memory_type_insight_accepted` updated to match the\nnew contract.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2613 passed** (+15), 0 regressions.\n- [x] `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `mypy`: 2 new errors of the systemic `_with_latency` `str |\nCallToolResult` shape — same class as 197 pre-existing in the file, out\nof scope.\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh `core-api` build on local-dev:\n`insight` / `outcome` / `rule` → 422 with clean `memory_type='<slug>'`\nin the message; `fact` → 201.\n\n```\n=== insight (expect 422) ===\n{\"detail\":\"memory_type='insight' is server-reserved and cannot be supplied on writes...\"}  HTTP 422\n=== outcome (expect 422) ===\n{\"detail\":\"memory_type='outcome' is server-reserved and cannot be supplied on writes...\"}  HTTP 422\n=== rule (expect 422) ===\n{\"detail\":\"memory_type='rule' is server-reserved and cannot be supplied on writes...\"}     HTTP 422\n=== fact (expect 201) ===\n{\"id\":\"f50b9503-...\",\"memory_type\":\"fact\",...}                                              HTTP 201\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- Cosmetic: the first wet-test pass surfaced `<MemoryType.INSIGHT:\n'insight'>` in error messages (the helper used `!r` on a str-Enum).\nFixed to use `.value` so the message is operator-friendly.\n- Closes C3 + C8 in one PR — they were two views of the same underlying\nboundary gap.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-01T06:34:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0abd727f31b53430519054cc339c238f319489ba","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0abd727f31b53430519054cc339c238f319489ba","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0abd727f31b53430519054cc339c238f319489ba/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"68f19773ecd0d840048b046071e42a813eb68d50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/68f19773ecd0d840048b046071e42a813eb68d50","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/68f19773ecd0d840048b046071e42a813eb68d50"}]},{"sha":"68f19773ecd0d840048b046071e42a813eb68d50","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDY4ZjE5NzczZWNkMGQ4NDAwNDhiMDQ2MDcxZTQyYTgxM2ViNjhkNTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-05-31T13:47:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-31T13:47:04Z"},"message":"fix(search): per-task timeout for parallel_embed_entity_boost (D7) (#260)\n\n## Summary\n\n`ParallelEmbedAndEntityBoost.execute` wrapped `asyncio.gather(emb_task,\nent_task)` in a single `asyncio.wait_for(..., timeout=15.0)`. The two\ntasks shared one cancellation scope, so a slow entity-boost lookup\ncancelled a completed embedding alongside itself — the request surfaced\nas a spurious HTTP 504 even though the vector for a vector-only search\nwas already in hand.\n\nD7's prescription: split the budget so the embedding (critical path) and\nthe entity-boost (supplementary signal) get independent timeouts. On\nentity-boost failure (timeout or otherwise) the step degrades to\nvector-only search with a warning log, not 504.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Two module-level constants: `_OVERALL_TIMEOUT_S = 15.0` (preserved\nfrom the prior shared timeout) and `_MIN_ENTITY_BUDGET_S = 0.1` (floor\non the entity leg so a near-instant embedding still gives the in-flight\nentity task a moment to finish).\n- Embedding is awaited first with `_OVERALL_TIMEOUT_S`. Timeout → still\nHTTP 504. ValueError → still HTTP 503. Either path cancels the in-flight\nentity task.\n- After the embedding resolves, the remaining budget (clamped below by\n`_MIN_ENTITY_BUDGET_S`) is used for the entity-boost. On any failure\n(timeout or other) the step logs a warning and proceeds with `(set(),\n{})`. Total wall-clock stays bounded by `_OVERALL_TIMEOUT_S`.\n\n## Tests — black-box by a subagent\n\nI implemented the production fix, then briefed a subagent on the\nbehavioural contract only (no access to the implementation file). The\nsubagent produced `tests/test_d7_parallel_embed_per_task_timeout.py`\ncovering 7 contract cases:\n\n1. happy path — both helpers return; ctx.data populated.\n2. embedding timeout → HTTPException(504); no partial writes.\n3. embedding ValueError → HTTPException(503); message preserved.\n4. entity-boost timeout → empty boost + WARNING log; no exception.\n5. entity-boost exception → empty boost + WARNING log; no exception.\n6. **D7 headline regression** — slow entity does NOT cancel fast embed.\n7. wall-clock ceiling — slow entity cannot push step past budget.\n\nAll seven pass; the budget knobs are monkey-patched down (~0.3s / 0.05s)\nso the suite runs in <2s.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New `tests/test_d7_parallel_embed_per_task_timeout.py`: 7 cases,\n1.74s.\n- [x] Existing\n`tests/pipeline/test_search_pipeline.py::test_parallel_embed_gather_has_timeout`\nstill passes (504 path under the 15s default).\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2598 passed** (+7), 0 regressions.\n- [x] `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `mypy`: 0 new errors (18 → 18).\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh core-api build on local-dev: D7\nheadline case (10ms embed + 5s boost under shrunken 0.3s budget)\ncompletes in 0.302s with embedding populated and the warning log fired —\nvs the prior code path which would have raised 504.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes D7 in the canonical task list.\n- The two constants are kept module-private (`_`-prefixed). Tests\nmonkey-patch them to keep wall-clock fast.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"c9662b670d9b4fa194adf140747bb7795a6c503b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/c9662b670d9b4fa194adf140747bb7795a6c503b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/68f19773ecd0d840048b046071e42a813eb68d50","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHDvYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMvsQACFoMKeyUHvPB//CdgG2x+Ul\n9SaY1YLoHUPqG5HrEsLGATtjmw8sknoyObgrK5V5AlVi/8RLl8gdKzKuoGsQB8xo\noDj2C22W+OgEV3WsUDJHM234uISPTbq4AKQGds5t295V5FbK8ZfTFfrTKzTdCWCB\nBcx6q2z3AgLRdM5aD8eSbPFNmBv/e/eBfW6BQyy2euKr0TKkDc1r8A9Qf5MKNb1G\nwMevg6jOxvo8rCEE7sYpekdP1ZnXpRfETh4pBG9M5dt11JH0RBMmWW5efXQ9pwZF\ny+LI1quI8+CDgLJ2CnDk9Rv7wd052Wk+FhHLnB9ffMBKA5vxBSomfNCOSFAB+zaZ\nk25YKdaUDI9JNBkTBMisqhbxUP+8i5YmEfo9mzdZreaUA+C4ZYtqWwrR9QPhs78X\nYFvZUba58JnGpm3vU5nJnz9vGO1Rz/+DGQonlzF3Y9zU1uBdNKuTDQynUoss0mVw\n8CFHxo7iAuQ1oQcK6eiDQXzdO8ViiqEuxroLMM8hW+3GSXTxxb252MBZt1tRIEXE\nfCYwjpkrCBA99fqmj5EGpCkMVEcY+aKDdoNIV6/VUIDNGyjuvDM6oHIP5xEZ+mip\n/RBND+mfr+et01RK6SbKjcglg7d0n51tG9hlar35GrS5KLqMpkAeDk6V3Yrn2nDi\nfYYylyi1+BCPWoZzRgfO\n=T29d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c9662b670d9b4fa194adf140747bb7795a6c503b\nparent 595300aae3e51d14d183a1f52a6461e3244e98ec\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780235224 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780235224 +0300\n\nfix(search): per-task timeout for parallel_embed_entity_boost (D7) (#260)\n\n## Summary\n\n`ParallelEmbedAndEntityBoost.execute` wrapped `asyncio.gather(emb_task,\nent_task)` in a single `asyncio.wait_for(..., timeout=15.0)`. The two\ntasks shared one cancellation scope, so a slow entity-boost lookup\ncancelled a completed embedding alongside itself — the request surfaced\nas a spurious HTTP 504 even though the vector for a vector-only search\nwas already in hand.\n\nD7's prescription: split the budget so the embedding (critical path) and\nthe entity-boost (supplementary signal) get independent timeouts. On\nentity-boost failure (timeout or otherwise) the step degrades to\nvector-only search with a warning log, not 504.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Two module-level constants: `_OVERALL_TIMEOUT_S = 15.0` (preserved\nfrom the prior shared timeout) and `_MIN_ENTITY_BUDGET_S = 0.1` (floor\non the entity leg so a near-instant embedding still gives the in-flight\nentity task a moment to finish).\n- Embedding is awaited first with `_OVERALL_TIMEOUT_S`. Timeout → still\nHTTP 504. ValueError → still HTTP 503. Either path cancels the in-flight\nentity task.\n- After the embedding resolves, the remaining budget (clamped below by\n`_MIN_ENTITY_BUDGET_S`) is used for the entity-boost. On any failure\n(timeout or other) the step logs a warning and proceeds with `(set(),\n{})`. Total wall-clock stays bounded by `_OVERALL_TIMEOUT_S`.\n\n## Tests — black-box by a subagent\n\nI implemented the production fix, then briefed a subagent on the\nbehavioural contract only (no access to the implementation file). The\nsubagent produced `tests/test_d7_parallel_embed_per_task_timeout.py`\ncovering 7 contract cases:\n\n1. happy path — both helpers return; ctx.data populated.\n2. embedding timeout → HTTPException(504); no partial writes.\n3. embedding ValueError → HTTPException(503); message preserved.\n4. entity-boost timeout → empty boost + WARNING log; no exception.\n5. entity-boost exception → empty boost + WARNING log; no exception.\n6. **D7 headline regression** — slow entity does NOT cancel fast embed.\n7. wall-clock ceiling — slow entity cannot push step past budget.\n\nAll seven pass; the budget knobs are monkey-patched down (~0.3s / 0.05s)\nso the suite runs in <2s.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New `tests/test_d7_parallel_embed_per_task_timeout.py`: 7 cases,\n1.74s.\n- [x] Existing\n`tests/pipeline/test_search_pipeline.py::test_parallel_embed_gather_has_timeout`\nstill passes (504 path under the 15s default).\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2598 passed** (+7), 0 regressions.\n- [x] `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `mypy`: 0 new errors (18 → 18).\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh core-api build on local-dev: D7\nheadline case (10ms embed + 5s boost under shrunken 0.3s budget)\ncompletes in 0.302s with embedding populated and the warning log fired —\nvs the prior code path which would have raised 504.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes D7 in the canonical task list.\n- The two constants are kept module-private (`_`-prefixed). Tests\nmonkey-patch them to keep wall-clock fast.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-31T13:47:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/68f19773ecd0d840048b046071e42a813eb68d50","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/68f19773ecd0d840048b046071e42a813eb68d50","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/68f19773ecd0d840048b046071e42a813eb68d50/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"595300aae3e51d14d183a1f52a6461e3244e98ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/595300aae3e51d14d183a1f52a6461e3244e98ec","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/595300aae3e51d14d183a1f52a6461e3244e98ec"}]},{"sha":"595300aae3e51d14d183a1f52a6461e3244e98ec","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU5NTMwMGFhZTNlNTFkMTRkMTgzYTFmNTJhNjQ2MWUzMjQ0ZTk4ZWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-05-31T13:10:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-31T13:10:03Z"},"message":"fix(search): include EMBEDDING_QUERY_INSTRUCTION in embedding cache key (C9) (#259)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe search-side embedding cache (``_get_or_cache_embedding`` in\n``memory_service.py``) keyed on\n``{model}:{VECTOR_DIM}:{tenant_id}:{normalized_query}``. For\ninstruction-aware models (Qwen3-Embedding, e5-instruct, KaLM), the\nprovider prepends ``EMBEDDING_QUERY_INSTRUCTION`` to each query at\nencode time — so the SAME raw query under TWO different instructions\nproduces TWO different embeddings. Omitting the instruction from the key\nmeant an env-var change served embeddings encoded under the prior\ninstruction until the TTL expired. Looks like a model regression; root\ncause is a cache-key omission.\n\nThe registry-level provider cache\n(``common/embedding/_registry.py:254-261``) already keys on\n``query_instruction``. This PR mirrors that contract at the search-cache\nlayer.\n\n## Changes\n\n- ``_get_or_cache_embedding`` reads ``EMBEDDING_QUERY_INSTRUCTION`` from\nthe env (same source the registry uses) and hashes it into the cache\nkey.\n- Cache prefix bumped ``qemb3:`` → ``qemb4:``. Old ``qemb3:*`` entries\nexpire naturally via ``EMBEDDING_CACHE_TTL`` — mirrors the prior\n``qemb2:`` → ``qemb3:`` migration when ``VECTOR_DIM`` was added.\n- Unset and explicit-empty resolve to the same key (both fall through to\nthe provider's no-prefix branch — equivalent downstream).\n\nPure correctness — no behavior change for symmetric-model deployments\n(OpenAI text-embedding-3-small, bge-m3, etc.), no change to the encode\npath itself.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New ``tests/test_c9_embedding_cache_instruction_key.py``: 4 tests\ncover the new ``qemb4:`` prefix, distinct keys under different\ninstructions, cache hit under same instruction, unset / empty\nequivalence.\n- [x] Existing ``tests/test_query_embedding_stampede_guard.py`` (6\ntests) pass unchanged.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2591 passed**, 0 regressions.\n- [x] ``ruff check`` clean; ``ruff format --check`` clean.\n- [x] ``mypy``: 0 new errors (78 → 78).\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh core-api build on local-dev: three\ndistinct ``qemb4:*`` keys for the same query under unset / instruction-A\n/ instruction-B.\n\n```\nunset instruction:  qemb4:8ae02b9687b775c56c21cc3bd61d93f05f7cf6ea3347260fea3bcb6a5909ea97\ninstruction A:      qemb4:768fdfe0eed12d5af3a9b1948b1881bff0a277d6e124d726196c7cf6c58bf1d7\ninstruction B:      qemb4:919a12fbc306bd8626824a53702cb5ab789a77eb6bfc723c55a29ac5543ac1d1\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes C9 in the canonical task list.\n- The fix only addresses the cache-key omission. If a future feature\nexposes per-call instruction overrides (the optional ``instruction`` arg\non ``get_query_embedding`` that this codebase doesn't use today),\nthat'll need its own threading into ``_get_or_cache_embedding``.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"cafb8ba33f50dab4ac2bd770089a20f8e49a1400","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/cafb8ba33f50dab4ac2bd770089a20f8e49a1400"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/595300aae3e51d14d183a1f52a6461e3244e98ec","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHDMrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB/QQAB7P0XEzLiZsi/G0EBOkv5kf\noAaZzNgnHnJ9D8+RtO51ulZVDZJrfx7okxUx8mHdQ2ijg+dz41tCMZmM8SlX7Elg\nS1Ghb5DUbF1/c0DXfdN+Eqd1QzC2oAwgCRZGCJWUC8Ye/MMeb8IJ5X32go4TASbt\nw2Aeetvn0XZNOmogBDbKBdJ5559/l27Ynr/s8x0n+zS2L5F5h9kSZlMFASm793oo\n4R3Fjo4/FdcPqk7v41Z5Ex/KHEnqzZbZXAaAr7mSPgjHLcMR0SlcqBc1137Rz8ae\nNdbs47VvYGgeGmRNnSl7BXWwRilnDlI120Tgo2fL0X49+JYi7xWTLkZbWsk/leFv\nFcqj9tW+MY62SakOny1imFXFmCHGT84hetBOiWPhJ0RxEUqw4n16n3Y8WopS62xE\nKGZeBhZthozCSM7nmMnasbazTAT6h1NPmm7VKnYSMgAXbaQjTkz938bBP/ff3Jf7\nom74uHy9UaB/PqS+M1ra25RqTL0K0XLxARbpFS5sJ9z0/zdvm55xHuO+PIxtruDM\nn3IxOl/Ghj33+QdF+OMUIS8WrmcGCKczKZlvfDHVsmjNldE3sk4BcAwJmd00nKwH\n3Jmag2Hg2l3aBrPosmk3FsDQy+K6J061sn/VAtIj0PBCbf0tJGeScQKi1UlR+/s0\nzGMnE9NJl55kTi6meE0X\n=k1E7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cafb8ba33f50dab4ac2bd770089a20f8e49a1400\nparent 71fd8412086f426519a401038f9954242c41e120\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780233003 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780233003 +0300\n\nfix(search): include EMBEDDING_QUERY_INSTRUCTION in embedding cache key (C9) (#259)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe search-side embedding cache (``_get_or_cache_embedding`` in\n``memory_service.py``) keyed on\n``{model}:{VECTOR_DIM}:{tenant_id}:{normalized_query}``. For\ninstruction-aware models (Qwen3-Embedding, e5-instruct, KaLM), the\nprovider prepends ``EMBEDDING_QUERY_INSTRUCTION`` to each query at\nencode time — so the SAME raw query under TWO different instructions\nproduces TWO different embeddings. Omitting the instruction from the key\nmeant an env-var change served embeddings encoded under the prior\ninstruction until the TTL expired. Looks like a model regression; root\ncause is a cache-key omission.\n\nThe registry-level provider cache\n(``common/embedding/_registry.py:254-261``) already keys on\n``query_instruction``. This PR mirrors that contract at the search-cache\nlayer.\n\n## Changes\n\n- ``_get_or_cache_embedding`` reads ``EMBEDDING_QUERY_INSTRUCTION`` from\nthe env (same source the registry uses) and hashes it into the cache\nkey.\n- Cache prefix bumped ``qemb3:`` → ``qemb4:``. Old ``qemb3:*`` entries\nexpire naturally via ``EMBEDDING_CACHE_TTL`` — mirrors the prior\n``qemb2:`` → ``qemb3:`` migration when ``VECTOR_DIM`` was added.\n- Unset and explicit-empty resolve to the same key (both fall through to\nthe provider's no-prefix branch — equivalent downstream).\n\nPure correctness — no behavior change for symmetric-model deployments\n(OpenAI text-embedding-3-small, bge-m3, etc.), no change to the encode\npath itself.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New ``tests/test_c9_embedding_cache_instruction_key.py``: 4 tests\ncover the new ``qemb4:`` prefix, distinct keys under different\ninstructions, cache hit under same instruction, unset / empty\nequivalence.\n- [x] Existing ``tests/test_query_embedding_stampede_guard.py`` (6\ntests) pass unchanged.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2591 passed**, 0 regressions.\n- [x] ``ruff check`` clean; ``ruff format --check`` clean.\n- [x] ``mypy``: 0 new errors (78 → 78).\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh core-api build on local-dev: three\ndistinct ``qemb4:*`` keys for the same query under unset / instruction-A\n/ instruction-B.\n\n```\nunset instruction:  qemb4:8ae02b9687b775c56c21cc3bd61d93f05f7cf6ea3347260fea3bcb6a5909ea97\ninstruction A:      qemb4:768fdfe0eed12d5af3a9b1948b1881bff0a277d6e124d726196c7cf6c58bf1d7\ninstruction B:      qemb4:919a12fbc306bd8626824a53702cb5ab789a77eb6bfc723c55a29ac5543ac1d1\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes C9 in the canonical task list.\n- The fix only addresses the cache-key omission. If a future feature\nexposes per-call instruction overrides (the optional ``instruction`` arg\non ``get_query_embedding`` that this codebase doesn't use today),\nthat'll need its own threading into ``_get_or_cache_embedding``.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-31T13:10:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/595300aae3e51d14d183a1f52a6461e3244e98ec","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/595300aae3e51d14d183a1f52a6461e3244e98ec","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/595300aae3e51d14d183a1f52a6461e3244e98ec/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"71fd8412086f426519a401038f9954242c41e120","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/71fd8412086f426519a401038f9954242c41e120","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/71fd8412086f426519a401038f9954242c41e120"}]},{"sha":"71fd8412086f426519a401038f9954242c41e120","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDcxZmQ4NDEyMDg2ZjQyNjUxOWE0MDEwMzhmOTk1NDI0MmM0MWUxMjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-05-31T12:48:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-31T12:48:46Z"},"message":"fix(search): share entity tokenizer between FTS-weight + entity-FTS gates (A27) (#258)\n\n## Summary\n\n`_adaptive_fts_weight` (the FTS-vs-semantic blend gate) used naive\n`query.split()`, while `extract_entity_tokens` (the entity-FTS\nshort-circuit gate) split on hyphens and stripped possessives. A\nhyphenated identifier like `claude-opus-4-7` gave **1 token to the\nFTS-weight gate but 4 tokens to entity-FTS** — the two gates routed the\nsame query inconsistently.\n\nA27's stated fix: share the tokenizer. The share required preserving two\nexisting behaviours of the FTS-weight gate:\n\n1. **Raw `MAX_TOKENS` gate** — a 4+ word natural-language sentence\n(`\"tell me about NEXAI\"`) should stay semantic-weight, even when the\nshared filter would collapse it to a single meaningful token.\n2. **Sigil signal** — `extract_entity_tokens` strips leading `$@#`\npunctuation, so handle / ticker / hashtag boost signals would otherwise\nvanish post-share.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `extract_entity_tokens` gains `preserve_case=False` kwarg. Default\nbehaviour (entity-FTS gate) is unchanged. The FTS-weight gate passes\n`preserve_case=True` so its proper-noun heuristic (CamelCase / ALL-CAPS\ndetection) keeps working.\n- `_adaptive_fts_weight` rewritten to: (a) gate `MAX_TOKENS` on raw\nwhitespace count, (b) call `extract_entity_tokens` for specificity\ncomputation, (c) sigil-detect on the raw query before tokenization\nstrips leading punctuation.\n- Dropped now-unused `ENTITY_STOPWORDS` / `ENTITY_TOKEN_MIN_LENGTH`\nimports from `memory_service.py` (filter logic lives in the shared\nhelper now).\n\n## Behavioural impact\n\n- **Hyphenated identifiers no longer auto-boost.** `claude-opus-4-7`,\n`gpt-5-turbo` etc. used to boost FTS via the \"lone-token-with-digits\"\nspecificity heuristic. After the share, the tokenizer splits them on\nhyphens, neither half is specific on its own, and the ratio falls below\nthreshold. This matches what the entity-FTS gate already saw — and\nthat's the A27 contract.\n- **Everything else preserved**: `NEXAI`, `CertiK OpenAI`, `$BTC`,\n`@karpathy`, `#trending`, `find $BTC price`, `GPT-5 release` all still\nboost. Long sentences with one rare term still stay default.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New `tests/test_a27_shared_tokenizer.py`: 13 tests cover the\n`preserve_case` kwarg, tokenizer agreement on hyphenated identifiers,\nsigil preservation, and the raw `MAX_TOKENS` gate.\n- [x] Existing `tests/test_adaptive_fts_weight.py` (24 tests) and\n`tests/test_entity_tokens.py` (40 tests) pass unchanged — no regressions\non the prior contracts.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2587 passed** (+13), 0 regressions.\n- [x] `ruff check` clean; `ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `mypy`: 0 new errors (78 → 78).\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh `core-api` build on local-dev: 8 probe\nqueries verified against expected weights and entity-token outputs.\n\n```\nclaude-opus-4-7                  0.3  ['claude', 'opus']\n@karpathy                        0.6  ['karpathy']\n$BTC                             0.6  ['BTC']\nNEXAI                            0.6  ['NEXAI']\nCertiK OpenAI                    0.6  ['CertiK', 'OpenAI']\ntell me about NEXAI              0.3  ['NEXAI']\nwhat is the address of OpenAI    0.3  ['address', 'OpenAI']\ngood crypto                      0.3  ['crypto']\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes A27 in the canonical task list.\n- Related: A7 (Query classifier mis-routes entity-token queries) is\nstill open. If A7's fix changes `extract_entity_tokens`, the FTS-weight\ngate now inherits those changes for free — they were the point of\nsharing.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"39ca272f07742ad5322863947afdc100e90c2434","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/39ca272f07742ad5322863947afdc100e90c2434"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/71fd8412086f426519a401038f9954242c41e120","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHC4uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/qMQAIddbmrZgA50/8KilEXuHwKl\ntIwNV21K1RLlH1tkQUp1OXI0fOHbMDdRIRunzJh5eSfavcwXM19tEfbHls+/icbH\nQRHGUpg1N87U36oe0st9uZH4iwKDamD/PFxduocqXqM/AMGtC5EYC2bGLMbTIaWu\ncHSZ1CTpm79xWBBuc8cr/D7emvo61rXpZKVHGXr4jWqbPodhwTzDKDiNq/cRaJ4+\ni1C2189HOv3xfc52UpAKtP7Jp4GVrugIs8w/Sic1e/a3hbvjn94OZeaZagdaorz9\nsnJXUeMh5JOnIXI9ZIoN//ZxaoFMGU3iZruzqGB1lN07qgsUze1VrOyETs6bGzpj\niJGenvTp2yWQoY4xmhky+MbV41yFoeIlGtz1XuUv0J3/IiZCM9KjvYohhqgd7+nv\n0/7x2St3v4YGHIkU1M4Ny8LyxNoxtFU/mRj6I6XHty+lMrDwy7jBqm4Kh5fbJ9M6\nDBA/dkXfW6N0b3mWO68+gUPcw0+Uz+J9scfPkfHI6nWqnqF7LKYAxdZbllopYF1j\n0QXgM8txhWah5AX51UErVrLBTY/kHbvqlZDly2R9heDmVio7AhZcojWMWGh2d5aa\nKKX7ekvTphUGp9VR4JB1Yca18aiG2dZefaq5sovJQ+3agu1VRlpsOEA6HVFbEpZx\nmvWaibQm6sE5PWEhZzhH\n=2Cle\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 39ca272f07742ad5322863947afdc100e90c2434\nparent 5f314d90c8e847b874a7d5fcd2c9e5218a4c0e1c\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780231726 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780231726 +0300\n\nfix(search): share entity tokenizer between FTS-weight + entity-FTS gates (A27) (#258)\n\n## Summary\n\n`_adaptive_fts_weight` (the FTS-vs-semantic blend gate) used naive\n`query.split()`, while `extract_entity_tokens` (the entity-FTS\nshort-circuit gate) split on hyphens and stripped possessives. A\nhyphenated identifier like `claude-opus-4-7` gave **1 token to the\nFTS-weight gate but 4 tokens to entity-FTS** — the two gates routed the\nsame query inconsistently.\n\nA27's stated fix: share the tokenizer. The share required preserving two\nexisting behaviours of the FTS-weight gate:\n\n1. **Raw `MAX_TOKENS` gate** — a 4+ word natural-language sentence\n(`\"tell me about NEXAI\"`) should stay semantic-weight, even when the\nshared filter would collapse it to a single meaningful token.\n2. **Sigil signal** — `extract_entity_tokens` strips leading `$@#`\npunctuation, so handle / ticker / hashtag boost signals would otherwise\nvanish post-share.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `extract_entity_tokens` gains `preserve_case=False` kwarg. Default\nbehaviour (entity-FTS gate) is unchanged. The FTS-weight gate passes\n`preserve_case=True` so its proper-noun heuristic (CamelCase / ALL-CAPS\ndetection) keeps working.\n- `_adaptive_fts_weight` rewritten to: (a) gate `MAX_TOKENS` on raw\nwhitespace count, (b) call `extract_entity_tokens` for specificity\ncomputation, (c) sigil-detect on the raw query before tokenization\nstrips leading punctuation.\n- Dropped now-unused `ENTITY_STOPWORDS` / `ENTITY_TOKEN_MIN_LENGTH`\nimports from `memory_service.py` (filter logic lives in the shared\nhelper now).\n\n## Behavioural impact\n\n- **Hyphenated identifiers no longer auto-boost.** `claude-opus-4-7`,\n`gpt-5-turbo` etc. used to boost FTS via the \"lone-token-with-digits\"\nspecificity heuristic. After the share, the tokenizer splits them on\nhyphens, neither half is specific on its own, and the ratio falls below\nthreshold. This matches what the entity-FTS gate already saw — and\nthat's the A27 contract.\n- **Everything else preserved**: `NEXAI`, `CertiK OpenAI`, `$BTC`,\n`@karpathy`, `#trending`, `find $BTC price`, `GPT-5 release` all still\nboost. Long sentences with one rare term still stay default.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New `tests/test_a27_shared_tokenizer.py`: 13 tests cover the\n`preserve_case` kwarg, tokenizer agreement on hyphenated identifiers,\nsigil preservation, and the raw `MAX_TOKENS` gate.\n- [x] Existing `tests/test_adaptive_fts_weight.py` (24 tests) and\n`tests/test_entity_tokens.py` (40 tests) pass unchanged — no regressions\non the prior contracts.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2587 passed** (+13), 0 regressions.\n- [x] `ruff check` clean; `ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `mypy`: 0 new errors (78 → 78).\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh `core-api` build on local-dev: 8 probe\nqueries verified against expected weights and entity-token outputs.\n\n```\nclaude-opus-4-7                  0.3  ['claude', 'opus']\n@karpathy                        0.6  ['karpathy']\n$BTC                             0.6  ['BTC']\nNEXAI                            0.6  ['NEXAI']\nCertiK OpenAI                    0.6  ['CertiK', 'OpenAI']\ntell me about NEXAI              0.3  ['NEXAI']\nwhat is the address of OpenAI    0.3  ['address', 'OpenAI']\ngood crypto                      0.3  ['crypto']\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes A27 in the canonical task list.\n- Related: A7 (Query classifier mis-routes entity-token queries) is\nstill open. If A7's fix changes `extract_entity_tokens`, the FTS-weight\ngate now inherits those changes for free — they were the point of\nsharing.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-31T12:48:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/71fd8412086f426519a401038f9954242c41e120","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/71fd8412086f426519a401038f9954242c41e120","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/71fd8412086f426519a401038f9954242c41e120/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5f314d90c8e847b874a7d5fcd2c9e5218a4c0e1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5f314d90c8e847b874a7d5fcd2c9e5218a4c0e1c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5f314d90c8e847b874a7d5fcd2c9e5218a4c0e1c"}]},{"sha":"5f314d90c8e847b874a7d5fcd2c9e5218a4c0e1c","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDVmMzE0ZDkwYzhlODQ3Yjg3NGE3ZDVmY2QyYzllNTIxOGE0YzBlMWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-05-31T12:12:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-31T12:12:41Z"},"message":"feat(evolve): surface weight-adjustment skip reason (A15) (#257)\n\n## Summary\n\nA15 mirrors [A10 / PR\n#199](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/199) for the\n**weight-adjustment** side of `report_outcome`. An evolve call that\nreturns 200 OK with `weight_adjustments=[]` had no contract for\ndistinguishing:\n\n- caller supplied no `related_ids`\n- scope filter dropped every `related_id` (agent / fleet / all mismatch)\n- bulk UPDATE found no matching rows (race / row deleted between filter\nand update)\n\n…from genuine success. RL feedback was silently lost.\n\nThis PR adds a `weight_adjustment_skipped_reason` field to the response\nthat names the silent-exit path. No change to persistence, scope-filter,\nor weight-adjustment logic.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **New module-level `WEIGHT_ADJUSTMENT_SKIP_REASONS`** tuple — 5 slugs\n(`no_related_ids`, `agent_id_mismatch`, `fleet_id_mismatch`,\n`all_out_of_scope`, `no_rows_updated`). Lives next to\n`RULE_SKIP_REASONS` for grep-ability.\n- **New `_log_weight_adjustment_skip`** helper — emits\n`evolve_weight_adjustment_skipped reason=<slug> tenant_id=<tid>\nscope=<scope>` in the always-fire / grep-friendly shape (matches A10 /\nGap-06).\n- **`_adjust_weights` return type widened**: `(list[str], list[dict])` →\n`(str | None, list[str], list[dict])`. First element is the slug when no\nrows moved (no UUIDs parsed, bulk UPDATE 0-rows, or bulk UPDATE raised),\nNone on success.\n- **`report_outcome` computes the upstream slug** based on\n`_filter_by_scope` output; **`_apply_outcome_to_db` overrides** it if\n`_adjust_weights` returns a more-specific reason (deeper-stage wins,\nmirrors A10's `rule_skipped_reason` flow).\n- **Response gains `weight_adjustment_skipped_reason`** — `None` on\nsuccess, slug otherwise.\n\n## What this doesn't do\n\n- Doesn't change which IDs get dropped, how the scope filter works, or\nthe bulk UPDATE atomicity contract.\n- Doesn't raise on `_adjust_weights` DB exceptions — they still log +\nreturn empty, just now with the `no_rows_updated` slug. Behavior change\nis out of scope.\n- Doesn't slug `db_update_failed` separately from `no_rows_updated` —\nkeeping the slug count minimal per the early-stage / no-overcomplication\nphilosophy. The exception detail is in the existing warning log.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New `tests/test_a15_evolve_weight_adjustment_skipped_reason.py`:\n11 tests cover the slug constant set, response field presence, all 5\nsilent-exit paths, success path returns None, structured log lines\nemitted with reason in message.\n- [x] Existing `tests/test_evolve_service.py` (9 callsites) and\n`tests/test_a10_evolve_rule_skipped_reason.py` (2 mock return_values)\nupdated for the widened `_adjust_weights` return tuple.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2574 passed** (+11), 0 regressions.\n- [x] `ruff check` clean; `ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `mypy` — **0 new errors** (18 → 18 on `evolve_service.py`).\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh `core-api` build on local-dev: each of\nthe 5 silent-noop slugs returns the right value; success path returns\n`weight_adjustment_skipped_reason=None` with weight_adjustments\npopulated.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes A15 in the canonical task list.\n- Pairs naturally with A10's just-shipped `rule_skipped_reason` (PR #199\n/ `b16de2b`) — same observability pattern, parallel field.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"030e6e89db3b9ed5cc064fe9c846e03c0475b2c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/030e6e89db3b9ed5cc064fe9c846e03c0475b2c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5f314d90c8e847b874a7d5fcd2c9e5218a4c0e1c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHCW5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA77sQADx/iDxnHR16dgwmTQtu4fxO\neH6NcWxkElelvtoyn10uIMDhVHrXjfZhQQAPoYL7Oh2ngy+c8SnnvTSg5pNwCLi+\nK5dmjOLdXJwwJ0VLFkiRXRl0dLXqbw7ZR5jEVWxxMyUkRDNqMBaiyIUo6FuJXHxA\nt1RvITdell1/gskRyNka7GguoGgaqPzjgJdXbl4m8TcxG6mQEWX2h7FFZV7OJhb5\nXi9CLFK9RZhJbx3Xq2E8TWZFrEyqg57Ib+YR5cDdAut51GzZoxp4QrkdY8wRWYvv\nuJx92k5VQmj5gyB5WaEZSh5gX4FNVmRadpBww6eY2HCULC2lPpDRO0i8I0ORYt3P\nmJ5VVCCUCVPOV8iU9tEzoupIAnYEz2AsaFhMTEOu7teugEthPeDPYwpzOliNCqqN\n1AyU/CVrCdWr+QtF8cDEFSG2PptUPAyJZvcwiDbZipJvzkGfVm1Bsb61zVJ80Zoh\nrksNglBnXNM9wYmuXYc7Sunotrnu83xECWEoxTsqLMWpfiB76Rd2bl+wGFNezQKJ\nlVjnYfvSQHKUBos9v6p7Je9aRFyaxs7IEeOyC2hacB/xN3t2XZfEhl5s/QoIkcL2\nl6UyKXuCEdG0k0QEdM8uSQBmm1Q6J4zYB0/j1iR0kzXRN+I6//Ox6pukg6BN1COi\nRFFJhquHgbhY/5hqlg0/\n=GDa5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 030e6e89db3b9ed5cc064fe9c846e03c0475b2c0\nparent 887c7021d6e00bab844a893005f723cda55f96c0\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780229561 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780229561 +0300\n\nfeat(evolve): surface weight-adjustment skip reason (A15) (#257)\n\n## Summary\n\nA15 mirrors [A10 / PR\n#199](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/199) for the\n**weight-adjustment** side of `report_outcome`. An evolve call that\nreturns 200 OK with `weight_adjustments=[]` had no contract for\ndistinguishing:\n\n- caller supplied no `related_ids`\n- scope filter dropped every `related_id` (agent / fleet / all mismatch)\n- bulk UPDATE found no matching rows (race / row deleted between filter\nand update)\n\n…from genuine success. RL feedback was silently lost.\n\nThis PR adds a `weight_adjustment_skipped_reason` field to the response\nthat names the silent-exit path. No change to persistence, scope-filter,\nor weight-adjustment logic.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **New module-level `WEIGHT_ADJUSTMENT_SKIP_REASONS`** tuple — 5 slugs\n(`no_related_ids`, `agent_id_mismatch`, `fleet_id_mismatch`,\n`all_out_of_scope`, `no_rows_updated`). Lives next to\n`RULE_SKIP_REASONS` for grep-ability.\n- **New `_log_weight_adjustment_skip`** helper — emits\n`evolve_weight_adjustment_skipped reason=<slug> tenant_id=<tid>\nscope=<scope>` in the always-fire / grep-friendly shape (matches A10 /\nGap-06).\n- **`_adjust_weights` return type widened**: `(list[str], list[dict])` →\n`(str | None, list[str], list[dict])`. First element is the slug when no\nrows moved (no UUIDs parsed, bulk UPDATE 0-rows, or bulk UPDATE raised),\nNone on success.\n- **`report_outcome` computes the upstream slug** based on\n`_filter_by_scope` output; **`_apply_outcome_to_db` overrides** it if\n`_adjust_weights` returns a more-specific reason (deeper-stage wins,\nmirrors A10's `rule_skipped_reason` flow).\n- **Response gains `weight_adjustment_skipped_reason`** — `None` on\nsuccess, slug otherwise.\n\n## What this doesn't do\n\n- Doesn't change which IDs get dropped, how the scope filter works, or\nthe bulk UPDATE atomicity contract.\n- Doesn't raise on `_adjust_weights` DB exceptions — they still log +\nreturn empty, just now with the `no_rows_updated` slug. Behavior change\nis out of scope.\n- Doesn't slug `db_update_failed` separately from `no_rows_updated` —\nkeeping the slug count minimal per the early-stage / no-overcomplication\nphilosophy. The exception detail is in the existing warning log.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New `tests/test_a15_evolve_weight_adjustment_skipped_reason.py`:\n11 tests cover the slug constant set, response field presence, all 5\nsilent-exit paths, success path returns None, structured log lines\nemitted with reason in message.\n- [x] Existing `tests/test_evolve_service.py` (9 callsites) and\n`tests/test_a10_evolve_rule_skipped_reason.py` (2 mock return_values)\nupdated for the widened `_adjust_weights` return tuple.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark suite: **2574 passed** (+11), 0 regressions.\n- [x] `ruff check` clean; `ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `mypy` — **0 new errors** (18 → 18 on `evolve_service.py`).\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh `core-api` build on local-dev: each of\nthe 5 silent-noop slugs returns the right value; success path returns\n`weight_adjustment_skipped_reason=None` with weight_adjustments\npopulated.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes A15 in the canonical task list.\n- Pairs naturally with A10's just-shipped `rule_skipped_reason` (PR #199\n/ `b16de2b`) — same observability pattern, parallel field.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-31T12:12:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5f314d90c8e847b874a7d5fcd2c9e5218a4c0e1c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5f314d90c8e847b874a7d5fcd2c9e5218a4c0e1c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5f314d90c8e847b874a7d5fcd2c9e5218a4c0e1c/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"887c7021d6e00bab844a893005f723cda55f96c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/887c7021d6e00bab844a893005f723cda55f96c0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/887c7021d6e00bab844a893005f723cda55f96c0"}]},{"sha":"887c7021d6e00bab844a893005f723cda55f96c0","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDg4N2M3MDIxZDZlMDBiYWI4NDRhODkzMDA1ZjcyM2NkYTU1Zjk2YzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-05-31T11:31:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-31T11:31:28Z"},"message":"fix(mcp): extend mcp-agent default refusal to all write tools (A14) (#256)\n\n## Summary\n\nPR #139 closed A14 for `memclaw_write` and `memclaw_doc op=write`. This\nPR\nextends the same `_refuse_default_agent_on_gateway` guard to the\nremaining\nfour write surfaces that PR #139 didn't touch:\n\n- `memclaw_manage` — guarded only on write ops\n(`update`/`transition`/`delete`/`bulk_delete`); reads keep current\nergonomics.\n- `memclaw_tune` — guarded (always a write).\n- `memclaw_evolve` — guarded (always a write).\n- `memclaw_keystones_set` — its schema `agent_id` is the TARGET agent\n(defaults to `None`), so the silent-attribution lived at the internal\n`caller_agent_id = _get_agent_id() or \"mcp-agent\"` line — guard runs\nagainst that fallback.\n\nSame mechanism (`_refuse_default_agent_on_gateway`), same error code\n(`MISSING_AGENT_ID`), same message — just at four more call sites.\n\n## What's intentionally out of scope\n\nRead tools (`memclaw_recall`, `memclaw_list`, `memclaw_stats`,\n`memclaw_insights`, `memclaw_keystones`, `memclaw_doc\nop=read/search/list`) are NOT guarded by this PR. The A14 failure mode\nis destructive writes silently attributed to the reserved identity;\nreads against an unscoped agent return an empty result, which is a UX\nissue, not data loss. Worth tracking separately if it surfaces in usage\n— see the task list.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New parametrized unit test\n`tests/test_mcp_default_agent_guard_a14.py` asserts `MISSING_AGENT_ID`\non all 4 tools when gateway-routed + literal default. (4 passed)\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh `core-api` build on local-dev (gateway\nrouting simulated via `_via_gateway_var = True`): each of the 4 returns\n`MISSING_AGENT_ID`; `memclaw_manage op=lineage` returns `NOT_FOUND` not\n`MISSING_AGENT_ID`, confirming writes-only scoping is correct.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark test suite: 2563 passed / 3 skipped / 1 xfailed\n/ 3 xpassed.\n- [x] `ruff check` clean on changed files; `ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `mypy` — 4 new `Incompatible return value type (got \"str |\nCallToolResult\")` errors of the same shape as 141 pre-existing ones in\nthe file (including the existing PR #139 guard at line 589). Systemic\n`_with_latency` typing, out of scope.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes part of task A14 (the destructive class). Read-side A14 is\nbeing left open per the shared task list.\n- Mirrors the call-site pattern from PR #139 for grep-ability.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"c27ea03455ad82cf92a07482927a5d9989950a72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/c27ea03455ad82cf92a07482927a5d9989950a72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/887c7021d6e00bab844a893005f723cda55f96c0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHBwQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhCsQACE71Kmk7Guktr9IL7GtX4P4\nb0Y+B+60UyZ6kkycvSpf5zjoFYJveD3xOzGhFWL+hhiiQ0qJ8eiJjYdj8tCbiY5J\njuo84VM/O70mLeCdhWmQOSI+xgqxTtZ/Gc3nBr+Lt3YtBABFAsyKI6030zRBG9QZ\nlH9LtV98odfczKS0JfERhMaB47CGMbT7Hgecr2oFRHKCUo4p6XyEblFCQUy8qRdB\nTnecUCvbTq08h71tvSxa9unRrDFpmYvLy/WsIjIT6XQES7bjLa92zINxgepbKJaP\nBdkcNN5j/l5gjwLSj6fdH2BnmTqm6ZhpeX2oKphGrAUnbPDkDUtIBxk3AMo59cCC\nLEdGU57yBMaUEyPMxoi0cc5QvtVlQ9nuzeaChhx5S/llb6un0P5eOxtBxZY/BbYU\nZHQf37fN1mK0mPYiNQXrR8VyIpplEq6yJZ1Pfqc9yoZQtxRkHek+/Jl2pDEdAlEs\nClfNykL4kOx2mfAhFg3k/Tz8BehFnE6pE/ZOkMw6reKBPTa3R1+NVfHLR9nZ6Bo/\nCAACVKzU/HzyuNog3VbkQkPjSLgPHHovWAgwhMJk9VC6r11ZPB3xj44munoDVSzC\nsJx7DNyNPTOJMoScTO+j6y7KErnEFrBDLWRIzIGgvjNyL4hlGZLqhR4QgBL/PeEQ\nHF+VdpX7HZDNUP2YLid1\n=/I2H\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c27ea03455ad82cf92a07482927a5d9989950a72\nparent 496717eeeb28cabdf07d8b690c07e2d03ac7aa2f\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1780227088 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780227088 +0300\n\nfix(mcp): extend mcp-agent default refusal to all write tools (A14) (#256)\n\n## Summary\n\nPR #139 closed A14 for `memclaw_write` and `memclaw_doc op=write`. This\nPR\nextends the same `_refuse_default_agent_on_gateway` guard to the\nremaining\nfour write surfaces that PR #139 didn't touch:\n\n- `memclaw_manage` — guarded only on write ops\n(`update`/`transition`/`delete`/`bulk_delete`); reads keep current\nergonomics.\n- `memclaw_tune` — guarded (always a write).\n- `memclaw_evolve` — guarded (always a write).\n- `memclaw_keystones_set` — its schema `agent_id` is the TARGET agent\n(defaults to `None`), so the silent-attribution lived at the internal\n`caller_agent_id = _get_agent_id() or \"mcp-agent\"` line — guard runs\nagainst that fallback.\n\nSame mechanism (`_refuse_default_agent_on_gateway`), same error code\n(`MISSING_AGENT_ID`), same message — just at four more call sites.\n\n## What's intentionally out of scope\n\nRead tools (`memclaw_recall`, `memclaw_list`, `memclaw_stats`,\n`memclaw_insights`, `memclaw_keystones`, `memclaw_doc\nop=read/search/list`) are NOT guarded by this PR. The A14 failure mode\nis destructive writes silently attributed to the reserved identity;\nreads against an unscoped agent return an empty result, which is a UX\nissue, not data loss. Worth tracking separately if it surfaces in usage\n— see the task list.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New parametrized unit test\n`tests/test_mcp_default_agent_guard_a14.py` asserts `MISSING_AGENT_ID`\non all 4 tools when gateway-routed + literal default. (4 passed)\n- [x] Wet-tested against a fresh `core-api` build on local-dev (gateway\nrouting simulated via `_via_gateway_var = True`): each of the 4 returns\n`MISSING_AGENT_ID`; `memclaw_manage op=lineage` returns `NOT_FOUND` not\n`MISSING_AGENT_ID`, confirming writes-only scoping is correct.\n- [x] Full non-benchmark test suite: 2563 passed / 3 skipped / 1 xfailed\n/ 3 xpassed.\n- [x] `ruff check` clean on changed files; `ruff format --check` clean.\n- [x] `mypy` — 4 new `Incompatible return value type (got \"str |\nCallToolResult\")` errors of the same shape as 141 pre-existing ones in\nthe file (including the existing PR #139 guard at line 589). Systemic\n`_with_latency` typing, out of scope.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Closes part of task A14 (the destructive class). Read-side A14 is\nbeing left open per the shared task list.\n- Mirrors the call-site pattern from PR #139 for grep-ability.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-31T11:31:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/887c7021d6e00bab844a893005f723cda55f96c0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/887c7021d6e00bab844a893005f723cda55f96c0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/887c7021d6e00bab844a893005f723cda55f96c0/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"496717eeeb28cabdf07d8b690c07e2d03ac7aa2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/496717eeeb28cabdf07d8b690c07e2d03ac7aa2f","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/496717eeeb28cabdf07d8b690c07e2d03ac7aa2f"}]},{"sha":"496717eeeb28cabdf07d8b690c07e2d03ac7aa2f","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQ5NjcxN2VlZWIyOGNhYmRmMDdkOGI2OTBjMDdlMmQwM2FjN2FhMmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-30T19:15:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-30T19:15:01Z"},"message":"docs: fix stale API paths, tool counts, and version references (#255)\n\n## Summary\n\nCustomer-facing docs had drifted from the code. Every fix was validated\nagainst `core-api` routes, `tools/_registry`, and `config` — corrections\nto existing docs, no new content.\n\n- **Stale `/api/*` → `/api/v1/*`** — the documented calls 404 as\nwritten: `AGENT-INSTALL.md` search/memories curls;\n`integration-guide.md` `tool-descriptions`, `fleet/heartbeat`, `agents`\n(×3), `memories/bulk`. Only the plugin-bootstrap router is mounted at\nbare `/api`; everything else is `/api/v1`.\n- **Tool counts** — 12 MCP tools / 11 plugin (plugin omits the MCP-only\n`memclaw_keystones_set`), replacing stale 9/10 counts and the \"plugin\nsurfaces all 12\" line.\n- **`memclaw_evolve` trust** — `scope=agent` (default) needs trust 1,\nnot 2; `fleet`/`all` needs 2. Documented signature now includes\n`scope`/`fleet_id`.\n- **`SECURITY.md`** — report version via `GET /api/v1/version` (no\n`VERSION` file exists); supported-versions line `1.x` → `2.x`.\n- **static skill install URL** → `/api/v1/install-skill`.\n- **`README.md` rollback** — `alembic downgrade 011` (was `009`, which\nover-reverted migrations `010` + `011`).\n\n## Testing\nDoc-only; no code paths changed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a4d890249aec920788f99cb5fa17bcc586e84d82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a4d890249aec920788f99cb5fa17bcc586e84d82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/496717eeeb28cabdf07d8b690c07e2d03ac7aa2f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGzc1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARoEQAKzA4Th4LhsVYXdnbxqe2AhY\nNE9N3IZyW6FkHTT1jnWUBUpjLHCfzS9TMJsDaqNA9ZOjitV0NXnJQAeF0odX2HAR\nfD6gRYgnFwvVV3ojMwfCMOsTPqLkef15qI+6ilq74znqljmpRf77za025wx1/a7K\nxuaTd37a9w7d4U3GSBdC0JpunRVSa96/Siw4zM9LxFWNUeWuK4YzPy52hJ+E8uY2\n8wCoMKmscz6TTNFvXTRi2YQdhwiQmQ0Y4OBEwguiduSIwPU1Y/c6tJ6Gw9AxCSpv\nLw24dkMhwyi+nfmtxBwHJCJb0VrpZ9v6QDTahwqTfMMKYp1x9+LkeCsWiz7sLNG/\nkCpbLbunT22bDwl8CWyghEI5NFxEPQ2+2MXn6uppdI5m3VkfGBSEczuJcNcS2FeO\nTuSouduYlIDbVg9o/K1gFkg85rW/8FDI1IDJNz9D3VqIXezkT09XmiKWOnWbBzQL\nRj0VCL0ewHvCcLIUm6yNi9q6qH/5mCeSQ+wM1EP69D7z3N/o8QL1jOa65MX0KL1i\ni+QOonuFOmDA5etReJBguVLlTHhL2Dd4os1uwtj7uxzeFbiUzTP5A263yrtbdCz9\nVIgnt4r7Gp5s1KUNvGsX2OpxLQ7DcGbYqmDh6j+4oclv4lgjHHRss24xJH/x5Vgi\nT1HzDEp/NkDdqd1weXTy\n=sxEu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a4d890249aec920788f99cb5fa17bcc586e84d82\nparent 045039f341ba54fe080d0e83f04e84fdc961750b\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1780168501 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780168501 +0300\n\ndocs: fix stale API paths, tool counts, and version references (#255)\n\n## Summary\n\nCustomer-facing docs had drifted from the code. Every fix was validated\nagainst `core-api` routes, `tools/_registry`, and `config` — corrections\nto existing docs, no new content.\n\n- **Stale `/api/*` → `/api/v1/*`** — the documented calls 404 as\nwritten: `AGENT-INSTALL.md` search/memories curls;\n`integration-guide.md` `tool-descriptions`, `fleet/heartbeat`, `agents`\n(×3), `memories/bulk`. Only the plugin-bootstrap router is mounted at\nbare `/api`; everything else is `/api/v1`.\n- **Tool counts** — 12 MCP tools / 11 plugin (plugin omits the MCP-only\n`memclaw_keystones_set`), replacing stale 9/10 counts and the \"plugin\nsurfaces all 12\" line.\n- **`memclaw_evolve` trust** — `scope=agent` (default) needs trust 1,\nnot 2; `fleet`/`all` needs 2. Documented signature now includes\n`scope`/`fleet_id`.\n- **`SECURITY.md`** — report version via `GET /api/v1/version` (no\n`VERSION` file exists); supported-versions line `1.x` → `2.x`.\n- **static skill install URL** → `/api/v1/install-skill`.\n- **`README.md` rollback** — `alembic downgrade 011` (was `009`, which\nover-reverted migrations `010` + `011`).\n\n## Testing\nDoc-only; no code paths changed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-30T19:15:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/496717eeeb28cabdf07d8b690c07e2d03ac7aa2f","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/496717eeeb28cabdf07d8b690c07e2d03ac7aa2f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/496717eeeb28cabdf07d8b690c07e2d03ac7aa2f/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"045039f341ba54fe080d0e83f04e84fdc961750b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/045039f341ba54fe080d0e83f04e84fdc961750b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/045039f341ba54fe080d0e83f04e84fdc961750b"}]},{"sha":"045039f341ba54fe080d0e83f04e84fdc961750b","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDA0NTAzOWYzNDFiYTU0ZmUwODBkMGU4M2YwNGU4NGZkYzk2MTc1MGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-30T16:55:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-30T16:55:20Z"},"message":"fix(security): gateway-shared-secret gate on the X-Tenant-ID auth path (CRITICAL-1, app side) (#254)\n\n## Summary\n\nApplication-layer mitigation for the **gateway-bypass** finding\n(CRITICAL-1):\ncore-api is reachable on its public `*.run.app` URL and **Path 4 trusts\n`X-Tenant-ID` / `X-Agent-ID` / `X-Readable-Tenant-IDs` with no\ncredential of its\nown** — safe only behind the gateway. A direct caller could set those\nheaders\nand impersonate any tenant (confirmed live: a keyless `GET` with\n`X-Tenant-ID`\nreturned data).\n\n## What changed\n\n- New setting **`GATEWAY_SHARED_SECRET`**. When set, **Path 4**\nadditionally\nrequires a matching **`X-Gateway-Secret`** header (injected by the\ngateway on\nevery core-api location), checked with `hmac.compare_digest`, before\nhonoring\nthe identity headers. A direct/gateway-bypassing request lacks it →\n**401**.\n- **Surgical**: only the unauthenticated header-trust path is gated.\nAdmin-key,\n  `MEMCLAW_API_KEY`, and standalone paths are untouched. Unset secret\n  (OSS / standalone / dev) is a **no-op** — fully backward compatible.\n- Reversible (unset the env var).\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_gateway_secret_gate.py` — missing/wrong secret → 401;\ncorrect →\nresolves the tenant; unset → no-op. Full non-benchmark suite green.\n\n## Rollout (coordinated — this is one of three pieces)\n\n1. **This PR** (core-api): deploy with `GATEWAY_SHARED_SECRET` set\n(Secret\nManager) — but only **after** the gateway is sending the header, or set\nit\n   empty first.\n2. **Gateway** (enterprise, separate PR): `proxy_set_header\nX-Gateway-Secret\n   <secret>` on every core-api/auth/audit location, same secret value.\n3. Deploy order: gateway first (sending the header is harmless if\ncore-api\nignores it while the secret is unset), then set the secret on core-api.\n   Verify the live PoC (`curl https://<core-api>.run.app/api/v1/memories\n-H 'X-Tenant-ID: t'`) now returns **401**, and the gateway path still\n200s.\n\nDefense-in-depth follow-up (Option B): lock core-api ingress to internal\n+\ngive the gateway a VPC connector, so it isn't publicly reachable at all.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2749711daa94dfd480b9eeef32d486a9feadd283","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/2749711daa94dfd480b9eeef32d486a9feadd283"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/045039f341ba54fe080d0e83f04e84fdc961750b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGxZ4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgmgQAEjL1Oeb7IEbJ/7hnvPVMa9D\nANb058vxpC18iYazOhsO60BryKRwVq4RzNgvVadYOpCzlS2FSJoz3spx6zoQP9Df\np3j63Aki4kBrp0Sf9VADjUQ2VF6kP84Rlwg7GWg3Wph7dChXOSQ1BpI6dT098lfh\ncQSFu4Qo1r6QgU1tAch9Y2zO3tHYPu8cVJxfwhH+63f34cxZdY6Usy8Di6kF9mSg\n+eBHEnf3W+WBTlwifqiBtRGru8ZwA6U0RwCXG+V0SQY9AslO/+3KEnLy9+5wFrCY\n0wZPCFhr7ngjw8q84Yjr+OOoGSx/k2WMbblRTywg9axvLTGLTx+CMA5mHQxi2k3P\nMhi42h/qob09r9996I4nN6DTyG8fjVV8f7YekN8JjliadK7mxaTnrmoKZugRCAZz\nCA3ohi4DCZgN/qlOtvH0oT3autUvZLOr3SSxOEiJZib5gGIDIdY1Y1TqBkw34wGw\nEsJhwb8KuqwBW6qg/HUgByGhy49A0oxKPJlQaRWoo9tGcDOE9J5c4f0NtqnaDZ5S\ng+JyN3gYg2PgaTatUh0T1O5uYaUcGETgLU/V/26vogc2HstEcRdj4WG1wQmHlihS\nAAnsZBjOoc2/Xusv342ZJz0nLtmD6oja2NLu9S2jbSfdYIfoWe482+lygHJ5bxnL\nHoRyyU0IRWHrkhRtesKw\n=vW4J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2749711daa94dfd480b9eeef32d486a9feadd283\nparent dab6b711921a5bba568a083eb6d8c09b2545870a\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1780160120 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780160120 +0300\n\nfix(security): gateway-shared-secret gate on the X-Tenant-ID auth path (CRITICAL-1, app side) (#254)\n\n## Summary\n\nApplication-layer mitigation for the **gateway-bypass** finding\n(CRITICAL-1):\ncore-api is reachable on its public `*.run.app` URL and **Path 4 trusts\n`X-Tenant-ID` / `X-Agent-ID` / `X-Readable-Tenant-IDs` with no\ncredential of its\nown** — safe only behind the gateway. A direct caller could set those\nheaders\nand impersonate any tenant (confirmed live: a keyless `GET` with\n`X-Tenant-ID`\nreturned data).\n\n## What changed\n\n- New setting **`GATEWAY_SHARED_SECRET`**. When set, **Path 4**\nadditionally\nrequires a matching **`X-Gateway-Secret`** header (injected by the\ngateway on\nevery core-api location), checked with `hmac.compare_digest`, before\nhonoring\nthe identity headers. A direct/gateway-bypassing request lacks it →\n**401**.\n- **Surgical**: only the unauthenticated header-trust path is gated.\nAdmin-key,\n  `MEMCLAW_API_KEY`, and standalone paths are untouched. Unset secret\n  (OSS / standalone / dev) is a **no-op** — fully backward compatible.\n- Reversible (unset the env var).\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_gateway_secret_gate.py` — missing/wrong secret → 401;\ncorrect →\nresolves the tenant; unset → no-op. Full non-benchmark suite green.\n\n## Rollout (coordinated — this is one of three pieces)\n\n1. **This PR** (core-api): deploy with `GATEWAY_SHARED_SECRET` set\n(Secret\nManager) — but only **after** the gateway is sending the header, or set\nit\n   empty first.\n2. **Gateway** (enterprise, separate PR): `proxy_set_header\nX-Gateway-Secret\n   <secret>` on every core-api/auth/audit location, same secret value.\n3. Deploy order: gateway first (sending the header is harmless if\ncore-api\nignores it while the secret is unset), then set the secret on core-api.\n   Verify the live PoC (`curl https://<core-api>.run.app/api/v1/memories\n-H 'X-Tenant-ID: t'`) now returns **401**, and the gateway path still\n200s.\n\nDefense-in-depth follow-up (Option B): lock core-api ingress to internal\n+\ngive the gateway a VPC connector, so it isn't publicly reachable at all.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-30T16:55:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/045039f341ba54fe080d0e83f04e84fdc961750b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/045039f341ba54fe080d0e83f04e84fdc961750b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/045039f341ba54fe080d0e83f04e84fdc961750b/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dab6b711921a5bba568a083eb6d8c09b2545870a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dab6b711921a5bba568a083eb6d8c09b2545870a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/dab6b711921a5bba568a083eb6d8c09b2545870a"}]},{"sha":"dab6b711921a5bba568a083eb6d8c09b2545870a","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGRhYjZiNzExOTIxYTViYmE1NjhhMDgzZWI2ZDhjMDliMjU0NTg3MGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-30T16:39:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-30T16:39:56Z"},"message":"fix(security): enforce fleet/agent scope on entity reads + document deletes (#253)\n\n## Summary\n\nTwo more instances of the intra-tenant-scope class (siblings of\n#250/#251), on\nnon-memory resources, found in the second-pass audit:\n\n- **Entity side-door (BOLA):** `get_entity` returned **every linked\nmemory's\n  full content**, checking only the entity's tenant — so a peer agent's\n`scope_agent` secret or a cross-fleet row leaked **by entity id**,\nrouting\naround the `GET /memories/{id}` fix (#250). Now each linked memory is\nfiltered\n  through `authorize_memory_access`; `GET /entities/{id}` and MCP\n  `memclaw_entity_get` pass the caller identity.\n- **Document delete (BFLA):** `DELETE /documents/{id}` and MCP\n`memclaw_doc\nop=delete` gated on write-capability only — a trust-1 agent could\ndestroy\ntenant documents (customer records/configs). Now `enforce_delete` (trust\n≥ 3)\n  for agent credentials.\n\nTenant/user/admin credentials (no gateway `X-Agent-ID`) are unaffected.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_entity_doc_authz.py` — entity filters\n`scope_agent`/cross-fleet\nlinked memories for an agent and stays unfiltered for tenant creds; doc\ndelete\nis 403 for a trust-1 agent, allowed for trust-3, tenant-key unaffected.\nFull\nnon-benchmark suite green.\n\n## Remaining backlog (flagged, not in this PR)\n\nDocument **read** fleet-scoping\n(`get`/`query`/`search`/`list_collections` —\ncross-fleet doc reads for trust<2 agents) is the next increment. Plus\nthe\nnon-memory items from the audit: STM notes cross-agent (`/stm/notes`),\n`/fleet/commands` missing `enforce_tenant`, SSRF DNS-rebinding in\ningest,\nprompt-injection in recall briefs, and the gateway `/api/` catch-all\nheader\nstrip. The **CRITICAL** infra finding (core-api publicly reachable,\nbypassing\nthe gateway) is handled out-of-band — it is not a code fix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7cda2ab666b193612d4776a6f72d460e2b156fa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/7cda2ab666b193612d4776a6f72d460e2b156fa3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/dab6b711921a5bba568a083eb6d8c09b2545870a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGxLcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX8oQAA+XeSW5kftq43zbg/jNpjKL\nYWxFOGuCK1Y1+tplDa9rK/RtjE+gn2eMFVXidjtMDrQTG6D1I0oAg8Oez/RGVIyZ\nH9tBKbGEYuroY0WHFDagGCabhRFKv7UuDBEzP2lSyP5HB+JUvPM2FrLOb20benqE\n9vTH2QOR/tH2wy1WQXaB5n2oWTJ1X19oLwdiO79A/ZJEH0Q1ISfw6SZxVw17OUsV\n9MsmE1EfZH4mqtfR3CsZjlvSf71OkLqVEE0EWNrZzX8uG5X+i2ax59W0GLUYE+9k\nOk4CID14uiIeG8EFIOvw7RVEuYZSgFitoM7mus6IASJdYLU1FaehCq1SFmC/FWYP\nRvzW6LDEe5oMRm3bsdLsmejypvExxfRdBJrY3/wG5TtVV1iiOyaEdI4ZM+9gROaz\nX8eXVipQbRp75OT0xouho9Vt8/TxUdiXs7NnCHZKdkNhQjY0kZEZGaTp04VUGRXc\nIC5mlnxXNA+7WUva+4Kz83OmiJaxhR8z0LNy3NM9RSlpLz+dmId0Bphl/1MXNlQw\nh/9ilVHenTLzt7VGMMP8Uaka8bO9vlfefP4cNOsDy1HsS7oP5eAg6mdcocMe1MNo\nbbuiwkhsDX21gVk/AHDv7gVpJ20eAMsuFQajMXXm5jfmnltr2deMOuDXvCtEMHa2\nHrFGRNN2Uh3mnJOic+8C\n=uhCD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7cda2ab666b193612d4776a6f72d460e2b156fa3\nparent 8475901603d52438638bb890c562017d3ea42fa1\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1780159196 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780159196 +0300\n\nfix(security): enforce fleet/agent scope on entity reads + document deletes (#253)\n\n## Summary\n\nTwo more instances of the intra-tenant-scope class (siblings of\n#250/#251), on\nnon-memory resources, found in the second-pass audit:\n\n- **Entity side-door (BOLA):** `get_entity` returned **every linked\nmemory's\n  full content**, checking only the entity's tenant — so a peer agent's\n`scope_agent` secret or a cross-fleet row leaked **by entity id**,\nrouting\naround the `GET /memories/{id}` fix (#250). Now each linked memory is\nfiltered\n  through `authorize_memory_access`; `GET /entities/{id}` and MCP\n  `memclaw_entity_get` pass the caller identity.\n- **Document delete (BFLA):** `DELETE /documents/{id}` and MCP\n`memclaw_doc\nop=delete` gated on write-capability only — a trust-1 agent could\ndestroy\ntenant documents (customer records/configs). Now `enforce_delete` (trust\n≥ 3)\n  for agent credentials.\n\nTenant/user/admin credentials (no gateway `X-Agent-ID`) are unaffected.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_entity_doc_authz.py` — entity filters\n`scope_agent`/cross-fleet\nlinked memories for an agent and stays unfiltered for tenant creds; doc\ndelete\nis 403 for a trust-1 agent, allowed for trust-3, tenant-key unaffected.\nFull\nnon-benchmark suite green.\n\n## Remaining backlog (flagged, not in this PR)\n\nDocument **read** fleet-scoping\n(`get`/`query`/`search`/`list_collections` —\ncross-fleet doc reads for trust<2 agents) is the next increment. Plus\nthe\nnon-memory items from the audit: STM notes cross-agent (`/stm/notes`),\n`/fleet/commands` missing `enforce_tenant`, SSRF DNS-rebinding in\ningest,\nprompt-injection in recall briefs, and the gateway `/api/` catch-all\nheader\nstrip. The **CRITICAL** infra finding (core-api publicly reachable,\nbypassing\nthe gateway) is handled out-of-band — it is not a code fix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-30T16:39:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dab6b711921a5bba568a083eb6d8c09b2545870a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/dab6b711921a5bba568a083eb6d8c09b2545870a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dab6b711921a5bba568a083eb6d8c09b2545870a/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8475901603d52438638bb890c562017d3ea42fa1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8475901603d52438638bb890c562017d3ea42fa1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8475901603d52438638bb890c562017d3ea42fa1"}]},{"sha":"8475901603d52438638bb890c562017d3ea42fa1","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDg0NzU5MDE2MDNkNTI0Mzg2MzhiYjg5MGM1NjIwMTdkM2VhNDJmYTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-30T16:37:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-30T16:37:13Z"},"message":"fix(security): block agent credentials from agent-management & settings (trust self-escalation) (#252)\n\n## Summary\n\n`PATCH /agents/{id}/trust` authorized on **tenant match only** — no\nadmin/trust\ngate (the router's `tags=[\"Admin\"]` is cosmetic; it's mounted at plain\n`/api/v1`). So an **agent-scoped credential could `PATCH\n/agents/{self}/trust\n{\"trust_level\": 3}` and self-promote to admin trust**, which unlocks\nevery\ncross-fleet read/write/delete and keystone-authoring gate the trust\nladder is\nbuilt on — defeating #250 and #251. The fleet-reassignment,\npeer-agent-delete,\nand tenant-settings (`PUT /settings`, e.g. `require_agent_approval`)\nendpoints\nhad the same tenant-only gate.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`AuthContext.enforce_not_agent_credential(action)`** — blocks\nagent-scoped\ncredentials (gateway `X-Agent-ID` present) from admin-plane operations.\n  Tenant/user/admin credentials (no `X-Agent-ID`) are unaffected, so the\ndashboard/admin tooling keep working **without** depending on `org_role`\n  being plumbed on the gateway auth branch.\n- Applied to: `PATCH /agents/{id}/trust`, `PATCH /agents/{id}/fleet`,\n  `DELETE /agents/{id}`, `PUT /settings`.\n- `PATCH /agents/{id}/tune` (search profile) allows **self** (`agent_id\n==\n  caller`) but blocks tampering with a peer's profile.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_agent_admin_authz.py` — helper unit tests + API: an agent\ncredential\ngets 403 on trust/fleet/delete/settings; self-tune passes the gate while\npeer-tune is 403; admin-key control is unaffected. Full non-benchmark\nsuite green.\n\n## Context\n\nFound in a second-pass audit after #250/#251. This is the *master key*\nto the\ntrust ladder — arguably more severe than the by-id BOLA/BFLA, since it\nlets a\nlow-trust agent grant itself everything those fixes gate. A separate,\neven more\nsevere **infra** finding (core-api reachable directly on its public\nrun.app URL,\nbypassing the gateway) is being handled out-of-band — that one is not a\ncode fix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"76778690586750db1a6f7047bc7a6f289f954e60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/76778690586750db1a6f7047bc7a6f289f954e60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/8475901603d52438638bb890c562017d3ea42fa1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGxI5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARN4QAK9aZjWfAz1RQIqwwP18twvJ\nxHciqAbvHA6agU9WUNwWu7FdqULUBhiruLj/7t5fwWesaaWQMZhGYcfXPUNJ4eZX\nJXvN39AawsitM6FSeZSww4Qd94YV/pkLby+61vKepDUTuJ+hI0TRwxznKZB+823b\nHBf2i0zw0P0dFscoHklFu/9evUKAMaLH1BtLl5bzzoWV51M0pEJ5c/Qw6ACm8eYW\nMx+blMeAo1MIVdP1XJ8TVNw+N/9A+JznwnyKlOUEOMkcT4GDEPvILuyv6rV20Lon\nAmdPPpVyGTujtQSJz7zNekRq1ZXRvRtGtbSddHacW2YVGhVfDJ+6Vl1QX8As4gN4\nCvuks50ygCe5s9Zmu+551C+hBX6YPBygla4p0SvY4qig9QLaJgpoyB5hZHWNi8Y8\n5Rf37boHBg3J03yBjn4G5uAlNX8RZkBDw0RhI/l5axlDQpApSa/GcW54P1Yn6kls\nSXh6fjz34XayKzTn0Y2+dEZyII4gn34ucyV/E5M1mkIHaXaXJUvp8B90t2OFAloM\n2WFUWxgJG3kSEiNPsMXjZTNAINh++wONgfG5paIaECAAdiUJtdWT8s8Z5p46DTl/\nl6voNmxzT6i9QEuUr0DEvWcta1FSIxN86jKYkm7E98O0Gk91yV6TF8GbDbjYIzY6\ngjFPmp7ueffNjTxSVTi/\n=hEMV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 76778690586750db1a6f7047bc7a6f289f954e60\nparent 9fcac01685dee45072b809cb45d9366e63898e13\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1780159033 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780159033 +0300\n\nfix(security): block agent credentials from agent-management & settings (trust self-escalation) (#252)\n\n## Summary\n\n`PATCH /agents/{id}/trust` authorized on **tenant match only** — no\nadmin/trust\ngate (the router's `tags=[\"Admin\"]` is cosmetic; it's mounted at plain\n`/api/v1`). So an **agent-scoped credential could `PATCH\n/agents/{self}/trust\n{\"trust_level\": 3}` and self-promote to admin trust**, which unlocks\nevery\ncross-fleet read/write/delete and keystone-authoring gate the trust\nladder is\nbuilt on — defeating #250 and #251. The fleet-reassignment,\npeer-agent-delete,\nand tenant-settings (`PUT /settings`, e.g. `require_agent_approval`)\nendpoints\nhad the same tenant-only gate.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`AuthContext.enforce_not_agent_credential(action)`** — blocks\nagent-scoped\ncredentials (gateway `X-Agent-ID` present) from admin-plane operations.\n  Tenant/user/admin credentials (no `X-Agent-ID`) are unaffected, so the\ndashboard/admin tooling keep working **without** depending on `org_role`\n  being plumbed on the gateway auth branch.\n- Applied to: `PATCH /agents/{id}/trust`, `PATCH /agents/{id}/fleet`,\n  `DELETE /agents/{id}`, `PUT /settings`.\n- `PATCH /agents/{id}/tune` (search profile) allows **self** (`agent_id\n==\n  caller`) but blocks tampering with a peer's profile.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_agent_admin_authz.py` — helper unit tests + API: an agent\ncredential\ngets 403 on trust/fleet/delete/settings; self-tune passes the gate while\npeer-tune is 403; admin-key control is unaffected. Full non-benchmark\nsuite green.\n\n## Context\n\nFound in a second-pass audit after #250/#251. This is the *master key*\nto the\ntrust ladder — arguably more severe than the by-id BOLA/BFLA, since it\nlets a\nlow-trust agent grant itself everything those fixes gate. A separate,\neven more\nsevere **infra** finding (core-api reachable directly on its public\nrun.app URL,\nbypassing the gateway) is being handled out-of-band — that one is not a\ncode fix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-30T16:37:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8475901603d52438638bb890c562017d3ea42fa1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8475901603d52438638bb890c562017d3ea42fa1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8475901603d52438638bb890c562017d3ea42fa1/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9fcac01685dee45072b809cb45d9366e63898e13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9fcac01685dee45072b809cb45d9366e63898e13","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9fcac01685dee45072b809cb45d9366e63898e13"}]},{"sha":"9fcac01685dee45072b809cb45d9366e63898e13","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDlmY2FjMDE2ODVkZWU0NTA3MmI4MDljYjQ1ZDkzNjZlNjM4OThlMTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-30T12:29:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-30T12:29:18Z"},"message":"fix(security): require admin-trust for bulk/whole-tenant memory deletes (#251)\n\n## Summary\n\nDestroy-side sibling of #250. The bulk-delete endpoints authorized on\n**write\ncapability + tenant match only** — no trust check — so a routine trust-1\nagent\ncredential could soft-delete an entire fleet or the whole tenant in one\ncall\n(broken function-level authorization). Same root cause as #250: the\ntenant is\nthe only enforced boundary; the intra-tenant trust ladder wasn't applied\nhere.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`delete_all_memories`** (`DELETE /memories`) and\n**`bulk_delete_by_ids`**\n(`POST /memories/bulk-delete`): when the caller is an **agent\ncredential**\n(gateway `X-Agent-ID` present), require **admin-trust (≥ 3)** via the\nexisting\n`enforce_delete` — the same gate as single-delete (#250) and the trust\nladder.\n- **Tenant/user credentials** (no `X-Agent-ID` → the tenant owner) keep\nfull\nreach, so dashboard reset and the load-test tagged cleanup are\nunchanged.\n- Deny-only — can only reject more requests; no data-loss/corruption\nrisk.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_memory_byid_authz.py` (+3): trust-1 agent blocked (403) on\nboth\nendpoints, trust-3 agent allowed, tenant-key control unchanged (204).\nFull\nnon-benchmark suite green (pre-existing unrelated `google-cloud-pubsub`\nimport failures aside).\n\n## Note for reviewers\n\nThis closes the demonstrated path (a trust-1 *agent* key). An optional\ndefense-in-depth — requiring org-admin even for a *tenant* key's\n*unfiltered*\nwhole-tenant purge — is deliberately **not** included here because it\nneeds\n`org_role` plumbed on the `X-Tenant-ID` auth branch and would change\ndashboard\n\"reset tenant\" behavior. Flagging as a follow-up decision rather than\nbundling\na UX/contract change into a security hotfix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c657253d3d7c7081722dffeb4f477ad88f7f5ddd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/c657253d3d7c7081722dffeb4f477ad88f7f5ddd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/9fcac01685dee45072b809cb45d9366e63898e13","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGtgeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjewQAHJR9wtju2SZENh2oUu7Mf7s\neJD20lGywJpQXzWkNlxxqNmgu9VOwxhFkjm9kD1FP/g/1DcPVT8lmgpU10D6yOuV\n/knNjwf5mcQhYw0Yxn2wDxUmi6bGsyl7xMCEuKX8n5XakY8bCsERyWY3NQZHtyQi\nhoD33rw/8qE/FI0DAgmK1QsKLnPuWKLJq+yg3kM5GiJlvOlfceeuNzH68i63j+LB\n6VOqL/TMAugaFpMop8MtWeCKBx+pDxFU3/LODHF001FiXGzyt2WMRPeaAXgK0jAV\nSOCkukTp/XC//ebVR+63WQV4R7RH5Cykg8l3DH+xa1PGGV9PfOVSceauQ/bwp29b\nAgdeLuJeph/SvrzUGfl/N2wanT8RjtezokOebkr/StDEahdu5ABMRzR9hBqPBvCV\nob6zwvOPCisjvFzRwbgMYFIwsCD6yPmxm90fvCRp/XIfe3+CZYPx/yi5qYlNiO/X\nFYLFnvKGvI2hWCTeTsIgyWT+JdUPeS1zs8QAJFiNZHVXHmK8S3CM+AtRNeeJi9JY\nYHudUJK5QcNiSsLHWRzohYQVbhvDBGTZZTTJlNOfmTgbc03fXjSfyphUKoiRc/1Q\nIg6we4gd/JY+r8y6j+bxv8+JwNXk3viS1CypKsAYPQ9/z57ugmUv7zb6NF8SgB7S\nmE8vd04wuxHwgRWRVbYc\n=GX7d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c657253d3d7c7081722dffeb4f477ad88f7f5ddd\nparent fde5cebe569e1fdb5c7cab101d60a4bc857719a8\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1780144158 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780144158 +0300\n\nfix(security): require admin-trust for bulk/whole-tenant memory deletes (#251)\n\n## Summary\n\nDestroy-side sibling of #250. The bulk-delete endpoints authorized on\n**write\ncapability + tenant match only** — no trust check — so a routine trust-1\nagent\ncredential could soft-delete an entire fleet or the whole tenant in one\ncall\n(broken function-level authorization). Same root cause as #250: the\ntenant is\nthe only enforced boundary; the intra-tenant trust ladder wasn't applied\nhere.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`delete_all_memories`** (`DELETE /memories`) and\n**`bulk_delete_by_ids`**\n(`POST /memories/bulk-delete`): when the caller is an **agent\ncredential**\n(gateway `X-Agent-ID` present), require **admin-trust (≥ 3)** via the\nexisting\n`enforce_delete` — the same gate as single-delete (#250) and the trust\nladder.\n- **Tenant/user credentials** (no `X-Agent-ID` → the tenant owner) keep\nfull\nreach, so dashboard reset and the load-test tagged cleanup are\nunchanged.\n- Deny-only — can only reject more requests; no data-loss/corruption\nrisk.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_memory_byid_authz.py` (+3): trust-1 agent blocked (403) on\nboth\nendpoints, trust-3 agent allowed, tenant-key control unchanged (204).\nFull\nnon-benchmark suite green (pre-existing unrelated `google-cloud-pubsub`\nimport failures aside).\n\n## Note for reviewers\n\nThis closes the demonstrated path (a trust-1 *agent* key). An optional\ndefense-in-depth — requiring org-admin even for a *tenant* key's\n*unfiltered*\nwhole-tenant purge — is deliberately **not** included here because it\nneeds\n`org_role` plumbed on the `X-Tenant-ID` auth branch and would change\ndashboard\n\"reset tenant\" behavior. Flagging as a follow-up decision rather than\nbundling\na UX/contract change into a security hotfix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-30T12:29:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9fcac01685dee45072b809cb45d9366e63898e13","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9fcac01685dee45072b809cb45d9366e63898e13","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9fcac01685dee45072b809cb45d9366e63898e13/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fde5cebe569e1fdb5c7cab101d60a4bc857719a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fde5cebe569e1fdb5c7cab101d60a4bc857719a8","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fde5cebe569e1fdb5c7cab101d60a4bc857719a8"}]},{"sha":"fde5cebe569e1fdb5c7cab101d60a4bc857719a8","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGZkZTVjZWJlNTY5ZTFmZGI1YzdjYWIxMDFkNjBhNGJjODU3NzE5YTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-30T06:50:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-30T06:50:02Z"},"message":"fix(security): enforce fleet/agent scope on by-id memory access (#250)\n\n## Summary\n\nBy-id memory handlers authorized on `tenant_id` alone, while the\nlist/search\npaths additionally enforce `scope_agent` ownership and the cross-fleet\ntrust\nladder. This change brings the by-id surface in line with that contract\nso a\nsingle shared check governs every access path.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **New `agent_service.authorize_memory_access` (+\n`enforce_memory_read`)** —\n  the single fleet/visibility contract shared by every by-id handler.\n  `caller_agent_id is None` (a tenant/user credential with no gateway\n`X-Agent-ID`) keeps full tenant access, so the dashboard is unchanged;\nonly\nagent-scoped credentials are constrained. The identity used is always\nthe\n  authenticated one (`auth.agent_id` / `_get_agent_id()`), never a\n  caller-supplied parameter.\n- **Reads** (`GET /memories/{id}`, `.../contradictions`, MCP\n`read`/`lineage`)\n  → 404 when out of scope (mirrors how list/search simply omit the row).\n- **Writes** (`DELETE`, `PATCH /status`, `PATCH`, MCP\n  `transition`/`update`/`delete`/`bulk_delete`) → 403, via the existing\n  trust ladder.\n- **`/search` and MCP `recall`** fall back to the authenticated agent\nfor\n  fleet-forcing + `enforce_fleet_read` + visibility scoping when\n`filter_agent_id` is omitted (these paths return content, so scope\nmatters\n  there too).\n- **`list_memories`** uses the authenticated identity for\nvisibility/fleet\n  scoping; the `?agent_id=` query param remains only the author filter.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_memory_byid_authz.py` — 18 tests: unit matrix on the helper,\nthe MCP `read` surface, and REST integration (cross-fleet denied/allowed\nby\ntrust, scope_agent author-only, and a no-agent dashboard regression\nguard).\nFull non-benchmark suite passes locally (pre-existing, unrelated\n`google-cloud-pubsub` import failures aside).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Behavior for tenant/user (dashboard) credentials is unchanged.\n- Error code on read denial is 404 by design (avoids confirming a row\nexists\n  outside the caller's scope).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"97bfbd81b26fc2370d80f5f7adc0b8fc08f2f20f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/97bfbd81b26fc2370d80f5f7adc0b8fc08f2f20f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/fde5cebe569e1fdb5c7cab101d60a4bc857719a8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGoiaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2YcQAKfU/24Nkaa20NadzakgdFDH\nsMfn1MUdCIOVGFaxK84rtxUsOxylTuh8DH40o1vwFG1BnF/2itoiAag0GbvqLfOi\nUandQQna1LHTX/vwNyKEM67TuXFVZs5KmTE+W4ovs0ZDP4xSOOgU+k7jfqkvd8sH\ngQpcRefV+zQdRVmHSi7FHVGBmi1o2kDziZe95gDiXi69/pDF6bG658XesxhyxIF0\nPH1sV2ixjBsHqGHPfib7ZKdD7hhnbYb4aJHAmJRzc42HH6j2TmgfQWGQamxj4hXV\nqEKJK9gt1AKKLwSHL6WsXMFuPd0a/hSY1QIppHZpcW9CMkW83wfBGih43Z1YQJLA\nRFc9XW01NQg4bG2aOcAqz7HcsD35+s7Mi9yvwzQkzFunSiFF395sGaCAGR6z1ij+\nq7ZcTTRuNKF0Uev+Hv7xKBTFt3s3cgoPPvTVEUPnOfMiso9UKeWTNzi4JX3yLTLV\nDEibNow/A81w6vn/BWRO8nL2sD2i1ZShVeg8oPRLFkMHbiFV1QNlZ21UUybpQ14j\nsdSLz/CSpDkYW/BnoBvaiLGFwSHYfJuc8ATeakErrjDXFXmRqulagJZwoJs4OH0+\n3KBMuA5CrOuGihuWZOigBCE9yjVXz1tv5o/A2/PWxtplLXqNHGHa7t810GYRYvyc\nD5ngJ4pFHR/EKUiBrmJx\n=qxHW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 97bfbd81b26fc2370d80f5f7adc0b8fc08f2f20f\nparent 9925ec209fece7243b1a467ed3865bc7d8ae0646\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1780123802 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780123802 +0300\n\nfix(security): enforce fleet/agent scope on by-id memory access (#250)\n\n## Summary\n\nBy-id memory handlers authorized on `tenant_id` alone, while the\nlist/search\npaths additionally enforce `scope_agent` ownership and the cross-fleet\ntrust\nladder. This change brings the by-id surface in line with that contract\nso a\nsingle shared check governs every access path.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **New `agent_service.authorize_memory_access` (+\n`enforce_memory_read`)** —\n  the single fleet/visibility contract shared by every by-id handler.\n  `caller_agent_id is None` (a tenant/user credential with no gateway\n`X-Agent-ID`) keeps full tenant access, so the dashboard is unchanged;\nonly\nagent-scoped credentials are constrained. The identity used is always\nthe\n  authenticated one (`auth.agent_id` / `_get_agent_id()`), never a\n  caller-supplied parameter.\n- **Reads** (`GET /memories/{id}`, `.../contradictions`, MCP\n`read`/`lineage`)\n  → 404 when out of scope (mirrors how list/search simply omit the row).\n- **Writes** (`DELETE`, `PATCH /status`, `PATCH`, MCP\n  `transition`/`update`/`delete`/`bulk_delete`) → 403, via the existing\n  trust ladder.\n- **`/search` and MCP `recall`** fall back to the authenticated agent\nfor\n  fleet-forcing + `enforce_fleet_read` + visibility scoping when\n`filter_agent_id` is omitted (these paths return content, so scope\nmatters\n  there too).\n- **`list_memories`** uses the authenticated identity for\nvisibility/fleet\n  scoping; the `?agent_id=` query param remains only the author filter.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_memory_byid_authz.py` — 18 tests: unit matrix on the helper,\nthe MCP `read` surface, and REST integration (cross-fleet denied/allowed\nby\ntrust, scope_agent author-only, and a no-agent dashboard regression\nguard).\nFull non-benchmark suite passes locally (pre-existing, unrelated\n`google-cloud-pubsub` import failures aside).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Behavior for tenant/user (dashboard) credentials is unchanged.\n- Error code on read denial is 404 by design (avoids confirming a row\nexists\n  outside the caller's scope).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-30T06:50:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fde5cebe569e1fdb5c7cab101d60a4bc857719a8","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fde5cebe569e1fdb5c7cab101d60a4bc857719a8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fde5cebe569e1fdb5c7cab101d60a4bc857719a8/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9925ec209fece7243b1a467ed3865bc7d8ae0646","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9925ec209fece7243b1a467ed3865bc7d8ae0646","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9925ec209fece7243b1a467ed3865bc7d8ae0646"}]},{"sha":"9925ec209fece7243b1a467ed3865bc7d8ae0646","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDk5MjVlYzIwOWZlY2U3MjQzYjFhNDY3ZWQzODY1YmM3ZDhhZTA2NDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-28T19:38:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T19:38:40Z"},"message":"ci(plugin): wire check:version script into CI (CAURA-000 follow-up) (#248)\n\n## Summary\n\nFollow-up to PR #247. The `scripts/gen-version.sh` header documents that\n\"CI also runs `npm run check:version` to fail fast if version.ts ever\ndrifts from package.json\" — but the script itself was not an npm entry\nand there was no CI step to invoke it. This PR closes both gaps.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`plugin/package.json`**: new `check:version` script (one line, no\nnew deps). Uses `grep -qF` for an exact-literal match on `PLUGIN_VERSION\n= \"<version>\"` in `src/version.ts`. Stricter than a substring check —\npasses only when the literal assignment is present.\n- **`.github/workflows/ci.yml`**: two new steps right after\n`actions/checkout`:\n1. `actions/setup-node@49933ea5288caeca8642d1e84afbd3f7d6820020`\n(v4.4.0, SHA-pinned matching the existing workflow's style).\n  2. `cd plugin && npm run check:version`.\n  \nPlaced before `Install uv` so a version drift fails fast without paying\nthe Python-deps install cost.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm run check:version` (in-sync) → `check:version ok: 2.6.5`,\nexit 0.\n- [x] Synthetic drift (`sed s/2.6.5/2.6.4/ src/version.ts`) →\n`version.ts out of sync with package.json (2.6.5): run bash\n../scripts/gen-version.sh`, exit 1.\n- [x] YAML validity confirmed (`python3 -c \"import yaml;\nyaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/ci.yml'))\"`); 18 steps total, new\nNode steps at positions 2-3.\n- [ ] CI run on this PR exercises the new step against a known-in-sync\nstate (should pass).\n\nNo code changes. Pure tooling.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8cf2349d24045e8378fded62689ab73fb7219f2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/8cf2349d24045e8378fded62689ab73fb7219f2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/9925ec209fece7243b1a467ed3865bc7d8ae0646","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGJnACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqpkQAEswlSFJQmU5RaClsqdPyO12\nhY4XJqcnc+ipaTPs/zCQZqE0DDG86twDAjCAYQ9Z0B82QPpTrJOgghRb3V7cd6gr\nIQ/zkXAb1X/B6+dbG+H/YBqyDM71qGxe4tQWSYh//gKO4SJu8NqB8MCxjy++UE+Q\npS3Dd21gS4mneKYKHMc7y18c0qsQIQJUZLISPOacPUOXgX7tOQmp7M0hLl5ZVxm+\nDMIJ47ttsFAx8dEIr7kDaXRYGDNzwL9fHT9EApi2Bt2wcGFThoBQi22jkISExKUJ\nAYNeRk0JjgeXDprZGT31FtJElCOqDhbCol3Ki1hwP3W92xNiR4saz1+zIQaYor7M\nKE/pCCtGlJdU+JJi2HQUYKYmOpRiU4oxDQmi3IhKtTBAiY9ii9+lHTAIs3FbGyLH\nyChoAMwKFF0mN0sWmN6F6cYH6cJB3dlhilV4+4TagZkIyseU8CDHuBi+xCsTdCKY\nu8XhyUSCuNQvujyD26/84xRiLwP5BsijQSjxUgaLr4z335J0/E3XCs9uLelnyqDy\nRmhxIu8u1RR6Pq6vcZvDK2enjVwRuBgAyqV2kuSG0kISJza9b+djtaJhnNfCEYoR\nWDL2m3sitC+9deYwvCLZa1AKCXiWbhl2w7loTVsWH+zI+F67oKfHXqQt3EGQ7J03\nvA9OemEjyXI7MmC7L8eN\n=4efg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8cf2349d24045e8378fded62689ab73fb7219f2d\nparent 6c3b021e4e011e1d1ada5e811b4e3ca68065e615\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1779997120 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779997120 +0300\n\nci(plugin): wire check:version script into CI (CAURA-000 follow-up) (#248)\n\n## Summary\n\nFollow-up to PR #247. The `scripts/gen-version.sh` header documents that\n\"CI also runs `npm run check:version` to fail fast if version.ts ever\ndrifts from package.json\" — but the script itself was not an npm entry\nand there was no CI step to invoke it. This PR closes both gaps.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`plugin/package.json`**: new `check:version` script (one line, no\nnew deps). Uses `grep -qF` for an exact-literal match on `PLUGIN_VERSION\n= \"<version>\"` in `src/version.ts`. Stricter than a substring check —\npasses only when the literal assignment is present.\n- **`.github/workflows/ci.yml`**: two new steps right after\n`actions/checkout`:\n1. `actions/setup-node@49933ea5288caeca8642d1e84afbd3f7d6820020`\n(v4.4.0, SHA-pinned matching the existing workflow's style).\n  2. `cd plugin && npm run check:version`.\n  \nPlaced before `Install uv` so a version drift fails fast without paying\nthe Python-deps install cost.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm run check:version` (in-sync) → `check:version ok: 2.6.5`,\nexit 0.\n- [x] Synthetic drift (`sed s/2.6.5/2.6.4/ src/version.ts`) →\n`version.ts out of sync with package.json (2.6.5): run bash\n../scripts/gen-version.sh`, exit 1.\n- [x] YAML validity confirmed (`python3 -c \"import yaml;\nyaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/ci.yml'))\"`); 18 steps total, new\nNode steps at positions 2-3.\n- [ ] CI run on this PR exercises the new step against a known-in-sync\nstate (should pass).\n\nNo code changes. Pure tooling.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T19:38:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9925ec209fece7243b1a467ed3865bc7d8ae0646","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9925ec209fece7243b1a467ed3865bc7d8ae0646","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9925ec209fece7243b1a467ed3865bc7d8ae0646/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6c3b021e4e011e1d1ada5e811b4e3ca68065e615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6c3b021e4e011e1d1ada5e811b4e3ca68065e615","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6c3b021e4e011e1d1ada5e811b4e3ca68065e615"}]},{"sha":"6c3b021e4e011e1d1ada5e811b4e3ca68065e615","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDZjM2IwMjFlNGUwMTFlMWQxYWRhNWU4MTFiNGUzY2E2ODA2NWU2MTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-28T19:23:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T19:23:38Z"},"message":"feat(plugin): bump MEMCLAW_KEYSTONES_TOKEN_CAP default 500 → 1500 (CAURA-000) (#249)\n\n## Summary\n\nCustomer escalation 2026-05-28: BankingClaw agent reports the\n`<keystone_rules>` block in its system prompt is being truncated every\nturn. Of 16 keystone rules in their tenant, only 12 are injected — the\nprompt ends with `... (4 more rules omitted)`.\n\nRoot cause: `MEMCLAW_KEYSTONES_TOKEN_CAP` defaults to **500 tokens**\n(~2000 chars). With ~120 chars/rule + header/footer overhead, only 12\nrules fit. The 500-token default predates the contextEngine-slot work\n(PR #212/234/247) — it was set when in-prompt keystone injection was\nexperimental. Now that keystones are a stable per-turn feature, and\nmodern context windows start at 200k+ tokens, 500 is overcautious.\n\n## Change\n\nSingle literal: `plugin/src/env.ts:269` `500` → `1500`. Doc comment\nupdated to explain the new headroom (~20-30 rules at ~120 chars each)\nand reference CAURA-000 for the precedent.\n\n## Tests\n\n`plugin/src/env.test.ts` — new `env.ts default-value source pins`\ndescribe block. Reads the source file and asserts the\n`_readIntEnv(\"MEMCLAW_KEYSTONES_TOKEN_CAP\", N, ...)` call has `N ===\n1500`. **Source-file** (not runtime) pin because `keystones.test.ts:26`\noverrides the env var at module-load time and `node --test` shares\nprocess env across files — a runtime read could see the polluted value.\nError message in the assertion points future maintainers at the\ncustomer-impact reasoning so accidental refactor reverts fail loudly.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` — **262/262 pass** (261 prior + 1 new source-pin).\n- [x] `npx tsc --noEmit` clean.\n- [x] Existing `keystones.test.ts:26` override still exercises\ntruncation logic at cap=120 explicitly — no regression of the truncation\nalgorithm itself, only the default ceiling.\n- [ ] Customer post-upgrade: ask the agent `Search your system prompt\nfor \"<keystone_rules>\" — paste the count of bullets and any \"N more\nrules omitted\" line` — should report 16 bullets, no truncation line.\n\n## Customer mitigation pending publish\n\n`MEMCLAW_KEYSTONES_TOKEN_CAP=1500` in `~/.openclaw/plugins/memclaw/.env`\n+ restart gives them the same result today without waiting for a\nrelease.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9c4636d618d9ef945e73368042d20c2b6941c58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a9c4636d618d9ef945e73368042d20c2b6941c58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/6c3b021e4e011e1d1ada5e811b4e3ca68065e615","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGJY6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARHsQAEJtRkvJvKvL0FJNYyd2Z+WH\n82cvA3+MWRk5YpLhq0uX1bjFxHiHeh9sUoaK0uvKIw1ofPKEd572wp0AD5XO8xfb\nGTPDwqQrOWR6hyzzzcmvamYkF011iIRHK3YO/Mq3Spcqt5GTx3fHciA+hayjBPBm\nTnE9pe+aHZa5biZ4F3RAUTMJKi++5lbMi7OzLdZHeAW6h0T94fc387BU7naaT8M/\n0xpF60y3FLWzYF9paAobLuU9h3eTEwhMFwj1uj/qaPWy8rAlkKLQ1xdUiriZSMSK\naX79Q8eN9lvXwrLSuiwPXIM0UUhcuGJ/fWoZVShQ0yujGrwjpFdwf8ZCbRR+VQs9\ntCLQfSCC9KO4n/yz+4ANsYJzqOG3kyI2zgs9Du8BzvCxnBd8g91n70J1GU6iXHuY\nczvOQ5+TODOXnFxNM5BS8vxVMzgiv4jf1HlmBmH3rUNNX3VIuJOzzrYuiF+scIhS\ncjkrhUyQ1I16cwnxt+6cvcZjLjtSmv84JUwyuQtD9sk+4d4kNxlJrxbaaSyAxcEj\npOh/AW86z3mBYWGCdIlbSZgaeGIvIPoDXpPAeCYfMJeGhpl5Jf0Nx+3+hZo8q7PY\nCozILYojqN2Y8cjB2lzT2rkv0kVtzfqN888GjYs6ev2rxbRcSOlvT1J7KaRysA75\n2BIP/P8XTWUR50sypyFa\n=3Vby\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a9c4636d618d9ef945e73368042d20c2b6941c58\nparent 78e10fb3cc21021883798d43d8e09f55bb33890d\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1779996218 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779996218 +0300\n\nfeat(plugin): bump MEMCLAW_KEYSTONES_TOKEN_CAP default 500 → 1500 (CAURA-000) (#249)\n\n## Summary\n\nCustomer escalation 2026-05-28: BankingClaw agent reports the\n`<keystone_rules>` block in its system prompt is being truncated every\nturn. Of 16 keystone rules in their tenant, only 12 are injected — the\nprompt ends with `... (4 more rules omitted)`.\n\nRoot cause: `MEMCLAW_KEYSTONES_TOKEN_CAP` defaults to **500 tokens**\n(~2000 chars). With ~120 chars/rule + header/footer overhead, only 12\nrules fit. The 500-token default predates the contextEngine-slot work\n(PR #212/234/247) — it was set when in-prompt keystone injection was\nexperimental. Now that keystones are a stable per-turn feature, and\nmodern context windows start at 200k+ tokens, 500 is overcautious.\n\n## Change\n\nSingle literal: `plugin/src/env.ts:269` `500` → `1500`. Doc comment\nupdated to explain the new headroom (~20-30 rules at ~120 chars each)\nand reference CAURA-000 for the precedent.\n\n## Tests\n\n`plugin/src/env.test.ts` — new `env.ts default-value source pins`\ndescribe block. Reads the source file and asserts the\n`_readIntEnv(\"MEMCLAW_KEYSTONES_TOKEN_CAP\", N, ...)` call has `N ===\n1500`. **Source-file** (not runtime) pin because `keystones.test.ts:26`\noverrides the env var at module-load time and `node --test` shares\nprocess env across files — a runtime read could see the polluted value.\nError message in the assertion points future maintainers at the\ncustomer-impact reasoning so accidental refactor reverts fail loudly.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` — **262/262 pass** (261 prior + 1 new source-pin).\n- [x] `npx tsc --noEmit` clean.\n- [x] Existing `keystones.test.ts:26` override still exercises\ntruncation logic at cap=120 explicitly — no regression of the truncation\nalgorithm itself, only the default ceiling.\n- [ ] Customer post-upgrade: ask the agent `Search your system prompt\nfor \"<keystone_rules>\" — paste the count of bullets and any \"N more\nrules omitted\" line` — should report 16 bullets, no truncation line.\n\n## Customer mitigation pending publish\n\n`MEMCLAW_KEYSTONES_TOKEN_CAP=1500` in `~/.openclaw/plugins/memclaw/.env`\n+ restart gives them the same result today without waiting for a\nrelease.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T19:23:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6c3b021e4e011e1d1ada5e811b4e3ca68065e615","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6c3b021e4e011e1d1ada5e811b4e3ca68065e615","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6c3b021e4e011e1d1ada5e811b4e3ca68065e615/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"78e10fb3cc21021883798d43d8e09f55bb33890d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/78e10fb3cc21021883798d43d8e09f55bb33890d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/78e10fb3cc21021883798d43d8e09f55bb33890d"}]},{"sha":"78e10fb3cc21021883798d43d8e09f55bb33890d","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDc4ZTEwZmIzY2MyMTAyMTg4Mzc5OGQ0M2Q4ZTA5ZjU1YmIzMzg5MGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-28T18:34:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T18:34:16Z"},"message":"fix(plugin): tolerate undefined config in ContextEngine constructor (CAURA-000) (#247)\n\n## Summary\n\n**Follow-up hotfix to PR #234.** Customer escalation 2026-05-28 surfaced\na *second* class of regression on the same deployment — a different\nagent (`dbaclaw`) hit:\n\n```\n[memclaw] assemble: unexpected error (returning safe fallback)\nTypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'tenantId')\n    at getTenantPrefix (...context-engine.js:29:19)\n    at getSessionKey   (...context-engine.js:32:26)\n    at _assembleInner  (...context-engine.js:519:28)\n    at MemClawContextEngine.assemble (...context-engine.js:452:20)\n    at invokeWithLegacyCompat (registry-hc1-G3yP.js:103:10)\n    at Object.mutableAgent.transformContext (model-context-tokens-z5hvDVkk.js:2679:22)\n```\n\nThe outer try/catch from PR #212 caught it — no gateway crash, no wedge\n— but every turn that hit this path silently bypassed keystones, recall,\nand afterTurn. **Behavioral degradation with no user-visible symptom.**\n\n## Root cause\n\n`getTenantPrefix(config)` accessed `config.tenantId` with no nullish\nguard. The throw means `this.config === undefined` inside the engine\ninstance. Validation against OpenClaw 2026.5.4 source\n(`registry-DFFgCbcm.js:241-289 resolveContextEngine`) confirmed the\nstandard factory call always passes a populated `factoryCtx` — so the\nbug doesn't repro on upstream 2026.5.4. The customer's bundle hash\n(`registry-hc1-G3yP.js`) differs from upstream (`registry-DFFgCbcm.js`);\nlikely a custom build whose legacy-compat invocation path reaches our\nfactory with `undefined`. Regardless of the upstream cause, the fix is\nuncontroversial: tolerate the input.\n\n## Fix (3 surgical edits)\n\n1. **Constructor coerces `undefined` / `null` → `{}`**:\n   ```typescript\n   constructor(config: Record<string, unknown> | undefined | null) {\n     this.config = config ?? {};\n   }\n   ```\n2. **`getTenantPrefix` optional-chains**: `config?.tenantId ||\nMEMCLAW_TENANT_ID || \"default\"`.\n3. **`getSessionKey` matches**: same widened signature + optional chains\n+ adapter for the already-tolerant `resolveAgentId`.\n\n## What's untouched\n\nPR #234's compaction-delegation work — `compact()`,\n`openclaw-sdk-bridge`, `info.ownsCompaction: true` — all unchanged. This\nhotfix only touches the pre-compaction assemble entry helpers.\n\n## Tests (`runtime-contract.test.ts`)\n\nNew `MemClawContextEngine.constructor — undefined-config tolerance`\ndescribe block with 2 tests:\n- `new MemClawContextEngine(undefined)` → `assemble` returns populated\n`AssembleResult` with `systemPromptAddition.length > 0`. The length\nassertion specifically distinguishes \"helpers worked through to the\ninner success path\" from \"helpers threw but outer try/catch caught it.\"\n- `new MemClawContextEngine(null)` — same tolerance, defense-in-depth.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` in `plugin/` — **261/261 pass** (259 prior + 2 new).\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_plugin_source_manifest.py` — **11/11 pass** (no\nnew src files, just edits).\n- [x] `npx tsc --noEmit` clean.\n- [x] Compiled dist verified — line 35 has `config?.tenantId`,\nconstructor has `?? {}` coercion.\n- [ ] Customer post-deploy: `journalctl --user | grep \"memclaw\\]\nassemble: unexpected error\" | tail -5` returns empty (was firing\nrepeatedly pre-fix).\n\n## Version\n\n2.6.3 → **2.6.5**. The 2.6.4 number is taken by PR #234's published\nartifact (already running on the customer's machine); release-please\nreverted `package.json` on main back to 2.6.3 (commit `fd253f76`) as\npart of its release-management workflow, so bumping from main's current\n2.6.3 to 2.6.4 would collide. **2.6.5 gives the customer an unambiguous\nversion string to verify the deploy.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"016e6b261fd30af9db11aab4f86bce05a7584904","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/016e6b261fd30af9db11aab4f86bce05a7584904"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/78e10fb3cc21021883798d43d8e09f55bb33890d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGIqoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5AAQAHnXAUMPFZNpHYEYGAjM0cE4\nATZjnfPPqsFne8CIS3aVnLGxj+vhb7zZSLB3qkjetc0S87lVskhqx6r9R9oRmMvW\nXmcI+TxpWfYVv9azluXRQXYCt1w9WU9Sm/NBr8ywj1b/tleWx59Msy6TOvpCCibA\nPVFvL473OGY7SWgRZkWUpieCb4IX2aAU4gzEhvx6NxUhyaQLCzHxONPW89Ayf51e\nRnyyV85OEt4agilaeEYwdqNOsrKPCkk7baf+UbC3TXjJ7Q8TiVuf4JC3YFNLm5Mn\nJY8b1Gba7H6etP3D3n6SXwmuX50tD0RcAypBHFA6lIKqkL3V/WFglss4oGh/k2PR\n88wyfLqShJRWb4QLpblqUd9FG2LckyVo4s2+GzNwgDO7QJ9TS2BFAwaT9HQsdPyv\nPUb3WupSuyQ1r18AgfzPWiLjECPtQFjaX19p8n1dMCdA5j+SaLUhQRXEwmRsDM4/\nu5H5yqxE+tzE0I0BfEKN4/KkcvEl/+D9Oq937F5Koq/i7vUcvJAiNB67ZenqNd/1\nDnJBRHAK0uvlfJ2a9m5JKL/k//UBchqqst53Zq5+ne77CTa5YgGbfoZUffAuJXmm\ndihRCdy3++ppQxIleTC68Fryp9pnzlJxgBmwV/8uhM1VJP6Vq+CS28jUPel/3ii0\n071SX9mm5eepIvRLrEBf\n=0Zs9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 016e6b261fd30af9db11aab4f86bce05a7584904\nparent e2d805e8b80aa24ba22312e4c9ee35b6381c56ce\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1779993256 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779993256 +0300\n\nfix(plugin): tolerate undefined config in ContextEngine constructor (CAURA-000) (#247)\n\n## Summary\n\n**Follow-up hotfix to PR #234.** Customer escalation 2026-05-28 surfaced\na *second* class of regression on the same deployment — a different\nagent (`dbaclaw`) hit:\n\n```\n[memclaw] assemble: unexpected error (returning safe fallback)\nTypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'tenantId')\n    at getTenantPrefix (...context-engine.js:29:19)\n    at getSessionKey   (...context-engine.js:32:26)\n    at _assembleInner  (...context-engine.js:519:28)\n    at MemClawContextEngine.assemble (...context-engine.js:452:20)\n    at invokeWithLegacyCompat (registry-hc1-G3yP.js:103:10)\n    at Object.mutableAgent.transformContext (model-context-tokens-z5hvDVkk.js:2679:22)\n```\n\nThe outer try/catch from PR #212 caught it — no gateway crash, no wedge\n— but every turn that hit this path silently bypassed keystones, recall,\nand afterTurn. **Behavioral degradation with no user-visible symptom.**\n\n## Root cause\n\n`getTenantPrefix(config)` accessed `config.tenantId` with no nullish\nguard. The throw means `this.config === undefined` inside the engine\ninstance. Validation against OpenClaw 2026.5.4 source\n(`registry-DFFgCbcm.js:241-289 resolveContextEngine`) confirmed the\nstandard factory call always passes a populated `factoryCtx` — so the\nbug doesn't repro on upstream 2026.5.4. The customer's bundle hash\n(`registry-hc1-G3yP.js`) differs from upstream (`registry-DFFgCbcm.js`);\nlikely a custom build whose legacy-compat invocation path reaches our\nfactory with `undefined`. Regardless of the upstream cause, the fix is\nuncontroversial: tolerate the input.\n\n## Fix (3 surgical edits)\n\n1. **Constructor coerces `undefined` / `null` → `{}`**:\n   ```typescript\n   constructor(config: Record<string, unknown> | undefined | null) {\n     this.config = config ?? {};\n   }\n   ```\n2. **`getTenantPrefix` optional-chains**: `config?.tenantId ||\nMEMCLAW_TENANT_ID || \"default\"`.\n3. **`getSessionKey` matches**: same widened signature + optional chains\n+ adapter for the already-tolerant `resolveAgentId`.\n\n## What's untouched\n\nPR #234's compaction-delegation work — `compact()`,\n`openclaw-sdk-bridge`, `info.ownsCompaction: true` — all unchanged. This\nhotfix only touches the pre-compaction assemble entry helpers.\n\n## Tests (`runtime-contract.test.ts`)\n\nNew `MemClawContextEngine.constructor — undefined-config tolerance`\ndescribe block with 2 tests:\n- `new MemClawContextEngine(undefined)` → `assemble` returns populated\n`AssembleResult` with `systemPromptAddition.length > 0`. The length\nassertion specifically distinguishes \"helpers worked through to the\ninner success path\" from \"helpers threw but outer try/catch caught it.\"\n- `new MemClawContextEngine(null)` — same tolerance, defense-in-depth.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` in `plugin/` — **261/261 pass** (259 prior + 2 new).\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_plugin_source_manifest.py` — **11/11 pass** (no\nnew src files, just edits).\n- [x] `npx tsc --noEmit` clean.\n- [x] Compiled dist verified — line 35 has `config?.tenantId`,\nconstructor has `?? {}` coercion.\n- [ ] Customer post-deploy: `journalctl --user | grep \"memclaw\\]\nassemble: unexpected error\" | tail -5` returns empty (was firing\nrepeatedly pre-fix).\n\n## Version\n\n2.6.3 → **2.6.5**. The 2.6.4 number is taken by PR #234's published\nartifact (already running on the customer's machine); release-please\nreverted `package.json` on main back to 2.6.3 (commit `fd253f76`) as\npart of its release-management workflow, so bumping from main's current\n2.6.3 to 2.6.4 would collide. **2.6.5 gives the customer an unambiguous\nversion string to verify the deploy.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T18:34:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/78e10fb3cc21021883798d43d8e09f55bb33890d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/78e10fb3cc21021883798d43d8e09f55bb33890d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/78e10fb3cc21021883798d43d8e09f55bb33890d/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e2d805e8b80aa24ba22312e4c9ee35b6381c56ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e2d805e8b80aa24ba22312e4c9ee35b6381c56ce","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e2d805e8b80aa24ba22312e4c9ee35b6381c56ce"}]},{"sha":"e2d805e8b80aa24ba22312e4c9ee35b6381c56ce","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGUyZDgwNWU4YjgwYWEyNGJhMjIzMTJlNGM5ZWUzNWI2MzgxYzU2Y2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-28T18:31:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T18:31:19Z"},"message":"perf(entity-extraction): collapse worker N+1 storage HTTPs (P1) (#245)\n\n## Summary\n\nAudit P1 — `process_entity_extraction` previously issued up to **6 HTTPs\nper entity**: 1 embed, 2-3 inside `upsert_entity` (find_exact /\nfind_similarity / update_or_create), 2 for the entity link (find /\ncreate). For a 10-entity memory that's ~60 HTTPs; the audit-validation\nflagged ceilings around 240.\n\nAfter P1: **one ``asyncio.gather`` round + 3 bulk HTTPs per memory**,\nregardless of entity count.\n\n## Sites collapsed\n\n| Stage | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Embeddings | Serial `await get_embedding(name)` per entity | One\n`asyncio.gather` with `return_exceptions=True` |\n| Entity upsert | Per-entity `upsert_entity` (2-3 HTTPs internally) |\nOne `sc.bulk_resolve_entities` + client-side merge + one\n`sc.bulk_upsert_entities` |\n| Entity links | Per-entity `find_entity_link` + `create_entity_link` (2\nHTTPs) | One `sc.bulk_upsert_entity_links` |\n\n## Correctness gate: first-seen-wins canonical_name\n\nThe audit's most important correctness rule — see\n[`entity_service.py:91-100`](../blob/main/core-api/src/core_api/services/entity_service.py#L91-L100).\nWhen an existing entity matches (exact or similarity), the **existing**\n`canonical_name` wins and the new surface form accumulates in\n`attributes[\"_aliases\"]`. This guards a real prior regression where\n\"longest-wins\" promoted LLM hallucinations to canonical rows.\n\nThe worker ports ``entity_service.upsert_entity``'s merge logic (lines\n74-100) verbatim into a client-side step between resolve and upsert.\n\n## Behavior preserved\n\n- Blocklist + min-length filter applied **before** the bulk batch (was\npreviously interleaved with per-entity HTTPs)\n- Duplicate `canonical_name` in `graph.entities` collapses to first\noccurrence (matches old `name_to_id`-dict semantics)\n- Per-entity embed failure → `None` in resolve payload → Phase 2 skipped\nserver-side; exact-match still runs (same skip semantic as old\nper-entity try/except)\n- Audit log, contradiction trigger, cross-link discovery wiring\nunchanged\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] **New** `tests/test_p1_entity_extraction_bulk.py` (11 tests):\n- **Shape** (5): one of each bulk call per memory; zero per-row HTTPs;\nempty graph skips bulk; blocklist filter; duplicate-name collapse with\nrole binding\n- **State-equivalence** (6): first-seen-wins canonical regression guard,\nalias preservation/extension, no-match→create, embed-failure→null,\nrole-per-entity link binding, `ENTITY_RESOLUTION_THRESHOLD` constant\nthreaded through\n- [x] Existing `tests/test_entity_linking_wiring.py` (3 tests) migrated\nto bulk mocks; same cross-link wiring assertions\n- [x] **140** entity-adjacent tests pass (P1, wiring, blocklist,\np0_1_matching, p3_1_resolution, a5c_tenant_config,\nstorage_bulk_endpoints)\n- [x] Full unit sweep: **1338 passing**\n- [x] Ruff lint + format clean\n- [x] mypy clean on core-api (pre-existing `config.py` croniter stub\nerror unrelated)\n\n## Audit queue status after this PR\n\n| Audit ID | PR | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| B4 (MCP error envelopes) | #217 | merged |\n| P1/P2/P5 storage foundation | #222 | merged |\n| T5 + #22/#25/#29/#31 | #235 | merged |\n| P2 (contradiction batch) | #236 | merged |\n| P5 (crystallizer archive) | #239 | open |\n| **P1 (this PR)** | — | open |\n\nAfter this PR + #239 merge, **all of Ran's assigned audit findings\nship.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6366f4167db63ebe117e55c09fb924a903b6fbcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/6366f4167db63ebe117e55c09fb924a903b6fbcc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/e2d805e8b80aa24ba22312e4c9ee35b6381c56ce","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGIn3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmmYQAGoS+pbsZJuDqbDtTLBY1ceW\nSl3OIeMJDNiLdwKb/NI+lGzS/3om/A6FnAi1hQu1LKFxVQzsPKxG50O9CCFUc3SD\njHS11EtJ2UbtrRDn7ZCCrSlW38SLOsMKRzMh1Ta21kjI7dVulJ4umTT0Rl5i3hD/\nTifEX7BHnsW8J1T1RqMUq9Eeconzzr/nMyztGnDOXYEsHOjGl+shsGstw19lh/62\nDdIzjYGB08X3s2i8wZoGDYK+GoKIvlNrREmy7JNNoHWBQj18CNbFGbdgxG1hWmMh\n2vZcstYwGM0frzFSTDRnTnGmuHXbO31UHfhW0XR7jSonLXBVht1iP7VakS84CgMU\noyGANoON6JUxGM0k3OdVozP5h5o+/q4bvygqtetb1+qku5Mig0k+H47+TF6o+R54\nBlwIjKeb76hN9lGxhVxxIJGAmcT+KeAg8uQnY2/S7mxv4fdvN1ArZakMw9CFK49K\nQF0DTZMbxNmkRMr+/8VixSWi8BMpOIG6z+5o138i9y8I/IQ1qR5OK4R05GzTjQss\nAtjt392T+PGQ4bZNk67gDDXXKFdLfD9HbOLDlBIdbwpV9/MA9dEprQcj3wHdj4vn\nqleIs33p0O5xwBJfWNRHB3bfj0GHjgEsT36kZ4an3EgVnk8WNNDybInzp6V3nwwe\n6sj1bCrVDQU5A72HBxXg\n=b5hl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6366f4167db63ebe117e55c09fb924a903b6fbcc\nparent 454a233d6fdbaaad67053bf40e3e7b584c956f52\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1779993079 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779993079 +0300\n\nperf(entity-extraction): collapse worker N+1 storage HTTPs (P1) (#245)\n\n## Summary\n\nAudit P1 — `process_entity_extraction` previously issued up to **6 HTTPs\nper entity**: 1 embed, 2-3 inside `upsert_entity` (find_exact /\nfind_similarity / update_or_create), 2 for the entity link (find /\ncreate). For a 10-entity memory that's ~60 HTTPs; the audit-validation\nflagged ceilings around 240.\n\nAfter P1: **one ``asyncio.gather`` round + 3 bulk HTTPs per memory**,\nregardless of entity count.\n\n## Sites collapsed\n\n| Stage | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Embeddings | Serial `await get_embedding(name)` per entity | One\n`asyncio.gather` with `return_exceptions=True` |\n| Entity upsert | Per-entity `upsert_entity` (2-3 HTTPs internally) |\nOne `sc.bulk_resolve_entities` + client-side merge + one\n`sc.bulk_upsert_entities` |\n| Entity links | Per-entity `find_entity_link` + `create_entity_link` (2\nHTTPs) | One `sc.bulk_upsert_entity_links` |\n\n## Correctness gate: first-seen-wins canonical_name\n\nThe audit's most important correctness rule — see\n[`entity_service.py:91-100`](../blob/main/core-api/src/core_api/services/entity_service.py#L91-L100).\nWhen an existing entity matches (exact or similarity), the **existing**\n`canonical_name` wins and the new surface form accumulates in\n`attributes[\"_aliases\"]`. This guards a real prior regression where\n\"longest-wins\" promoted LLM hallucinations to canonical rows.\n\nThe worker ports ``entity_service.upsert_entity``'s merge logic (lines\n74-100) verbatim into a client-side step between resolve and upsert.\n\n## Behavior preserved\n\n- Blocklist + min-length filter applied **before** the bulk batch (was\npreviously interleaved with per-entity HTTPs)\n- Duplicate `canonical_name` in `graph.entities` collapses to first\noccurrence (matches old `name_to_id`-dict semantics)\n- Per-entity embed failure → `None` in resolve payload → Phase 2 skipped\nserver-side; exact-match still runs (same skip semantic as old\nper-entity try/except)\n- Audit log, contradiction trigger, cross-link discovery wiring\nunchanged\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] **New** `tests/test_p1_entity_extraction_bulk.py` (11 tests):\n- **Shape** (5): one of each bulk call per memory; zero per-row HTTPs;\nempty graph skips bulk; blocklist filter; duplicate-name collapse with\nrole binding\n- **State-equivalence** (6): first-seen-wins canonical regression guard,\nalias preservation/extension, no-match→create, embed-failure→null,\nrole-per-entity link binding, `ENTITY_RESOLUTION_THRESHOLD` constant\nthreaded through\n- [x] Existing `tests/test_entity_linking_wiring.py` (3 tests) migrated\nto bulk mocks; same cross-link wiring assertions\n- [x] **140** entity-adjacent tests pass (P1, wiring, blocklist,\np0_1_matching, p3_1_resolution, a5c_tenant_config,\nstorage_bulk_endpoints)\n- [x] Full unit sweep: **1338 passing**\n- [x] Ruff lint + format clean\n- [x] mypy clean on core-api (pre-existing `config.py` croniter stub\nerror unrelated)\n\n## Audit queue status after this PR\n\n| Audit ID | PR | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| B4 (MCP error envelopes) | #217 | merged |\n| P1/P2/P5 storage foundation | #222 | merged |\n| T5 + #22/#25/#29/#31 | #235 | merged |\n| P2 (contradiction batch) | #236 | merged |\n| P5 (crystallizer archive) | #239 | open |\n| **P1 (this PR)** | — | open |\n\nAfter this PR + #239 merge, **all of Ran's assigned audit findings\nship.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T18:31:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e2d805e8b80aa24ba22312e4c9ee35b6381c56ce","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e2d805e8b80aa24ba22312e4c9ee35b6381c56ce","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e2d805e8b80aa24ba22312e4c9ee35b6381c56ce/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"454a233d6fdbaaad67053bf40e3e7b584c956f52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/454a233d6fdbaaad67053bf40e3e7b584c956f52","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/454a233d6fdbaaad67053bf40e3e7b584c956f52"}]},{"sha":"454a233d6fdbaaad67053bf40e3e7b584c956f52","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQ1NGEyMzNkNmZkYmFhYWQ2NzA1M2JmNDBlM2U3YjU4NGM5NTZmNTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-28T12:44:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T12:44:45Z"},"message":"feat(core): deletion-preview counts (CAURA-696 PR A — OSS half) (#246)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds the **read-only forecast** of what a subsequent hard-delete would\nremove. Mirrors `purge_tenant_data` (CAURA-689) one-for-one — same table\nset, same scoping columns — so the preview is a faithful \"what will be\ndeleted\" view for the OPS UI (CAURA-693) and the customer self-delete\nflow (CAURA-697).\n\n## Layers (OSS)\n\n| Layer | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `core-storage-api` | New\n`PostgresService.count_tenant_data(tenant_id)` — `SELECT count(*)` per\ntable over the same `_PURGE_TENANT_TABLES` + `_PURGE_ORG_KEYED_TABLES`\nconstants. Returns the full per-table breakdown including zeros. New\n`POST /api/v1/storage/preview/tenant-counts` router — same VPC-internal\ntrust model as the existing `purge` route. Hardened JSON-decode\n(`JSONDecodeError` + `UnicodeDecodeError`) and non-object-body guard —\nsame defences PR #244 round 1 added to the suppression router. |\n| `core-api` | New `CoreStorageClient.count_tenant_data` HTTP wrapper.\nNew `POST /admin/org/preview-data` admin route. Body `{tenant_ids}`.\nReturns `{counts: {tenant_id: {table: row_count}}, failed: {tenant_id:\nerror}}`. Per-tenant isolation; 200 clean / 207 Multi-Status partial.\n**No `lifecycle_audit` row** — a preview is a query, not a lifecycle\nevent. Same validation + 100-tenant cap as `purge_org_data`. |\n\n## Why a separate route from purge\n\n- Read-only — should be cheap to call from the preview UI on every\nconfirm-dialog open.\n- No state side-effects → no audit row → no on-call noise.\n- Same per-tenant isolation + 207 contract → admin-api can use one code\npath for both.\n\n## What's not in this PR (PR B follow-up)\n\n- Per-org count endpoint on `platform-storage-api` (enterprise rows:\norg, tenants, members, api_keys, etc.).\n- Aggregator at `platform-admin-api`: `GET\n/api/v1/org-lifecycle/{org_id}/deletion-preview` that combines\nplatform-storage (enterprise) + core-api (OSS, all tenants in the org)\ninto a single unified payload for the OPS UI / self-delete UI.\n- OPS UI panel itself — that's CAURA-693.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `core-storage-api/tests/test_preview.py` — happy path (3 seeded\nmemories → `memories=3` + zeros), unknown-tenant returns all zeros,\nread-only, 422 on missing/empty/malformed/non-object body.\n- [x] `uv run mypy src/` on core-api + core-storage-api → clean\n- [x] `uv run ruff check` + `format --check` → clean\n- [ ] CI integration suite against ephemeral postgres\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Eldad Caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd291d276fb1ffe7b45cecbbb6c4fec4a0ca7650","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/cd291d276fb1ffe7b45cecbbb6c4fec4a0ca7650"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/454a233d6fdbaaad67053bf40e3e7b584c956f52","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGDi9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzXEQAEF6y7xY+8W2lBG6jSjNgVl5\n0gY/bW3wJT5alye39hZ916m2GYKKYLyEpihZcZGQcuqZIhw4v+dVpG6/4FkGBasZ\nu6RX+Sxe2HVsw/a6DYD98xHrMqubpWKOB0485g7W64T2dJuhwuE0HOmYEyNBSdCK\nMXhMHTtuWwD1CjQCh74/zUgI5y14Tuo0m84ibjCfNvWDx0+7o2+XUQwNgcCD5FjN\nHhvQ5/C24Oj9ez4ppHQXplQA6YnLSRXmFqQlqRLudLqHTVfXCQIfft118aE5NULc\nrD7zDDyGiLoKpaE8HeFdRGmgci+K3PMtzOATDSw/vhMnhTw6GAUJ6xh8/FPWDVDb\njvUZ45TFp8azzwCfyqPeOdcZsUCgl2tJm61ChCW9mugFTnaspam/g7D6r8IZYiYJ\nxE/Rj1c/JgDbAmVNjBZrOtho7Z5W/PR5F4ZFwHM8BUxy57ZlVEEdj4BL+YxIy3so\nPBNyrBSAdPJkQ+kre38PYVA+OArKXTaQOHG52cytkvVpdEcjgl/m+D8uxgWTYo7/\nTc2jHEdVIynvlyAvbme/RnpzuBbbANeFyzEJybxDEMgC7FVG13nOFI2t4gfk9ZB3\nxUXhUZWm1kpRdvt14AWnelV9/Cc+5gxqzV6IWJlDJ0bmXLY3nQqgeQu5Rk9TCrAA\n08SkzJtiYJU8vW2vgm8C\n=f9/x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cd291d276fb1ffe7b45cecbbb6c4fec4a0ca7650\nparent 64cf3e446cf26b634e3dee39197f2fcc76affe88\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1779972285 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779972285 +0300\n\nfeat(core): deletion-preview counts (CAURA-696 PR A — OSS half) (#246)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds the **read-only forecast** of what a subsequent hard-delete would\nremove. Mirrors `purge_tenant_data` (CAURA-689) one-for-one — same table\nset, same scoping columns — so the preview is a faithful \"what will be\ndeleted\" view for the OPS UI (CAURA-693) and the customer self-delete\nflow (CAURA-697).\n\n## Layers (OSS)\n\n| Layer | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `core-storage-api` | New\n`PostgresService.count_tenant_data(tenant_id)` — `SELECT count(*)` per\ntable over the same `_PURGE_TENANT_TABLES` + `_PURGE_ORG_KEYED_TABLES`\nconstants. Returns the full per-table breakdown including zeros. New\n`POST /api/v1/storage/preview/tenant-counts` router — same VPC-internal\ntrust model as the existing `purge` route. Hardened JSON-decode\n(`JSONDecodeError` + `UnicodeDecodeError`) and non-object-body guard —\nsame defences PR #244 round 1 added to the suppression router. |\n| `core-api` | New `CoreStorageClient.count_tenant_data` HTTP wrapper.\nNew `POST /admin/org/preview-data` admin route. Body `{tenant_ids}`.\nReturns `{counts: {tenant_id: {table: row_count}}, failed: {tenant_id:\nerror}}`. Per-tenant isolation; 200 clean / 207 Multi-Status partial.\n**No `lifecycle_audit` row** — a preview is a query, not a lifecycle\nevent. Same validation + 100-tenant cap as `purge_org_data`. |\n\n## Why a separate route from purge\n\n- Read-only — should be cheap to call from the preview UI on every\nconfirm-dialog open.\n- No state side-effects → no audit row → no on-call noise.\n- Same per-tenant isolation + 207 contract → admin-api can use one code\npath for both.\n\n## What's not in this PR (PR B follow-up)\n\n- Per-org count endpoint on `platform-storage-api` (enterprise rows:\norg, tenants, members, api_keys, etc.).\n- Aggregator at `platform-admin-api`: `GET\n/api/v1/org-lifecycle/{org_id}/deletion-preview` that combines\nplatform-storage (enterprise) + core-api (OSS, all tenants in the org)\ninto a single unified payload for the OPS UI / self-delete UI.\n- OPS UI panel itself — that's CAURA-693.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `core-storage-api/tests/test_preview.py` — happy path (3 seeded\nmemories → `memories=3` + zeros), unknown-tenant returns all zeros,\nread-only, 422 on missing/empty/malformed/non-object body.\n- [x] `uv run mypy src/` on core-api + core-storage-api → clean\n- [x] `uv run ruff check` + `format --check` → clean\n- [ ] CI integration suite against ephemeral postgres\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Eldad Caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T12:44:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/454a233d6fdbaaad67053bf40e3e7b584c956f52","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/454a233d6fdbaaad67053bf40e3e7b584c956f52","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/454a233d6fdbaaad67053bf40e3e7b584c956f52/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"64cf3e446cf26b634e3dee39197f2fcc76affe88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/64cf3e446cf26b634e3dee39197f2fcc76affe88","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/64cf3e446cf26b634e3dee39197f2fcc76affe88"}]},{"sha":"64cf3e446cf26b634e3dee39197f2fcc76affe88","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDY0Y2YzZTQ0NmNmMjZiNjM0ZTNkZWUzOTE5N2YyZmNjNzZhZmZlODg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-28T10:57:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T10:57:17Z"},"message":"feat(core): OSS suppression mirror + boundary guard (CAURA-694) (#244)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds the OSS-side consumer of the `memclaw.org.suppression-changed`\nevent that enterprise `platform-admin-api` already publishes (CAURA-691\n/ -695). Synchronously gates **core-api** on the mirrored state so a\nsuppressed org cannot read or write through any auth path — even before\nthe durable hard-delete sweep lands.\n\n## Layers\n\n| Layer | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `common/events` | `Topics.Org.SUPPRESSION_CHANGED` constant, typed\n`OrgSuppressionEvent` payload (`{tenant_ids, action: \"suppress\" \\|\n\"restore\"}`), shared `register_suppression_consumer` factory. Per-tenant\nfailures re-raise so Pub/Sub redelivers (DLQ on max-delivery, configured\nin CAURA-695). |\n| `core-storage-api` | Migration **019** creates\n`public.tenant_suppression` (`tenant_id` PK + nullable `suppressed_at`).\nService primitives `set_tenant_suppression` / `is_tenant_suppressed`.\n`ON CONFLICT` preserves the original `suppressed_at` on duplicate\n`suppress` so the canonical timestamp survives Pub/Sub redelivery. New\n`POST /tenant-suppression` + `GET /tenant-suppression/{tenant_id}`\nendpoints under the same VPC-internal trust model as `routers/purge.py`.\n|\n| `core-worker` | `upsert_tenant_suppression` client method +\n`_SuppressionAdapter` wiring in `register_consumers`. |\n| `core-api` | `suppression.is_tenant_suppressed` with a **30-s TTL**\ncache (mirrors the auth-api `_is_org_deleted` pattern from CAURA-690).\n**Fail-open** on storage transport errors so a storage flap can't take\ncore-api down. `auth._block_if_suppressed` injected into all four\ntenant-resolving paths in `get_auth_context` (memclaw-key standalone /\nheader, standalone mode, X-Tenant-ID). Admin paths bypass via `tenant_id\nis None`. |\n\n## Defence-in-depth\n\nThe CAURA-690 auth-api gate is still the first-line synchronous block\nfor JWT / cookie / API-key login. This guard catches the remaining\nAPI-key paths and OSS-standalone deployments where there is no auth-api\nin front.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `uv run pytest tests/test_suppression_handlers.py\ntests/test_suppression_boundary.py` → 13 passed\n- [x] `uv run mypy src/` on core-api / core-storage-api / core-worker →\nall clean\n- [x] `uv run ruff check` + `ruff format --check` on every touched file\n→ clean\n- [ ] `core-storage-api/tests/test_tenant_suppression.py` (integration\nsuite, requires CI DB)\n- [ ] End-to-end against staging once CAURA-695's pubsub resources land:\npublish a `suppress` event, observe row in `tenant_suppression`, observe\n403 on a request keyed by the suppressed tenant.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Eldad Caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9668e024fe4b981cebbd5acdbe22bc8fae0ba1d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9668e024fe4b981cebbd5acdbe22bc8fae0ba1d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/64cf3e446cf26b634e3dee39197f2fcc76affe88","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGB+OCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2HcQAHyPPqEhXbqKkbvCwggkVXaH\nCzvqu28TcvZN7bFUCS0SHpdmbhQsZ+2XXpxznPHv3aRodCryNZ8320S1Ba0EN/va\nkuIXzURQuErAVMO2I2OBxTmDGUNBzdrr8fBhlF+SwSDWtYvf4c63NeLfoW5mJy7J\ncyjfY6fUTStdurSHWxEK5Ka8aj/6Dn6xKbsRAYQRhuL0AAHHmKMcnGgUH8qdpSOr\nHVbM7sZXOGWD+MZRVL/zpXlp8c26N5wnI6wUQhepP8R9qvk1hIVU6OsMkXB6wzU+\nSihb2IDWnFfyQeVV4cYkLT8jrnaci58IH6RhqdrVkEXLIdCC9NVhdnstoYRl3udn\ngsHtAD14/ULfQ5hMktlC/haCM/5Ev9fKFC/OgHArqcX4262m5MIpZ6YH7vWrGhk9\n4J7DFvIgRubZeXpjWARAUa/rF/Ay5qVh58H/67n49UXeV700iYk6J29P8S3xaXVk\nPJw0QlgedjYQf3dvLKV9ouV+nOsrf5O4dSBpnSHwujZfhqL8mHsvxKFYO194FHNL\npTKFjQ4W+3JTuzDO/tDxtVZPvByN/PBrP8CF/c1TLN9tLRUpGFldHSnufCyyhjgd\nuFE41LBc1QxgU2VvRo2pRmsgJakBnMqVbfUj6Coeu+y9kulNpCieQKplXgOl2opw\nIfkj3Qcr3DLOvxjYfm26\n=CEya\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9668e024fe4b981cebbd5acdbe22bc8fae0ba1d2\nparent f3d896b1890e5e2e46e166afdf225d475046ebf0\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1779965837 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779965837 +0300\n\nfeat(core): OSS suppression mirror + boundary guard (CAURA-694) (#244)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds the OSS-side consumer of the `memclaw.org.suppression-changed`\nevent that enterprise `platform-admin-api` already publishes (CAURA-691\n/ -695). Synchronously gates **core-api** on the mirrored state so a\nsuppressed org cannot read or write through any auth path — even before\nthe durable hard-delete sweep lands.\n\n## Layers\n\n| Layer | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `common/events` | `Topics.Org.SUPPRESSION_CHANGED` constant, typed\n`OrgSuppressionEvent` payload (`{tenant_ids, action: \"suppress\" \\|\n\"restore\"}`), shared `register_suppression_consumer` factory. Per-tenant\nfailures re-raise so Pub/Sub redelivers (DLQ on max-delivery, configured\nin CAURA-695). |\n| `core-storage-api` | Migration **019** creates\n`public.tenant_suppression` (`tenant_id` PK + nullable `suppressed_at`).\nService primitives `set_tenant_suppression` / `is_tenant_suppressed`.\n`ON CONFLICT` preserves the original `suppressed_at` on duplicate\n`suppress` so the canonical timestamp survives Pub/Sub redelivery. New\n`POST /tenant-suppression` + `GET /tenant-suppression/{tenant_id}`\nendpoints under the same VPC-internal trust model as `routers/purge.py`.\n|\n| `core-worker` | `upsert_tenant_suppression` client method +\n`_SuppressionAdapter` wiring in `register_consumers`. |\n| `core-api` | `suppression.is_tenant_suppressed` with a **30-s TTL**\ncache (mirrors the auth-api `_is_org_deleted` pattern from CAURA-690).\n**Fail-open** on storage transport errors so a storage flap can't take\ncore-api down. `auth._block_if_suppressed` injected into all four\ntenant-resolving paths in `get_auth_context` (memclaw-key standalone /\nheader, standalone mode, X-Tenant-ID). Admin paths bypass via `tenant_id\nis None`. |\n\n## Defence-in-depth\n\nThe CAURA-690 auth-api gate is still the first-line synchronous block\nfor JWT / cookie / API-key login. This guard catches the remaining\nAPI-key paths and OSS-standalone deployments where there is no auth-api\nin front.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `uv run pytest tests/test_suppression_handlers.py\ntests/test_suppression_boundary.py` → 13 passed\n- [x] `uv run mypy src/` on core-api / core-storage-api / core-worker →\nall clean\n- [x] `uv run ruff check` + `ruff format --check` on every touched file\n→ clean\n- [ ] `core-storage-api/tests/test_tenant_suppression.py` (integration\nsuite, requires CI DB)\n- [ ] End-to-end against staging once CAURA-695's pubsub resources land:\npublish a `suppress` event, observe row in `tenant_suppression`, observe\n403 on a request keyed by the suppressed tenant.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Eldad Caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T10:57:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/64cf3e446cf26b634e3dee39197f2fcc76affe88","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/64cf3e446cf26b634e3dee39197f2fcc76affe88","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/64cf3e446cf26b634e3dee39197f2fcc76affe88/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f3d896b1890e5e2e46e166afdf225d475046ebf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f3d896b1890e5e2e46e166afdf225d475046ebf0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f3d896b1890e5e2e46e166afdf225d475046ebf0"}]},{"sha":"f3d896b1890e5e2e46e166afdf225d475046ebf0","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGYzZDg5NmIxODkwZTVlMmU0NmUxNjZhZmRmMjI1ZDQ3NTA0NmViZjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-28T07:35:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T07:35:43Z"},"message":"feat(storage): purge_org_data primitive for org hard-delete (CAURA-689) (#241)\n\n## Summary\n\nOSS side of the organization hard-delete (epic CAURA-513). Permanently\nremoves all `public.*` data for a set of `tenant_ids` (every tenant of\nan enterprise org being deleted). Enterprise `platform-admin-api` calls\nthis during the hard-delete sweep / force-delete; the `enterprise.*`\nrows are torn down separately by `platform-storage-api`.\n\n- **core-storage-api** — `PostgresService.purge_tenant_data(tenant_id)`\nhard-deletes every row scoped to a tenant across the OSS schema in **one\ntransaction, children-before-parents** (so a FK never blocks a delete),\nreturning per-table counts. `memory_entity_links` cascades from\n`memories`/`entities`; `organization_settings*` are keyed by `org_id`\n(== tenant id in OSS). **`lifecycle_audit` is intentionally retained** —\nit's the audit trail. Exposed via `POST /purge/tenant-data`.\n- **core-api** — admin route `POST /admin/org/purge-data` (admin-key)\nloops the `tenant_ids`, wrapping each storage purge in a\n`lifecycle_audit` row (`hard-delete-org`, `pending` →\n`success`/`failure`) and **isolating per-tenant failures**. The route\nopts out of the request-timeout middleware (terminal batch op, bounded\nby the storage client's own timeout).\n\nIdempotent: re-purging an already-purged tenant deletes nothing and\nreturns zeros, so a retried org hard-delete is safe.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `core-storage-api/tests/test_purge.py` — 4 integration tests (real\nPG): deletion + per-table counts, idempotency, tenant-isolation,\nvalidation. All pass.\n- [x] `ruff check src/` + `ruff format --check src/` + `mypy src/` clean\nfor both core-storage-api and core-api.\n- [ ] Reviewer: confirm the purge table set stays in sync with the OSS\nschema (new tenant-scoped tables must be added to\n`_PURGE_TENANT_TABLES`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"13d83087537a5890cf2ea5b03bf02eb7dfa0cd57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/13d83087537a5890cf2ea5b03bf02eb7dfa0cd57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/f3d896b1890e5e2e46e166afdf225d475046ebf0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqF/BPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASnkQABuGRZ5eA4Ad8oLyJ3E5AUtM\n+jWiFSHrpp/uhwdECIN24iIQQyGzEK3Adt7nE/qRRp2PPPtSwYWLumBQEpNNQTp7\nGV3prOFUrBct0zSffJRgFg8FrC/bVBeFrdGi6H6y3r/0HnGO/9KdetQfIrNwBzzV\n63fP45HXYGXjhQmF3de9NtpAm655jJMjIgxBmER9gg19BipPQ/BOYucMwMg+YE7l\nNAFh5qDTliJTzSoKQSldMKuQIE/YeQr1C1pZMQEaiigYhuEoONcE1H8GjAPpc4rb\nEYUQM6TzWTGzOHA5xb7XmZiXaLr7EQYr2CUqLhywVRWOPpgndE9vdAL1i+JGpfyz\nt5SlmKKHrg9bsQu87ii/JP4UeflklRVVftqH1Smnegi8Wivqp2wDaOeIwbPtr+bE\nJUt7+aBXz9WQtai/M+OsOhl9IfZBtkSA0mdAyfMgHWBoX6SHWJbcgQ6NPFUC/d42\nyZx4np0FwtTiLM+W0b8Lbmq4unyEeYKIYq0u3xPvrvEdwvT9IEbOu3GaFi43ygCA\nTkOjeQkBRWzb6mMghlWz8/7M4T6SHauL0YfCpFqHCtdaCOvyLW5nysGqciq2uuzi\n5EBEB1FmGEwLbmZ9AW00XsL+rLNq2Ltq+3cQQghd0pqErxixZ9lC7kUlljP77qGY\nVvVbrN7PhzVq8xNTl7er\n=dd5R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 13d83087537a5890cf2ea5b03bf02eb7dfa0cd57\nparent fd253f76b8103876d5b69134201d82fcf2fa316e\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1779953743 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779953743 +0300\n\nfeat(storage): purge_org_data primitive for org hard-delete (CAURA-689) (#241)\n\n## Summary\n\nOSS side of the organization hard-delete (epic CAURA-513). Permanently\nremoves all `public.*` data for a set of `tenant_ids` (every tenant of\nan enterprise org being deleted). Enterprise `platform-admin-api` calls\nthis during the hard-delete sweep / force-delete; the `enterprise.*`\nrows are torn down separately by `platform-storage-api`.\n\n- **core-storage-api** — `PostgresService.purge_tenant_data(tenant_id)`\nhard-deletes every row scoped to a tenant across the OSS schema in **one\ntransaction, children-before-parents** (so a FK never blocks a delete),\nreturning per-table counts. `memory_entity_links` cascades from\n`memories`/`entities`; `organization_settings*` are keyed by `org_id`\n(== tenant id in OSS). **`lifecycle_audit` is intentionally retained** —\nit's the audit trail. Exposed via `POST /purge/tenant-data`.\n- **core-api** — admin route `POST /admin/org/purge-data` (admin-key)\nloops the `tenant_ids`, wrapping each storage purge in a\n`lifecycle_audit` row (`hard-delete-org`, `pending` →\n`success`/`failure`) and **isolating per-tenant failures**. The route\nopts out of the request-timeout middleware (terminal batch op, bounded\nby the storage client's own timeout).\n\nIdempotent: re-purging an already-purged tenant deletes nothing and\nreturns zeros, so a retried org hard-delete is safe.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `core-storage-api/tests/test_purge.py` — 4 integration tests (real\nPG): deletion + per-table counts, idempotency, tenant-isolation,\nvalidation. All pass.\n- [x] `ruff check src/` + `ruff format --check src/` + `mypy src/` clean\nfor both core-storage-api and core-api.\n- [ ] Reviewer: confirm the purge table set stays in sync with the OSS\nschema (new tenant-scoped tables must be added to\n`_PURGE_TENANT_TABLES`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T07:35:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f3d896b1890e5e2e46e166afdf225d475046ebf0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f3d896b1890e5e2e46e166afdf225d475046ebf0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f3d896b1890e5e2e46e166afdf225d475046ebf0/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fd253f76b8103876d5b69134201d82fcf2fa316e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fd253f76b8103876d5b69134201d82fcf2fa316e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fd253f76b8103876d5b69134201d82fcf2fa316e"}]}]